window.AKK_STREET_SMART_HEIRESS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_STREET_SMART_HEIRESS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: Are They Really Demoting the Second Male Lead","paragraphs":["He lowered his head and pressed on, \"Why did Brother Bao send you guys to abduct people?\"","Xiao Qian's eyes darted around, then he answered, \"The compound's short on people, plain and simple. We need both men and women—we snatch who knows how many people every day.\"","Qi Yuan sneered and slapped him across the face. A handprint instantly bloomed on his tan cheek.","\"Do you take me for a fool?\"","Bribing Liwei Spring to fake the records, first-class direct flights, five-star hotel stays the whole way...","All that, just so this Brother Bao could snatch two girls back to the compound for some online scam scheme?","Does that even make sense?","Xiao Qian, face red, insisted, \"What else could it be? Don't believe me? Ask them—Brother Bao runs a telecom fraud racket up in northern Myanmar.\"","\"Let me out—mmph—\" Sang Biao thrashed around like a fish on dry land, desperation written all over his face.","Let him talk. Let him talk!","The stinking sock was yanked from his mouth, and Sang Biao shouted at the top of his lungs, \"Brother Bao's a fraud boss, sure—but Xiao Qian's definitely holding something back!\"","\"Don't slap him! He's into that—you're rewarding him! Shove a stinky sock in his mouth instead, choke him out with the stench!\"","Xiao Qian snapped, \"What the hell's wrong with you?\"","No one was even interrogating him. Why was he showing off like that?","Sang Biao just wanted a few minutes of clean air. That's all. Just a few minutes.","Qi Yuan slowly pulled a scalpel from his coat. The sharp tip pressed against Xiao Qian's cheek. \"Rewarding him? That won't do. How about I carve this piece of flesh off and take the reward back?\"","His tone was calm, but Xiao Qian shivered involuntarily. \"I... I...\"","Sang Biao got excited again: \"Damn! That's still a reward for him! Just stuff a sock in his mouth—he'll spill everything for sure—\"","The sock was shoved back between his lips, and he went back to muffled, frantic grunts.","Wrong move! Not in his mouth—in Xiao Qian's!","The scalpel stood upright, the tip almost piercing skin. Qi Yuan stared at him coldly. \"This is your last chance.\"","Xiao Qian's eyes kept shifting away. \"You... you wouldn't dare. Killing someone is against the law...\"","Qi Yuan let out a scoff. \"Kid, this is Sawa. You're not a local. How much police effort do you think Sawa's force will waste on you? By the time they figure out the facts, do you think I'll still be in Sawa?\"","Cross-border manhunts aren't exactly easy.","Besides, \"I'm a doctor. Making someone die quietly is very easy for me.\"","A hint of a smile crept into his eyes—one laced with barely concealed eagerness. It made Xiao Qian's heart pound with dread.","\"I don't know what their grievance is! I swear!\"","He spilled quickly. \"But Brother Bao's been back in the country lately. That woman—she probably pissed him off somehow, and he wanted to get even. That's all I know. Really!\"","\"Brother Bao's back in the country?\"","Qi Yuan was surprised. A northern Myanmar scam boss operating on home soil?","He remembered He Huanhuan was also in Jiangcheng—meaning Brother Bao was in Jiangcheng too.","He glanced at Qi Jin, whose face had gone dark. \"Looks like you guys aren't doing a great job.\"","Qi Jin grabbed his phone to call his superior, but Qi Yuan snatched it away. He panicked. \"Bro, what are you doing? I need to report this up the chain!\"","Qi Yuan shot him a look. \"Jiangcheng has twenty million residents. You plan on telling your boss to search one by one?\"","Qi Jin's face carried that stubborn, law-enforcement resolve: \"One by one—we'll find him eventually.\"","Qi Yuan rolled his eyes at him. \"The second you make that call, your vacation ends. And this Brother Hu we've got here—who's going to look into him? The Sawa police?\"","That would mean writing a several-thousand-character application for international cooperation.","The moment Qi Jin thought about the paperwork, his head cleared up. \"Bro, you mean...\"","Investigating on their own first, then reporting it later?","Qi Yuan gave him a none-too-gentle kick. \"What else?\"","Why take the long, painful route when there's an easier way?","\"Load them into the car. We've got a show to watch.\"","Let Brother Hu rack his brain wondering where all his men went.","Once they'd stuffed everyone into the trunk, Qi Jin couldn't help asking, \"Bro, why didn't you ask them where Brother Hu is? We could storm his place and squeeze the truth out of him.\"","Qi Yuan opened He Huanhuan's chat. [They've got an elephant show today. Want to watch?]","A reply came back instantly. [Watch! Definitely watch!]","The corner of his mouth lifted. \"We paid for this tourist package. Are you that rich, wasting it just like that?\"","Qi Jin was speechless. Wasn't it all his own money anyway?","Qi Yuan had only finished his residency a couple of years ago, and the economy had been rough since. His department had just gotten last year's bonus this year—this year's wouldn't come until at least next year.","Dr. Qi looked fancy, but his wallet was emptier than anyone's.","Didn't matter though. His little brother had been working for years, no girlfriend, and a fat savings account.","Brother's money is his money. Brother's elegance wasn't all for show after all.","He took He Huanhuan to see the elephant show, then dragged her into a photo with ladyboys across the border. Her laughter wouldn't stop. \"God! Dr. Qi, you're the best! When are you flying back? I have to treat you to dinner!\"","Qi Yuan smiled lightly. \"Treat me to spicy malatang or beef noodles?\"","She'd once posted a WeChat moment: [No more pretending. Sister's got money now—living large! Eating malatang without wringing the broth dry! Treating all my ride-or-die girls to malatang! P.S.: don't come begging if you're not that close—one bowl of beef noodles is already generous!]","The photo showed three bowls of beef noodles—so she'd been eating with not-so-close friends.","He had no idea that the people sitting behind that photo were Han Mo and Qi Meili.","That \"don't come begging if you're not that close\" line was the edgy flirting of a hidden alt-girl.","But Dr. Qi had never dabbled in that scene. He figured it was just her quirky caption.","On the other end of the video, He Huanhuan beamed. \"You like malatang too? I thought doctors were all strict about food hygiene.\"","Qi Yuan chuckled. \"I used to order it all the time during night shifts at the hospital.\"","\"Done deal!\" He Huanhuan agreed readily. \"When you're back, hit me up. I'll get you malatang—for real now!\"","\"Alright.\"","\"I'll hang up then...\"","\"We're about to go snorkeling by the coast. Want to watch?\"","Her peach-pink hair zoomed into the frame. \"Yes! Make sure you show us handsome guys with abs! Lots of them!\"","Qi Yuan couldn't help but laugh. \"Will do.\"","The video call kept going, never dropped.","At Han Group headquarters, Han Mo brought Wang Qiang back to his office and asked, \"Can you drive?\"","Wang Qiang shook his head. \"No.\"","\"Then I'll arrange for you to get a license. Once you have it, how about being my driver?\"","Wang Qiang hesitated. \"Um... I actually don't really want to be a driver...\"","Han Mo gave him a curious look. \"Then what do you want to do?\"","Wang Qiang's face turned red. \"I want to be a security guard...\"","A poor man's natural destination—the golden trio of gigs: security guard, cleaner, and nanny.","Wang Qiang didn't have big ambitions, nor did he want to take too much from Han Mo.","He'd secretly looked it up on his phone during the ride—even a security guard at Han Group made eight thousand a month. He figured that would be perfect for him.","Han Mo said helplessly, \"How is driving for me taking advantage of you? I told you I'd give you a good life—how could I let you work as a security guard?\"","But Wang Qiang was a stubborn kid and insisted on being a security guard.","Unable to talk him out of it, Han Mo decided to video-call He Huanhuan to have her persuade him instead.","Unexpectedly, the call went through—but was cut off with a single busy tone.","Alarm bells rang instantly in his mind. What did this mean? Was he really about to get demoted from the male lead's sidekick?"]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: Is He Your Boyfriend","paragraphs":["He thought for a moment, then transferred another sum of money to He Huanhuan.","He knew her well—when his sister saw a transfer come in, she'd accept it right away. Not accepting would drive her crazy.","But he waited, and waited, and the money never got picked up.","He drummed his fingers on the office desk, tapping until his knuckles were faintly flushed. His phone remained still.","Finally, he couldn't take it anymore. He stood and headed out.","Downstairs, Wang Qiang had already received his beloved security uniform and was standing proudly at the company entrance.","Seeing Han Mo come out, the kid snapped a crisp salute: \"President Han!\"","Han Mo: ... This kid... did he drink from the same cup as Liang Ye in the underworld?","He grabbed Wang Qiang and started pulling him away, but Wang Qiang dug his heels in and resisted: \"President Han, what are you doing? My onboarding is done—you can't back out now!\"","Han Mo shoved him into the car: \"I'm not backing out. You're coming with me on an outside job.\"","He needed to check on what He Huanhuan was doing, and Wang Qiang made the perfect excuse.","The car pulled up to the hotel. He called Gu Jinghan and asked, \"Which room are Huanhuan and the girls staying in?\"","Gu Jinghan: \"Why are you asking? That's a young lady's privacy, you know?\"","Han Mo: \"I need to talk to her, but I can't reach her. Her phone's been busy.\"","The excuse was solid, so Gu Jinghan relented: \"Thirteenth floor, the corner suite at the end. I haven't seen her leave all day, so she might just not be checking her phone.\"","He was He Huanhuan's second brother—nobody could take that away from him.","He didn't understand the urgency of being threatened in status.","Han Mo didn't hesitate. He took Wang Qiang straight into the hotel, rode the elevator to the thirteenth floor, and headed for the corner suite.","\"Knock, knock, knock...\"","The sound of knocking rang out. He Huanhuan said to the person on the video call, \"Wait for me a second, I'm going to answer the door. Don't hang up, okay!\"","Qi Meili, meanwhile, had her entire mind lost in the video—oh my god, there were so many handsome guys doing snorkeling!","She'd been mixing with the wrong crowd all along. Why had she been wasting her time as some edgy young punk?","She should've been a lifeguard at the beach!","The door opened, and He Huanhuan was stunned: \"Han Mo! What are you doing here?\"","Didn't he have a meeting this afternoon?","Han Mo's gaze silently swept across the room before landing on the phone Qi Meili was holding.","The screen was facing the doorway. Across a few meters, Han Mo spotted the man on the other side of the screen.","A handsome young man with gold-rimmed glasses, looking about twenty-six or twenty-seven, a hint of a smile at the corner of his mouth.","Though he was speaking to Qi Meili, his eyes from behind the glasses were fixed directly on the doorway.","They locked eyes from a distance.","Han Mo quickly looked away and stepped closer to He Huanhuan: \"I tried calling you, but your line was busy the whole time. I transferred you some money, but you didn't accept it. I got a little worried, so I came to check on you.\"","\"Money?!\"","He Huanhuan's eyes lit up instantly: \"You transferred me money again!\"","Oh! He was just too good!","She immediately turned around and threw herself onto the bed, opening her phone and exiting the video call. The message notifications popped up one after another—one, two, three, four, five zeros. Han Mo had sent her another hundred thousand!","Hehe, that's five more square meters toward her three-bedroom apartment.","In an instant, she was smiling so hard her eyes squinted shut.","On the other end of the video, Qi Yuan looked at the person on his screen, her face brimming with joy she couldn't contain.","His heart gave an involuntary lurch, and before he knew it, he asked the question he shouldn't have: \"Is that... your boyfriend?\"","He had only just met her, just an online conversation so far. Asking that was crossing a line.","But the way He Huanhuan looked at Han Mo was so familiar, and the two of them were so at ease with each other. He couldn't help but ask.","He didn't even know what answer he wanted to hear.","Yes, he's my boyfriend.","Or, no, I'm currently single.","As these thoughts churned, he realized with shock that he was hoping for the denial.","Hoping she was single.","Had he really... fallen for this girl he'd never met in person?","But how was that possible?","He had been clever since childhood, and his model for love had always been his parents—","A quiet devotion, love growing over time.","He'd always believed love was an illusory thing, something pure fiction dreamed up by literature.","It was through grinding together, getting along, talking and sharing every little detail—feelings nurtured by years and time—that made real love.","So how could he like a girl he'd only video-called twice?","He didn't even know a thing about her.","All he knew was that she showed up bright and sunny, a person whose eyes held endless laughter.","Beyond that, nothing.","In mere moments, these thoughts swirled wildly in his head.","But on the other end of the video, He Huanhuan had no idea. She just figured Qi Yuan was being nosy.","She smiled cheerfully and replied, \"He's far from being my boyfriend! For now, he's just a rather thick-skinned suitor~\"","Her tone was filled with affection she couldn't hide, and Han Mo's lips couldn't help but curl up.","If that wasn't a public announcement of sorts, what was?","He knocked on the door and asked He Huanhuan, \"Do you have a minute now? I need to talk to you about something.\"","He Huanhuan instantly shoved the phone into Qi Meili's hands: \"Of course I do!\"","Her face vanished from the screen, and Qi Meili eagerly urged Dr. Qi: \"Turn the camera around again! I just spotted a golden-haired hottie—his nose is so sharp, and his abs are fabulous...\"","He Huanhuan bounced over to the door, grinning, and asked Han Mo, \"What's up?\"","Han Mo pulled Wang Qiang over beside him: \"He doesn't want to be a driver, insists on being a security guard at the company.\"","\"...... And then?\"","He Huanhuan stared at him with wide eyes, waiting for the rest.","Han Mo shook his head: \"There is no 'then'... I tried to convince him, but he wouldn't listen. Thought I'd bring him here so you could talk some sense into him.\"","He Huanhuan and Wang Qiang exchanged glances, both utterly confused.","He Huanhuan asked, \"Why should I convince him?\"","Wang Qiang nodded frantically—yeah! Why?","A security guard job making eight thousand a month, off on weekends? That's an amazing job, right?","Han Mo: ......","His original plan was to make Wang Qiang his driver first. Once he adjusted, Han Mo would arrange a suitable school to send him to for further studies. Then he could bring him back into the company for a proper position.","Wang Qiang didn't get it: \"But I'm already working at the company right now?\"","Why go around in circles? It was still just working a job.","Wasn't being a security guard working, too?","......","Han Mo sighed in frustration: \"Security doesn't have much room to grow. You've got to think about your future.\"","Wang Qiang was even more confused: \"The company has a dorm and a cafeteria—room and board included. I can save seven thousand five hundred a month, which is ninety thousand a year. After a few years, I can buy a place. What else do I need to think about?\"","A man's whole life, isn't it all about getting a place and a car?","Once he saved up for a few years, bought himself an apartment and a car, he'd be a certified winner in life. Why chase anything more?","He Huanhuan gave him a thumbs up: \"Well said! I'll send you a neighborhood name later—buy your place in the same community as me, and we'll be neighbors, alright.\"","Han Mo: ...... How was it that everything he said actually sounded kind of convincing?"]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: Liang Zheng and Brother Hu","paragraphs":["It wasn't until Qi Jin finished snorkeling and came back that that striking pineapple-yellow head finally made its way back into frame.","A wave of disappointment welled up inside him, cresting again and again. Qi Yuan decided he couldn't wait any longer—he needed to figure things out faster.","He needed to get back to China, and soon.","Smiling, he said to Qi Meili, \"I've got some personal matters to attend to, so I won't video call you for a while.\"","Qi Meili didn't push him, nodding happily. \"Sure thing, Dr. Qi. We can video chat again next time we're free!\"","The moment the call ended, she thought she caught a glimpse of a familiar handsome face in the corner of the screen.","\"Huh? Isn't that...?\"","Before she could get a closer look, the call had already disconnected.","She rested her chin on her hand and thought, what a handsome face! And strangely familiar too. Who was it?","Out on the reef, Liang Zheng stood in his wetsuit with a grim expression.","He had spent two afternoons sitting in the lobbies of two different hotels, and hadn't run into a single soul.","He was starting to wonder—had they even come to Sava at all?","He couldn't help but call Liang Ye and ask, \"Didn't you say that He Huanhuan from the Gu family was traveling in Sava recently?\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"Yeah, Huanhuan won the grand prize and went to Sava with Meili for a seven-day trip!\"","Liang Zheng frowned. \"But I haven't seen them.\"","\"What?\"","Liang Ye was confused. \"Bro, how would you have seen them? They're in Sava—you're not there!\"","Liang Zheng replied flatly, \"The company is expanding into Southeast Asia. I came to Sava for a business inspection...\"","\"You're talking nonsense!\"","Liang Ye, as if blessed with a sixth sense, immediately saw through his brother's real motive: \"How big could Sava's market possibly be? There's no way they'd send you to inspect it!\"","Liang Zheng's heart skipped a beat. Before he could come up with an excuse, Liang Ye had already lost it: \"Bro! Are you into our Huanhuan or something?\"","......","What on earth was this nonsense?","\"How could you do this! You're my brother! How can you compete with me over a girl?\"","Liang Ye was in full meltdown mode: \"Han Mo's already generous enough—if you come in too, I won't stand a chance at all! I can't live like this! I really can't!\"","When his brother went all out, he could spend just as lavishly as Han Mo.","By then, Huanhuan would have Han Mo on her left, whooping money transfers left and right, and his brother on her right, casually gifting apartments and cars...","And he'd be stuck crying on an electric scooter!","He wailed so loudly that Liang Zheng's head began to throb. \"Stop crying.\"","The voice on the other end sniffled hard and lowered the volume by three notches. \"Waaaaah...\"","Liang Zheng sighed in exasperation. \"How old is He Huanhuan? How could I possibly like her?\"","As far as he remembered, he had even attended the Gu family's daughter's first birthday banquet back in the day.","He Huanhuan was probably about the same age as the Gu family's young lady. How could he ever be interested in such a young girl?","Liang Ye wasn't buying it. \"Huanhuan's gorgeous—how could you not like her? You're not telling me you like Qi Meili, are you? She's so fierce!\"","Liang Zheng blurted out, \"Where's she fierce?\"","She's just a bit forgetful and way too fond of good-looking men, that's all.","\"Ha!\"","Liang Ye got excited. \"You still say you don't like Huanhuan? You won't even admit Qi Meili is fierce! Bro, love the person, love their dog—you're head over heels, admit it!\"","......","There was no reasoning with a fool. Liang Zheng hung up and called Gu Jingchen instead. \"I heard your sister won the grand prize and is in Sava? I happen to be here too for the next couple of days...\"","\"She doesn't have a passport. She didn't go. What's up?\"","In one sentence, Gu Jingchen crushed all his probing.","Liang Zheng was stunned. \"She... they didn't what?\"","Gu Jingchen replied calmly, \"No passport.\"","The young master born with a silver spoon never dreamed he'd get such an answer after waiting around for two whole days.","For a moment, he didn't even know what to say.","Gu Jingchen waited a beat, got no response, and followed up: \"Are you looking for Huanhuan about something?\"","Liang Zheng snapped back to his senses. \"I just happen to be in Sava on business. I remembered your sister and her friend really like dyeing their hair all sorts of wild colors. I had an event I was thinking of inviting them to. Since they're not here, never mind.\"","Gu Jingchen nodded. \"Huanhuan does like that kind of thing. If you don't mind, I'll ask Huanhuan and Meili later and add you as friends on both their contacts.\"","Liang Zheng frowned. \"You have both of them as friends?\"","Qi Meili too? They were that close?","Gu Jingchen was puzzled. \"Is that strange?\"","He Huanhuan was his sister—of course they'd be friends.","And as for Qi Meili, needless to say, she'd want to add Gu Jingchen right away.","Sis only adds handsome men as friends, and the more, the better.","Liang Zheng replied with a hint of sourness, \"I don't mind. When you get the chance, ask for me.\"","\"Sure.\"","The call ended, and Gu Jingchen went about his own business.","Huanhuan was playing over at Jinghan's hotel lately, so there was no rush to ask.","But it was torture for Young Master Liang. He waited from day to night, then from night to day again, and still no word came.","He sat on the bed with a darkened face. She wouldn't even add him as a friend?","He hadn't done anything wrong—so why?","Just the last two times they met, she was calling him \"handsome\" and shamelessly taking advantage of him.","And now, just like that, she'd changed?","He couldn't wrap his head around it. He really, truly couldn't.","Love baffles the mind.","And women baffle it even more.","Brother Hu lay back on his recliner all night. Sang Biao didn't come back. Xiao Qian didn't come back either.","Brother Hu really couldn't figure it out—who exactly were those two women?","How could he have sent four of his men out, and all four of them simply vanished?","Where were they?","Success or failure, at least give him some kind of signal!","His phone buzzed furiously in his hand, but he didn't dare pick it up.","He couldn't bear to think about how angry Brother Bao would be if he found out it had failed again.","But then again, ignoring the call would probably make Brother Bao even angrier.","Either way, it was a knife to the throat. He steeled himself and switched the phone to airplane mode.","Don't call him—he was busy.","Why airplane mode instead of just turning it off?","Heh, because he didn't have Brother Bao on social media, and this way he could still play his online card game.","After a few rounds of cards, having lost two hundred million happy beans, he finally calmed down a little.","He sat in his chair, lit a cigarette, and thought—hell! They're just two little girls. I'll go catch them myself!","He refused to believe he'd end up disappearing too!","After waiting anxiously at the shop until past midnight, he shoved a gun in his left waist and a cleaver in his right, then strutted out the door, full of swagger.","No matter how skilled you are, fear the cleaver.","No matter how fast you are, one shot drops you flat!","Hey, little ladies—big bro's coming!","Following the information on his phone, he crept up to the suite door.","The hallway was dead silent, the only sound being his own heartbeat thumping wildly in his chest.","He couldn't help but swallow hard. This wasn't his first rodeo, so why was he nervous?","He pressed the master key card against the door. Click—the door opened.","He peeked inside. The room was pitch black, impossible to see anything.","All he could make out was a thick, human-shaped lump rising from the bed against the wall.","He slipped into the room and groped his way toward the bedside."]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: Case Reporting","paragraphs":["Brother Hu had originally started out in Sava doing kidnappings, so this kind of work came to him as naturally as breathing.","Unlike Sang Biao, who would pounce and pin someone down, he slipped a single hand under the blanket, planning to twist the person's arm behind their back in one smooth move.","Under normal circumstances, once you got someone's arm twisted behind them like that, even a grown man lying in bed couldn't struggle free.","He felt around cautiously under the blanket, then felt again... Wait. Where's the arm?","He didn't believe it, so he shoved his hand in deeper. Damn! Rope!","A trap!","He went to pull out his gun, only to hand his wrist straight to Qi Jin.","\"Ow ow ow... that hurts, that hurts...\"","Brother Hu's case proved it: a grown man's arm, once twisted behind his back, really can't break free.","Qi Jin kicked him in the face and pinned him hard to the floor. Then, with one hand, he threw back the blanket and asked Sang Biao, who was lying there obediently: \"Who is he?\"","Sang Biao's gaze met Brother Hu's instantly. \"He's Brother Hu.\"","\"Sang Biao, you're betraying me?\"","Brother Hu demanded loudly, but Sang Biao didn't even flinch. \"Bro, I only charged you five hundred. You can't expect me to play loyalty for that price, right? That's way too cheap!\"","Brother Hu fumed: \"Five hundred is still money! I'm never hiring you again!\"","\"Ha!\"","Qi Jin let out a cold laugh. \"You think you're gonna have another job after this? Get ready to spend your days at a sewing machine, pal!\"","He pulled a rope from the bed and tied Brother Hu up tight in no time, then, along with Xiao Zuo and Xiao You, tossed him against the wall to lie in a row.","In the corner of the room, on the sofa, Qi Yuan sat in front of them, a scalpel in his hand. He looked down at Brother Hu. \"Why did Brother Bao have those two girls taken?\"","Brother Hu shot him a glare. \"You ask me, who do I ask? I take money; I do the job. Chit-chat costs extra!\"","\"Is that so?\"","Qi Yuan smiled slightly. A glint of cold steel flashed in his hand, and the scalpel plunged straight into Brother Hu's thumb web.","The web of the thumb is dense with nerves and lacks thick fat for protection. Brother Hu jolted in agony. \"You son of a bitch! I told you! I don't—\"","Before he could finish cursing, the scalpel was yanked out and redirected toward his face!","\"Ahhh...!\"","When the blade came at his face, he'd actually breathed a sigh of relief.","Anyone in the underworld had been stabbed a time or two, right?","But the blade grazed his cheek and buried itself in the soft flesh behind his ear.","Damn! That hurt like hell!","The knife tip twisted around in the tender flesh, and he broke out in a cold sweat from the pain. \"Damn it! Fine, I'll talk—\"","But before he could finish, his fingertip suddenly erupted in agony.","He looked down. Damn it! He'd become Xia Ziwei [a reference to a character from the classic Chinese melodrama \"My Fair Princess\" who gets her fingers tortured with needles]!","\"Damn it! I said I was going to talk!\"","Why stab his fingers too? It hurts so much!","Qi Yuan looked at the blade tip lodged into the cuticle and laughed softly. \"I've always wondered what 'ten fingers connected to the heart' actually feels like. Thanks for the demonstration.\"","Thanks my ass! He was worse than Nurse Rong [the notorious torturer from the same drama]!","Afraid Qi Yuan might go further, he rushed to confess: \"All I know is that girl was in his way. What exactly she was in the way of, I really don't know.\"","In the way?","Qi Yuan's eyes flickered. \"Give me more details.\"","The \"in the way\" part was actually Brother Hu's own guess. Brother Bao never gave him reasons when he gave orders, and Brother Hu never asked.","One ran telecom fraud, the other ran kidnappings — a perfect crime chain. Why bother asking?","Especially since Brother Bao had splashed out big this time, handing over 200,000 upfront.","To be clear, in the past, when Brother Hu kidnapped someone for Brother Bao, it was 50,000 per person, not a cent more.","200,000 for two girls — such a good gig, he wasn't about to ask questions.","But that time, after Brother Bao finished giving orders, he didn't hang up the phone in time, and Brother Hu overheard him murmuring two sentences to a woman.","Qi Yuan's gaze sharpened. \"What did they say?\"","Brother Hu tried to recall: \"Brother Bao said, 'It's all arranged. From now on, she'll never get in your way again.' Then a woman's voice answered, 'Got it,' and the call ended.\"","He thought for a moment, then added: \"That woman's voice was real pretty. Must have been a looker.\"","Sang Biao couldn't help but jump in: \"You've never tried online dating. Some people have the sweetest voice but look like a flounder! Ahh, don't get me started...\"","Brother Hu shot him a dirty look. \"Would Brother Bao be with her if she were ugly? You idiot!\"","Sang Biao snapped back: \"Can't Brother Bao pursue love? You're so shallow!\"","...","Whether it was because they were thick-skinned or just dim-witted, the two actually started bickering.","They argued so loudly that Qi Yuan's head ached. He waved a hand and had Qi Jin stuff dirty socks into both their mouths.","So this \"Brother Bao\" was right there beside He Huanhuan.","He glanced at Qi Jin. \"Call your superior. Report the details clearly.\"","\"On it!\"","Qi Jin had been dying to report to his boss anyway. Just thinking about that fraud kingpin living it up in Jiangcheng was driving him crazy.","The call went through. Before the superior could even start scolding him, what Qi Jin said snapped the man fully awake.","The superior sat bolt upright and asked Qi Jin: \"Really?\"","Qi Jin nodded. \"Really. They're all in my hands. Not one missing — every last one tied up.\"","\"Good, good, good...\"","The superior scrambled to get dressed. \"Hold them there for now. I'm heading to the bureau to file a request. We need to investigate this thoroughly!\"","\"Got it!\"","After hanging up, Qi Jin slept like a baby. He didn't get a call back until the afternoon.","On the other end, the superior's voice was dead serious: \"The Sava police will come by to pick them up soon. Cooperate with them properly. Don't go cracking jokes — don't embarrass the image of Chinese police. Understand?\"","Qi Jin grinned. \"Don't worry, boss! I'm the picture of seriousness!\"","...","The Sava police arrived fast — less than half an hour after the call ended, there was a knock at the door.","Qi Jin opened it to find a team of Sava officers standing there, all stern-faced.","Their leader, a middle-aged man, spoke in halting Chinese to Qi Jin: \"Officer Qi, hello. We're here under orders to arrest the suspects.\"","As a Chinese police officer, Qi Jin wasn't authorized to make arrests in Sava.","However, since Brother Hu and his crew had come to provoke him first, Qi Jin's act of capturing and interrogating them could barely pass as self-defense.","But the extradition and handover afterwards would have to follow the extradition treaty between the two countries and go through proper legal procedures.","Qi Jin had been working on anti-fraud operations since graduation, so he knew all these regulations inside and out.","He cooperated fully, handing Brother Hu and the others over to the Sava police.","Watching the officers leave with the captives, he clutched his chest in pain. \"My premium travel package! I spent seventy thousand on that!\"","His boss had called him back to China to assist the investigation, and just like that, his vacation was gone.","Seventy thousand — it would take him nearly a year to save that up again.","Back in the room, Qi Yuan had already packed all his luggage. He picked up his suitcase and said flatly: \"When my bonus from last year comes in next year, I'll cover thirty-five thousand of it.\"","Such a convoluted sentence. Such a heartbreaking one."]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: Returning Home","paragraphs":["The two of them dragged their suitcases downstairs to check out, and once that was done, they hailed a taxi and headed for the airport.","The taxi sped through the streets, the two of them each typing away furiously on their phones. Neither of them noticed that the police car at the hotel entrance had been sitting there quietly the whole time.","Inside the police car, the middle-aged man untied Brother Hu and the others with a look of disgust. \"Do you have any idea how much trouble you've gotten yourself into?\"","Brother Hu hastily pulled out his phone and gestured to the man. \"You've worked hard, you've worked hard...\"","The man pulled out his own phone and put his payment QR code right in front of him. Brother Hu scanned it and was about to transfer the money, but hesitated for a moment over the number keypad.","He typed in 1000, and Xiao Qian immediately elbowed him. \"Bro, you typed it wrong!\"","At a time like this, and still being stingy!","Was he really not afraid of losing his life over a few bucks?","Brother Hu looked up, and sure enough, the officer's face had turned black as thunder.","He quickly nodded and bowed. \"Mistyped, mistyped, so sorry...\"","He hesitated for a moment in his heart, gritted his teeth, and figured he'd transfer 5000 instead—pay some money to buy himself some peace.","Usually, they paid protection money of about 1,000 RMB a month, which came out to about 6,000 Thai baht.","He typed in 5000, and Xiao Qian quickly shot a glance at the middle-aged man's face—it still didn't look good.","He knew it then: this was serious, and that amount wasn't going to cut it.","But Brother Hu was a stubborn cheapskate by nature. There was no way he'd voluntarily pay more on his own.","Xiao Qian's eyes flickered for a moment, and he quickly reached over, added an extra zero after the 5000, and hit transfer.","Before Brother Hu even realized what was happening, the facial recognition had already gone through!","\"Hey? No no, that's wrong, that's wrong...\"","Brother Hu tried to get the money back, but the middle-aged man accepted the payment and walked away in under a second, the police car vanishing from their sight immediately.","\"Don't leave! Give me back the extra 45,000!\"","He couldn't catch up to the car, and Brother Hu was fuming inside. He was this close to kicking Xiao Qian to death on the spot!","He glared at Xiao Qian furiously. \"You damn kid! What the hell were you thinking sending that money? You just transferred half a dragon-skin leather away!\"","Xiao Qian rolled his eyes at him in disgust. \"Didn't you see how black his face was? Forget dragon-skin leather! If you hadn't paid him, you'd be lucky to keep any skin at all!\"","He wasn't some local criminal boss—just a small-time crew that paid monthly tribute and pulled off minor kidnappings.","Did Brother Hu really think the Sava police didn't dare touch him?","Brother Hu understood that logic well enough; otherwise he would've kicked Xiao Qian ages ago.","But understanding something and accepting it were two different things. His heart was bleeding.","He'd barely muttered Brother Bao's name when his phone screen lit up instantly. His heart skipped a beat, but he obediently answered.","The voice on the other end was blazing with fury. \"So you finally picked up, huh? Why didn't you just die in that hotel?\"","Brother Hu was stunned. \"Huh? Brother Bao, you knew I got arrested?\"","Chen Jiarong sneered. \"If I hadn't known, you think you'd be out by now?\"","\"What? Brother Bao, you pulled strings to get me out?\"","Brother Hu got so excited he kept slapping Xiao Qian. \"I told you we didn't need to give him 50,000! Brother Bao got us set free! You reckless little piece of trash!\"","\"Cut the nonsense!\"","Chen Jiarong was fed up hearing his drivel. \"If you can't handle the job, let Xiao Qian do it! If you're that keen on retiring, then what are you still doing in Sava?\"","Brother Hu's momentum deflated instantly. \"Brother Bao...\"","All these years, if it weren't for Brother Bao keeping his business alive, he never would've made this much money or gotten this far in Sava.","Chen Jiarong couldn't be bothered to waste more words on him. \"Tell Xiao Qian to bring a few guys back to China. I've got something for them to do.\"","Brother Hu hesitated. \"The plane tickets back to China aren't cheap...\"","Chen Jiarong gritted his teeth. \"I'll pay!\"","If his own men weren't being watched so closely, would he even lower himself to ask this useless crew?","What a bunch of good-for-nothings!","\"Alright!\"","Brother Hu agreed immediately. As long as he didn't have to pay, everything else was no big deal!","He turned and told Xiao Qian, \"Brother Bao wants you to bring some guys back to China. He's got something for you to do.\"","Sang Biao's eyes lit up instantly. He'd recently been in a long-distance online romance with a sweet girl back in China, so this could be the perfect chance—","The next second, Brother Hu's phone pinged. He opened it and read: \"Don't bring any idiots with you.\"","The \"idiot\" specifically referred to Sang Biao.","On the flight back, in first class, Qi Jin let out a contented sigh. \"At least we could use points to upgrade to first class on the way back. Otherwise we'd have been totally ripped off.\"","Qi Yuan had his eyes closed, lost in thought, ignoring him.","In economy class, Xiao Qian, along with Xiao Zuo, Xiao You, and Sang Biao, were sitting not too far from them.","Sang Biao was sprawled contentedly in his cramped seat. \"Xiao Qian, you're so good to me~ When I get back, I'll have my girl set you up with someone. You more of a sweet girl or a hot older woman type?\"","Xiao Qian shot him a look. The only reason he brought him along was because Sang Biao had practically begged on his knees.","\"Keep a low profile when you're back in China. Don't let Brother Bao find out you came too.\"","Sang Biao nodded frantically. \"I know, I know. I'll just focus on my love life and stay out of your way.\"","After the plane landed, first class was the first to disembark. The two brothers grabbed their suitcases and walked straight out.","Outside the airport, while waiting for a taxi, Qi Jin caught a glimpse of a few vaguely familiar figures heading toward them, joking and shoving each other.","He was about to take a closer look when a e-hailing beep suddenly blared, and the taxi driver leaned out to urge them. \"Passengers, let's go. Can't stay here long.\"","He pulled his gaze away, grabbed his suitcase, and got in.","The car slowly pulled away, and at that same moment, Xiao Qian and his crew reached the cab stand, still pushing each other around.","Sang Biao held up his phone. \"My girl booked us a ride-hailing car. It's on its way.\"","Xiao Qian grimaced. \"Why are you letting a woman spend money on you?\"","He was from the north, with traditional values—having a woman pay for things in a relationship just wasn't right. Real men paid for their women!","Sang Biao pouted. \"I'd love to pay for her. But do I even have the money?\"","Good point. Xiao Qian had no comeback to that.","Neither did he, honestly.","Boys of eighteen or nineteen were exactly at that age where money slipped through their fingers—if they had a hundred, they'd spend a hundred twenty.","And Brother Hu was such a miser, he gave them peanuts for wages. Barely enough to cover their own expenses, let alone spoil a girl.","Xiao Qian couldn't help sighing for that sweet girl back home. \"When did you even start this online thing? How come I never heard about it?\"","Sang Biao grinned slyly. \"Just a few days ago. She's crazy about me—calls me 'brother' day in and day out. How could I not come see her?\"","Xiao Qian looked at Sang Biao. He was about as average-looking as a guy could get, with that very typical small-town northern kid vibe—not ugly, but definitely not handsome.","What did that girl see in him?","He had to ask, \"You sure you're not getting catfished again? You forgot what happened with that three-hundred-pound chick last time?\"","Sang Biao pulled out his phone. \"You think I could forget that? This time I made sure we swapped real pics before we kept talking!\"","He held the phone up to Xiao Qian's eyes. A pair of big, sparkly eyes under a head of bubblegum-pink hair popped up on the screen.","Xiao Qian stared at the screen in shock. \"You're using fake photos for your online romance?\"","Back in the hotel suite, Qi Meili was posing in front of the mirror like crazy. \"Huanhuan, get ready! I'm taking you to see some hot foreign guys! Blonde, blue-eyed, eight-pack abs—absolutely gorgeous!\""]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: Where Is Her Blonde-Haired, Blue-Eyed Handsome Guy","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan was puzzled. “When did you meet a handsome foreign guy?”","Qi Meili pulled up a photo on her phone. “We met online. He’s insanely handsome. His eyes are this gorgeous blue-green—absolutely mesmerizing at first sight~”","He Huanhuan glanced at the screen. The man in the photo had fair skin, deep-set features, and sharply defined features.","His vivid blue-green eyes paired with his light blond hair made him undeniably handsome.","Unable to hold back her curiosity, she asked, “Where on earth did you meet someone that good-looking?”","With features this perfect, she figured you could only see a face like that on the runway at some high-end modeling show.","Qi Meili gave her a sly smile. “On an English-learning community app. Liang Ye told me to download it.”","“Liang Ye?”","He Huanhuan hadn’t expected Liang Ye to be involved. “Why did he tell you to download it?”","Qi Meili shook her head. “No idea. He asked me for a favor, and it wasn’t any trouble, so I helped him.”","As for the reason, she hadn’t bothered to ask.","She probably should have. Although the app was a global English-learning community, most of its users were from Southeast Asia.","Someone as exceptionally model-like as the man in the photo would never normally show up in a community like that.","So why was Liang Ye on the app?","Because it was free.","He didn’t want to work at the village committee and was hoping to transfer to the residents’ committee near their apartment complex.","But there was an international community near their complex, where all kinds of foreign residents lived.","So the job listing for the residents’ committee had an additional requirement: applicants had to be fluent in spoken English.","He wanted to learn English, but he was too stingy to pay for classes or hire a foreign tutor. So he bounced from one free app to another, shamelessly sending people messages like, “Say hello,” and, “Can I communicate with you in English?”","The app Qi Meili downloaded had a daily limit on greetings to strangers.","However, every successful referral earned the user ten extra greetings.","And for the referral to count, the new user had to successfully greet a stranger on the app at least once.","Liang Ye bombarded Qi Meili with eighteen messages in a row. He annoyed her so much that she finally downloaded the app.","She randomly picked a handsome profile picture, sent him a quick greeting, and was about to uninstall the app when, unexpectedly, the handsome guy replied within seconds.","The warm, exotic hunk instantly convinced her to stay. They chatted about everything under the sun for several days, after which the guy said he was coming to China to meet her.","Qi Meili had never met a foreigner that handsome before, so she agreed without a second thought.","She even thoughtfully booked him a ride-hailing car, sending it straight from the airport to his hotel.","He Huanhuan clicked her tongue. “You’re having an online romance with a foreigner? Is that even reliable?”","Qi Meili glanced at the ride’s location on her phone. “How can you call it an online romance? I only called him ‘big brother’ twice, and he was already hooked. Foreign boys are so easy to sweet-talk.”","She looked up at He Huanhuan. “Remind me to get the fare back from him later.”","Jason didn’t have any of the ride-hailing apps used in China, so she had booked the car for him.","But the first rule of Qi Meili’s man-appreciation code was simple: never spend money on a man.","There was a saying online—something like, “Spend money on a man, and you’ll be unlucky for the rest of your life.”","Qi Meili thought that saying was absolutely right!","So she had to get the ride fare back.","But she was afraid that seeing a handsome guy would make her mind go blank, so she asked He Huanhuan to remind her.","A ride from the airport would cost over eighty yuan. Way too expensive.","She curled her hair into pretty, girlish waves, cleared her throat, and put on the perfect sweet-girl voice.","Qi Meili pressed her lips together and flashed He Huanhuan a sugary smile. “Come on, let’s go meet the handsome guy!”","Meanwhile, in the ride-hailing car, Xiao Qian stared at the photos on his phone, utterly speechless. “Using fake photos for online dating is one thing, but why the hell did you use a foreigner’s photo?”","Sang Biao was wracked with guilt. “I didn’t mean to catfish her. I used that picture as my profile photo, and she thought I really looked like that. She was so sweet to me...”","She called him “big brother,” and even sent him such sweet selfies. How could he not fall for her?","By the time he’d come to his senses, there was no turning back.","Heaven only knew how hard he’d worked to find the Instagram account of the guy in the profile picture!","All those foreign hunks looked exactly the same to him: big eyes, high noses, the works. They were genuinely impossible to tell apart.","In fact, he’d gotten it wrong before.","Of the photos he’d sent Meili, at least three different handsome men had made an appearance.","But as luck would have it, Qi Meili couldn’t tell them apart either.","So the two of them carried on chatting for several days, each mistake building on the other. Qi Meili sent him several voice messages, and whenever he opened one, a sweet voice would coo, “Big brother, what are you doing~~”","Oh no!","He was in love!","He cast Xiao Qian an ingratiating glance. “When we get there, don’t expose me, okay?”","Xiao Qian was speechless. “Do you really think this is a matter of whether I expose you or not? You look absolutely nothing like the guy in those photos! She’ll be able to tell at a glance!”","“You’re not even the same race, for crying out loud!”","This online romance was doomed from the start.","Unexpectedly, Sang Biao wagged his index finger. “You just don’t get it. Have you heard the saying, ‘Since you’ve come all this way’?”","If he hadn’t returned to China, his baby would have discovered the catfishing online, and that would have been the end of it.","But he had traveled thousands of miles back to China and pursued love all the way to her doorstep.","Sure, he’d used fake photos, but as long as he wasn’t so ugly that he could shake the heavens and earth, there was no way things would fall apart.","Xiao You nearly burst out laughing. “Oh, stop talking nonsense. By your logic, what about that three-hundred-kilo girl you dated online last time? She came all that way too, so why didn’t you get together with her?”","To everyone’s surprise, Sang Biao answered with a perfectly straight face, “I did get together with her.”","She’d come all the way to Sava for him. How could he just send her home?","Besides, she was only a little on the plump side.","If you looked closely, she was actually quite pretty and delicate...","Xiao You fell silent. Was that really “a little on the plump side”? The girl had genuinely weighed three hundred kilos. That wasn’t an exaggeration—it was an objective description.","Xiao Zuo couldn’t help asking, “Then why didn’t she come back afterward? What, did she dump you?”","Sang Biao immediately fell silent. The others fell silent too.","So he really had been dumped by that huge girl?","Why?","Sang Biao said not to ask. Some things were better left unsaid.","Xiao Qian’s head was throbbing from listening to all this. “Oh, for heaven’s sake. I give up on you. You’re such a complete weirdo!”","He couldn’t be bothered to get involved anymore. The moment the car reached their destination, he was leaving. He absolutely refused to get dragged into Sang Biao’s ridiculous mess.","Even if that girl beat him to death, he was determined not to get involved. Serves him right!","That was what he was thinking when the car quickly came to a stop. The ride-hailing driver’s eyes lit up like copper bells. “Passenger, we’ve arrived at your destination!”","This was going to be good! He couldn’t wait to see whether this young fellow was about to get beaten up.","At the entrance to the hotel, Qi Meili saw on her phone that the car had pulled up right in front of them, and she instantly grew excited. “Huanhuan’s here, he’s here...”","Her gorgeous, blond-haired, blue-eyed hunk had arrived!","Their gazes quickly locked onto the black car by the roadside. The door slowly opened, and one sharp-looking young man stepped out. Then another...","By the time the door had closed completely, four sharp-looking young men were standing in a neat row. Qi Meili felt the sky come crashing down.","“Wait—what happened to my blond-haired, blue-eyed hunk?”","Where was he???"]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: Definitely Will Kill That Person for You","paragraphs":["She stared at the four young men by the roadside in disbelief: two average-looking guys, one slightly below average, and one who was at least halfway decent-looking.","But not a single one of them was her blond, blue-eyed European heartthrob!","Before she could recover, the gaze of the slightly-below-average guy had already landed on her, and his eyes instantly lit up. “Meili! You really came to pick me up! God! You’re even cuter than you looked in your pictures!”","......","The eternal law of online dating: your online lover will always be the ugliest one in his friend group.","The law never fails!","Qi Meili’s vision went black for a moment. “Huanhuan, is something wrong with my eyes? Why do I feel like I’ve gone back to my old county town?”","That obnoxious small-town street-punk vibe was just too familiar.","He Huanhuan couldn’t suppress her grin. “Aren’t you going to give your Jason a loving hug?”","She quickly pulled out her phone, secretly snapped a picture of the four street punks, and sent it to Han Mo. “Guess which one of these is the blond, blue-eyed European heartthrob?”","Han Mo: [? Is this a trick question?]","He Huanhuan burst out laughing. She reached over and pushed Qi Meili’s gaping mouth shut. “Hahahaha... Forget it, just consider this a lesson learned.”","She tried to pull Qi Meili back into the room, but the slightly-below-average guy suddenly rushed over. “Meili Baby, why did you stop calling me Big Bro?”","Qi Meili jolted back to her senses. “Oh my God! What a disgrace! I’m going to die!”","She leaped into the air and slapped him across the face!","“Smack!”","The slap landed perfectly on Sang Biao’s cheek, and five bright-red fingerprints immediately rose on his skin.","Sang Biao looked aggrieved. “Meili Baby, why’d you hit me?”","“Shut up! Don’t call me by my name!”","Furious, Qi Meili pointed at him and cursed, “You used a handsome guy’s photos to trick me? Don’t you have any shame?”","“Meili bb...”","Sang Biao gazed at her with tears in his eyes. “Didn’t you say you loved me for what was inside?”","Qi Meili snorted and grabbed him by the collar, hauling him upright. “I also said I was a sweet girl! Do I look sweet to you?!”","Those had only been sweet words to make a handsome guy happy. If he had a good-looking face, then of course she could fall in love with everything inside him too.","But without a good-looking face... hmph. Her love was in very short supply.","She shoved her phone in front of Sang Biao’s eyes. “Pay me back for the taxi fare!”","Sang Biao looked guilty. “I don’t have any money...”","He always spent whatever money he had. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have clung to Brother Hu’s leg, crying and begging him to let Sang Biao return to China with Xiao Qian.","Qi Meili snatched his phone away and opened WeChat to check his balance.","Good grief! 52.13.","Without a second word, she transferred every last cent to herself. The instant the payment went through, she added Sang Biao to her blacklist.","She tossed the phone back to him and kicked him. “Get lost! If I see you again, I’ll beat you up again!”","“Meili bb...”","Sang Biao refused to give up and still wanted to plead his case, but Xiao Qian grabbed him by the arm. “You’d better know when to quit!”","The girl had already been furious enough over being fooled by those fake photos. Going up to bother her now was practically begging to get beaten up.","After dragging him to the side of the road, Xiao Qian took out his phone to call a cab.","The ride-hailing car that had just brought them from the airport was still parked by the roadside. The driver rolled down the window with a beaming smile and glanced at Sang Biao’s flushed cheeks.","“Where to, handsome? I can take you there.”","What a show this was—better than anything on TV!","The four of them took a taxi to the location Brother Bao had given them. After getting out, Xiao Qian glanced at Sang Biao’s long face.","“When we go in, make sure you say something nice to Brother Bao. Earn enough money to pay the driver back for the fare, got it?”","He couldn’t even afford a fare of eighty-some yuan. Wasn’t that embarrassing?","Sang Biao sniffed. “Xiao Qian, do you think she transferred 52.13 yuan from my phone because it means ‘I’ll love you for the rest of my life’?”","Xiao Qian rolled his eyes so hard they nearly disappeared. “Wasn’t that all the money you had on your phone?”","He could even turn being broke into romance. Seriously!","They took the elevator to the twentieth floor and found the room Brother Bao had mentioned. Xiao Qian pressed the doorbell.","“The door’s unlocked. Come in.”","When they pushed open the door, they saw a spacious living room. In the middle stood a six-seat sofa, its back facing the entrance.","Brother Bao was sitting on the sofa in a relaxed posture. He didn’t turn to look at them, merely extending an arm and snapping his fingers in their direction.","“Come sit.”","The four of them obediently walked over and took the seats beside him.","“Brother Bao.”","Chen Jiarong glanced at the four of them, his brows drawing together slightly.","“Sang Biao, what are you doing here?”","Hadn’t he told them not to bring any idiots?","Sang Biao hunched his shoulders. “Brother Bao...”","Chen Jiarong’s brows furrowed even more deeply. Xiao Qian hurriedly shifted over and blocked Sang Biao from view.","“Brother Bao, Sang Biao’s pretty skilled in a fight. Just give him a chance.”","If Sang Biao weren’t useful in a fight despite his awful temperament, Brother Hu wouldn’t have taken him on.","Chen Jiarong waved impatiently. “Fine, fine... Just keep an eye on him when the time comes. Don’t let him do anything stupid.”","Xiao Qian hurriedly nodded. “Thank you, Brother Bao. I’ll watch him.”","Chen Jiarong turned to Xiao Qian.","“I called you back because of those two girls. Something happened before they set out, and they never made it to Sawa. That’s why everything that followed happened.”","He reached out and tapped the documents on the table.","“These are the girls’ details. Study them carefully and memorize everything. Find an opportunity to kill them for me. Once they’re dead, I’ll send you straight back to Sawa. You must be cautious. There can be no mistakes. Understood?”","Xiao Qian nodded. “Don’t worry, Brother. We know what we’re doing.”","This wasn’t the first job like this they had taken. They had plenty of experience.","Getting captured by Qi Jin had been unavoidable. Qi Jin was simply too strong. They were nothing more than street thugs—how were they supposed to fight him?","But killing two young women would be easy. They just needed to find an empty alley and stab each of them once.","Sang Biao grinned and nodded. “Brother, you can count on me. I’ll make sure the job is done beautifully!”","Chen Jiarong couldn’t be bothered to respond. He only asked Xiao Qian, who was studying the information seriously, “Well? Any problems?”","Xiao Qian stared at the documents in his hands, his pupils contracting violently.","It was them?","Just half an hour ago, the pink-haired girl in the photograph had slapped Sang Biao across the face. The red mark on his cheek hadn’t even faded yet!","The world was far too small.","Sang Biao noticed that he hadn’t said anything for quite a while and leaned over curiously to take a look. “Why are you staring at it for so long? Is she that pretty?”","Xiao Qian abruptly snapped the file shut, blocking Sang Biao’s view.","He looked seriously at Chen Jiarong. “Brother Bao, you can rest assured. I definitely won’t let you down.”","Chen Jiarong smiled and nodded at him. “I’ve booked rooms for you at a hotel. It’ll be more convenient for you to work if you’re staying in the same place.”","With that, he pulled a thick wad of cash from his wallet and tossed it onto the table. “You young people never know how to manage your money. You’re probably broke by now, right? Take this and spend it. Once the job is done, I’ll give each of you another sum of money.”","Money they wouldn’t have to report to Brother Hu.","Xiao Qian’s eyes immediately lit up. He gripped the file in his hand even more tightly. “Don’t worry, Brother Bao. I’ll make sure I kill him.”","[The book is currently undergoing a trial reading. If you’ve made it this far, please leave a review if you can~ Thank you, everyone!]"]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: Hello, Dr. Qi","paragraphs":["With Chen Jiarong’s promise of a little extra money secured, Xiao Qian waved them off in satisfaction.","As they turned to leave, Xiao Qian’s sharp eyes caught a slender figure flickering past the door.","That fleeting glimpse of a delicate face reminded him of what Brother Hu had said: Brother Bao had killed those two girls for the sake of one woman.","Curiosity stirred in his heart. The moment he left the room, he pulled out his phone and searched online.","Reports about the Gu family’s real and fake heiresses quickly popped up. The two faces matched perfectly.","So that was it.","Sang Biao leaned over curiously. “What are you looking at?”","Xiao Qian shut off his phone and shot him a disdainful look. “Why are you curious about everything? Are you three years old?”","Sang Biao shrank his neck. “You don’t want to show me, then don’t. Why are you snapping at me? I just got dumped...”","Xiao Qian couldn’t help rolling his eyes again.","When the taxi stopped in front of the hotel, Sang Biao was stunned to discover that they had returned to the very hotel where he had just been beaten up!","He was baffled. “Why are we here?”","Xiao Qian paid the fare and got out. “We stay wherever Brother Bao tells us to stay. Why do you have so many questions?”","After swiping the room card and entering, Xiao Qian pulled out a hundred yuan and handed it to Sang Biao. “Go pay the driver back. Don’t make us men look bad.”","Sang Biao accepted the money with a grin. “Xiao Qian, you’re so good to me.”","Xiao Qian couldn’t be bothered to answer. “Hurry up. We still have serious business to discuss when you get back.”","“Got it!”","Sang Biao took the money and left without the slightest hesitation.","Once the door closed, Xiao Qian’s expression turned solemn. He pulled the file from inside his shirt and handed it to Xiao Zuo and Xiao You.","“This is a little complicated. Take a look and tell me what we should do.”","“What’s so complicated about killing two people?”","Xiao You accepted the file with a cheerful grin, but the moment he opened it, he froze.","“Holy crap! No way! Is this some kind of TV drama?”","Xiao Zuo’s eyes widened instantly. “What the hell? Isn’t this Sang Biao’s online girlfriend?”","If Sang Biao found out, how were they supposed to carry out the job?","That guy was unreliable enough as it was!","Xiao Qian nodded. “That’s why we can’t let him know. The three of us will handle it. Don’t let him get involved.”","Xiao Zuo nodded along. “Right, right... absolutely don’t let him know.”","What if the guy went berserk? Wouldn’t their trip back to the country be for nothing?","He hadn’t smoked weed for several days and was already dying for it. He still wanted to return to Sawa and spend a whole week getting high!","They absolutely couldn’t let Sang Biao ruin their business.","Xiao You couldn’t help asking, “Do we still split the money with him?”","They couldn’t exactly let him do nothing and still take an equal share, could they?","Xiao Qian glared at him irritably. “Of course we split it with him. Do you think he’d be happy otherwise?”","Obviously not. He had followed them back to the country, so he was definitely expecting to earn this money.","If Xiao Qian and the others kicked him out without a word, he would surely make a scene.","To be safe, they’d better give him a share.","Xiao You pursed his lips unhappily. “That’s way too easy for him. He does nothing and gets a share for free!”","The instant he finished speaking, a devastated sob came from behind the three of them.","“Don’t give me any of it! I don’t want this money!”","...","The three men turned around. Sang Biao was standing in the doorway, though none of them knew when he had arrived. His face was full of disbelief.","“Xiao Qian, you were just putting on an act, right? You were deliberately messing with me, weren’t you?”","How could something this absurd happen by coincidence?","He wasn’t the male lead in a cheesy romance drama. How could he possibly run into a situation like this?","But Xiao Qian stood there with a stern expression and said nothing, while Xiao Zuo and Xiao You immediately charged toward Sang Biao.","Everything was telling him the same thing: he really had become the tragic male lead in a melodramatic romance!","He slammed the door shut, then ran toward the elevator.","He had to go protect his love!","Xiao Zuo and Xiao You chased after him. Sang Biao had no choice but to dart into the stairwell and race downward.","He wanted to find Meili, but he had no idea which floor she was staying on. All he could do was charge frantically toward the lobby.","“Sang Biao! Get your ass back here!”","Xiao Zuo chased him down the stairs, shouting angrily, “Come back and we’ll talk this over!”","Sang Biao ran even faster. “I don’t believe you!”","He sprinted into the hotel lobby, and the moment he looked up, he saw Qi Meili standing by the entrance.","“Meili!”","Without a second thought, he rushed over and threw his arms around her.","“Waaah... Meili! Be with me! I swear I’ll never hurt you!”","He was so emotional that he lost control of his strength. In an instant, he had lifted Meili completely off the ground.","The sight left the siblings standing nearby speechless.","Gu Jinghan rubbed his eyes. “Has Meili’s taste really gotten this bad after just one day?”","He Huanhuan quietly pulled out her phone and snapped a picture. Then she pushed Gu Jinghan forward.","“Go rescue Meili!”","But their help wasn’t needed at all. Meili swung her legs up and delivered a flying kick, making Sang Biao yelp and release her.","“Ow!”","Before Meili had even fully regained her balance, her palm was already swinging.","“Didn’t I warn you?”","Smack!","“Stay the hell away from me!”","Smack!","“Otherwise, I’ll hit you every time I see you!”","Smack!","The sound of slaps mixed with her curses, echoing through the hotel lobby.","Xiao Zuo and Xiao You took advantage of the opportunity to rush out. They grabbed Sang Biao by the arms and tried to drag him away.","“Sorry about this, sis! We’ll take him away right now!”","Sang Biao struggled wildly. “I’m not leaving! Meili! Be with me! I’ll treat you well!”","Meili raised her middle finger without the slightest hesitation.","“I don’t like ugly guys. Get lost.”","Her rejection was so crisp and complete that she left Sang Biao no room for hope.","Sang Biao burst into tears. “If you won’t be with me, then I won’t protect you anymore!”","Meili shot him a disgusted look. “Get lost!”","Who needed him to protect her anyway? He could barely speak properly!","All of a sudden, Sang Biao stopped struggling and allowed Xiao Zuo and Xiao You to drag him into the stairwell.","After shutting the stairwell door, Xiao You cautiously asked, “What’s wrong with you?”","Why did he suddenly look so utterly heartbroken? It was kind of frightening.","Sang Biao rose to his feet with a mournful expression. “Now that I’ve lost love, I can’t lose the money too. Let’s go back and discuss how we’re going to do the job.”","The three of them quickly headed upstairs and disappeared into the stairwell.","At that moment, a cool, elegant figure stepped out of a taxi in front of the hotel entrance. Wearing gold-rimmed glasses, he walked slowly into the hotel.","He Huanhuan jumped up and waved at him. “Dr. Qi, over here!”","Qi Yuan spotted He Huanhuan at once. She was even more vibrant and lively in person than she had been in her photos and videos, smiling and waving at him like a little sun.","The corners of his mouth lifted involuntarily. Then he strode toward her.","When he reached He Huanhuan, he smiled and asked, “Have you been waiting long?”","He Huanhuan waved dismissively. “Not at all!”","If she hadn’t been waiting for him, they wouldn’t have come downstairs so early—and they certainly wouldn’t have gotten to witness such an entertaining spectacle!","She asked Qi Yuan, “Dr. Qi, what do you feel like eating?”","Qi Yuan reached up and adjusted his glasses. “Anything is fine.”","He Huanhuan lowered her head to look at the map. “Then how about mala tang? You said you wanted to try it. There’s a mala tang restaurant nearby. Let’s go eat there together. How about it, Han Mo?”","“Of course,” Han Mo replied.","A clear, warm male voice suddenly sounded behind him. Qi Yuan spun around and saw Han Mo standing there, the corners of his lips curved ever so slightly. “Hello, Dr. Qi.”"]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: Flashing Wealth","paragraphs":["Qi Yuan’s eyes flickered. “Hello. And you are?”","Han Mo didn’t answer his question. He simply smiled and said, “Thank you for taking Huanhuan sightseeing around Sava a couple of days ago. To show my appreciation, let me treat you to a casual meal today.”","He Huanhuan beamed. “So we get to have an expensive meal today!”","Han Mo affectionately patted her on the head. “Are you saying I don’t usually feed you well enough?”","Huanhuan didn’t notice the intimacy in his gesture at all. Wrinkling her nose, she said, “You really don’t. You’ve been so busy lately that Meili and I have been eating takeout at the hotel.”","The fondness in Han Mo’s eyes deepened. “Then today we’ll have something expensive.”","He gave Qi Yuan an apologetic look. “Dr. Qi, I’m afraid we won’t be able to have malatang today. Would you mind joining us for something else?”","Their gazes met in midair. Qi Yuan nodded. “Not at all. I’m fine with anything.”","Gu Jinghan immediately raised his hand. “Let’s eat at Mr. Chichen’s! I haven’t had their Maotai-marinated drunken crabs in ages!”","Maotai-marinated drunken crabs?","Qi Yuan’s expression shifted slightly. They sounded expensive.","And they were. When the car pulled up outside the restaurant, Qi Yuan knew at once that this was a place he could never afford.","He had never imagined that, right in the heart of the bustling city, there could be such a secluded and elegant villa-style restaurant.","From the outside, you wouldn’t even think it was a restaurant. You’d assume it was the home of some wealthy family.","The dark gates swung open, and a middle-aged man in a suit came out. He approached the car respectfully and said to Han Mo, “President Han, all the ingredients have been prepared. You can drive straight to the Yulan Pavilion.”","Qi Yuan understood every word, yet somehow understood none of it.","Wasn’t the car supposed to be driven to a parking lot?","He buried these thoughts deep inside and sat silently in the back seat.","He watched Han Mo take several hundred-yuan bills from his wallet and casually hand them to the middle-aged man.","The man bowed neither obsequiously nor excessively, simply lowering his head in thanks. “Thank you, President Han.”","There had to be five or six bills—about a day’s wages for him.","The car drove along a tree-lined road inside the gates, then turned left into a vast sea of magnolia blossoms.","Rows upon rows of white-and-green magnolias filled their view, and Qi Yuan fell completely silent.","Han Mo hadn’t said a word, yet he had laid bare the enormous gap between them.","Noticing his silence, Huanhuan turned to him and wrinkled her nose. “Dr. Qi, isn’t this restaurant ridiculously over-the-top?”","Qi Yuan gave a faint smile. “It’s all right.”","“The first time I came here, I was stunned too. They charge several hundred yuan just for the tip at the entrance. My goodness, it nearly scared me to death!”","How many funerals would she have to conduct before she could afford a meal here?","Her exaggerated remark brought a hint of amusement to Qi Yuan’s eyes. He couldn’t help nodding. “It really is astonishing. One day’s wages would only be enough to cover the tip.”","“Your salary is that high?”","Her gaze was completely sincere, as if he truly had an exceptionally well-paid job.","Warmth rose in his chest. He nodded. “Doctors do earn a decent income.”","At least among ordinary people, it was considered a respectable profession.","Han Mo nodded along. “Saving lives and healing the wounded is a great service. You deserve better pay.”","He didn’t take the opportunity to belittle Qi Yuan. Instead, he chatted with him in a genial manner, discussing a few details of his daily work and then touching on the tense relationship between doctors and patients.","Polite, yet distant.","The car finally drove into the sea of magnolias and stopped in front of a small building that radiated exquisite craftsmanship and refined elegance in every detail.","Han Mo pushed open the door and got out. “We’re here.”","Qi Yuan followed him out and walked toward the building.","Gu Jinghan’s car arrived behind them, with Qi Meili inside.","Watching the three of them enter the building, Gu Jinghan clicked his tongue. “Han Mo is quite the schemer!”","Qi Meili looked confused. “How is he being bad? He’s taking us out for a meal.”","A meal this expensive—if it weren’t for Han Mo, how could she and Huanhuan ever afford to eat here?","Gu Jinghan shot her an exasperated glance. “There’s no explaining it to you.”","“Then explain it properly.”","...","Gu Jinghan clapped his hands. “He’s showing off his wealth to that young doctor. Didn’t you notice?”","Qi Meili shook her head. “Wasn’t this the place you said we should eat at? What does it have to do with Han Mo?”","Besides, they were rich to begin with. Just standing there and breathing counted as showing off. They were both wearing Italian bespoke suits while she was dressed in polyester. What more did they need to do to flaunt their wealth?","Gu Jinghan grabbed her head and turned it toward the window. “I said we should eat at Mr. Chichen’s. I never said anything about reserving the Yulan Pavilion. The minimum spend at the Yulan Pavilion is twenty thousand yuan. What do you think that means?”","He was clearly trying to make that young doctor realize the difference between them and give up on Huanhuan.","Qi Meili’s eyes widened. “How much is the minimum spend?”","Gu Jinghan held up two fingers. “Twenty thousand.”","Qi Meili’s heart began to pound. “Do you think I could work here? I’m not greedy. I’d just like to stand at the entrance and greet people.”","Gu Jinghan burst out laughing. “You want the tips, don’t you?”","Qi Meili nodded earnestly. “Five hundred yuan! Who wouldn’t want that? Ask Huanhuan if you don’t believe me. She’d definitely want to work here too.”","On the second-floor balcony, Huanhuan gazed at the endless magnolia blossoms and sighed. “Wouldn’t it be wonderful if I could work here as a greeter? I’d get to look at the magnolias for free every day, and I could collect five-hundred-yuan tips.”","As expected of best friends—their thoughts were perfectly in sync.","Han Mo handed her a menu. “If you become a greeter, I’ll give you a thousand-yuan tip.”","Qi Yuan’s brows drew together slightly. He didn’t like the sound of that.","Huanhuan, however, didn’t mind in the slightest. She grinned and gave him a salute. “Thank you, boss. I’ll take you out for malatang after work.”","Han Mo returned the salute. “Thank you, greeter. I want the forty-yuan kind.”","Huanhuan glared at him. “You’re getting greedy. Thirty yuan at most. Anything over that won’t be reimbursed.”","Their familiarity and intimacy left him completely unable to get a word in.","Han Mo handed Qi Yuan another menu. “Dr. Qi, take a look and see what you’d like.”","Qi Yuan opened it. The very first dish was the Maotai-marinated drunken crab Gu Jinghan had mentioned—688 yuan for half a crab.","Wonderful. One day’s wages would only buy him half a crab.","He flipped through the menu. Iberian ham salad: 1,888 yuan.","Half a month’s departmental bonus, gone.","He closed the menu and handed it back to Han Mo. “I’ve never eaten food this expensive. President Han, you can order whatever you think is best.”","Han Mo smiled as he accepted it. “All right. I’ll have them serve some seasonal dishes. Fresh ingredients always taste best.”","Huanhuan immediately looked up. “Why does that sound so familiar?”","How could it not sound familiar? When she had first returned to the Gu family, Gu Chacha had said exactly the same thing while Gu Dad was taking her out for Japanese food!","Without hesitation, she shot Han Mo a glare. “I can’t believe it. You look exactly like Gu Chacha when you’re showing off!”","Han Mo: ...That wasn’t what he’d intended at all."]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: Do You Know Brother Leopard","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghan sat in the car without getting out, while Qi Meili was practically frantic. “If we don’t go now, we won’t get anything to eat!”","Gu Jinghan gave her a sly smile. “The dishes haven’t even been served yet. What are you rushing for? Let them chat for a while. It has nothing to do with us.”","He nudged Qi Meili with his elbow and asked curiously, “What was up with that guy at the hotel just now? Since when did you develop such terrible taste?”","Qi Meili’s face darkened instantly. “Don’t remind me. He used a handsome guy’s photo to trick me! I’m furious! I thought he was going to be some gorgeous, blue-eyed blond!”","Gu Jinghan recalled Sang Biao’s face. “He looked painfully average. Don’t bother with him anymore. If you really want, I can drug my brother and send him over to you.”","Qi Meili’s eyes lit up at once. “Really?”","His long, distinct knuckles knocked against her forehead. “You little pervert! I knew you had your eye on my brother!”","Every time Gu Jingshen came back, Qi Meili’s eyes would automatically grow misty.","Gu Jinghan glanced at himself in the rearview mirror. “Am I not handsome? Why don’t you get all misty-eyed when you look at me?”","Qi Meili looked confused. “Aren’t you trying to marry into money? I’m not rich.”","Gu Jinghan shot her an exasperated look. “You’re actually very principled.”","Qi Meili grinned. “Hehe. Not making things difficult for a beauty is basic courtesy.”","The two of them chatted in the car for a while before finally getting out and heading upstairs. Surprisingly, the atmosphere upstairs was quite harmonious. He Huanhuan was animatedly chatting with Qi Yuan.","She asked Qi Yuan, “Wasn’t the package supposed to last seven days? Why did you come back early?”","Qi Yuan explained gently, “My brother had some business at work, so we came back ahead of schedule.”","He didn’t mention the attempted ambush by Brother Hu and the others in their room.","Everyone looked as if they knew nothing. He was afraid that bringing it up recklessly might alert Brother Bao.","Did they know Brother Bao?","After thinking it over, he tentatively said to He Huanhuan, “It’s a shame. I heard there’s a Brother Bao performance the day after tomorrow. Apparently, it’s quite entertaining.”","“An Indian myna?”","He Huanhuan looked puzzled. “What’s so entertaining about a myna performance? Doesn’t it just imitate people?”","Qi Yuan understood immediately. She didn’t know who Brother Bao was.","Then why had Brother Bao tried to abduct her?","He glanced at Qi Meili beside him. Qi Meili smiled sweetly and looked back at him. “Dr. Qi, you like mynas? What a coincidence! I used to raise one when I was little.”","Gu Jinghan was astonished. “Seriously? You used to raise one of those things?”","...","Of course it was a lie! If you wanted to make a beauty happy, naturally you had to appeal to her interests!","What else was she supposed to say?","“Watching a bird talk isn’t entertaining at all”? Honestly, he had no idea how to play along.","The two of them turned around and began bickering. Qi Yuan merely smiled and didn’t interrupt.","Looks like she didn’t know either.","The instant he withdrew his gaze, he suddenly sensed something wrong. His eyes shifted sharply to the left, where they met a heavy gaze.","The eyes were filled with wariness and scrutiny.","It was Han Mo. He knew who Brother Bao was.","Neither of them said a word. Their gazes met silently in the air, probing each other. In the end, they lowered their eyes in tacit understanding.","The rest of the meal went remarkably smoothly. Han Mo no longer flaunted his wealth or displayed his intimacy with He Huanhuan.","He simply ate in silence.","It wasn’t until they had finished eating and settled the bill that Han Mo glanced at him with a smile. “Where do you live, Dr. Qi? Is it far? Why don’t I drive you home?”","Qi Yuan nodded agreeably. “Then I’ll trouble you.”","The other three stared in confusion.","Since when had those two become so friendly?","Sitting in Gu Jinghan’s car, He Huanhuan watched Han Mo’s vehicle slowly drive away and asked, utterly baffled, “What’s with Han Mo? Why is he driving Dr. Qi home for no reason?”","Were they really that close?","Why wasn’t he driving her home?","Gu Jinghan frowned in thought. “Dr. Qi has a PhD. He may have been overwhelmed by the power of knowledge and decided to set sail for the sea of learning, saying goodbye forever to uncultured people like us...”","Smack!","He Huanhuan slapped him on the back of the head. “Shut up! You’re always saying things I don’t want to hear!”","How was she uncultured?","She had passed the entrance exam for high school. She just hadn’t gone.","These days, as long as you passed the high school entrance exam, you could go to college.","By a generous process of rounding up, she was a college student too, all right?","Gu Jinghan silently gave her a thumbs-up. “I admire your confidence. Keep it up.”","He started the car and drove toward home. “Maybe he suddenly felt threatened. He could be threatening the doctor in the car right now, telling him to stop coveting you.”","“What?”","He Huanhuan was dumbfounded. “You think Dr. Qi is interested in me? Are you out of your mind?”","She had only video-chatted with Qi Yuan twice. They were barely more familiar than strangers passing on the street.","How could Qi Yuan possibly like her?","That was ridiculous.","Qi Meili was even more bewildered. “He likes Huanhuan? No way! He’s so old. How could he possibly be good enough for our Huanhuan?”","Didn’t you have to be thirty by the time you finished a PhD? Good grief! That was ancient!","Gu Jinghan: “...”","“You just said he was handsome.”","Wasn’t her attitude changing a little too quickly?","Qi Meili pursed her lips. “So what? Handsome is handsome, but he’s still not good enough for our Huanhuan, okay?”","Gu Jinghan glanced at He Huanhuan and couldn’t help nodding. “That’s true. He is a little lacking.”","His little sister was wonderful—lively, adorable, sunny, and beautiful. She was only a bit too old.","If she were a little younger, she could wait until he was old and then smash the funeral basin and arrange his funeral for him.","What a pity!","He still had to marry into money. When he got old, he would hire a dozen caregivers to look after him around the clock.","The atmosphere in Han Mo’s car was nowhere near as cheerful. He looked heavily at Qi Yuan. “How do you know Brother Bao?”","“What about you?”","Qi Yuan’s gaze remained firmly fixed on Han Mo. “How do you know Brother Bao?”","Brother Bao was a major cyberfraud king in the northern part of Myanmar. How could Han Mo know him?","What relationship did they have?","Han Mo’s eyes flickered, but he didn’t answer. Instead, he asked, “At the dinner table, you were testing Huanhuan. Why? What did Brother Bao do in Sawa?”","Qi Yuan’s gaze grew even more certain. “You really do know him.”","Han Mo’s expression turned icy. “Mr. Qi, I’m sure you’re also very worried about Huanhuan’s safety, aren’t you?”","Don’t test him. Tell him everything you know.","Their goals were the same: to keep Huanhuan from falling into danger and make sure she wasn’t harmed in the slightest.","Their gazes remained locked in a silent standoff through the rearview mirror until a soft ding came from a phone.","Qi Yuan glanced at the screen. It was a message from Qi Jin:","Bro! All the people we captured in Sawa escaped! I swear, is the Sawa police force made of shit or what?","The tension drained away in an instant.","They had personally handed those people over to the Sawa police, yet somehow they had escaped.","He wasn’t stupid enough to actually believe they had gotten away on their own. Just who was the all-powerful Brother Bao?","What did he want with He Huanhuan?","He didn’t know, and there was no way for him to find out.","He was just an ordinary doctor. In fact, once he got back, he still had an overnight shift to work.","He glanced at the man beside him.","Money could indeed accomplish many things.","In a low voice, he said, “Brother Bao had people stationed in Sawa. They planned to abduct Huanhuan and the others in the middle of the night...”"]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: Handsome, wanna grab a meal together","paragraphs":["“...My younger brother just sent me a message saying that Brother Hu and the others have run away.”","Han Mo's face instantly turned several shades worse. “Run away?”","Qi Yuan nodded. “I don't think you're stupid enough to believe that they ran away on their own.”","In a police station in the distance, Qi Jin was so angry that he was jumping up and down in his office. “I'm done! I'm really done! With their skills, how could they let the people run away? They can't even handle such a small thing properly...”","The car quickly stopped in front of the hospital. Qi Yuan opened the door and got out. “President Han, you'll protect her, right?”","Han Mo glanced at him. “Of course.”","“Okay.”","He turned around and walked into the hospital to start his long night shift.","Han Mo sat in the car, silently looking in the direction of the city.","Why did Chen Jiarong want to hurt Huanhuan?","Just for Gu Chacha?","It couldn't be. He didn't believe that Chen Jiarong was such a affectionate person.","Suddenly, a possibility flashed through his mind. He took out his phone and called Gu Jingchen. “Are you at the company now?”","Gu Jingchen replied, “Yes. What's up?”","Han Mo said, “I have something to talk to you about. Wait for me.”","“Okay.”","Half an hour later, in the top - floor office, Gu Jingchen frowned. “You shouldn't have taken such a big risk before.”","No matter how much he wanted to take revenge on his father, he shouldn't have gotten involved with such a dangerous person.","Han Mo explained, “I have nothing to do with him. I just introduced Han Xuan to him through an intermediary.”","From beginning to end, it was all about Han Xuan's own choice.","If Han Xuan hadn't been tempted, he wouldn't have gotten into trouble.","Gu Jingchen looked at him disapprovingly. “I know you've had a hard time, but forget it...”","Without experiencing the pain, one shouldn't judge right or wrong.","He wasn't Han Mo, so he naturally couldn't understand Han Mo's pain and hatred.","Brother Bao had already come to Jiangcheng, and the thing had already happened. There was no need to say more.","He looked up at Han Mo. “Are you sure what the doctor said is true?”","This was no small matter and couldn't tolerate the slightest mistake.","Han Mo nodded. “If it were false, he couldn't have known about Brother Bao.”","Qi Yuan had described it very specifically and in detail, and it couldn't have been made up casually.","Moreover, on the way here, he had asked someone to make some inquiries, and indeed, the police station had reported an application for cross - border law enforcement in the past few days.","Gu Jingchen frowned even more tightly. “Wait for me to make a call.”","After saying that, he stood up, walked to the window, and dialed a number.","A few minutes later, he walked back with a cold expression on his face. “The situation is a bit tricky. Brother Bao has a powerful protector in Jiangcheng. It won't be easy to arrest him.”","It wasn't difficult to catch the person, but there was someone behind him.","If they arrested the person in the front, the person might just swagger out later.","Neither his family nor the Han family had strong enough connections in this regard.","Unless...","A glint flashed in his eyes. “I've thought of someone who might be able to help.”","Han Mo quickly asked, “Who?”","Gu Jingchen curled his lips into a faint smile. “Liang Zheng.”","If Liang Zheng was willing to step in, Brother Bao wouldn't stand a chance once he was arrested.","Han Mo hesitated. “Do you want Liang Ye to ask his brother for help? Will it work?”","After all, this matter had nothing to do with the Liang family. Would Liang Zheng be willing to get involved for Liang Ye's sake?","The smile on Gu Jingchen's lips deepened. “He will.”","Not only would he, but he would also get actively involved.","At the Liang family, Liang Zheng was struggling with how to find an excuse to visit the Gu family.","The relationship between their family and the Gu family was just so - so, and it seemed a bit inappropriate to visit rashly.","Just as he was annoyed, his phone suddenly vibrated. He looked down and saw it was Gu Jingchen calling.","Why would he call him?","Before he could sort out his thoughts, his finger had already pressed the answer button. “Hello?”","On the other end of the phone, Gu Jingchen's voice was full of worry. “I'm really sorry to call you so late. It's just that my sister and Meili have run into some trouble recently. I don't have Liang Ye's phone number. Could you give it to me?”","Liang Zheng frowned instantly. “What kind of trouble have they run into?”","Gu Jingchen sighed. “It's nothing. Just ask Xiao Ye to go and accompany Huanhuan. I can handle things here for now.”","After saying that, he hung up the phone. Han Mo gave him a disdainful look. “You're so sly.”","Gu Jingchen smiled calmly. “It's better to have someone offer to help than to beg for it.”","As soon as he finished speaking, his phone started vibrating wildly, and the screen clearly showed the name Liang Zheng.","A glint of amusement flashed in Gu Jingchen's eyes. One, two, three, four, five.","He answered the call. Liang Zheng urgently asked, “Tell me clearly. What kind of trouble have they run into?”","Gu Jingchen sighed. “Do you know about Han Xuan's matter?”","Liang Zheng nodded. “Yes.”","“His superior from the north has come to Jiangcheng recently. That person has his eyes on Meili and Huanhuan. A few days ago, he sent people to Savar to kidnap them. If they hadn't been without passports, they might have been kidnapped to God knows where by now...”","He told Liang Zheng in detail what he knew. “...We're just worried that it'll be easy to arrest the person, but difficult to convict him.”","Liang Zheng readily agreed without hesitation. “Don't act rashly. Wait for me to sort out the relationships first.”","Gu Jingchen smiled and nodded. “Okay. I'll hang up then.”","Suddenly, Liang Zheng realized something. “Gu Jingchen, are you...”","Before he could question further, the voice on the other end of the phone suddenly became lower. Gu Jingchen seemed to be talking to someone else. “Tell Huanhuan later to keep an eye on Meili. Online dating is unreliable. Don't let her play around with that...”","“What did you say?”","“Beep, beep, beep...”","...","A message came in on his phone, still from Gu Jingchen. “Thank you for your trouble. After this is all over, I'll take Huanhuan and Meili out to have a meal with you. Let them thank you properly.”","Have a meal together?","Liang Zheng made one call after another. It was not until the moon was high in the sky and the battery of his phone showed a red light that he finally put down the phone.","He sat quietly on the sofa, his eyes wandering aimlessly around the living room.","Then he let out a soft laugh. Good old Gu Jingchen, dangling a carrot in front of him and making him work all night.","He took out a cigarette, lit it, took a puff, and then put it out. Then he stood up, went down to the basement, and drove out.","The SUV sped through the suburbs, heading towards the destination in his heart.","The car stopped at an intersection. In the distance was the gate of the Gu family. He sat in the car, quietly looking at that gate.","He was the eldest son in the family and Liang Ye's elder brother. The whole family's burden was on his shoulders.","He knew that the most suitable path for him was to be with a girl from a family of similar status, and live a life of mutual respect.","No, perhaps they would develop some feelings for each other.","Perhaps they would...","“Hey, handsome! Why are you sitting here looking so down? Tell me what's bothering you. Sister can lend you her shoulder to cry on.”","A familiar voice suddenly interrupted his train of thought. The bright red hair had been changed to a gorgeous peach - pink color, but the flirtatious smile remained the same.","Qi Meili was lying on the car window, looking at the man in front of her with admiration all over her face. “Such a chiseled face. So handsome! Handsome guy, do you have a girlfriend? If not, sister will treat you to a meal.”","A smile instantly filled Liang Zheng's eyes. He nodded with a smile. “Sure.”"]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: You're a restaurant decoy","paragraphs":["Qi Meili’s eyes lit up instantly. “Really?”","The smile in Liang Zheng’s eyes deepened. “Why would I turn down a free meal?”","“Huanhuan! Come on! Let’s take this handsome guy out for dinner!”","Qi Meili immediately turned around and called for He Huanhuan to get in the car, only to find Huanhuan staring at her stiffly. “Sis, are you all right?”","Isn’t this Liang Ye’s brother? Why did she suddenly rush over to him like that?","Qi Meili shamelessly examined Liang Zheng’s face. Handsome—handsome enough to bring the heavens crashing down. Handsome enough that she could have her ID and household register ready in one second and get married at once.","With a beaming smile, she said to He Huanhuan, “Oh, come on, Huanhuan, don’t be so stingy. It’s fine to spend a little money on a handsome man this good-looking.”","She had just suffered the trauma of a misleading online photo earlier that day. Right now, she desperately needed to hit on an extremely handsome man to soothe her wounded soul.","He Huanhuan was speechless. “Don’t you think he looks familiar? This is—”","Before she could finish, Qi Meili giggled. “You noticed too? All top-tier beauties look somewhat alike. They’re not like ugly people, who come in every imaginable variety of ugly.”","......","Was that what she meant?","“This is Liang—”","Once again, she was interrupted. Liang Zheng glanced at He Huanhuan and asked, “What are you two doing out here so late?”","His gaze was intimidating, and He Huanhuan answered instinctively, “I came home to pick up a few things.”","Liang Zheng smiled. “Then we won’t keep you. We’ll go eat first.”","He Huanhuan: ......","Bro, are you being a little too obvious?","Those words had clearly landed right in Qi Meili’s sweet spot. She quickly climbed into the back seat and waved at Huanhuan. “Huanhuan, you go on home. I’ll come find you after I eat~”","“But...”","Her words once again went unfinished. The car started up and quickly disappeared before her eyes.","......","Face blindness, an outgoing personality, and lecherous tendencies all rolled into one. She really was something else!","She turned around angrily and started walking home, but the sound of a car came from behind her again.","“Why is there another... Han Mo! What are you doing here?”","Her voice rose involuntarily. She hurried into the car and urged Han Mo, “Quick, quick, quick... We have to follow Meili! She went to dinner with Liang Ye’s brother!”","But the car didn’t move. Han Mo smiled at her. “It’s only dinner. There’s no need to follow them, is there?”","“Oh, you don’t understand!” He Huanhuan was beside herself with anxiety. “Meili didn’t recognize him. She thinks he’s just some random handsome stranger!”","Han Mo nodded. “Isn’t that even better? If she were going out to eat with someone she didn’t know, then we’d really have to worry, wouldn’t we?”","“Huh?”","He Huanhuan suddenly came to her senses. “Oh... I guess so?”","Then what was she so worried about?","Looking at her dazed expression, the amusement in Han Mo’s eyes became impossible to suppress. “Are you going back to the hotel, or are you planning to move straight back home?”","He Huanhuan shook her head. “I think Second Brother’s hotel is pretty comfortable. I don’t want to go back for now.”","She felt more at ease staying at the hotel than at home. Gu Chengye and his wife truly weren’t bad to her. Every night, Jiang Yulan would come ask what she wanted to eat the next day, what she liked, and what she didn’t like...","Yes, she asked every single day.","She had been back for quite a while, yet Jiang Yulan still hadn’t remembered what she liked or disliked.","Gu Chengye was the same. He treated her with excessive concern, but none of it felt sincere.","It was like an employee placating their boss—going through the motions every day just to check a task off the list.","But she wasn’t their boss. She only found it annoying.","Han Mo didn’t ask any further questions. He simply nodded. “If you don’t want to go back, then stay at the hotel. Stay as long as you like.”","Brother Bao’s plan in Sawa had failed, so he would undoubtedly make another move soon.","The safest option was definitely for her to return to the Gu family home. The Gu family had security guards patrolling every day, and ordinary people couldn’t get in.","But she didn’t want to go back, so she wouldn’t.","Hiring a few extra bodyguards was all it would take. It was nothing.","He asked, “Want me to drive you around and help you clear your head?”","He Huanhuan shook her head. “I don’t want to sit in a car. Let’s get out and walk.”","It seemed like it had been a long time since she’d done any training. Her skills were almost getting rusty.","Han Mo nodded. “All right.”","Under the streetlights, their two shadows stretched longer and longer, then gradually shrank again.","He Huanhuan chatted with him intermittently as they walked, jumping from one topic to another and talking about whatever came to mind.","“What do you think Meili and Liang Ye’s brother are doing right now?”","“Eating, probably.”","“Do you think she’s realized who he is?”","“Probably not.”","“......”","And sure enough, Qi Meili hadn’t recognized him at all. She was too busy admiring his looks.","The car turned into a somewhat narrow alley and stopped in front of a restaurant.","Qi Meili looked up at the tiny storefront. A blissful smile immediately spread across her face. “Not only is he ridiculously handsome, he’s considerate enough to take me somewhere like this~”","He was even trying to save her money. What a perfect husband!","They had to get married. Immediately!","Liang Zheng smiled, pushed open the door, and got out. “Let’s go.”","The shop was small, but the service was excellent. As soon as they got out of the car, a handsome waiter over six feet tall approached them.","“Welcome, esteemed guests.”","Qi Meili couldn’t help staring. “Oh my...”","A displeased gaze instantly swept over from beside her. Qi Meili smiled sweetly and patted Liang Zheng on the arm. “Don’t be jealous. He’s not as handsome as you.”","Though that was what she said, her eyes followed the waiter involuntarily as he walked away.","That youthful, handsome energy was simply too alluring.","Liang Zheng’s face darkened instantly. He shot the waiter a glance, and the waiter immediately understood. He nodded and said, “Please wait a moment. I’ll have the manager come and assist you.”","He then quickly turned around and left, replaced by a beautiful woman who was both gentle and efficient.","The manager inclined her head slightly. “Your private room is this way. I’ll show you to it.”","She addressed them as “esteemed guests” at every turn, treating them with the utmost respect.","Qi Meili gave her a thumbs-up. “Your service is really good. No wonder this place can stay open despite being so tiny.”","The manager paused slightly.","Being this small? And still managing to stay open?","Their restaurant was a private kitchen that only accepted reservations. Its appeal lay in being tucked away amid the bustle of the city, while remaining refined and elegant. Naturally, they had no reason to make the place enormous.","She smiled politely at Qi Meili. “Thank you for your kind words. We’ll be sure to maintain our standards and continue working hard to provide our guests with even better service.”","After opening the door, the manager led them into the private room and quickly handed them two brand-new menus.","“We just received some wild Yunnan matsutake mushrooms this afternoon, as well as several five-year-old tender abalone. They’re all listed on the menu. Please take a look.”","After introducing the dishes, she quietly stepped aside and waited for Qi Meili and Liang Zheng to order.","Qi Meili opened the menu and glanced at it.","Her vision instantly went black, and she nearly fainted on the spot!","Holy crap! This place was a scam!","One abalone cost forty-eight thousand yuan!","Without hesitation, she glared at Liang Zheng. “So you’re a restaurant tout!”","No wonder he was so handsome and had agreed to take her out after just one invitation.","No wonder he’d looked familiar. He must have been exposed online before!","She stood up and was about to leave, but Liang Zheng looked up with a smile. “Relax. I’m paying.”","Qi Meili clutched her lower back and shook her head. “I’m afraid you’re eyeing my kidneys.”","Even if they cut out both her kidneys, she still couldn’t afford an abalone that cost forty-eight thousand yuan."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: This Is a Reward","paragraphs":["Liang Zheng walked over to her and sat down with her. “It’s only a meal. Why would I want your kidney?”","Qi Meili gave him a suspicious once-over. He still seemed like a plant hired to lure customers in.","She turned to the manager. “He’s paying for this meal today. You heard that, right?”","The manager nodded. “I heard you, ma’am.”","Qi Meili held up her phone to record her. “So you’re not going to make me pay later, are you?”","The manager continued nodding. “Don’t worry. Absolutely not.”","Mr. Liang still had over a million yuan in unused credit at their restaurant. There was no way they would ask Qi Meili to pay.","However, before coming over, Liang Zheng had contacted the manager online and instructed her not to mention his name.","Although the manager couldn’t figure out what kind of game he was playing, the customer had made a request, and they had to accommodate it.","After all, this was what they were paid for.","So when Qi Meili pointed her phone at her, the manager merely turned slightly and offered the camera her attractive left profile.","“Rest assured, ma’am. We are absolutely not the kind of shady restaurant that hires dining companions to trick customers into spending money. This meal was reserved by the gentleman. We will only charge him, and we won’t make things difficult for you.”","Hearing that, Qi Meili finally relaxed.","In the past, she wouldn’t have hesitated to order whatever she wanted. At worst, she could have stayed behind to wash dishes.","But she couldn’t do that now. She really had forty-eight thousand yuan in her phone.","Curious, she asked the manager, “What does ‘one-head abalone’ mean? Does this abalone only have one head? Are there abalones with eight heads? What would those be called—eight-head abalone?”","A single one-head abalone already cost forty-eight thousand yuan. How much would an eight-head abalone cost?","Four hundred thousand?","Good heavens!","The manager smiled and explained, “The term ‘one-head’ usually refers to how many dried abalones there are in one jin. A one-head abalone means that a single dried abalone weighs an entire jin, which makes it especially rare and precious.”","Qi Meili nodded earnestly. “I see. I’ve learned something new.”","Liang Zheng looked at the manager. “How many one-head abalones do you have today?”","“Four,” the manager replied quietly.","Liang Zheng closed the menu. “We’ll take all of them. As for the rest, serve whatever you think is appropriate. You know my preferences.”","“Of course.”","The manager took the menu and was about to leave when Qi Meili grew so anxious that her voice turned hoarse.","“Why did you order so much?”","Four of them would cost nearly two hundred thousand yuan!","Liang Zheng replied, “I’ll have one packed up for your friend to take home. Isn’t that a good idea?”","Qi Meili was instantly rendered speechless.","Well, yes... Of course it was a good idea...","“Um... Ordering two would be enough. One for the two of us to share. They’re so expensive...”","Even if she wasn’t the one paying, she couldn’t bring herself to take advantage of someone to this extent.","Liang Zheng smiled faintly. “My younger brother likes them too. I’ll have one packed up for him.”","Qi Meili had nothing left to say. She could only nod. “All right, then.”","The manager left, and soon the private room held only the two of them.","Her gaze drifted over Liang Zheng’s face of its own accord. No matter how many times she looked, she found every part of him pleasing.","“How did you end up with such a face?” she murmured. “Every inch of you is beautiful.”","His deep-set eyes met hers, carrying an almost hypnotic allure.","“Really?” he asked. “I’m that good-looking?”","Meili nodded vigorously. “Really. I couldn’t be more serious. Your eyes are beautiful, your nose is beautiful, and your mouth is even better. It looks so soft... I want to kiss it.”","“Then do you want to kiss me?”","“What?”","Qi Meili was stunned for a moment. “Things are moving that fast?”","She had never met such a handsome guy who was so forward!","Her eyes immediately lit up. “Sure!”","With a quick scoot, she sat down beside Liang Zheng and leaned her face toward him, squeezing her eyes shut. “Come on!”","Looking at her tightly scrunched-up face, Liang Zheng couldn’t help laughing.","That posture looked less like she was about to kiss someone and more like a child getting ready to be punished.","He asked, “You’ve never kissed anyone before?”","Qi Meili felt terribly guilty and scrunched up her face even more. “Who said that? I kiss people all the time! I’m an expert!”","Yet her eyelids trembled several times despite herself. The sight made the corners of Liang Zheng’s lips turn upward. “Then I might not be as experienced as you. Why don’t you kiss me?”","“Huh?”","Qi Meili opened her eyes in surprise. Liang Zheng was still sitting right where he was, without leaning toward her at all.","Was she supposed to make the first move?","She—she was only all talk!","Back when she used to hang around the alternative scene, she’d dated a few times, but not a single relationship had lasted longer than one bowl of spicy hot pot...","She and Huanhuan had been poor back then, and those edgy young guys were even poorer.","Three people would share one bowl of spicy hot pot, and the guy would eat the most while still refusing to pay the bill. No matter how handsome he was, that was impossible to put up with.","So although she’d drifted through a whole field of flowers, she had never actually kissed anyone...","After hesitating for a moment, she leaned a little closer. Her heart began pounding uncontrollably.","A chance this good didn’t come along often. Come on, Qi Meili, do yourself proud!","The closer she got, the more his sharply defined features filled her vision. She couldn’t help stopping mid-motion. “Huh? You look awfully familiar...”","“Do I?”","His deep-set eyes fixed intently on her. “Do you know what this kiss means?”","“What?”","“It means confirmation—and it’s the reward for keeping busy all night.”","“What do you mea—”","A large, well-defined hand covered the back of her neck, and soft lips followed, pressing against hers.","Her heart clenched. They had actually kissed!","Her mind instantly dissolved into a tangled mess, leaving her unable to think of anything.","Her eyes were wide open, fixed stupidly on the person right in front of her.","Then her senses suddenly returned. She sat bolt upright. “Liang Zheng! You tricked me into kissing you!”","A smile spread all the way into his eyes. “You finally recognize me?”","Qi Meili glared at him. “How could you do that? You lied to me!”","His sharply defined face moved close again, his magnified good looks making her head spin. “Did I ever say I wasn’t Liang Zheng?”","Qi Meili shook her head. “I don’t think so...”","She was the one who hadn’t recognized him...","“Was I the one who said I wanted to kiss you?”","Qi Meili continued shaking her head. “I was the one who said it...”","But she’d only been running her mouth. She had never expected them to actually kiss...","His lips pressed against hers once more, giving her a light peck. “That’s for the meal.”","Qi Meili tried to retreat. “But you said you’d pay!”","“Didn’t you say you were treating me to dinner?”","Qi Meili felt guilty. “I did say that, but...”","His soft lips pecked her again. “That’s payment for my hard work.”","She had owed several people favors in the course of one evening. The least he could do was collect a little compensation for all his trouble.","Gu Jingchen, that big-tailed wolf, actually thought he could fob me off with a single meal.","Hmph. As if.","Qi Meili had no idea what he was talking about. “What trouble fee? I never asked you to do anything!”","The large hand moved away from her neck, and Liang Zheng sat up straight. “You’ll find out.”","The next second, someone knocked on the door.","“Sir, your food is here.”","“Come in.”","The door was gently pushed open. The manager stood in the doorway, carrying an enormous porcelain platter.","“Sir, your whole abalone is ready.”"]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: Rest assured, you won't be held responsible.","paragraphs":["The manager carefully set the plate on the table. “We’ve prepared it in the most classic style—abalone slices in scallion oil. Please give it a try...”","Before she could finish, the manager tactfully noticed the hint of disappointment on Meili’s beautiful face and quickly asked, “Do you not like this preparation, ma’am? The other two haven’t been cooked yet. We can prepare them however you like.”","Qi Meili looked at her earnestly. “Didn’t you just say the special thing about these abalones is how big they are?”","The manager nodded. “Yes.”","Meili’s gaze grew even more sincere. “Then why did you slice it? Once it’s sliced, how are we supposed to tell how big it was?”","She’d been planning to take a picture and post it on her social media to show off.","The manager smiled considerately. “Would you like a picture of the dried abalone or of the finished dish? Would you like a video of the cooking process as well? The kitchen can take one for you.”","So thoughtful. Almost too thoughtful.","At 48,000 yuan, half the price was probably for the service.","Liang Zheng nodded at the manager. “Please prepare one of the remaining two whole and slice the other.”","“Of course.”","Only after the manager had left did he smile and explain to Meili, “A whole abalone is too large. Cooking it whole doesn’t bring out the best flavor.”","“Huh? Then tell the manager to slice both of them. It’s so expensive—don’t waste any.”","Meili was about to get up and call the manager back, but Liang Zheng tugged her down into her seat. “It’s fine. The other one is for Xiao Ye. His tongue is practically numb—he won’t be able to taste the difference.”","For Liang Ye? Then never mind.","Qi Meili sat back down. “He deserves to eat the inferior one. If it weren’t for him, would I have downloaded that stupid app? Would I have been catfished?”","A flicker passed through Liang Zheng’s eyes. “Xiao Ye told you to download the app?”","His little brother had taught her how to date online?","Meili nodded angrily. “He wanted to learn English but didn’t want to pay for lessons... The picture he used was really handsome! Blond, blue-eyed, and incredibly good-looking!”","To prove her point, she pulled up the fake photo and handed her phone to Liang Zheng. “Look. Isn’t he gorgeous?”","Liang Zheng glanced at the screen. The man in the photo was blond and blue-eyed, with deep, well-defined features. There was no denying that he was handsome.","He helplessly lifted his eyes to the woman beside him. This woman, whose heart was filled with handsome men from all over the world, seemed to have completely forgotten that they had just kissed.","He reached over and turned off her phone, then stared at her seriously. “What did we just do?”","Meili was perfectly composed. “We kissed. So what?”","Kissing might have been a little embarrassing while it was happening, but once it was over, it was over.","Now that she was talking about it, she wasn’t embarrassed in the slightest.","Her gaze even swept suggestively over Liang Zheng’s lips. “Your lips are soft. You’re pretty good to kiss. Hehe...”","...","His gaze tightened on her. “And what happens after people kiss?”","How were things between them supposed to progress?","The expression on his face was far too serious. Meili’s eyes immediately widened. “Wait, what? It was just a kiss, big guy. Are you expecting me to take responsibility for you?”","Before Liang Zheng could reply, she hurriedly picked up her chopsticks, stuffed a slice of abalone into her mouth, and chewed it several times with great determination. Then she clapped her hands and announced, “Anyway, I’m full. I should get going.”","He wanted her to take responsibility? No way!","She would never give up an entire forest for a single tree!","She rose to leave, but Liang Zheng didn’t stop her. He merely sat there and asked, “Is the abalone good? Aren’t you taking some for He Huanhuan?”","Oh, right. She still had to take one home for Huanhuan.","Meili stood there with a frown, caught between sitting down and leaving.","Then a soft laugh came from behind her. “Relax. I’m not asking you to take responsibility.”","She dropped right back into her seat. “Hey, it’s not that I don’t want to take responsibility. It’s just that, you know, right now I...”","“We’ll talk about it if I really ask you to.”","Meili instantly shut her mouth and obediently began eating the abalone.","She buried her head in her food and ate with great enthusiasm, completely unaware that in the eyes of the man beside her, his apparent retreat was merely a calculated step toward getting what he wanted.","After dinner, Liang Zheng drove her back to the Gu residence.","When they reached the intersection, she immediately spotted Han Mo’s car parked by the roadside and hurriedly said, “You can let me out here. I’ll go straight to Huanhuan!”","As soon as the car stopped, she pushed open the door and got out without a hint of reluctance.","“Meili.”","“Hmm?”","She turned around. Liang Zheng was sitting in the driver’s seat, looking at her. His eyes seemed to hold a great many emotions, and yet perhaps none at all.","Either way, she couldn’t make sense of them.","“What is it?” she asked.","Liang Zheng shook his head and smiled. “Next time you feel like kissing, come find me first. I’m always available.”","He would make sure no one else was.","Meili waved him off perfunctorily. “Got it, got it...”","Honestly, he was acting like he’d become addicted to kissing her. Tsk, tsk, tsk...","After finally sending him away, she carried the takeout box along the road for quite a while before running into the two people returning from their stroll.","Like a cannonball, she shot straight toward He Huanhuan and held out the takeout box. “Look what delicious food I brought you!”","Han Mo glanced at the box, the corners of his mouth lifting in a teasing smile. “Young Master Liang is pretty generous.”","A meal at Dream Garden was far from cheap.","Qi Meili shot him a look. “You know this place?”","Han Mo nodded. “I’ve eaten there a few times.”","The restaurant only accepted reservations, and the prices were truly exorbitant. He didn’t go often.","Meili gave him a sidelong glance. “Capitalist scum. You’re not allowed to eat any. It’s all for Huanhuan.”","She opened the box. Inside, the abalone slices had been arranged perfectly, just like they had been on the plate, stacked in neat, orderly layers. They looked incredibly satisfying.","She eagerly handed He Huanhuan a pair of chopsticks. “Try it! One piece costs 48,000 yuan. It’s insanely expensive!”","He Huanhuan was stunned. “Did Liang Ye’s brother get caught committing murder by you?”","What kind of crime would require spending that much money to buy Meili’s silence?","Meili giggled. “I traded a kiss for it. Hurry and eat. It’s delicious.”","“What?”","He Huanhuan jumped to her feet. “What did you trade?”","“A kiss.”","“How many times did you kiss? How did it happen? Why did you kiss? How did you two just suddenly start kissing? Why did you kiss him at all?”","Whenever a woman started seeing a man, the first person to lose her mind was always her best friend.","What kind of shameless man had taken advantage of her Meili?","She and Han Mo had known each other for so long, and they’d only ever held hands.","Who was Liang Zheng, anyway? What gave him the right to kiss her Meili?","“He kissed you and you didn’t refuse? Did he force you? Boo-hoo...”","Meili stuffed a piece of abalone into her mouth and, feeling guilty, fed her another one. “Oh, stop asking. Don’t worry—I only kissed him. I’m not going to take responsibility for him.”","“Really?”","He Huanhuan eyed her suspiciously. Somehow, those words didn’t sound very reliable.","“Truer than gold!”","Cradling the takeout box, Meili began ingratiating herself with her friend. “Don’t worry. My heart belongs to my girlfriends, not men.”","With 48,000-yuan abalone in her mouth and her best friend’s sweet assurances in her ears, He Huanhuan couldn’t help feeling pleased.","She picked up a slice and fed it to Meili. “No wonder this stuff is so expensive. It really is delicious.”","Meili nodded. “Exactly! One abalone costs 48,000 yuan, and they even sliced it for us. I didn’t even get a picture!”","He Huanhuan frowned. “What? Then you ate it for nothing?”","Something that expensive had to be photographed properly and posted on social media!","Han Mo explained from the side, “Slicing it before braising it with scallions gives it more flavor. If you braise it whole, the flavor can’t seep in, and the texture won’t be as good.”","Meili was astonished. “Liang Zheng said exactly the same thing! Oh my God! You rich people are so pretentious!”","Han Mo: ...","He hadn’t even gotten to eat it, let alone kiss anyone. How was he being pretentious too?"]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: A True Phoenix Does Not Cling to High Branches","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan was eating abalone while scrolling through her phone when she came across Meili’s Moments post. The sight of that enormous whole abalone was astonishing.","Curious, she asked, “Didn’t you say you didn’t take any pictures? Then how come you have a photo of a whole abalone on your Moments?”","Meili explained, “I had it packed up for Liang Ye. Liang Zheng told the kitchen to cook it whole.”","He Huanhuan was stunned. “Liang Ye actually lets himself eat abalone that expensive? Wouldn’t it break his heart?”","The moment Liang Ye came up, Qi Meili couldn’t help rolling her eyes. “Who knows? Maybe being stingy is just an act. What do you call that kind of person again? Histrionic personality, right? Maybe that’s what he has.”","Who knew how deliciously he was eating it right now!","“So good!”","Wearing disposable gloves, Liang Ye held the whole abalone in both hands and ate with utter bliss. “Bro, this abalone is amazing!”","He loved abalone more than anything, but the ones sold at supermarkets were always too small to be satisfying. As for the large ones, he couldn’t bear to buy them.","Luckily, his brother would occasionally pack up a big one for him so he could satisfy his craving.","Holding the abalone, he wore an expression of pure happiness. “Bro, you’re too good to me.”","Liang Zheng looked at him and smiled helplessly. “As long as you like it. Next time you want some, just tell me. I’ll buy it for you.”","Liang Ye hurriedly shook his head. “Once a year is plenty. You know what our family’s circumstances are like. How could we eat this all the time? You’re great in every other way, Bro, but you’re just too wasteful...”","If he knew his brother had ordered four of them in one night, he would probably jump straight out the window the moment it opened.","“Shut up and eat.”","“Oh.”","After licking every drop of sauce clean, he couldn’t help asking, “Bro, I think I was a little extreme just now. It’s fine to treat yourself once in a while when something tastes this good. You only live once, so you should be a little kinder to yourself.”","Liang Zheng glanced at him. “What are you trying to say?”","Liang Ye gave an embarrassed chuckle. “Where is this restaurant? I want to take Huanhuan there.”","Something this delicious—Huanhuan would definitely love it.","Liang Zheng asked, “Split the bill?”","“Of course!”","...","“This place only does delivery. There’s no dine-in option.”","He had never told Liang Ye how much the abalone cost. If Liang Ye found out that he had just eaten 48,000 yuan in only a few bites, he would probably turn around and go howl at their grandparents’ graves for three days straight:","“Grandpa! Grandma! My brother was spoiled rotten by our parents! He’s gone astray! He ate a 48,000-yuan abalone! How is that something people from our working-class family can afford...?”","Liang Ye sighed regretfully. “How can abalone this delicious not be served in a restaurant?”","He had even been planning to grit his teeth and take Huanhuan there someday.","Even if the bill came to 48,000 yuan, split between them, he wasn’t afraid of being murdered by He Huanhuan.","“Right, Bro, what’s the name of the delivery place? I’ll keep an eye out and see if they ever offer a discount...”","He took out his phone and asked his brother. Liang Zheng smiled.","“They don’t deliver to your area. Don’t bother looking into it.”","“Oh.”","He obediently took his brother’s word for it and casually scrolled through his Moments.","The very first post he saw was from Qi Meili:","“One abalone costs 48,000 yuan. Let’s just say it—how extravagant is that?”","His hand trembling, he tapped on the photo.","It was exactly the same!","Exactly the same as the one he had just eaten!","Forty-four-four... 48,000?!","“Grandpa! Grandma!”","His eyes rolled back, and he promptly keeled over.","“Xiao Ye!”","That painfully familiar wail made Liang Zheng snatch the phone from him. The moment he saw Qi Meili’s post, he immediately understood why Liang Ye had collapsed.","He quickly pressed Liang Ye’s philtrum. “Xiao Ye, wake up...”","Liang Ye lay there motionless, like a dead fish.","“Bro’s abalone didn’t cost him anything.”","“Heh!”","The breath that had lodged in Liang Ye’s throat instantly returned. He sat up, still dazed. “Really?”","Liang Zheng nodded without hesitation. “Han Mo paid for it. Bro didn’t spend a cent.”","Liang Ye shot upright. “Han Mo is way too wasteful! How could he casually treat someone to a 48,000-yuan abalone?”","His brother patted him on the back and helped calm him down. “It wasn’t my money, anyway. Stop twitching.”","“But my heart still hurts! Forty-eight thousand! If I’d known, I would’ve eaten it more slowly...”","Liang Ye continued lamenting until he suddenly realized something was wrong.","“What about the abalones you used to bring me, then?”","His brother said, “A friend invited me to dinner, and I had one packed up for you afterward.”","Liang Ye’s heart ached. “Bro, don’t pack any more for me in the future. They’ll look down on you...”","His brother nodded. “It’s fine. I’m not afraid.”","Meili had no idea that her Moments post had nearly sent Liang Ye to the grave. By then, she and He Huanhuan had already returned to the hotel, where Meili was leaning over the front desk and chatting with Gu Jinghan.","Gu Jinghan stared at her in disbelief. “What did you say? You kissed who?!”","Was it the Liang Zheng he knew?","The Liang Zheng from the Liang family?","“It was Liang Ye’s brother. What’s the big deal?”","Meili didn’t understand why he was so worked up. Wasn’t it just a kiss?","She asked Gu Jinghan, “You want to kiss someone too? But aren’t you trying to marry a rich woman? You need to guard your virtue. A man’s virtue is his best dowry, remember? That’s what you said.”","Gu Jinghan’s eyes nearly popped out of his head. “Do you know how rich the Liang family is?!”","If Liang Zheng were a woman, he would be Gu Jinghan’s dream rich wife.","Rich, powerful, handsome, and not promiscuous—he was practically perfect.","Gu Jinghan nudged Qi Meili with his elbow and sighed. “You’re about to transform from a sparrow into a phoenix!”","Liang Zheng was just as impressive as his elder brother. He was devoted to his work and had an exceptionally clean private life.","He had actually kissed Meili. Didn’t that mean... his buddy had fallen for her?","Meili shot him a glance. “What do you mean, transform from a sparrow into a phoenix? I’m already a phoenix.”","She tugged at her clothes, revealing the phoenix tattoo on her shoulder blade. “See that? Even phoenixes have to fly up to my shoulder.”","Don’t think she hadn’t seen those TV dramas. That sort of “lofty branch” wasn’t anything special.","All she wanted was to buy a large three-bedroom apartment with Huanhuan and remain best friends for the rest of their lives. Wouldn’t that be wonderful?","Wasn’t that much more reliable than some illusory “lofty branch”?","He Huanhuan reached out and touched her phoenix tattoo. Its color had faded considerably since the day Meili first got it inked.","She turned to Gu Jinghan and asked, “Do you know what this is called?”","Gu Jinghan looked completely baffled. “Isn’t it just a tattoo?”","He Huanhuan flashed him a brilliant smile. “It’s called: A true phoenix never clings to a lofty branch, idiot.”"]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: Looks Like Someone's Following","paragraphs":["In the stairwell, Sang Biao crouched by the door, staring miserably at the three people in the lobby. “How can she let people see her shoulders...?”","Smack.","He got a slap on the head. Xiao Qian’s voice was full of disdain. “If you’re not going to do the job properly, get back to the room.”","Sang Biao looked aggrieved. “How am I not doing the job properly? I can’t even say a couple of words?”","Xiao Qian shot him a glare. “From now on, she’s a target. Nothing else. Got it?”","“Got it.”","Sang Biao secretly pouted. It wasn’t like he was planning to do anything.","They had already taken the job. Even if he didn’t make this money, Xiao Qian and the others would. Either way, she was going to die.","Besides, she ignored him completely. What could he possibly do?","He was just being sour for the sake of it.","He looked up at Xiao Qian. “So how are we doing this?”","Those two had a car picking them up whenever they went out, and as soon as they came back, they stuck to Gu Jinghan like glue. There was practically no chance to catch either of them alone.","Xiao Qian’s expression turned grave. “We need to find a way to lure Gu Jinghan away.”","They needed to leave themselves enough time to escape. At the very least, the domestic police couldn’t get on their trail before they boarded the plane.","So they couldn’t kill them at the hotel. There were too many surveillance cameras there; they would be discovered too easily.","They had to do it outside, preferably somewhere with as little surveillance as possible. That would require careful planning.","He kicked Sang Biao. “Go bother Qi Meili for a bit.”","Sang Biao’s eyes immediately lit up. “Xiao Qian, how come you’ve got a new idea every minute? Are you shipping our international BE couple? The ultimate tragic, life-and-death romance...”","He immediately received a hard kick in the backside. “Get going!”","“Okay, okay!”","He flung open the door and charged outside. “Meili! How can you let people see your bare shoulders?”","He spread his arms, trying to hug Qi Meili, but she instantly ducked down to evade him. Then she stomped hard on the top of his foot!","“Ah!”","Sang Biao howled, clutching his foot. Qi Meili jumped up and slapped him across the head.","“Didn’t I tell you—”","Smack!","“Every time I see you, I’ll hit you!”","Smack!","“Get the hell away from me!”","“Meili!”","Sang Biao grabbed her in a bear hug and wailed dramatically, “Even if you hit me, I still love you! You’re the one I love most! Hit me, hit me, hit me...”","“Let her go!”","Gu Jianghan’s face darkened at once. He stepped forward and grabbed Sang Biao. “Why are you putting your hands all over a girl? Let go!”","Meanwhile, He Huanhuan simply reached over and shoved at his face. “Stay away from my Meili!”","But Sang Biao ignored them completely, only tightening his hold on the person in his arms.","The scene instantly descended into chaos. Taking advantage of the confusion, Xiao Qian pushed open the door and darted out. With a quick sidestep, he squeezed into the melee.","“Let go of the young lady!”","He shouted loudly, but his hand immediately reached for the side of Qi Meili’s waist. In a flash, he unzipped her waist pouch and slipped a tracker into its inner compartment.","His hands were incredibly fast. The entire thing took less than five seconds, and none of the three people caught up in the chaos noticed a thing.","After zipping the pouch back up, he immediately turned and hooked an arm around Sang Biao’s neck, dragging him away. “Sorry, sorry... I’ll make sure to keep an eye on him next time...”","He bowed and apologized repeatedly to Qi Meili, then gave Sang Biao another hard kick. “Apologize! Promise you’ll never bother her again!”","Sang Biao promptly dropped to his knees. “I was wrong. I’ll never harass you again...”","Meili was sick of seeing his face. “Get lost, get lost, get lost...”","“Sorry, sorry...”","Xiao Qian hurriedly dragged Sang Biao into the elevator. Once inside, Sang Biao’s miserable expression vanished instantly.","“Well? Did you pull it off?”","Xiao Qian looked surprised. “You knew what I was doing?”","A sly smile tugged at Sang Biao’s lips. “Come on, man. How many years have we known each other? You think I don’t know your little tricks?”","Planting a tracker wasn’t exactly hard to figure out. And Xiao Qian had tried to keep it from him—like he would ever sabotage the operation.","Sang Biao put away his frivolous expression and solemnly patted Xiao Qian on the shoulder. “I know what matters, bro. Once we get back to Sawa, drinks are on me.”","Xiao Qian nodded. “Let’s get back to the room. Little Zuo and Little You should be back soon.”","The moment they pushed open the door, the dark muzzle of a gun was pressed against their heads.","“Don’t move!”","Before the words had even faded, Xiao Qian snatched the gun away. The instant he seized the barrel, he shoved the other man onto the bed and swung the gun around, aiming it at the person lying there.","“That’s all you’ve got?”","The man on the bed lay sprawled out with a grin. “I was just messing around. Why so serious?”","Xiao Qian put the gun away, his face grim. “What we’re about to do isn’t a game. If anything goes wrong, we won’t make it back to Sawa. You want to stay in China and go to prison?”","Xiao You sat up, still grinning. “Brother Bao got us two guns. How could we possibly fail?”","In Sawa, they had failed because they were unlucky. They had run into a police officer who was highly skilled in a fight; they simply couldn’t beat him.","This time was different. They had seen both girls in person, as well as in photos. There wouldn’t be any problems.","There were four of them now, and they had two guns. How could they possibly fail to kill two young women?","If they couldn’t manage even that, what kind of gangsters were they? They might as well wash their hands of it all, go back home, and work in a factory.","“Holy crap, it’s a real gun!”","Sang Biao snatched the gun from Xiao Qian’s hand and stroked it fondly.","He remembered that gun control in China was extremely strict. Brother Bao had actually managed to get hold of these?","He was endlessly curious. “How did Brother Bao get them?”","Xiao Qian snatched the gun back. “None of our business. Just do your job.”","He carefully put the gun away. Neither weapon had a suppressor, so unless they had no other choice, it was best not to use them.","He opened his phone and synced Qi Meili’s location. It was almost exactly on top of their own location.","It was already late. The girls should have returned to their room to sleep.","He placed the phone on the table, and the four of them took turns watching the tracker.","In the middle of the night, Sang Biao was exhausted and couldn’t help asking, “Why don’t I just go downstairs, knock on their door, and shoot both of them right now?”","They could call a car after killing them and head straight to the airport for the earliest flight back to Sawa. Wouldn’t that work?","Xiao Qian glared at him. “You think we’re in Sawa?”","If they dared to go that crazy, heavily armed forces would be waiting for them before their car even reached the airport.","Xiao Qian had no intention of ending up behind bars.","For the next two days, the four of them did nothing but keep watch from the hotel.","But He Huanhuan and Qi Meili had plenty of ways to entertain themselves. During the day, they never went out, just stayed in their room eating, drinking, and playing around.","In the evening, Han Mo would drive over to take them out to dinner. Afterward, he would bring them back to the hotel.","The two of them would chat with Gu Jinghan at the hotel reception for a while before returning to their room to sleep.","There was never a single moment when either of them was alone.","Sang Biao stared at the motionless tracker, irritated out of his mind. “What’s with them? Don’t they get bored cooped up in their room all day?”","They were not bored. Not even a little. At that very moment, the two of them were enthusiastically doing flashy hand-dance moves in front of the enormous TV screen."]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: Did Brother Leopard send you here","paragraphs":["Xiao You glanced out the window. It was almost time for dinner again. “That damn rich second-generation brat is going to come pick the two of them up for dinner soon.”","Every day, the restaurants Han Mo took them to were expensive places that required reservations.","The four of them could only sit outside, each with a cup of instant noodles, waiting for them. Wasn’t this miserable?","Sang Biao’s brows drew tightly together. “If those two never go anywhere alone, are we supposed to waste our whole lives here?”","He had to get back to Sawa! If he didn’t get a few hits soon, he was going to go crazy!","Extremely irritable, he stood up and kicked the table hard. “Damn it! I’m going downstairs and shooting the two of them right now! I have to get back to Sawa!”","With that, he charged over to Xiao Qian and tried to snatch the gun away. Xiao Qian immediately restrained him. “Calm down!”","“Calm down, my ass!”","He was so agitated he could barely stand it. “I feel like I’m dying! I can’t calm down! Fuck!”","Xiao Qian looked just as awful. “You think you’re the only one suffering? We’re all suffering! Who isn’t forcing themselves to hold out?”","Sawa had very lax controls on weed. All you had to do was find a small clinic, and they could legally prescribe it for you.","All four of them were regulars at those little clinics, every last one of them.","They had been back in the country for several days, and had been cut off from weed for just as long. By now, they were all suffering terribly from withdrawal.","Xiao Qian glanced darkly at his phone. It was five-thirty. The rich second-generation brat would be arriving again in no more than half an hour.","He shoved Sang Biao aside. “I’m calling Brother Bao.”","They might not be able to handle someone that rich, but that didn’t mean Brother Bao couldn’t.","The call was answered almost immediately. Brother Bao’s voice sounded lazy. “What? You got it done that quickly?”","Xiao Qian replied cautiously, “Brother Bao, this isn’t easy. Those two stay holed up in the hotel every day and never go out...”","The voice on the other end instantly turned cold and hard. “If it were easy, why would I have hired you? Are you trying to quit on me?”","Xiao Qian hurriedly shook his head, though the other man couldn’t see it. “No, we’re not trying to quit. It’s that Han guy. He takes them out to dinner every night. Brother Bao, can you think of something...?”","“You mean Han Mo...”","At the mention of Han Mo, Brother Bao’s voice softened considerably. “I know. I’ll arrange it.”","After hanging up, he scrolled through his phone and made another call. Only after receiving a definite answer from the other end did he end the call with satisfaction.","He stood up and walked out of the room. Gu Chacha was sitting in the living room drinking tea. He went over and sat down beside her.","“Go to dinner by yourself tonight. I have something to take care of, so I won’t be eating with you.”","Gu Chacha nodded. “Okay.”","He lowered his head to look at her. “Aren’t you curious what it is?”","Her heart suddenly began to race. “You mean...?”","A smile curled at the corner of his mouth. “That’s right. It’ll happen tonight.”","Unable to hold back, Gu Chacha asked, “Will it work?”","The matter had been dragging on for too long, and there had been too many variables. She couldn’t help feeling nervous.","Chen Jiarong rubbed his fingers twice between her brows. “Don’t worry. Nothing will happen. Even if it doesn’t work, it won’t be traced back to us.”","Gu Chacha nodded distractedly. Although Chen Jiarong had said that, she still felt inexplicably uneasy.","Chen Jiarong put an arm around her shoulders. “Why don’t you go have dinner with your big brother? You can ask him how the Dongcheng project is going while you’re there.”","Gu Chacha’s eyes flickered involuntarily. She had already asked her big brother a couple of days ago. He had told her that the project was settled and that he would not be bringing Chen Jiarong in on it.","But she didn’t know how to tell Chen Jiarong. She was afraid he would think she was useless and take his anger out on her.","She blinked and softly replied, “Okay. I’ll ask Big Brother out.”","Back at the hotel, the sisters had worked up a sweat after filming twenty mindless little videos.","Qi Meili carefully selected from the twenty clips, which featured almost exactly the same movements. “Why do I feel like my hair wasn’t done right? Should we film one more?”","He Huanhuan waved both hands. “No, I can’t anymore. I’m starving. We’ll film some more after we come back tonight.”","She could stay up all night filming, but right now she absolutely had to go eat!","Meili glanced at the time. It was already after six. No wonder she was hungry.","She leaned over beside He Huanhuan and asked, “Are we eating with Han Mo tonight?”","He Huanhuan nodded. “He’s already on the way. He said that restaurant got two three-kilogram deep-sea yellow croakers this afternoon, and he reserved them. We can go straight there and eat them.”","The two of them flopped onto the bed and searched up why a three-kilogram deep-sea yellow croaker was so rare. Then they quickly changed and sat around waiting for Han Mo.","He Huanhuan rubbed her hands together eagerly. “Meili, I think my mouth’s been spoiled. I could actually taste the fragrance of that wagyu yesterday. Do you know how terrifying that is?”","Meili nodded gravely. “Exactly! How about we go eat hot-and-spicy rice noodles after the yellow croaker tonight, just to bring ourselves back down to earth?”","Let technology corrupt their palates thoroughly, but not let them get carried away!","He Huanhuan nodded. “Sure, sure...”","Her phone screen lit up. It was Han Mo. His car had arrived downstairs.","The two of them sprang to their feet. A three-kilogram deep-sea yellow croaker was waiting for them!","On the eighteenth floor, the four men watched the rapidly moving location marker and stood up at once.","They were going back to Sawa tomorrow!","The car moved smoothly along the road. Han Mo handed his phone to He Huanhuan. “I’ve pinned the restaurant owner’s WeChat chat. Just tell him we’ll be there in ten minutes and ask him to start cooking.”","He Huanhuan took the phone and sent the owner the message. The other side quickly replied with an “OK.”","A few seconds later, Chen Jiarong’s WeChat buzzed. He, too, received an “OK.”","He lowered his head to look at Gu Chacha. “It’s time. Let’s go.”","Gu Chacha said nothing. She simply followed obediently behind him as they left.","The two of them drove separately toward the city center. He went to the restaurant, while she went to the company.","By the time she arrived at the office, it was already past closing time. The company building was eerily quiet. Her high heels clicked crisply against the floor, each sound striking her heart and making her even more unsettled.","She went up to the top floor and, standing outside the office, took a deep breath before knocking.","“Come in.”","A familiar voice drifted out from inside, calm and devoid of emotion.","She pushed open the door and looked at Gu Jingchen. Her lips immediately drew into a wounded pout. “Big Brother, are you angry with me?”","Gu Jingchen smiled and patted the desk. “Come sit down.”","He was always so gentle and considerate with her, which only made Gu Chacha feel more aggrieved. “Big Brother, I’m sorry. I shouldn’t have argued with you last time...”","Gu Jingchen didn’t respond to her apology. Instead, he asked with a smile, “What made you think of asking Big Brother out to dinner today?”","Gu Chacha sat down demurely in front of the desk. “I missed you a little, so I wanted to come see you...”","“Is that so?”","A meaningful smile tugged at the corner of Gu Jingchen’s mouth. “It wasn’t Chen Jiarong who sent you here?”","“Oh, no.”","He tapped his knuckles against the desk and asked with a smile, “I should say, it wasn’t Brother Bao who sent you here?”","Gu Chacha’s face changed dramatically. “Big Brother, what are you talking about?!”"]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: You Have a Choice","paragraphs":["Gu Jingchen looked at her with a dark, heavy gaze. “Chacha, what are you panicking about?”","“I—I’m not...”","Gu Chacha’s eyes trembled several times before she finally managed to steady herself.","She tried to pretend she didn’t understand. “Big Brother, what were you talking about just now? Why can’t I understand?”","Gu Jingchen tapped the desk again. “You know Han Xuan has confessed everything?”","Her heart jolted, and Gu Chacha nearly lost control of her expression. “Really? He finally agreed to talk? That’s good. If he confesses properly, perhaps his sentence will be shorter...”","She repeated to herself over and over that Chen Jiarong had spent a great deal of money bribing the right people. There was no way Big Brother could know what Han Xuan had confessed.","He truly hadn’t known before.","But with Liang Zheng stepping in, everything had become much simpler.","It had taken Liang Zheng only two phone calls for Han Xuan to be brought in for another interrogation. His statement had then been submitted through a special-review procedure and delivered to people whom Chen Jiarong’s money could never reach.","So Chen Jiarong didn’t know.","And Gu Chacha knew even less.","Her mind had dissolved into chaos. All the words she had prepared vanished without a trace, leaving her able to say only, “Big Brother, why are you bringing up Han Xuan all of a sudden? Whatever happened between us is already over...”","Gu Jingchen’s scrutinizing gaze fixed on her. “Chacha, you knew he was laundering money for an overseas telecommunications-fraud operation, didn’t you?”","Gu Chacha was so guilty that she couldn’t answer his question at all. “Big Brother, can we not talk about him?”","But Gu Jingchen had no intention of indulging her. “Do you know who his contact is? Chacha?”","Gu Chacha instinctively shook her head. “How would I know? He didn’t tell me everything...”","“Chacha, are you sure he didn’t tell me anything?”","Gu Jingchen’s voice was filled with helplessness. “You still have a choice.”","Once Chen Jiarong was arrested, she would have no choice at all.","Her actions were enough to make her an accomplice to money laundering.","Gu Chacha’s eyes reddened despite herself. “Big Brother, do you really think I have a choice?”","She had already helped Chen Jiarong launder a great deal of money. She and Chen Jiarong were now tied to the same sinking ship.","What else could she do?","Betray Chen Jiarong and become a tainted witness for the prosecution?","She glanced at Gu Jingchen. Would Big Brother find a way to get her out of it?","But what then?","With this case hanging over her, how could she continue pursuing her dreams?","All the effort and sacrifices she had made before would become meaningless.","No. That wouldn’t do.","Just thinking about that possibility made her feel chilled to the bone.","It was too terrifying.","She had no choice. She truly had no choice.","She had already boarded the ship, and now she could only follow that path to the very end.","She had to trust Chen Jiarong—trust his abilities, his methods, and his money.","She could feel Gu Jingchen’s gaze fixed on her, waiting for her decision.","Little by little, her heart settled.","He didn’t actually know, did he?","He was only testing her.","Hoping she would stand up and report Chen Jiarong?","For whose sake? Han Mo and He Huanhuan’s?","Had the family already accepted the two of them so completely?","A faint hatred began to rise in her heart. Even Big Brother, who had always loved her most, had completely taken He Huanhuan’s side?","Her eyes instantly grew even redder as she stared at Gu Jingchen. “Big Brother, am I still your sister?”","A flicker of astonishment trembled in Gu Jingchen’s pupils. “Why would you ask that?”","She stubbornly pressed him. “Am I?”","Gu Jingchen nodded without hesitation. “Yes.”","Though they were no longer bound by blood, she was still the younger sister he had watched grow up with his own eyes. That was an unchangeable fact.","“What about He Huanhuan?”","“She is too.”","Gu Jingchen frowned slightly as he looked at Gu Chacha. “Chacha, you shouldn’t compare yourself with Huanhuan like this. There’s one thing you have to admit: she suffered for many years out there, and those hardships were never meant for her to endure.”","She was the Gu family’s true daughter. The wealth and comfort Chacha had enjoyed during the first twenty years of her life should have belonged to Huanhuan.","That was an indisputable fact.","He looked at Gu Chacha seriously. “I know this is hard for you to accept, but it couldn’t be avoided. Huanhuan has a good nature, so she doesn’t hold this mistake against anyone. But that doesn’t mean the suffering she endured never happened.”","“Chacha, you should help us make it up to Huanhuan, not take her side as an enemy.”","These words had been weighing on his heart for a long time. He had always wanted to say them to Gu Chacha, but he had never found the right opportunity.","Gu Chacha was sensitive by nature. If he brought it up too abruptly, she would only think he was lecturing her and become upset.","But if he didn’t say it today, there might truly never be another chance.","It had been his negligence. He had been so busy with work that he had failed to realize Gu Chacha had caused such a serious disaster.","A disaster too great for him to cover up.","But Gu Chacha couldn’t understand his feelings at all.","Make it up to He Huanhuan?","Was Big Brother insane?","Why should she make anything up to He Huanhuan?","She was a victim of this whole affair too!","She had been the youngest daughter of the Gu family for twenty years, only to suddenly become the fake one. Wasn’t she suffering as well?","She was suffering terribly!","Her hands clenched tightly beneath the desk. “Big Brother, I suddenly don’t feel hungry anymore. Let’s have dinner another time.”","She stood up and was about to leave, countless emotions churning violently in her heart.","Anger. Resentment. And the ruthless determination of someone staking everything on one final gamble.","Make it up to her?","Then He Huanhuan would have to be alive to receive that compensation!","Tonight would be her death sentence.","She could go below and collect her compensation there!","“Chacha.”","Gu Jingchen’s voice came from behind her, carrying what sounded like restrained helplessness.","She turned around. “Big Brother, what is it?”","Gu Jingchen looked at her steadily for a moment, then sat back down. “I want you to understand that people have to pay for the choices they make.”","Once she walked out that door today, if what came next happened, he would no longer help her clean up the mess.","Doing so would mean hurting Huanhuan. He couldn’t take advantage of Huanhuan’s straightforward nature and hurt her without limit.","She was his sister—his true sister.","Gu Chacha, however, failed to understand what he meant. Without the slightest hesitation, she turned around. “I know. I’ll pay for my own choices.”","The same went for He Huanhuan. She had hurt her, so she would have to pay for the harm she had caused as well.","Gu Chacha decisively pushed open the door and left, shutting away the last person who might have protected her.","Gu Jingchen sat quietly behind his desk, motionless for a long while.","It wasn’t until the phone on the desk began vibrating incessantly that his gaze darkened. He immediately answered.","A soft chuckle came from the other end. “What, were you sitting there waiting for my call?”","Gu Jingchen gave a helpless laugh. “Do you think I’m in the mood to do anything else?”","Liang Zheng glanced at the computer screen. He Huanhuan and Qi Meili were strolling hand in hand through a shopping mall, wandering into one store after another and leaving each one without buying anything.","The camera was positioned about five meters away from them. The footage was somewhat unsteady because the person filming was walking.","Liang Zheng clicked the mouse, and the image quickly zoomed in.","Qi Meili’s voice came through indistinctly. “Labubu can even do collaborations with Hello Kitty? They’re pretty cute. Oh my gosh! More than seven hundred? That’s robbery!”","In the display case beside them, a cold-faced, powerfully built man nearly six and a quarter feet tall stood in front of an entire row of Labubu dolls.","A voice sounded in his earpiece.","“Buy one for her.”"]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: Whose Tire Blew Up","paragraphs":["The tough guy hesitated for a moment. “I shouldn’t be distracted by anything else while protecting the target.”","Liang Zheng chuckled. “Flying Eagle, have you lost confidence in yourself since retiring?”","A bodyguard team made up of former special forces soldiers couldn’t spare one person to buy a Labubu?","It was an utterly blatant provocation, but it instantly struck a nerve with Flying Eagle. He switched channels and said to the people outside the shop, “Stay with them. I’ll buy something and be right back.”","“Yes, sir.”","Watching the man leave the shop, he quickly returned to the spot where the two of them had just been standing and reached out to take the Labubu from the shelf.","The moment his hand extended, an arm suddenly shot out from beside him, snatched up the Labubu, and walked away. It happened so quickly that he almost failed to react.","When he looked again, the only Hello Kitty Labubu on the shelf was gone!","He immediately turned to look. The man was over six feet tall, dressed in a black hoodie and sweatpants, with an earpiece in one ear as well.","He couldn’t help asking Liang Zheng, “Did you hire someone else?”","Liang Zheng was confused. “What do you mean?”","He swept his camera toward the man who was preparing to pay at the counter. “He bought the toy.”","Liang Zheng’s expression immediately darkened. “He wasn’t hired by me. Where’s the toy?”","The man paused. “He bought it.”","......","The voice in his earpiece instantly turned low and grim. “You can’t even handle something this simple? What have you been doing since you retired? Drinking yourself silly at home every day?”","The man didn’t answer. He hurried to the counter and pointed at the Labubu. “Do you have any more of these? I want one too.”","The cashier gave him an apologetic smile. “I’m sorry, sir. That was the last one in the store’s inventory. This gentleman just bought it.”","The man turned to look at the man in the black hoodie. Without changing expression, the other man tucked the Labubu into his arms and turned to leave.","“Wait.”","He reached out and grabbed him. “Sell it to me. I’ll pay double.”","The man in the black hoodie rolled his eyes. “Do I look like I’m short of money?”","With that, he shook off the man’s hand and walked out of the shop. He didn’t hear the familiar voice of Liang Zheng coming through his earpiece:","“Well done. I’ll reimburse you three times the price.”","The cold expression on the man in the black hoodie instantly melted into a foolish grin. “Thank you, boss!”","Inside the store, the man exchanged an awkward glance with the embarrassed cashier.","The cashier gave him an uncomfortable smile. “There really aren’t any more...”","The man pulled several bills from his wallet. “Could you check whether any of your other stores have one? If they do, please ask them to hold it for me. Thank you.”","The cashier’s eyes lit up at the sight of the four red banknotes.","“Of course! I’ll check right away!”","A minute later, she hung up with a beaming smile. “The Tianyue store has one in stock. I’ve already had them reserve it for you. You can go pick it up later!”","Money was the most efficient weapon.","After solving the problem, the man hurried out of the shop to chase after them.","By then, He Huanhuan and Qi Meili had already left the mall and were on their way to get malatang.","They still couldn’t stop thinking about the Labubu. Qi Meili counted on her fingers. “I work two shifts a day and only make a little over five thousand yuan a month. I work twelve hours a day for barely a hundred yuan. My God! Do you think we could make our own Labubu?”","She had no intention of buying one. She only wanted to sell the things and become a wealthy woman who had nothing but money.","He Huanhuan couldn’t help fantasizing. “What should we call it? Bulala? No, that sounds like a knockoff...”","Before she could finish, her expression suddenly changed, and she turned to look behind her.","“What is it?” Qi Meili asked, turning around as well.","There was nothing there.","He Huanhuan scratched her chin. “I don’t know. I just got this creepy feeling, like someone’s following us.”","Qi Meili tightened her hold on He Huanhuan’s arm. “Who would bother following us? It’s probably because that black guy from earlier was so ugly that he made you sick.”","Earlier, right after they had finished eating the three-pound yellow croaker in the private room, the door had been pushed open rudely.","A man as black as charcoal had stood in the doorway and glanced at them. “Ladies, long time no see.”","Qi Meili had glared at him. “Hey, ugly guy, who are you?”","Chen Jiarong had frozen at the question. “You don’t remember me?”","Back when He Huanhuan and Han Mo had returned after disappearing, he had attended the welcome-home dinner as Gu Chacha’s companion.","Qi Meili had frowned and thought hard, but she couldn’t recall him at all. “Hey, black guy, did you sneak into the country?”","......","Chen Jiarong’s face had darkened as he glanced at the two women. Then he raised his eyes toward Han Mo. “President Han, do you have a moment to talk?”","Han Mo had asked the two women to browse around the mall first. Once he finished talking with Chen Jiarong, he would take them home.","Even now, the two men still hadn’t finished talking, so the women decided to grab a bowl of malatang before heading back.","The mall was in a somewhat remote area, and the route to the malatang shop took them along a quiet, deserted lane. After walking for less than two minutes, He Huanhuan felt the prickling sensation on her back grow stronger.","She spun around. “Come out!”","In the shadows, three groups of people immediately ducked out of sight.","Qi Meili frowned. “You feel like someone’s following us again?”","He Huanhuan nodded. “Yes. I’ve got goosebumps all over.”","Qi Meili instantly flew into a rage. She grabbed He Huanhuan and started walking back. “Come on! Whoever’s following us, show yourself! Your sister here would love to have a little chat!”","There was no response from the empty lane. The two women looked at each other uneasily.","Could it be...","Good heavens! They had already experienced the extraordinary event of transmigrating into a book, so they were more than a little superstitious.","Without another word, they turned and ran!","They were living perfectly good lives here now. They did not want to go back to working two shifts a day!","Behind them, Xiao Qian and the other three men remained perfectly still by the roadside.","Sang Biao whispered, “Why didn’t we go out just now?”","Xiao Qian kept a stern face and pointed outside. “There are surveillance cameras over there.”","There were simply too many surveillance cameras in China. They made everything so inconvenient.","He pulled out his phone and looked at the map for the nearest malatang shop. They were still some distance away. He carefully studied every intersection.","“Here.”","He tapped a section of the route. “We should be able to avoid the cameras here. We’ll take a detour and run over.”","“Sounds good.”","The four men quickly backed away, then sprinted off.","They failed to notice the two silent tails following behind them.","Meanwhile, the two women followed the navigation and arrived at the malatang shop. Each ordered a huge bowl loaded with sesame sauce, extra numbing spice, and extra chili. They sat outside the shop and ate with great enthusiasm.","Qi Meili looked up at He Huanhuan. “Does your back still feel creepy?”","He Huanhuan shook her head vigorously. “It’s so strange. The creepy feeling disappeared as soon as I started eating malatang!”","Qi Meili reached out and tapped her on the forehead. “You were just hungry, weren’t you?”","The two women leaned together and giggled.","Then, from somewhere in the distance, came a sudden bang!","Another followed.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","He Huanhuan jumped. “Who blew a tire? That was loud!”","Qi Meili looked around. “All four tires blew out? Whoever it was must be having a terrible day!”","Down the path to the left, Sang Biao, Xiao Zuo, and Xiao You were pinned firmly to the ground, unable to put up even the slightest struggle.","With a gun in each hand, Xiao Qian fired wildly at the two groups before turning and darting into an alley by the roadside, fleeing at full speed!"]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: Should We Kiss Tonight","paragraphs":["Several dark figures quickly chased into the alley, but Flying Eagle barked, “Don’t follow! He has a gun. Don’t corner him! Come back and protect the targets—that’s what matters!”","This was an old neighborhood, with homes packed tightly along the alleys. Since he was carrying a gun, chasing him too aggressively might drive him to do something extreme.","Xiao Qian was fast, too. In just a few moves, he vanished into the narrow alleyways.","The two teams pinned Little Zuo and Little You and Sang Biao firmly to the ground, then each reported the situation through their earpieces.","The six-foot-three man in black carefully relayed the situation to Liang Zheng. “There were four in total. One got away. He has a gun, and there are a lot of residents around here. We didn’t dare continue the pursuit in case he did something reckless.”","The moment he finished speaking, the man in the black hoodie beside him said, “A bunch of idiots suddenly came charging out and let one of them escape.”","???","He turned to the man in the black hoodie. “We let one escape?”","The man in the black hoodie glanced at Little Zuo and Little You, who had been pinned down by his own men. “There were four people in total. We caught two, and you caught one. If the last one wasn’t the person you let get away, then who let him go—me?”","The man in black’s expression turned extremely grim. “He had a gun.”","“Then he was still the one you let escape.”","......","The man in black’s subordinates immediately flared up. “Say that again!”","The two teams instantly became tense, as if a fight could break out at any moment. Han Mo’s helpless voice came through the man in the black hoodie’s earpiece: “I’m not docking your pay. Stop provoking them.”","The man in the black hoodie grinned. “Then I guess he just ran away on his own.”","As long as money wasn’t involved, principles were a minor issue.","Each team loaded their captives into their respective vehicles, then cautiously waited at the malatang shop, afraid Xiao Qian might suddenly come charging out with a gun.","He Huanhuan poked at the bottom of her bowl with her chopsticks and couldn’t help frowning. “Do you feel like someone’s watching us?”","Today was seriously strange. Everywhere they went, she felt like someone was keeping an eye on them. What was going on?","Meili looked up at her. “You just finished eating and you’re already getting paranoid? Did the medicine wear off that fast?”","He Huanhuan waved her off irritably. “I’m not craving anything. I really feel like someone’s watching us. You don’t?”","Meili tried to sense it, then suddenly realized something was off. “Oh my God, that handsome guy in the black suit is so stylish!”","Sitting behind them, the vigilant man in black immediately heard a voice in his earpiece: “Switch to someone uglier.”","Flying Eagle’s face went cold. “Are you kidding me? Who’s going to take responsibility if something happens during the switch?”","There was a two-second pause on the other end. “Cover your face.”","......","Since the person paying was the boss, Flying Eagle scowled and propped up a hand to cover his features.","Behind him, Meili’s eyes lit up even more. “Oh my God! No wonder he’s such a heartthrob. His hands are so long, and look at those prominent knuckles. They look so strong!”","......","The man in black fell silent. Liang Zheng fell silent too.","In a private dining room, Han Mo sat in a relaxed posture. Across from him, Chen Jiarong smiled and asked, “Have you made up your mind? I can provide financial backing for the East City project.”","Before coming, he had received a call and only then learned that Han Mo had actually secured the supporting-contractor rights for the entire East City project.","With the Gu family and Han Mo involved, there were barely two pieces of the East City pie left.","He had paid a great deal of money to the people above him, yet he still hadn’t made any progress on the project.","He glanced at Han Mo. He had assumed Han Mo was flattering He Huanhuan because he wanted Gu Jingchen to let him join in.","He hadn’t expected Han Mo to secure the contract without relying on Gu Jingchen.","Then why had he been fawning over that Rainbow Head?","He couldn’t figure it out, and Han Mo had no intention of explaining.","Listening to the voice in his earpiece, Han Mo raised his head and looked at Chen Jiarong. “You should be worrying about something else right now, Brother Bao.”","Chen Jiarong narrowed his eyes. “What do you mean?”","The corners of Han Mo’s lips lifted slightly. “Why did you come looking for me today? It wasn’t really about the project, was it?”","Chen Jiarong’s heart jolted.","Did he know what he was planning? Had Xiao Qian and the others failed?","No. Impossible.","He had gotten Xiao Qian two guns. They couldn’t possibly have failed.","But Han Mo’s smile was far too certain, making him begin to suspect the worst.","His expression darkened. “Since you’re unwilling to cooperate, we’ll talk another time.”","With that, he stood up, opened the door, and left. As soon as he reached the parking garage, he called Xiao Qian. The phone rang for a long time with no answer.","His heart sank inch by inch. Then he slammed the phone onto the ground. “Useless pieces of trash!”","Four people, two guns, and they couldn’t even kill two young women!","The phone screen instantly cracked into a spiderweb pattern. The shattered screen flickered, then began vibrating wildly. The name Xiao Qian appeared across the web of cracks.","He hurriedly crouched down and picked it up. “Hello!”","“Brother Bao, we were ambushed. There were a lot of people—at least a dozen. The other three were captured, but I got away. Brother Bao, send me back to Sawa. I can’t take this job anymore.”","Xiao Qian’s voice was extremely urgent, and he sounded as though he were running at full speed.","Brother Bao asked anxiously, “What about the guns I gave you?”","“I have them. I brought them out with me.”","“Good.”","He nodded in satisfaction. “I’ll send you a location. Come straight to me, and I’ll arrange for someone to get you out of the country.”","After hanging up, he immediately sent Xiao Qian a set of coordinates.","Then he opened another chat and sent the same coordinates to the person on the other end: “I’m giving you an easy win. Remember to get rid of those two guns.”","The other party quickly replied with an “OK.”","He sat in the car and carefully sorted through his thoughts. Things had been going badly lately. Should he return to the compound and lie low for a while?","But he had already poured an enormous amount of money into the country. He was truly unwilling to leave just like that.","In recent years, the crackdown on telecom fraud had grown increasingly severe, and several of his compounds had been raided.","If he didn’t find a way out soon, he would eventually be finished.","After thinking it over again and again, he finally decided to take a gamble.","There was no one in their line of work who didn’t risk their life.","As long as he kept Xiao Qian and the others quiet, everything would be fine.","And money? He could afford to pay.","What he didn’t know was that the city police bureau had already established a special task force and was waiting to interrogate Sang Biao and the other two.","As for his connection within the authorities, he hadn’t received any news at all.","At the malatang shop, Han Mo’s car pulled up by the roadside. Carrying a Labubu box, he sat down on a plastic stool.","He Huanhuan stared at the box in astonishment. “Labubu! Han Mo, how did you know we went shopping for these today?”","Han Mo gave a sly smile. “I bought out that store. The staff told me you liked them, so I brought one to you.”","He Huanhuan was stunned. “Seriously? You’re that powerful?!”","The amusement in Han Mo’s eyes deepened. “This was the last one in the store. I snatched it up.”","From Liang Zheng, actually. He absolutely had to show off about it.","Meili couldn’t help giving him a thumbs-up. “Han Laodeng, I’ll give you this much: when it comes to generosity, you’ve got what it takes.”","After finishing their malatang, the three of them stood up and prepared to leave.","As they got into the car, the handsome man in the black suit sitting behind them suddenly bumped into Meili by accident.","“Sorry.”","The handsome man apologized in a low voice.","Meili pursed her lips and smiled. “It’s okay. Getting bumped into by a handsome guy was exactly what I prayed for~~”","......","The handsome man in black looked as though he’d been struck by lightning. He spun around and hurried away.","After getting into the car, Meili suddenly realized that her waist bag had become much bulkier.","She opened her waist bag in confusion. A Hello Kitty Labubu lay quietly inside. Then her phone chimed with a message from Liang Zheng:","Want to make out tonight?"]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: I'm Here","paragraphs":["Meili glanced at the Labubu in her belt bag, then at the message on her phone, and asked him, “You bought it?”","The reply came almost immediately:","Don’t you like it?","Well, it really was him.","He Huanhuan gave her a pat. “Meili, I’m talking to you!”","Meili instinctively zipped the bag shut, locking the Labubu inside.","But the bulging belt bag kept reminding her that it contained a Labubu worth several hundred yuan.","She had only admired it in the store that afternoon, completely unwilling to spend the money on it. And now it was lying in her bag.","How had he known she liked it?","Had he bought it for her simply because she liked it?","The importance he placed on her left her at a loss. Could it be that he really liked her?","She turned to Huanhuan. “Huanhuan...”","“Yeah? What is it?”","“Nothing. I just wanted to call you.”","Her heart felt strangely heavy. Maybe she was simply bewildered and helpless because the kind of attention she had longed for since childhood had suddenly been given to her.","After thinking it over, she opened her phone and tapped into her chat with Liang Zheng.","On the other end, Liang Zheng had been waiting for her reply for a long time. He sent another message:","Do you like it?","A bright red exclamation mark immediately appeared on the screen.","Great. She’d been deleted.","Meili stared at the contact list after deleting him and let out a long breath of relief.","That had been close. She’d almost fallen for him!","Unlike Huanhuan, she had grandparents who doted on her.","After her parents divorced, they each quickly started new families and soon had children of their own.","From a very young age, Meili had lived between the two households. Both places were her home, yet neither truly felt like one.","That feeling became especially obvious during the holidays.","New Year’s was the worst. Her mother would take her husband and child back to their hometown and have no time to look after Meili, so she would send her to her father’s place.","Her father and his new wife had two children, and their small two-bedroom apartment could barely fit the family as it was, let alone her.","She had long grown used to living without anyone’s love. Liang Zheng’s affection was dangerous to her.","A rich man like him could like someone one day and, the moment he stopped liking them, vanish without a trace.","She absolutely couldn’t let herself be fooled by his sweet trap. Otherwise, when she ended up crying, she wouldn’t even have a place to do it.","After thinking for a moment, she said to Huanhuan, “Let’s not go back to the hotel today. How about we go to your house instead?”","She could have dinner with Gu Jingchen, bask in the charm of a gentle older man, and hug her beloved “forest.”","Huanhuan eyed her suspiciously. “You’re acting weird. What’s wrong?”","Meili blinked. “Don’t you think it’s been ages since we last saw your big brother? Don’t you miss him?”","He Huanhuan: ...","Her friend’s thirst had flared up again. That was perfectly normal.","The car drove back to the Gu residence, and Gu Jingchen had just arrived home as well.","Meili jumped out of the car and dashed straight toward him.","“Big Brother, can I borrow your pecs for a minute?”","Gu Jingchen took two steps back. “That doesn’t seem very appropriate.”","Meili blinked up at him. “Big Brother, did you know? I suddenly realized today that I’m a child nobody loves...”","Huanhuan nodded seriously from the side. “She’s not wrong. Let her lean on you.”","...","The moment she leaned against those solid pecs, Meili felt her energy return.","Yes. This was exactly the feeling she’d been looking for.","Falling in love or whatever—it had all been an illusion.","Once they returned to the third floor and were alone, Huanhuan stared at her with a stern expression. “What was that about today?”","Meili put on an innocent face. “Nothing! I only leaned on him for two seconds. That’s not excessive, is it?”","But Huanhuan had no intention of letting her off the hook.","“You’ve known Big Brother for years. Why did you suddenly want to lean on his chest now? Be honest. What happened in the car?”","She knew Qi Meili very well. Meili was all talk—a shameless flirt.","Her mouth could say all kinds of outrageous things, but she would never actually take advantage of someone.","And this was Gu Jingchen they were talking about, not the usually carefree Gu Jinghan. Gu Jingchen was gentle, serious, and proper.","That made the whole thing even more suspicious.","Huanhuan was certain Meili hadn’t been acting like this when they were eating malatang.","That meant something must have happened in the car to upset her.","Meili’s eyes darted left and right, but there was no escaping her interrogation.","That was what happened with a true best friend. You simply couldn’t get away with anything.","“All right, all right! I’ll tell you!”","She opened her belt bag and showed Huanhuan what was inside. “Look. It’s this. I noticed it as soon as I got in the car...”","Before she could explain the details, Huanhuan immediately guessed the answer.","“Liang Zheng gave it to you?”","Qi Meili’s eyes widened. “How did you know?”","Huanhuan rolled her eyes. “Who else would it be? Han Mo secretly slipping it to you?”","She and Liang Zheng had only kissed last night, for heaven’s sake!","Meili said guiltily, “Don’t bring up the kissing. I regret it so much...”","She shouldn’t have kissed him. A man’s lips really weren’t something you could kiss casually. Once you did, trouble was bound to follow!","Huanhuan sat down beside her. “Why are you upset that he gave you something?”","Meili hesitated. “Do you think he likes me?”","“Obviously!”","Huanhuan was speechless. “If he didn’t like you, why would you two have kissed?”","Meili grew even more flustered. “He made the first move... I didn’t feel right refusing...”","As for the fact that she had practically bounced over to sit beside him and offered up her lips herself, she chose to forget that part.","She ventured, “Do you think he might like me today and stop liking me tomorrow? What am I supposed to do then?”","Huanhuan smacked her lightly, exasperated. “You’re all talk! Is that really all you’ve got? If that happens, just hug Gu Jingchen and cry. I’ll make sure he doesn’t go anywhere!”","She grabbed Qi Meili’s phone. A friend request was waiting on the screen:","I’m almost at the hotel. Can we talk?","She held the screen out to Meili. “He followed you to the hotel.”","Meili looked nervous. “What should I do?”","Huanhuan stuffed the phone back into her hands. “Accept the request first!”","Meili obediently added him back. A message from him appeared almost instantly.","Sorry.","Meili: Why are you apologizing to me?","I’m sorry for upsetting you.","She immediately had no idea how to respond.","She was good at teasing handsome men, and tossing out a few witty remarks was easy enough. But she had never dealt with a situation like this before.","She looked at Huanhuan for help. “What should I say?”","Huanhuan glanced at the screen, then at her. “Say whatever you actually feel about him.”","Meili shook her head. “I don’t know what I feel.”","“Do you dislike him?”","Meili shook her head. “No.”","With a face like his, how could she possibly dislike him?","Huanhuan asked again, “Why did you kiss him last night?”","Meili thought about it. “His lips were soft. He looked easy to kiss.”","Huanhuan pressed on. “Do you want to kiss Second Brother when you look at him? What about Big Brother?”","Meili shook her head. “That wouldn’t be appropriate, would it?”","Maybe they weren’t close enough for that kind of thing?","Huanhuan laughed disdainfully. “You’re such an idiot! Tell him to come over.”","Meili hesitated. “But what if he’s only temporarily infatuated...”","“So what?”","Huanhuan put an arm around her. “You still have me! I’ll always be here for you, okay?”"]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: We Can Take It Slow","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan's words were like a magic needle that instantly soothed all the uneasiness in her heart.","Yes, no matter what happened, she had Huanhuan by her side.","With that thought in mind, she picked up her phone and sent a message to the other person: \"I'm at the Gu family's place. Come and find me here.\"","The reply came quickly: \"Wait for me.\"","Half an hour later, a SUV stopped outside the Gu family's gate.","Through the car window, seeing that chiseled side - profile, Qi Meili's heart fluttered as she got into the car.","She explained guiltily, \"Well, I didn't mean to delete you just now. It was just a slip of the hand, really.\"","Liang Zheng looked at her and nodded, \"Just don't let your hand slip next time.\"","...","\"I won't.\"","She had already figured it out. She wouldn't do such a stupid thing again.","\"Why aren't you even looking at me? Am I not good - looking anymore?\"","Liang Zheng's soft question rang in her ear, and her heart skipped a beat. She immediately looked over bravely.","Her eyes were instantly dazzled. Oh my goodness! He was truly perfect!","Her gaze swept from his cold and deep eyes, over his high - bridged nose, and then across his petal - like lips...","Damn it! Memories came flooding back into her mind like a tide.","\"Where are you looking?\"","Suddenly, his handsome face magnified several times in front of her eyes, and her heart started pounding wildly.","Thump, thump...","It was like the excited pounding of her heart when her dad was about to take the whole family out for a trip.","She tried hard to pull her senses back. \"Well... actually, I'm still young... I'm not planning to be in a relationship for now...\"","She was more than two years older than He Huanhuan and hadn't even turned twenty - one this year.","When she was a child, she heard too many of her mother's cries, complaining about getting married too young and being dragged down by a scumbag man.","That scumbag man was her dad.","She didn't have any strong feelings about her parents' separation. Instead of forcing a miserable marriage, it was better to part ways cleanly.","But her mother's tears had planted many seeds in her young heart, which had grown into numerous branches over time.","One shouldn't lose their head in love when they're young. Getting married too early would ruin one's life...","She thought Liang Zheng was very handsome, and it was a pleasure to look at him.","But when it came to taking the relationship further, she couldn't help but feel a bit panicked.","If they could just keep the relationship of kissing each other, that would be great...","Liang Zheng's gaze was firmly fixed on her. \"Then let's take it slow and get to know each other gradually. But there's one thing you have to promise me.\"","\"What?\"","\"Don't kiss anyone else.\"","You can look at handsome guys all you want, but no kissing.","Meili licked her lips. \"I don't just kiss anyone...\"","His handsome face magnified in front of her again. \"I know. You only kiss good - looking people.\"","Meili nodded. \"Yes...\"","\"What if you meet someone better - looking than me in the future?\"","Meili couldn't help but fantasize. \"How good - looking would that person have to be...\"","An even better - looking version of Liang Zheng? Oh my god! Her mind involuntarily started to conjure up the image.","\"Um...\"","Suddenly, his lips pressed against hers, disrupting her train of thought.","After a long kiss, Liang Zheng reached out and wiped her lips. \"Don't think so much. We have plenty of time to get to know each other.\"","Meili nodded with a blushing face. Her hands didn't know where to put themselves. Her fingertips accidentally brushed against her fanny pack, and she suddenly remembered. \"By the way, how did you know I like this Labubu?\"","Before going to the store during the day, she didn't even know that Labubu had a collaboration with Hello Kitty. How did he buy it for her right after she found out?","Did he and Han Mo install surveillance cameras in the store?","But Liang Zheng only asked her, \"Do you like it?\"","She nodded. \"Yes, I do.\"","Then she frowned and shook her head. \"But it's too expensive. A small doll costs hundreds of dollars. It's really too much.\"","Liang Zheng smiled and reached out to touch her pink hair. \"If you like it, it's not expensive.\"","He didn't explain how he knew she liked it. Some things were too dangerous for her to know.","Thinking about the armed kidnapper who had escaped from the scene, his eyes darkened instantly.","He had to catch the person as soon as possible and make sure that neither she nor He Huanhuan was in any danger.","In fact, the person in danger now was not He Huanhuan or Qi Meili, but the disheveled Xiao Qian.","He really thought that Brother Bao would send him back to Sava, so he went to the location Brother Bao had given him without any precautions.","It was an abandoned factory building, located in a remote and sparsely populated area.","As soon as he approached the factory, he felt something was off. His heart was pounding wildly.","He hesitated for a moment and didn't go straight in. Instead, he crouched down and carefully circled around it, but he didn't find any problems.","But his heart was beating faster and faster.","He thought for a while and called Brother Bao again. \"Beep, beep, beep... Sorry, the number you dialed is busy...\"","His face turned black immediately. Something was wrong!","Then he turned around without hesitation and started running. Immediately, there came a noisy sound from behind: \"The criminal is on the run!\"","\"Southeast direction! Chase quickly!\"","Then came the persistent shouts: \"Stop! Don't run!\"","\"Stop right now!\"","It was the police!","The voices were getting closer and closer. Panic welled up in his heart instantly. Then he took out his gun without hesitation and fired at the people behind him. \"Bang, bang, bang!!!\"","\"The criminal is armed! Be careful!\"","\"Put down your gun! Don't resist!\"","\"...\"","It was so dark that he couldn't see anything. He could only fire crazily at the back to stop the police from chasing him.","He ran in the wild and then jumped into the river beside the road without hesitation!","He grew up by the river and was an excellent swimmer. After holding his breath and sinking to the bottom of the river, he swam away quickly like a fish.","The darkness was his best cover. By the time the police caught up, there was no sign of him in the river.","An hour later, he was lying in a haystack by the river, gasping for breath.","He shouldn't have called Brother Bao. He should have taken a taxi to the airport right away. Maybe he could have caught the earliest flight then.","Brother Bao had informed the police. He definitely couldn't go back to Sava now.","Thinking of this, a glint of cruelty flashed in his eyes.","He couldn't be caught. He had to go back to Sava. He had to make Brother Bao send him away. He had to...","Suddenly, a delicate face flashed through his mind. Yes! He still had a way!","He immediately took out his phone and searched online for the time of Gu Chacha's concert.","The next concert would start at 6:30 p.m. and end at 9 p.m. tomorrow.","After confirming the time and location, he quickly took out the phone card, broke it, and then threw the phone into the river.","He must leave safely tomorrow night.","In the hotel suite, Gu Chacha had no idea that she had been targeted. With red eyes, she cried to Chen Jiarong, \"Eldest brother's heart has completely turned towards He Huanhuan. I'm sorry. I couldn't help you...\"","Tears streamed down her cheeks like strings, making her look so pitiful and endearing.","Chen Jiarong reached out and pulled her into his arms, wiping away her tears. \"Why are you crying? There are so many projects in this big Jiangcheng. Don't cry. When you cry, my heart breaks...\""]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: Are You Threatening Me with Her","paragraphs":["Gu Chacha nestled against Chen Jiarong, worry written across her face. “If tonight’s plan fails, will it affect us?”","Chen Jiarong smiled and pulled her closer. “What are you afraid of? Have you forgotten what I do for a living?”","As long as no one had been killed, it was all a minor matter.","No matter the dynasty, there had never been a clean officialdom. As long as he paid enough, the sky over Jiangcheng would always shelter him.","Besides, the Gu family had no real connections in official circles. Even if Gu Jingchen wanted to take him down, he would have to think carefully about how much money he was willing to spend.","Gu Chacha obediently nodded. “All right. Are we still going ahead with the concert?”","She was afraid that the money-laundering operation would be dragged into the light and investigated in detail. Wasn’t that how Han Xuan had ended up behind bars?","Han Mo definitely knew how they operated. What if he used this to come after them?","At the mention of Han Mo, Chen Jiarong let out a cold laugh. “You think this is how Han Xuan found out about me? Master Han isn’t exactly a good person.”","Although Han Mo had no conflict of interest with him, the two of them had once worshipped the same deity. Han Mo would never expose the matter—there was nothing in it for him.","He sounded utterly certain, and only then did Gu Chacha relax.","Chen Jiarong had arranged a great deal of publicity for her, and at last, her performances had begun attracting people who actually bought tickets. To her, it was a tremendous leap forward. She didn’t want the performances to stop.","How many of the people who came to hear her play truly understood piano or art? They were only there for the spectacle.","As long as she held on, she would eventually break through.","Once she had completely made it, everything would be different.","She repeated those words to herself over and over. She could do this. She had truly seized her opportunity. She had made it onto the stage and stood beneath the spotlight.","After the performance, people even came over to take pictures with her.","She straightened her back and smiled sweetly at the phone’s camera. “Thank you for your support.”","The girl taking the photo gazed at her with the admiration she had longed for so desperately. “Chacha, I’ve seen so many of your videos! I love you!”","She was gentle and beautiful, radiated the elegance of a rich heiress, came from a good family, and played the piano wonderfully. She had even won so many awards.","Every single one of those qualities was enough to make people envious, yet she possessed them all.","The envy in the girl’s eyes was impossible to suppress. What window had God possibly closed on her?","The girl’s undisguised envy put Gu Chacha in an excellent mood, and her smile grew even brighter. “Thank you for liking me. I’ll keep playing for as long as I can. I hope we’ll be able to take pictures together many more times.”","The girl nodded excitedly. “Yes, yes! I’ll definitely come to your performances often!”","Even after the photo was taken, the smile remained on Gu Chacha’s lips. The feeling was simply too wonderful. She was completely intoxicated by it.","When she pushed open the door to the dressing room, she was surprised to find someone hiding inside.","At first, she instinctively assumed it was a fan who had followed her in, and her happiness grew even stronger.","She smiled at the intruder. “You’re not allowed in the dressing room. Did you want a picture? I can—”","“Ah!”","After a short cry of alarm, the dressing-room door was quickly shut.","More than ten minutes later, Gu Chacha had changed into a light tracksuit. With her arm linked through that of a man dressed in black, their bodies pressed almost against each other, she left the room and headed down to the parking garage.","The car soon departed from the concert hall and drove toward the hotel where she and Chen Jiarong had been staying recently.","“D-Don’t do anything rash. Brother Bao will give you whatever you want...”","The hand gripping the steering wheel trembled uncontrollably. A sharp dagger was pressed firmly against Gu Chacha’s thigh beneath the wheel, and Xiao Qian’s voice was cold enough to freeze blood.","“Shut up. Drive. Don’t try anything.”","Gu Chacha shook her head frantically. “I won’t. I really won’t. Could you please take the knife away? I’m scared.”","She was genuinely terrified. She had only just obtained a little of what she wanted. She couldn’t lose it now. She absolutely couldn’t.","“Shut up!”","The car reached the hotel as quickly as possible. Xiao Qian ordered her, “Call him and ask if he’s home.”","Gu Chacha’s body instantly began to tremble. “He is. He’s always home at this hour.”","The knife pressed more firmly against her skin. “Call him!”","“I will, I will...”","With trembling hands, Gu Chacha pulled out her phone and called Chen Jiarong. He answered quickly, his voice languid. “The performance’s over? Do you want me to come pick you up?”","Gu Chacha tried her best to remain calm. “No, I’ll be home soon. Are you there?”","Chen Jiarong laughed. “Where else would I be if I weren’t home? What is it? Do you miss me?”","Gu Chacha forced a smile. “Yes. I want to see you as soon as possible.”","“Then hurry back. I’ll be waiting for you.”","“Okay.”","After hanging up, Gu Chacha cautiously looked at Xiao Qian. “He’s home.”","“Get out.”","The two of them remained arm in arm, pressed close together as they walked toward the elevator. When it stopped on the twentieth floor, Xiao Qian pushed Gu Chacha forward and marched her toward the suite.","Beep.","The moment the door opened, the dark barrel of a gun was pointed at them. A mocking smile curled Chen Jiarong’s lips.","“Xiao Qian, you shouldn’t have come.”","Xiao Qian immediately tightened his grip on Gu Chacha and pulled her in front of him. The dagger pressed hard against her neck. “Send me back to Sawa, and I’ll let her go!”","“Heh...”","Chen Jiarong’s smile became wild and unrestrained. “You’re threatening me with a woman? Xiao Qian, have you lost your mind?”","Standing opposite him, Gu Chacha could clearly see that there wasn’t the slightest trace of concern in his eyes.","Not even a trace.","Her heart sank to the bottom. He hadn’t been lying.","She pleaded with Chen Jiarong in panic. “Brother, let him go. Once he leaves, we’ll be safe too, won’t we? Let him go...”","Chen Jiarong glanced at her indifferently. “Chacha, a woman needs to know how to behave. Understand?”","The country’s border controls were extremely strict. Getting Xiao Qian out of the country would be far more difficult than killing him.","His index finger rested on the trigger, and a flicker of regret crossed his eyes. “Chacha, you were too careless. You’re so obedient and easy to handle. Where am I supposed to find another girl like you after this?”","“No! No! You can’t!”","Gu Chacha broke down completely and began struggling frantically.","She couldn’t die!","She was only twenty!","Her life had only just begun!","She couldn’t die!","“Go! Hurry, go! Get out of here!”","She shoved Xiao Qian backward in a frenzy. Get out! Once you reached the hallway, you’d be safe! If he wouldn’t send you away, escape on your own! Don’t drag her down with you!","Xiao Qian had never imagined that Gu Chacha would mean absolutely nothing to Brother Bao.","He frantically dragged Gu Chacha backward toward the door. But just as his fingers reached for the doorknob, the door was kicked open from outside!","“Everyone, don’t move! Put your hands on your heads and get down!”","“Drop the gun! Get down!”","“Down!”","The police had arrived too suddenly. Chen Jiarong had no time to react before he was pinned to the floor. He tried to struggle, but the officers holding him gave him no opportunity.","“Don’t move!”","Chen Jiarong forced his head up. “Which department are you with? Director Chen of the Municipal Public Security Bureau is my friend. I want to see him.”","The officer on top of him gave a cold laugh at the mention of Director Chen. “You’ll see him.”","【Ladies, it looks like the book trial failed, haha! The traffic has been dropping like crazy lately. Sisters who’ve read this far, please leave a five-star review! And send a few free gifts if you can—thank you, thank you! I’ll do a little hand-waving dance for you~】"]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: I Want to See My Brother","paragraphs":["As Chen Jiarong was shoved into the police car, he remained relatively calm. As long as Director Chen still wanted his money, nothing would happen to him.","And if there was one thing he had no shortage of, it was money.","But as the police car drove on, unease began to tighten in his chest.","Something was wrong. This wasn’t the road to the Municipal Bureau!","His face instantly went stiff. “Whose people are you? Where’s Director Chen? Does he know about this?”","The man seated opposite him curled his lips into a mocking smile. “Brother Bao, is it? You’re in quite the mood to worry about Director Chen when you’re in this state yourself.”","The contempt in his tone when he mentioned Director Chen sent a chill through Chen Jiarong.","Had something happened to Director Chen?","How could that be possible?!","There was someone powerful backing Director Chen!","He frantically repeated to himself that it couldn’t be true. It absolutely couldn’t.","If Director Chen had fallen, then he was finished.","After all, nearly all the people lured and forcibly taken to his compound were Chinese nationals.","Fraud, murder, rape...","If any of those crimes came to light, the death penalty would be unavoidable.","Panic surged through him. Struggling wildly, he shouted, “I want to see a lawyer! I want to see a lawyer right now!”","He was immediately forced back down. “Don’t worry. That is your right. You’ll be allowed to request one.”","But the crimes he had committed were not something a few lawyers could smooth over. Han Xuan’s testimony and the financial records had all been officially filed.","And his compound was probably in an uproar by now.","Every crime he had committed, every single one, would be uncovered and brought into the open.","At the Liang residence, Liang Zheng sat on the sofa, listening to the report over the phone.","“Good. Interrogate him thoroughly. Make sure his crimes are nailed down beyond doubt.”","It could only be the death penalty. There was no other possibility.","A man like Brother Bao was extremely vindictive. Now that they had caught him, Liang Zheng would never give him the chance to get out again.","In another police car, Gu Chacha was pale as a sheet, trembling uncontrollably. “Why are you arresting me? I was being held hostage... I don’t know anything...”","She looked fragile and terrified, pitiful beyond measure.","Ordinary people might have softened toward her. But the people before her were law enforcement officers, and all she received was a cold, impersonal reply.","“Ms. Gu, you are implicated in criminal activities including money laundering and fraud. You will come with us for questioning...”","“No! You can’t!”","Gu Chacha shook her head in utter collapse. “I can’t be arrested! I have a performance tomorrow! I can’t have any negative publicity! I... I want to see my brother! I want to see my brother!”","She needed her brother to get her out, to bury everything she had done. She could not let all her efforts be destroyed in an instant!","“Ms. Gu, you may request a lawyer. However, during the investigation and prosecution process, visits from family members cannot be arranged.”","Those cold words pushed Gu Chacha over the edge. “No... I want to see my brother. I have to see my brother...”","But no amount of crying would help. This was not some competition where looking pitiful enough earned someone sympathy. Her tears won her not even the slightest softness.","By the time she was taken into the detention center and locked up, Gu Chacha’s heart had completely shattered.","She sat anxiously in the detention center until dawn. She wanted to see a lawyer. She wanted to find her brother.","At the very least, she could not go to prison.","The next day, she got her wish and met with a lawyer. But the news he brought was not what she wanted to hear.","The lawyer’s expression was unusually cold. “President Gu said that he warned you before—you must take responsibility for the choices you make.”","That conversation between the siblings had been her final chance to come clean.","At that time, Xiao Qian and the others had not yet made their move.","All she had needed to do was tell them about Brother Bao’s plan. Just say it.","By then, the arrangements that needed to be made had already been made. What Gu Jingchen wanted was to see where she stood.","But she had said nothing. She did not know about their preparations. In her heart, she truly wanted Huanhuan to die.","The conflict between her and Huanhuan had never warranted such a thing, yet she could be so cruel.","Gu Jingchen found it difficult to face Gu Chacha, the younger sister he had watched grow up.","He had always known that she was spoiled and willful, but he had never imagined she could be this ruthless.","He thought of Brother Bao’s original plan: to abduct Huanhuan and Meili and take them to the compound.","He did not dare imagine what kind of situation they would be in now if they had possessed passports.","So he could not help Chacha. He had to make her understand that some evil deeds could not be committed without consequence. Once she had done them, she had to pay the price.","“No, no... That’s not true!”","Gu Chacha shook her head hysterically. “I didn’t do anything bad. I didn’t do anything at all!”","Like a madwoman, she lunged at the table and stared at the lawyer, emphasizing every word. “Go tell my brother that I don’t know anything. I was forced into it. I really don’t know anything. I’m innocent!”","The lawyer said calmly, “President Gu asked me to ask you one question.”","A flicker of hope rose in Gu Chacha’s eyes. “Ask me! I’ll tell him anything!”","The lawyer fixed his gaze on her. “President Gu wants to know: did you know that Brother Bao planned to abduct Miss Huanhuan in Sava?”","Gu Chacha’s eyes darted away for an instant. Then she quickly shook her head. “I didn’t know. I didn’t know anything. He never told me about his affairs, really.”","She had no idea how obvious that moment of guilt had been.","The lawyer rose to his feet, his expression calm. “Miss Gu, you were only involved in assisting with money laundering. Your sentence will not exceed five years. President Gu wants you to reflect on your actions and live properly while you are inside. Five years will pass quickly.”","“No! You can’t! My brother would never treat me like this! You’re lying!”","Gu Chacha threw herself at him like a madwoman. “You’re Huanhuan’s lawyer, aren’t you? You want me dead, don’t you? I want to see my brother! I want to see my brother!”","Before she could reach the lawyer, she was immediately restrained with her arms twisted behind her back. “Don’t move!”","She lay sprawled across the table in utter disarray, but she no longer cared about anything else. Her eyes remained fixed on the lawyer.","“I want to see my brother! My brother would never treat me this way!”","The lawyer gave her a detached look. “Miss Gu, I was commissioned by President Gu to meet with you. What I have conveyed is also President Gu’s decision.”","With that, he pushed open the door and left, leaving Gu Chacha behind in complete collapse.","“No... I didn’t do anything wrong. I didn’t do anything. How could my brother abandon me? How could he...”","What she did not know was that while Gu Jingchen had given up on her, Gu Chengye and his wife had not.","It was not because they loved her so deeply. Rather, Old Mr. Gu cared greatly about appearances. Gu Chacha was his daughter—how could his daughter commit such crimes?","He had Jiang Yulan call all three children and order them to return home that day.","He sat rigidly on the sofa, waiting for them to come back.","“Old Gu, don’t be angry. It’s bad for your health.”","Jiang Yulan sat beside him, rubbing his back to soothe him.","Gu Chengye was consumed with fury. “How can I not be angry? Jingchen has become far too bold! Something this serious, and he didn’t even tell me a word! How could he send his own sister to prison? What will people think of our Gu family? What will they think of me?”","Jiang Yulan’s movements became even gentler. “We can have a proper talk with him when he gets back. Don’t make yourself ill with anger...”"]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: Huanhuan, Don't Blame Chacha","paragraphs":["The children all arrived home around the same time. When Gu Chengye saw Qi Meili following them in, his expression darkened further. “Miss Qi, this is a family matter. It’s not appropriate for you to be here.”","Qi Meili waved a dismissive hand. “Who doesn’t know about your family’s mess? Stop putting on airs, old man. Get on with it.”","Gu Chengye’s face darkened even more. “Jingchen!”","This was their family business. How could an outsider be allowed to interfere?","He Huanhuan shot him a look. “Meili is the family I’m closest to. If she can’t stay and listen, then neither can I. We’re leaving.”","With that, she grabbed Qi Meili’s hand and turned to go. Gu Jinghan followed them without missing a beat. “Are you going back to the hotel or going out to eat? Is that brat Han Mo taking you two somewhere good again? Why do you always leave me out...?”","Fury churned in Gu Chengye’s chest, but he had no choice but to compromise. “I called you all back because there’s something important to discuss! What are you making a fuss about? Come back!”","Seeing how upset he was, Jiang Yulan hurried after them. “Huanhuan, don’t make things difficult for your father...”","It took Jiang Yulan a whole lot of gentle coaxing before she finally persuaded them to return.","She held He Huanhuan’s hand in one hand and tugged Qi Meili along with the other. “Mom knows you and Meili are close. In Mom’s heart, both of you are my good daughters. It’s just that something happened to Chacha. Your father is worried, so he spoke a little harshly...”","He Huanhuan looked surprised. “Something happened to Gu Chacha? What happened to her?”","Gu Jinghan eagerly leaned in. “She finally got herself into trouble? Did she get dumped again? Or did one of her crappy performances get canceled?”","Gu Jinghan knew absolutely nothing about Brother Bao. Gu Jingchen hadn’t told him either.","He had a big mouth. Telling him was no different from issuing a public announcement.","Tell him one minute, and Huanhuan and Meili would know the next.","So when Jiang Yulan said Gu Chacha was in trouble, the three of them were genuinely shocked—not the slightest bit fake.","Only Gu Jingchen stood there with an indifferent expression, without saying a word.","One look was all Gu Chengye needed to know that this had been Gu Jingchen’s idea alone. His anger immediately found an outlet. “Jingchen, why would you do this to your sister? She’s the little sister you raised with your own hands! Do you have no heart?”","Jiang Yulan had had a difficult time giving birth to her third child, and her body had remained weak for years after the delivery.","Gu Chacha had been raised mostly by Gu Jingchen when she was little, and the siblings had once been very close.","Gu Chengye rebuked Gu Jingchen sternly. “She’s your sister! How could you send her to prison?”","“Huanhuan is my sister too.”","Gu Jingchen looked calmly at Gu Chengye, his face betraying little emotion. “Dad, Huanhuan is my sister too.”","Gu Chengye guiltily shifted his gaze away. “I never said Huanhuan wasn’t! I’m talking about Chacha...”","Gu Jingchen cut him off. “Dad, do you really not know why Chacha was arrested?”","Gu Chengye’s gaze became even more evasive. “Why are you asking that...?”","How could he not know? He had personally helped Gu Jingchen build and maintain all those connections, little by little.","Gu Chacha had been arrested last night, and he had received the news first thing this morning.","Gu Chacha had helped Brother Bao launder money. Brother Bao had arranged for someone to assassinate He Huanhuan...","Every detail had been reported to him.","But he had chosen to ignore the latter part. Huanhuan wasn’t hurt, was she?","Since she was fine, they should just let it go.","The family’s reputation was more important. They couldn’t let people laugh at them.","But Gu Jingchen had no intention of letting it go. He stared steadily at Gu Chengye. “Dad, you knew all along, didn’t you?”","Gu Jingchen’s relentless questioning ignited Gu Chengye’s anger. Was this brat condemning him?","His eyes widened at once. “What do you mean by that? Are you accusing me? Do you think I’m wrong? What did I do wrong? Everything I’ve done has been for the company, for all of you! This family raised you—”","“Dad, this family didn’t raise Huanhuan.”","Gu Jingchen interrupted him again. “Have you forgotten? This family raised Chacha, not Huanhuan.”","His biological daughter had spent her first twenty years living in poverty in the countryside. After she was finally brought back, Gu Chacha had resented her, targeted her, kidnapped her, and tried to have her killed...","Gu Jingchen lowered his eyes toward Gu Chengye, who was seated on the sofa. “Dad, do you really consider Huanhuan your daughter?”","Gu Chengye was instantly speechless, unable to think of a reply. “That’s not what I mean. I just...”","He considered this family, the company, everything.","It was just that He Huanhuan had never been included in those considerations.","He straightened up, as though he had done nothing wrong. “I’ll make up for what needs to be made up for. But this situation is different. If Chacha’s matter gets exposed, the impact on the company will be extremely serious...”","Even after Gu Jingchen had laid it out so plainly, he still refused to give in. He wanted to protect Gu Chacha and get her completely out of this mess.","“Heh.”","Gu Jingchen gave a quiet laugh. “Dad, I knew you’d be like this. It’s useless. You can’t get Chacha out.”","Gu Chengye frowned. “What do you mean?”","The smile at Gu Jingchen’s lips deepened. “The Liang family has stepped in. Chacha isn’t getting out. She’ll receive the punishment she deserves.”","“How dare you!”","Gu Chengye had never imagined that Gu Jingchen would go this far!","Instead of covering up the family scandal, he had actually exposed it to outsiders and humiliated the family!","He abruptly rose to his feet and glared at Gu Jingchen. “Do you think there’s nothing I can do to you?”","Gu Jingchen smiled and shook his head. “Of course you can do something, Dad. You can force me out of the company. You can take everything back. But what I’ve already done is beyond your control.”","Gu Chengye’s expression turned awful. “Do you really think I wouldn’t hand the company over to Jinghan?”","Gu Jinghan pointed at himself, the genius that he was. “Give it to me? Dad, are you okay? Do you want to experience bankruptcy in your old age?”","Why else would he want to marry a rich woman? Obviously, he wasn’t cut out for this kind of work!","The hotel accounts were sent to the company for his big brother to review every month, right on schedule...","“You—”","Gu Chengye shot him an irritated glare. “Useless! Jade must be polished to become a gem. Why can’t you be properly honed?”","Gu Jinghan grinned like the brilliant mind he was. “But it has to be jade before you can polish it. If you polish plastic too hard, it’ll catch fire!”","...","Gu Chengye’s gaze shifted unwillingly to He Huanhuan. She flashed a broad grin. “What? You want to hand the company over to me? Sure! I think I’ve got the look of a boss.”","...","To her surprise, Gu Chengye simply asked, “Huanhuan, can you stop blaming Chacha?”","He Huanhuan spread her hands. “This isn’t about whether I blame her or not. What are you all even talking about? I don’t understand a thing, okay?”","Why exactly had Gu Chacha gone to prison? What had she done?","Could someone please tell her? She was dying of curiosity!","Gu Chengye’s gaze flickered away. “That isn’t important. Huanhuan, Dad is just asking you one thing: can you stop blaming Chacha?”","He Huanhuan crossed her hands into an X. “Don’t try to put words in my mouth. I need to know what happened first. If she secretly plotted to stab me to death, and you still expect me not to blame her? I might as well stab you instead!”","...","[Thank you, sisters, for all the love and support! I’m putting every one of you on the ‘Make the Old Man Collapse’ leaderboard! In no particular order!]"]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: Huanhuan, Please Move Out","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan’s attitude was crystal clear: she could let the little things go, but she would never tolerate anything serious.","Gu Chengye was instantly left speechless. What Chacha had done really was an attempt to stab Huanhuan to death...","He awkwardly looked away. “You child... Why do you always resort to violence?”","He Huanhuan immediately noticed that something was wrong with his expression. She glared at him and demanded, “Why, you old geezer! Is Gu Chacha trying to kill me?!”","She had only thrown the question out casually, but Gu Chengye was so obviously guilty that she could only have hit the nail on the head!","Did Gu Chacha really want her dead? Why?","What had she done?","She racked her brains but couldn’t come up with a reason. She might not have been universally adored, but surely she hadn’t done anything to make someone want her dead, right?","Ever since she had been brought back, Gu Chacha had been the one targeting her. She hadn’t done a thing!","Why on earth did Gu Chacha want to kill her?","What the hell! Did she have no sense of right and wrong?","The more He Huanhuan thought about it, the angrier she became. Her life was precious, okay?","She stared fixedly at Gu Chengye. “Tell me honestly. Is Gu Chacha trying to kill me?”","Gu Chengye’s eyes darted around. “You child, why do you keep talking about killing people...?”","Seeing their father’s reaction, Gu Jinghan was utterly dumbfounded. “Has Gu Chacha’s brain been kicked by a donkey? Why would she kill Huanhuan for no reason? Huanhuan hasn’t even provoked her!”","What was wrong with their family? Were they some kind of mafia? Killing people was against the law!","Besides, why would she kill Huanhuan? Huanhuan was just a silly girl who spent her days eating and drinking. She barely even spent any money. What was there to kill her for?","He honestly couldn’t understand how Gu Chacha’s mind worked.","Gu Jingchen had never wanted He Huanhuan to find out about this, but Old Mr. Gu had been so determined to save face that he had gone and let the cat out of the bag.","Jingchen sighed inwardly as he remembered what Han Mo had told him before they came.","“Let Huanhuan move out. Your father has lost his mind. She can’t keep living at your house.”","At the time, he hadn’t said anything, but deep down, he had been unwilling.","Only close, constant contact could foster deep affection. Huanhuan hadn’t been back for long, and what his parents felt toward her was mostly guilt, not love.","If she moved out this soon, even that guilt would quickly fade.","He didn’t want to see that happen, but reality had slapped him hard across the face.","Gu Chengye was simply too muddleheaded. He hadn’t even been willing to phrase it tactfully; he had gone straight to asking Huanhuan to forgive Chacha.","It was absurd. What if this had happened to him? What if Chacha had been the one trying to harm him?","Would he still forgive Chacha for the sake of his pride?","Gu Jingchen let out a quiet laugh inwardly. He knew the answer was no.","He turned to He Huanhuan. “Huanhuan, it was Chacha’s boyfriend, Chen Jiarong, who wanted to kill you...”","“Jingchen!”","Gu Chengye tried to stop him, but Jingchen ignored him completely.","“He arranged for people to ambush you in Sawa before, but you and Meili didn’t go, so nothing happened...”","He told them everything from beginning to end, leaving the three of them dumbfounded.","He Huanhuan pointed at herself. “Why did he want to kill me?”","She and Chen Jiarong had met only twice in total, and they hadn’t exchanged more than a few words either time. Why would he want her dead?","A trace of guilt flashed through Gu Jingchen’s eyes. “He wanted to get involved in our family’s business empire. He was afraid that Chacha wasn’t our parents’ biological daughter and that our family wouldn’t accept him for her sake, so he wanted to eliminate you.”","Without He Huanhuan, Gu Chacha would be the family’s only daughter. All their guilt and affection would belong to her as well, so Gu Chacha was happy to let things unfold that way.","Meili clicked her tongue repeatedly. “Rich people are seriously awful!”","Even if she tried, she couldn’t come up with such twisted schemes.","What kind of mind worked that way? How could someone go from doing business together to plotting murder?","She was truly impressed!","They clearly hadn’t gone to school. Didn’t they know that murder was against the law?","Complete illiterates!","Gu Jinghan shrank back and moved to He Huanhuan’s side. “Damn! Good thing I’m useless. Otherwise, I’d be in danger too!”","What did this have to do with him?","He didn’t know, but he felt that he was in danger, so he had to get involved.","Gu Jingchen looked at He Huanhuan. “Huanhuan, move out.”","There was indeed no reason for her to stay in this family anymore. She hadn’t grown up here, so there was no reason for her to keep suffering here either.","Gu Jinghan hurriedly nodded. “That’s right! Move out. I’ll move out with you. We can live together from now on. Your brother will take care of you.”","They could stay at his hotel from then on. They could even live there for the rest of their lives.","“Enough nonsense!”","The situation had completely deviated from Gu Chengye’s intentions, and he couldn’t help growing angry.","“Your home is right here. Where are you planning to move? Are you abandoning this family?!”","He had no awareness whatsoever of the problems with his own behavior. He only stared at He Huanhuan and asked, “Huanhuan, won’t you give your father a chance to make it up to you?”","Make it up to her, make it up to her—everything he said was just another way of making things difficult for her.","He Huanhuan looked at him speechlessly. “How exactly do you plan to make it up to me? Is making me forgive Gu Chacha your idea of compensation? Your family has a pretty strange way of making amends—by forcing people into impossible situations?”","...","She wasn’t some meek pushover with a saintly temper. The reason Chen Jiarong’s attempts to harm her had failed wasn’t because of anything Gu Chacha had done.","It was because she had been too poor to have a passport.","It was because Han Mo and her brothers had been capable enough to capture the people involved.","None of that had anything to do with Gu Chacha. Why should she forgive her?","The fact that she wasn’t kicking her while she was down already proved that she was beautiful inside and out, okay?","As for Gu Chengye and his wife, she had no expectations of them.","Without filial attachment, there could be no disappointment.","She might as well move out. It would be a good thing. She had never felt comfortable living in that house anyway.","Even Gu Jinghan’s hotel felt more like home.","She didn’t have many belongings to begin with. Most of them were things Han Mo had bought for her over the past few months, so packing up was easy.","Seven or eight boxes were enough to erase every trace of her months there. After loading everything into the car, she turned around and glanced at Gu Chengye and his wife, who were standing at the entrance.","Gu Chengye wore a stern expression. He didn’t say anything, but the reproach in his eyes was impossible to hide.","Jiang Yulan looked sorrowful and aggrieved as she gazed at He Huanhuan, as if Huanhuan were the one who had wronged her.","He Huanhuan had originally intended to say goodbye, but seeing the look on their faces, she couldn’t bring herself to say a word.","She merely waved a hand. “I’m leaving!”","The car quickly disappeared from view.","Jiang Yulan let out a long sigh. “A child you didn’t raise yourself really doesn’t feel close...”","Her life was so bitter. The Chacha she had painstakingly raised had gone astray and become a convict.","The Huanhuan she had risked her life to give birth to didn’t have her mother in her heart at all.","How could Heaven be so cruel to her?","She had spent her entire life getting along peacefully with everyone and had never even had a serious quarrel. How had things ended up like this?","She couldn’t understand it.","She couldn’t understand it, and neither could Gu Chengye.","He didn’t think he had done anything wrong. After He Huanhuan returned, they had even given her Chacha’s third-floor suite. They provided her with delicious food and comfortable living every day, and they hadn’t skimped on her allowance either. What more was he supposed to do? When would it ever be enough?","The truth was simple: Love made people constantly feel that they owed someone more, while a lack of love made them find fault with everything.","Deep down, they didn’t love He Huanhuan, so they were completely incapable of recognizing their own mistakes."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: The Twin Mothers of the Spirit","paragraphs":["Ever since moving out, all those aggravating troubles vanished from He Huanhuan’s life overnight.","The case involving Gu Chacha and Chen Jiarong had nothing to do with her anymore either.","By the time the case was finally closed, Gu Chacha was sentenced to five years in prison for aiding and abetting money laundering, along with a three-million-yuan fine.","Chen Jiarong, meanwhile, was sentenced to death for cross-border fraud and intentional homicide.","In the end, even Old Mr. Gu had been unable to suppress the matter involving Gu Chacha. The promotional campaigns she had paid for before finally produced explosive results.","A favored daughter of heaven, a wealthy heiress, an artist...","Imprisoned for money laundering—what a sensational headline.","The entire video-sharing internet exploded. Performances that had once drawn empty halls were dug up and reposted.","Only then did netizens belatedly understand. No wonder someone they had never even heard of had suddenly appeared out of nowhere. No wonder her concerts had come one after another, each more grandly publicized than the last.","So it had all been for money laundering!","My God! Rich people are really greedy! Her family was already one of the elite! How could they still do something like this?","The company’s stock price plummeted in a frenzy over the short term. But as time slowly passed and the incident faded from people’s memories, everything gradually returned to normal.","After staying in a hotel for a while, He Huanhuan threw herself wholeheartedly into the great undertaking of house hunting.","Gu Jingchen had told her that her brother would pay for the house. She could look to her heart’s content—whatever she liked, her brother would buy for her.","Well, then, what was there to say? The secondhand housing market, here she came!","After looking at house after house, the one that ultimately won her over was the large three-bedroom apartment she had viewed at the very beginning.","It was 130 square meters, with three spacious bedrooms and two big balconies. The natural light was so good she wouldn’t even need a fill light to perform hand-waving dances.","The only problem was that it was a little expensive: 2.5 million yuan, and the owner refused to lower the price by even a single cent.","The landlord had a terrible temper. When they tried to negotiate, he glared at them.","“Buy it if you want. If you don’t, then get lost!”","The layout and location of his place were excellent in every respect. Haggling? Absolutely impossible!","She had already decided to buy it outright, but somehow, Liang Ye found out about it. The guy immediately grew excited.","“Why didn’t you tell me you were buying a house? I could’ve helped you negotiate! This is what I’m best at!”","When he bought his small place, the landlord had also stubbornly insisted on 1.3 million yuan, refusing to lower it by a single penny.","But hadn’t Liang Ye still managed to haggle the price down by fifty thousand?","There was a strategy to bargaining when buying a house. Clearly, they had no idea what they were doing.","With great wisdom, he thumped his chest.","“Don’t rush into buying it. The real-estate market isn’t doing that well this year. I’ll come with you to look at it this weekend when I’m off work. I’ll help you knock two hundred thousand off the price!”","How could that landlord have the nerve to ask for 2.5 million for a 130-square-meter apartment?","Did he not know what an economic downturn was? Did he not know this was a buyer’s market?","When Saturday arrived, the house-hunting party gained three more members.","Han Mo, Liang Ye, and Gu Jinghan, who had nothing better to do, all showed up.","Gu Jinghan drove a luxury car worth nearly two million yuan. Han Mo drove the cheapest BYD Qin. Liang Ye rode an electric scooter...","The real-estate agent was completely baffled. How had those three even ended up becoming friends?","The agent had briefly dabbled in the online mental-health community before. With one glance at He Huanhuan and Qi Meili, he immediately sensed that familiar kind of vibe from the two of them.","He secretly gave her a thumbs-up in his heart. What a spiritual role model!","Even an old geezer can somehow land a luxury car and a handsome guy. Impressive!","She landed a luxury car and a handsome guy, yet she still didn’t kick out that poor, lovesick simp. What loyalty!","Especially after seeing He Huanhuan and Qi Meili get into the BYD, his eyes lit up.","No wonder she managed to snag such a high-quality older man! She had a strategy!","She deliberately passed up the luxury car for the BYD, creating a stark contrast. That way, the rich second-generation heir would be haunted by her memory and never forget her.","Brilliant! Absolutely brilliant!","He couldn’t do that. If he didn’t ride in a luxury car today, he might never get another chance.","The agent eagerly sidled up to Gu Jinghan’s car. “Handsome, can I ride with you and give you directions?”","Gu Jinghan generously waved him in. “Sure, hop in!”","“Thanks, handsome!”","The cars drove into the residential compound. The landlord had already been waiting by the window.","When he saw the luxury car leading the way, his eyes lit up.","These buyers had money. Maybe he could finally sell the place today.","But behind the luxury car came a BYD?","What was going on?","Behind the BYD was an electric scooter, with Liang Ye sitting on it, wearing a stern expression.","The landlord immediately sensed trouble. They had brought two cars and still hadn’t been willing to give the agent a ride. These buyers were going to be difficult. This deal was in danger.","The guys had mistaken Liang Ye for the agent. And, to be fair, his demeanor did suit the role rather well.","The apartment was on the fifth floor. By the time they reached it, the landlord was already waiting at the door.","He sized up Gu Jinghan, then Han Mo. They were clearly wealthy men.","His gaze swept over He Huanhuan and Qi Meili next. Hmm. Two silly young girls.","What kind of combination was this?","He couldn’t make heads or tails of it.","Then he nodded at Liang Ye and the agent. “You’re here? You’ve already shown them the details of my apartment, right?”","Well, even after getting off the scooter, Brother Liang was still being treated as the agent.","The agent nodded. “We’ve gone over everything. We’re just here to take a look at the place in person.”","Liang Ye shot into the apartment and began inspecting it at top speed.","“Tsk, tsk, tsk... The floor tiles are scratched. No good, no good... Why didn’t you install concealed lighting? It’s not stylish enough... Why haven’t you knocked out the bay window in the bedroom? What a waste of space... The bathroom...”","In less than five minutes, he had found at least twenty things to criticize. The landlord’s face darkened until he finally shoved Liang Ye toward the door.","“What kind of agency do you work for? Do you even know how to do business? What’s wrong with my apartment? Get out, get out! I’m not selling through your agency anymore!”","Liang Ye tried his best to explain. “I’m not an agent! I’m here to buy the apartment! I—”","The landlord pushed him outside. “Buy my ass! I’m not selling to someone who’s just here to cause trouble! Get lost!”","The door slammed shut.","The landlord turned around and glared at He Huanhuan and the others. “You’re with him?”","He Huanhuan immediately shook her head. “I don’t know him. He forced his way into our group halfway here.”","Meili lowered her head and stared at the floor tiles. “Where are the scratches? He was deliberately nitpicking. What a terrible person!”","The four of them quietly looked around the apartment. It had only been bought five years ago and had barely been lived in, so it was still very well maintained.","Seeing how much He Huanhuan liked the place, Han Mo sincerely negotiated with the landlord.","“We’ll pay in full. Could you lower the price a little?”","To Han Mo, a difference of thirty or fifty thousand yuan was nothing. But He Huanhuan wanted to negotiate the price, and because he wanted to make her happy, he was willing to discuss that small sum at length with the landlord.","The landlord’s expression darkened. “Didn’t I already say I won’t lower the price? I won’t budge whether you’re paying in full or taking out a mortgage. I poured a tremendous amount of effort into renovating this place. I personally oversaw everything—the furnishings, the structural work, the plumbing, and the electrical. I’m not taking a single cent off!”","Han Mo nodded with a smile. “I can see that. But the house is priced ten percent above the market value in this area. It can’t be easy to sell at that price, can it?”","The property market had been extremely sluggish these past two years, with the economy in such poor shape.","As solidly as the house had been renovated, it was still priced two hundred thousand yuan higher than comparable homes of the same layout in the neighborhood. The truth was, it wouldn’t be easy to sell."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: Four Million","paragraphs":["The landlord’s expression darkened further at that. “So what? If I can’t sell it, I just won’t sell it! Are you buying or not? If not...”","He impatiently waved a hand, wanting to drive them away. All they knew how to do was haggle. What a nuisance!","He was selling the house so he could take the money and travel around the country. He didn’t like traveling on a shoestring. What was the point of roughing it? You couldn’t eat well, sleep well, or stay anywhere decent. What was there left to enjoy?","Travel was supposed to be comfortable: good food, good drinks, good sights, and good sleep. You had to take your time eating, playing, and sleeping.","That was why he couldn’t bear to lower the price of the house even a little.","But the listing had been up for several months. Fewer and fewer people came to view the place, while more and more wanted to haggle.","It was driving him crazy, and he had already postponed his travel plans three or four times!","Before he could finish telling them to leave, Han Mo suddenly handed him a dark green card glinting with a golden sheen.","“Mr. Jin, I’ve looked at your social media profile. You’re planning to travel around the country for the next five years, aren’t you?”","The landlord suspiciously glanced at the card, then found that he couldn’t take his eyes off it. “This is...”","A confident smile curved Han Mo’s lips. “A Jin Yue Hotel VIP card. The chain operates nationwide, and it gives you fifty percent off year-round on deluxe suites...”","The landlord’s eyes grew brighter with every word. “Th-this is for me?”","He couldn’t help reaching out to take the card, but Han Mo pulled it back. “How about we discuss the price again? We’ll pay in full.”","“Discuss, discuss... Of course we can discuss...”","He knew about Jin Yue. You needed to spend more than two hundred thousand yuan a year at the hotel to upgrade to a VIP card!","Licking his lips, the landlord asked Han Mo, “How many years does it last?”","Han Mo smiled. “Five.”","Not one year more or less—exactly five years, which happened to be the length of his planned trip around the country.","That would take care of the landlord for the next five years.","The landlord’s heart began to race. Whenever he traveled, he stayed only in five-star hotels.","According to his original plan, hotel accommodations and meals would account for the bulk of his expenses on this trip around the country.","With this VIP card, he could cut his hotel expenses in half and put more money toward food!","It was practically a VIP card made specifically for him!","And it really had been made specifically for him. The hotels all belonged to Han Mo. How many years the card lasted and what discount it offered were entirely up to him.","The landlord’s heart fluttered again and again. Finally, he cautiously asked, “How about you knock off fifty thousand?”","His accommodation budget was five hundred yuan a night. Over five years, that would come to more than nine hundred thousand yuan.","With this VIP card, he could save over four hundred thousand.","But he couldn’t put all of that saving into the price of the house. Otherwise, it would be no different from buying the VIP card himself.","He calculated silently. One hundred thousand—he could lower the price by ten thousand at most...","As though he had heard the landlord’s thoughts, Han Mo said with uncanny precision, “One hundred thousand, then. How about two million four hundred thousand? If that works for you, we can complete the transaction today.”","Two million four hundred thousand yuan in cash, plus a VIP card valid for five years. The landlord agreed without a second thought.","“Deal! Two million four hundred thousand!”","As soon as the transfer was complete, he would leave for his travels. He wouldn’t waste even a single day!","Once the landlord nodded, everything else was simple.","Gu Jinghan had his brother’s black card tucked in his arms. They signed the contract, swiped the card, paid the taxes, and completed the transfer.","He Huanhuan soon received the property deed that belonged to her. She now had a home of her own in Jiangcheng.","She stared at the name on the deed, unable to believe it. “I actually have a home of my own?”","The feeling was so strange and wonderful, as if her heart had suddenly found somewhere to settle.","She had lived in a huge villa at the Gu residence before, and in a lavish suite at Gu Jinghan’s hotel. But this felt completely different.","Her heart had finally found a home—a real, tangible place to belong.","She looked up at Qi Meili. “Meili, I didn’t touch the money in my account. We should buy you a place later too. Having a home feels amazing!”","Qi Meili smacked her lightly, exasperated. “Why waste that money? Your home is my home too! What, are you planning to leave me out?”","The market wasn’t doing well right now. What was the point of buying so many houses? Just leave them sitting there while their value dropped?","He Huanhuan shook her head with a silly grin. “How could I? This is our home—the home we’ll have for the rest of our lives.”","In this world, Qi Meili was the closest person she had. How could she possibly not let Meili live with her?","This was their home. Their forever home.","Only after the deed was safely in hand did she remember the VIP card.","Embarrassed, she asked Han Mo, “That VIP card you gave away must cost you quite a bit, right?”","Han Mo shook his head with a smile. “Once he has this card, Jin Yue will be his first choice whenever he travels. He won’t consider other hotels. It’s a win-win situation, isn’t it?”","He wasn’t lying about that. An empty hotel room made no money.","Even at half price, as long as the landlord stayed there, Han Mo would still earn.","Over five years, the landlord would contribute at least four or five hundred thousand yuan in revenue to the hotel.","The VIP card really was a win-win.","What actually cost him money, however, was something he hadn’t told He Huanhuan.","He Huanhuan’s new residential complex consisted of the most traditional layout: two homes per floor, with the doors directly facing each other.","After He Huanhuan bought the landlord’s place, Han Mo took a liking to the apartment opposite hers.","He wanted to buy it so he could become He Huanhuan’s neighbor.","They could see each other whenever they looked up or lowered their heads, and they’d run into each other every time one of them opened or closed the door. That kind of constant contact would make their relationship more secure.","After all, he still hadn’t officially become her boyfriend.","The family living opposite He Huanhuan consisted of three generations under one roof and two children. It was the only home they owned, so they had no plans to sell anytime soon.","But Han Mo made a generous offer right from the start: two million eight hundred thousand yuan.","Two million eight hundred thousand might not sound like much—only three hundred thousand more than the price of He Huanhuan’s apartment.","But He Huanhuan’s apartment had been solidly renovated, barely lived in, and was practically new. Even so, the landlord had only asked for two million five hundred thousand.","This family had two mischievous children, and with so many people living there, the apartment had already been thoroughly worn down.","With two million eight hundred thousand in hand, they could immediately buy another apartment with the same layout and newer renovations, while still having two or three hundred thousand left over.","How hard was it for an ordinary family to save two or three hundred thousand yuan?","At their age, with elderly parents above and young children below, they could work themselves to the bone for five or six years and still might not manage to save three hundred thousand.","Naturally, the family was instantly tempted. The deal had practically been finalized, but just before they signed the contract, a spoiler suddenly appeared out of nowhere.","That spoiler was Liang Zheng.","No one knew where he had heard the news, but he raised the price to three million yuan without hesitation. The family immediately threw themselves into Liang Zheng’s arms.","Three million!","They could use the money to buy another apartment with the exact same layout and still have five hundred thousand left over.","Good heavens! The internet was always shouting that life was impossible on an annual salary below five hundred thousand, but in the real world, how many families could casually produce five hundred thousand yuan in cash?","Almost none.","They had to sell to Liang Zheng. They absolutely had to sell to Liang Zheng!","The contract had already been printed, and everyone was seated together. Yet just like that, the deal fell through.","Han Mo’s face turned black. He called Liang Zheng. “We don’t have any history between us, do we?”","On the other end, Liang Zheng laughed. “I’m not getting any younger either. It’s time I moved out and got a place of my own.”","Last time, Han Mo had snatched his Labubu. This time, Liang Zheng had snatched his apartment. It was only fair—one for one.","Han Mo tapped his knuckles against the table. “The contract hasn’t been signed. Nothing’s final yet, is it?”","Wasn’t it just a matter of raising the price? It wasn’t as if he couldn’t afford to do that.","And so, without He Huanhuan or Qi Meili knowing, the two men vying for her affection began driving up the price against each other.","Three million three hundred thousand, three million five hundred thousand, three million eight hundred thousand, four million...","Watching the price skyrocket, the homeowner’s whole family felt as if their hearts were about to stop.","Good heavens! They weren’t dreaming, were they? If this was a dream, please don’t let them wake up! Don’t wake up!","If He Huanhuan knew about this, her heart would stop too!","What were they fighting over? Did they think money grew on trees? They were bidding on her house! She’d sell it!","Four million? She’d sell!"]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: Where the Flowers Fall","paragraphs":["Once men started competing for a woman, they became ruthless and completely lost their heads. The market price no longer mattered to them at all.","In just a few days, the two of them had driven the price up to over seven million yuan.","The bidding war had the homeowners so excited that they didn’t dare sleep at night, afraid they would wake up and discover it had all been a dream—and be unable to take the shock and pass out.","That evening, lying in bed, the homeowner’s wife pressed a hand to her pounding heart and asked her husband, “Honey, check your phone. Have they raised the price again?”","“I’ve checked it several times already. No, nothing...”","He was holding his phone right in his hand. The moment a message came through, he would feel the vibration.","Each vibration represented tens of thousands of yuan. How could he not be paying close attention?","But ever since the price reached 7.8 million, neither side had made a move for several days.","No one raised their offer, and no one came to buy.","The couple grew increasingly anxious, unable to get anything done.","Whatever they were doing, they had to ask as a matter of routine:","“Have they raised the price?”","“No.”","“Are they going to buy?”","“They didn’t say.”","“Why haven’t they come yet?”","“How would I know?”","“Why are you snapping at me?”","“When did I snap at you?”","“...”","So what were Han Mo and Liang Zheng doing?","The two of them were stuck in a stalemate.","They had bid far too aggressively. A house worth only two million had been pushed to nearly eight million between them. It was insane.","When Gu Jingchen found out, he immediately went to talk some sense into them.","He didn’t need to say much. He only asked them one question:","“If Huanhuan and Meili find out you’re wasting money like this, have you thought about the consequences?”","...","They didn’t need to think about it. The consequences would definitely be severe.","And so, the two of them became locked in a standoff.","Neither was willing to let the other have the house, but neither was willing to pay that price either.","The only ones suffering were the homeowners. They waited and waited, and not only did no one raise the price—neither man even made another move.","Yet another sleepless night passed. Lying in bed, the homeowner’s wife said, “Honey, what do you think? Should we lower the price a little?”","Her husband’s eyes flew open. “Of course not! Are you crazy? Seven-point-eight million! With that kind of money, we wouldn’t have to work for the rest of our lives!”","Clutching his phone, he wore an extremely serious expression. “Not only can’t we lower it—we have to raise it!”","“Raise it? How?”","His eyes gleamed. “Tomorrow, tell the agent to say someone has offered 8.5 million. Let’s provoke them a little.”","All the offers had been relayed through the agent, so the homeowner had no idea that the two buyers knew each other.","Early the next morning, he called the agent and said someone had offered 8.5 million.","“Tell those two buyers that if they don’t raise their offers, I’ll sell it to the other person.”","Eight-point-five million was more money than he could earn in his entire life.","The agent immediately understood what he was trying to do and couldn’t help advising him, “Brother, don’t do this. You...”","But the homeowner had already become obsessed with the idea. He simply shouted, “Why are you talking so much? I told you to go tell them, so go tell them! You’re just some lousy agent—why do you care so much?”","If he could really sell the place for 8.5 million, would he short the agent on his commission?","What a fool. He had no sense at all!","The agent had no choice but to pass the message on to Han Mo and Liang Zheng.","Han Mo laughed as soon as he heard it. “Someone offered 8.5 million? Fine. Tell him to sell it to that person, then. I’m not interested in viewing the house anymore.”","Did the homeowner really think they were suckers?","One sentence, and he wanted to add seven hundred thousand yuan to the price!","Liang Zheng didn’t even laugh. “Eight-point-five million? He certainly has the nerve to ask for that. Let him sell it. I’d like to see who’s willing to spend that much.”","The homeowner never imagined that his greed would end up ruining everything.","When the agent called him back, he panicked. “No, no, wait... Tell those two gentlemen that 7.8 million is fine. I’ll sell it for 7.8!”","The agent scolded him irritably. “Sell what? They don’t want to buy anymore!”","The homeowner grew even more frantic. “Then I’ll lower it. Seven million—will that work?”","“Seven million won’t help either!”","The agent sighed. “Do you know why those two wanted to buy your house in the first place?”","The homeowner shook his head. “How would I know?”","His family had lived in the house for several years, and there was nothing special about it. At most, two young women had moved into the apartment across the hall a few days earlier.","“It’s because of those two young women!”","The agent rubbed his palms together and lowered his voice as he explained, “They wanted to buy your house to pursue those girls. Otherwise, who would be interested in your lousy place? But you went and got carried away when they pushed the price up a couple of times!”","“Then you tried to play mind games with them. They aren’t idiots. Did you really think they’d fall for it?”","The homeowner’s mind instantly became a complete mess. “Then what do we do? Will they still buy the house?”","If necessary, he didn’t want seven million anymore. Six million would be fine.","No—five million would be fine too!","The house was only worth two million in the first place. As long as he could make some money, what more could he ask for?","He earned four thousand yuan a month, while his wife earned three thousand.","With seven thousand yuan a month, they had to support both their elderly parents and their children. They couldn’t save any money at all.","How many times in his life would he ever come across an opportunity like this?","At the thought that he had driven the buyers away, tears nearly sprang to his eyes.","“Please, help me talk to them. Tell them I won’t raise the price anymore. I really won’t...”","The agent sighed helplessly. “What’s the point of saying that now? They don’t want to buy it anymore! What are they? Rich people! Rich people have countless ways to pursue a girl. Why would they have to buy your house?”","After hearing that, the homeowner’s tears finally fell.","The only chance in his life to become rich overnight was gone...","“Why are they like this? If they’re pursuing a girl, shouldn’t they show a little persistence? They’ll never win her over like that...”","“Honestly, you...”","The agent sighed again. “How about this? I have an overseas client who just returned to the country a couple of days ago. He wants to buy a place as a temporary residence. He doesn’t know the going rates in Jiangcheng. Would you sell the house for 2.8 million? If you’re willing, I’ll send him the listing and let him take a look...”","The homeowner’s heart ached terribly. “Only 2.8 million? They offered 7.5 million before...”","The price had dropped far too much. It felt like someone was cutting flesh from his body.","The agent was speechless. “Don’t you know what your house is actually worth? You’d still make a tidy profit selling it for 2.8 million! If you won’t sell, I’ll take my client to look at another house.”","“No, no, wait...”","The homeowner’s mind immediately descended into chaos, and he hurriedly called out, “Let me think about it. Let me think...”","After hanging up, he told his wife everything.","She was instantly furious. She pinched his chubby belly and twisted it around and around.","“I told you! It was already too much! But you wouldn’t listen! Look what happened now! We’ve lost everything!”","“Ow, ow, ow...”","The homeowner groaned in pain. “So, are we selling for 2.8 million or not?”","“Selling!”","His wife’s eyes widened. “We can use two million to buy another place, and still have eight hundred thousand left in savings. Why wouldn’t we sell?”","This time, they didn’t dare put on any airs whatsoever.","When the agent brought the buyer to see the house, they practically wanted to carry him around in their arms as he looked it over.","The overseas Chinese buyer appeared very young and had a gentle, refined air about him. After looking around, he nodded in satisfaction.","“Pretty good. It’s spacious too. I’ll take it.”","The agent smiled and nodded. “All right, Mr. Gu.”"]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: Liang Zheng's Revenge","paragraphs":["The sale of the house went remarkably smoothly. From signing the contract and transferring the money to completing the title transfer—and all the way until the entire family had moved out—the two tycoons never said another word.","The homeowner cursed inwardly. Damn rich people. All it took was a flick of their fingers to make his life unforgettable!","From now on, he was going to do nothing but hate on the rich.","Fortunately, his overseas-Chinese friend had still proved reliable. As he looked at the 2.8 million yuan in his bank account, he finally felt a little comforted.","At least his parents’ retirement funds were secured, and so were the fees for his child’s tutoring and extracurricular classes.","He and his wife could finally breathe a little easier, too.","The family climbed into the truck and left the neighborhood for good, heading off to live better lives.","Meanwhile, on the fifth floor, He Huanhuan and Qi Meili opened the door, ready to go out for dinner. The moment they saw the people in the apartment across from them, they were utterly stunned.","He Huanhuan exclaimed, “Big Brother? What are you doing here?”","Gu Jingchen smiled gently. “You used to live alone on an entire floor. I was worried you wouldn’t be able to adjust after moving into a smaller place, so I bought the apartment next door as well and had the two units connected. That way, you’d be more comfortable.”","He had also conveniently kept a room for himself, so he could come over and stay for a few days whenever he wanted.","He Huanhuan was so touched she could hardly contain herself. “Big Brother, you’re way too considerate! Oh my gosh! You’re my favorite person in this family!”","Qi Meili nodded frantically. “Mine too! Big Brother is my favorite!”","From now on, the entire floor belonged to the two of them. Oh my gosh, this was amazing.","The smile at the corners of Gu Jingchen’s lips deepened. “Remember to save a room for me. I’ll come stay for a couple of days whenever I miss you.”","The two women nodded vigorously. “We’ll save one! We definitely will!”","By the time Han Mo and Liang Zheng realized what was happening, the wall between the two apartments had already been knocked through, and the renovation crew had moved in and started work.","Liang Zheng sat on the sofa and let out a cold laugh. “Well played, Gu Jingchen!”","So he had used the old “when the snipe and clam fight, the fisherman benefits” trick on them, had he?","He immediately got up and went to his father’s study, where he retrieved his father’s address book.","Gu Jingchen wasn’t getting any younger. It was time he started thinking about his personal life.","Page by page, Liang Zheng carefully browsed the address book, seriously helping Gu Jingchen select the most suitable blind-date candidate.","He had already figured it out. Qi Meili had a knot in her heart, and he would slowly work on untying it.","Qi Meili liked handsome men. As long as he remained the best single man by her side, she would never notice anyone else.","The foremost candidates were, of course, the brothers Gu Jingchen and Gu Jinghan.","And the first person he had to deal with was Gu Jingchen.","Gu Jingchen was far too cunning. Liang Zheng had to find him someone he absolutely couldn’t refuse—and couldn’t bear to refuse, either.","Matchmaker Zheng flipped through half of his father’s address book before finally finding a woman who was a perfect match for Gu Jingchen.","Uncle He’s beloved daughter, He Yunzhi.","She came from a highly educated family, had earned her doctorate from a top-tier university, and was now an associate professor at Jiangcheng University. Gentle, elegant, and intellectually accomplished, she was practically the ultimate all-rounder on the blind-date market.","He opened his phone’s contacts, found He Yunzhi, and began carefully scrolling through her social-media posts one by one.","He went all the way back five years. Five years ago, He Yunzhi had yet to graduate, and her posts were much livelier than they were now.","“An academic air is the most precious gift.”","The accompanying picture showed a male celebrity who had been popular at the time. He looked refined, with a gentle smile playing at the corners of his lips.","Liang Zheng’s lips curled upward slightly.","Wasn’t this just Gu Jingchen in his cultured persona?","He immediately stood up and went to find his father, who was taking a walk in the courtyard...","The next day at noon, just after finishing an online meeting, Gu Jingchen received a call from Old Mr. Gu.","“Jingchen, come home tonight.”","Ever since He Huanhuan had moved out, the two Gu brothers had been returning home much less often.","Gu Jinghan had moved straight into a hotel and couldn’t be bothered to go home unless necessary.","It wasn’t that he was unfilial. The main problem was that every time he went home, Jiang Yulan would cry at him.","She cried over how Gu Chacha had ended up like this, and how He Huanhuan was heartless—after living with them for so long, she had simply left without a second thought...","It drove him crazy. Didn’t she know perfectly well why it had happened?","Did she really need him to spell it out?","Whenever he did, the old man would get angry, slam the table, and yell at him. Then, after yelling, he would dock his allowance.","His allowance really couldn’t take many more deductions!","If he went home a few more times, he’d have to beg on the street for a living.","Gu Jingchen was in a slightly better situation. Whenever Jiang Yulan started crying, he would simply tell her to stop. He’d say that crying too much would cause fine lines, and Jiang Yulan would immediately rein herself in.","His mother spent at least three to five million yuan a year on facial treatments.","If she really cried herself into fine lines, she’d have to spend several million more.","Gu Jingchen checked the date. It had been two or three days since he’d gone home, so he nodded and agreed.","“Alright. I’ll head home after work.”","There wasn’t much to do that afternoon, so he drove home early.","The moment he stepped through the door, he sensed that something was off about the atmosphere. His parents’ faces were practically glowing with delight.","He hadn’t seen either of them look this happy in quite some time. What had happened?","He sat down across from them and asked, “Is there some good news?”","“There is! There is indeed good news!”","The smile reached all the way to the corners of Gu Chengye’s eyes. “Old Liang has introduced you to someone. Do you want to take a look?”","Gu Jingchen frowned. “Uncle Liang? Since when have you been in touch with him? Why is he introducing someone to me?”","Could it be Liang Zheng?","Why would he suddenly introduce a woman to him?","Before he could think it through, Gu Chengye had already handed him He Yunzhi’s résumé.","“Take a look first. She’s an exceptionally good girl. Everything about her is excellent—not a single flaw.”","Jiang Yulan nodded along. “She’s a professor, and she’s beautiful too. Her family is respectable as well. You have to go meet her.”","Gu Jingchen stared at the résumé in his hand, his brows drawing together even more. “Where did this résumé come from? Does the young lady know you have it?”","Such a detailed résumé contained personal information. How had it ended up in their hands?","Jiang Yulan smiled gently. “Uncle Liang gave it to your father. He probably got it from her parents. Just look it over properly. Her education, family background, appearance, and career are all excellent...”","Gu Chengye patted his knee. “Your Uncle Liang and I have already arranged it. The two of you will meet sometime this weekend. Make sure you keep your schedule free. Your Uncle Liang will let us know the details.”","Gu Jingchen’s eyes swept seriously over the résumé.","He Yunzhi, thirty-one years old, associate professor at Jiangcheng University.","She was an exceptionally accomplished woman.","Beside him, Gu Chengye began rambling on about the He family. “Yunzhi’s father is the president of Jiangcheng University of Technology. I believe the university is on the eastern side of the city. Once the East District project gets underway, you’ll be seeing him...”","The president of the University of Technology—a vice-ministerial-level official.","What an impressive family background. And her own qualifications were just as formidable.","His gaze passed over the photograph on the résumé. She had a delicate, refined face, and the smile on her lips was gentle yet full of strength.","She was the kind of woman no one could easily refuse.","Gu Jingchen nodded and agreed. “Alright. I’ll keep the weekend free.”"]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: Blind Date Let's Get Married.","paragraphs":["Gu Jingchen didn't have much expectation for this blind date. In He Huanhuan's words, who still goes on blind dates these days? How old - fashioned!","When He Huanhuan invited him to supervise the decoration on the weekend on Friday, he told her, \"I have a blind date tomorrow. I'll come to you after it's over.\"","He Huanhuan was stunned. \"A blind date! Brother, you're going on a blind date? How old - fashioned you are!\"","Gu Jingchen smiled helplessly. \"Uncle Liang introduced her. She's a very nice girl. It's only polite to go.\"","He Huanhuan immediately got excited. \"Let's go with you!\"","She used to be too young, and the people around her were just like her, young and full of energy. Blind dates were never their thing.","She had only heard about blind dates from others. They said it was boring and embarrassing, with two complete strangers sitting dry - faced, taking turns to introduce themselves one by one.","She couldn't even imagine Gu Jingchen introducing himself dryly. She just had to go and see.","Gu Jingchen refused. \"She's coming alone. It's not polite for me to bring a younger sister. She'll feel uncomfortable.\"","Suddenly, a beautiful voice came closer. \"Brother, not one, but two.\"","They pleaded with him, but Gu Jingchen still didn't agree to take them.","The blind date was at half - past ten in the morning. Around ten o'clock, he arrived at the appointed coffee shop.","As soon as he reached the door, he saw two very eye - catching heads sitting in the shop. One was bright yellow, and the other was pink.","His gaze swept across to the opposite side, where Han Mo was holding a coffee cup and gave him a slight wave. Liang Zheng beside him nodded at him, with a teasing smile in his eyes.","He then knew that this blind date today was his doing.","He glanced at Liang Zheng and then at Qi Meili. A look of confusion flashed in his eyes. He wasn't his rival. What was he trying to eliminate?","Walking into the shop, he immediately spotted a woman in the corner who resembled the photo about 80%.","It was He Yunzhi. She had already arrived.","He quickly walked to the corner. \"Sorry, I'm late.\"","He Yunzhi smiled faintly and shook her head. \"I came early.\"","The atmosphere at home was too oppressive, so she came early.","She sized up Gu Jingchen. He was much better - looking than the people she had met before.","He looked gentle, not like someone with a bad temper. He was also in good physical condition. He was about over 1.8 meters tall, with broad shoulders and long legs.","She smiled. Anyway, at least her eyes were in for a treat today.","But unexpectedly, after Gu Jingchen sat down, he handed her his resume. She looked at him in surprise. \"What's this for?\"","Gu Jingchen smiled. \"Uncle Liang gave me your resume. Out of politeness, I thought you should have a look at mine.\"","He Yunzhi's face froze for a moment. \"You said you've read my resume?\"","How could her resume...","A bitter smile crept onto her face. Right, her parents were crazy about her getting married. What's the big deal about giving out her resume?","No wonder the previous blind - date partners knew so much about her life. No wonder they could talk about her past as if they were reciting a well - known poem.","A wave of bitterness welled up in her heart. She felt it was so absurd. When she was a child, her parents were crazy about her studies and grades.","She had to get into the top high - school in the city, get into a 985 university, and win all kinds of competitions. If she didn't, she was a failure, a mess, and her life was over.","But after she got her doctorate and entered the workplace, all that suddenly became unimportant. The only thing she had to do was find a partner and get married.","All her previous efforts and her glory had become mere embellishments. Embellishments on her to match someone who was completely unworthy of her.","She looked down at the resume in her hand. Gu Jingchen, 29, two years younger than her.","A graduate of Stanford University with a master's degree in business administration, he took over his family's company right after graduation...","He was very excellent, much more excellent than all the blind - date partners her parents had introduced to her before.","She closed the resume and handed it back to Gu Jingchen. \"Thank you. I've read it. You're very excellent.\"","Gu Jingchen smiled. \"So are you.\"","Then there was a long silence. She felt so stuffy in her heart and didn't know what to say.","\"You...\"","She wanted to break the silence but found that the person opposite was looking past her, at what was behind her.","She couldn't help but turn around and saw two extremely flamboyant girls.","Flamboyant hair, unrestrained smiles. Their faces were full of brightness.","They seemed to be from a different world from her.","A smile involuntarily curled up on her lips. \"You also think they're so lively, don't you?\"","But then she heard Gu Jingchen say, \"They're my sisters. Sorry. They were curious about my blind date, so they followed me secretly...\"","\"You said they're your sisters?\"","The dead - like eyes of He Yunzhi suddenly lit up a bit. \"Is it okay in your family for your sisters to be like this?\"","So rebellious, so free.","Gu Jingchen looked at the two in the distance. Huanhuan and Meili didn't know what they were talking about and were laughing with their eyes almost shut.","He couldn't help but smile too. \"As long as she's happy.\"","As long as she's happy? Is being happy really enough?","He Yunzhi felt that the emotions that had been pent up in her heart seemed to have suddenly found an outlet. So in other families, being happy was enough.","A bold idea suddenly popped into her mind, so bold that she could hardly hold it back.","Gu Jingchen could tell that she was very interested in Huanhuan and the others, so he asked her with a smile, \"I think they really want to talk to you. Do you mind?\"","She shook her head without hesitation. \"It's okay. Sure.\"","Gu Jingchen waved at the two behind her. The next second, the bright - yellow figure rushed in front of her. \"Hello, Sister Yunzhi! I'm my brother's sister. My name is Huanhuan!\"","\"My name is Meili!\"","The two plopped down beside her. He Huanhuan looked at her with admiration in her eyes. \"Sister, you're a doctor?\"","He Yunzhi nodded. \"Yes.\"","Qi Meili propped her chin up, with pink bubbles in her eyes. \"Sister, you're so amazing! Do you learn things really fast?\"","Then she quickly waved her hand in a fancy way. \"Sister, how about this? Can you learn it at a glance?\"","...","Gu Jingchen smiled and poured water for the two of them. \"Stop making a fuss and have a good chat with her.\"","\"I'm not making a fuss.\"","Qi Meili was really curious. It had taken her several days to learn this.","She was really curious if people who were good at studying could also learn to wave their hands like this easily.","He Yunzhi gently raised her hand and mimicked the action she had just done in a small - scale way. \"Is it like this?\"","\"Yes, yes, yes!\"","The two nodded frantically. \"Sister, you're so amazing! You can learn it just by looking at it once! If you hang out in our spiritual circle, you'll definitely be the big sister!\"","He Yunzhi smiled gently. \"Really? Am I that good at it?\"","He Huanhuan gave her a thumbs - up. \"Super good!\"","She asked He Yunzhi with a big smile. \"Sister, how's your blind date with my big brother going? Is it off? Have you added each other as friends? Do you want to add a friend?\"","Gu Jingchen looked at her embarrassedly. \"Huanhuan is straightforward. She doesn't mean anything...\"","But unexpectedly, the person opposite stared at him. \"Let's get married directly.\"","Gu Jingchen was stunned. \"What did you say?\"","【Dear sisters, I'm taking a one-day leave. I've been having a stomachache all day, so bad that I can't even get out of bed. I managed to scribble a chapter while holding my phone...】"]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: Belated Rebellion","paragraphs":["“I said we should get married. Straight away.”","He Yunzhi looked at him decisively. Her eyes held certainty, reckless abandon, and a sliver of anticipation so faint it was almost impossible to notice.","She wanted to go crazy—completely crazy.","Her parents wanted her to get married, didn’t they? Fine. She would get married. Immediately.","They wanted a good son-in-law? Well, the man in front of her was exactly that.","He was handsome, well-educated, and came from an excellent family.","He was perfect in every way. Surely that would satisfy them!","Even when someone who was usually calm went off the rails, there was still a certain rationality to her considerations. At the very least, he was good-looking, well-born, highly educated, and appeared gentle and polite.","She had assumed Gu Jingchen would think she was insane. Instead, he merely looked at her and asked, “Are you sure?”","She nodded firmly. “I’m sure.”","A wild, uninhibited exhilaration began surging madly from the depths of her heart. She was certain she wanted to do this.","“All right.”","Gu Jingchen put away the résumé and stood up. “Let’s go.”","This time, it was He Yunzhi’s turn to stare at him in shock. “Go where? What are we doing?”","Gu Jingchen smiled gently. “Aren’t we getting married? We’ll buy wedding rings, then get our marriage license. You brought your ID card, right?”","He Yunzhi nodded blankly. “I did.”","Then she shook her head. “But today’s Saturday. The Civil Affairs Bureau is closed.”","“That’s not a problem.”","He tapped his phone and dialed a number. Not far away, Liang Zheng’s phone immediately began to ring.","When Liang Zheng saw the name on his screen, he turned around in surprise and glanced at him. What was he up to?","Still, he answered. Gu Jingchen’s voice came through, carrying an annoyingly smug lilt. “We’re going to get our marriage license in a little while. You can take care of it, right?”","“You two? Getting married?”","Liang Zheng raised his brows in astonishment. Although he had carefully matched the two of them, wasn’t this moving a little too fast?","Gu Jingchen glanced at Meili, then asked, “Just tell me whether you can handle it.”","“...I can.”","For Young Master Liang, a minor matter like this only required one phone call.","After hanging up, he nodded toward Gu Jingchen with an unpleasant expression.","He had wanted to eliminate all potential rivals, but seeing how smoothly everything was going still made him unhappy.","After all, he and Qi Meili had kissed just moments ago, only for her to delete him moments later...","If Han Mo could hear his thoughts, he would have wiped away tears of sorrow. He hadn’t even managed to kiss her on the lips!","But He Huanhuan’s situation was special. He simply couldn’t convince himself that, because her body was already twenty, they could take things any further.","She was, after all, only eighteen. That was truly very young.","Sometimes Han Mo felt that when he took her and Qi Meili out, he looked less like their companion and more like an older relative taking two children outside. Whenever they brought up some newfangled topic, he couldn’t understand a word of it.","If he tried to force his way into the conversation, he always said something wrong. He constantly felt that growing older meant everything he did became painfully awkward.","For example, right now, they were following Gu Jingchen and He Yunzhi to buy wedding rings.","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili were leaning over the counter, choosing with utmost seriousness. He Huanhuan turned to him and asked, “Do you think the bow-shaped one looks good?”","He nodded. “The smaller one looks better.”","The large one seemed a little too flashy.","The moment he finished speaking, the two girls suddenly covered their mouths and giggled.","He was even more confused. “Then we’ll get the bigger one? More eye-catching?”","The two of them burst into louder laughter. He was genuinely baffled. “Then should I buy both for you?”","He Huanhuan’s eyes curved with laughter. “Meili and I just made a bet. I said that if I didn’t say anything, you’d help me buy both of them. Meili didn’t believe me.”","She looked at him, her eyes full of triumphant certainty. “I won! Hahaha!”","He couldn’t help laughing along. “What’s the prize?”","He Huanhuan swiftly leaned close to his ear and announced in a voice loud enough for everyone to hear, “For the next month, you’re not allowed to kiss Liang Zheng!”","Young Master Liang, who had been dragged into the crossfire for no reason: ...","Cancel the contest. Immediately. Right now.","He Yunzhi didn’t have much of an opinion about the wedding ring. What she was really looking forward to was her parents’ reaction after they got the marriage license.","The saleswoman did her best to make a recommendation. “Miss, your fingers are long and slender. Why not try this pear-shaped diamond? It would really complement your—”","But He Yunzhi merely shook her head. “They all look about the same. Just pick one.”","Gu Jingchen could tell that her mind was elsewhere, so he nodded at the saleswoman. “Please choose a larger one that suits her.”","The saleswoman’s eyes lit up instantly. “Of course, no trouble at all...”","Naturally, it wasn’t any trouble. What was that saying again? The bigger the waves, the more expensive the fish!","No, wait—the bigger the diamond, the higher the commission!","She immediately selected an even larger pear-shaped diamond and held it out for them to see. “What do you think of this one?”","Money had to be made, but her sense of aesthetics still had to be upheld.","He Yunzhi’s fingers were long and slender, and the pear-shaped diamond made them look even more delicate.","He Yunzhi glanced at the ring and couldn’t help frowning. “Isn’t it a little too big?”","It seemed rather extravagant.","The saleswoman’s face stiffened for a second. Oh no, she had been too greedy.","Gu Jingchen, however, shook his head with a smile. “There’s nothing wrong with a larger wedding ring. If you like smaller ones, I’ll buy you a few more later.”","He Huanhuan nodded in agreement from the side. “Bigger is better. It’ll be more noticeable. People will be able to see it from far away!”","He Yunzhi paused.","That was true. A bigger ring would be more noticeable. A bigger ring would be more brazen.","Wasn’t that exactly what she wanted?","She unconsciously tightened her fist, then held out her hand. “This one, then. Put it on for me.”","She was going to wear this ring to get their marriage license, and wear it home afterward.","She was even a little impatient to see her parents’ reactions—shock, anger, panic...","She was looking forward to every bit of it.","After buying the ring, they drove to the Civil Affairs Bureau.","At the back entrance stood Gao Ming, an old acquaintance of Liang Zheng’s. Beside him was a woman in her forties, her face pulled into a deep scowl. She looked extremely displeased.","No one was happy about being called in to work overtime on a weekend.","Gao Ming nudged her with his elbow. “Don’t look so miserable. Smile a little.”","The woman’s expression darkened further. “Secretary, I can’t smile.”","It was a rare weekend, and an even rarer occasion when her husband had been thoughtful enough to take her to the cinema. Then she had been summoned here. How could she possibly smile?","“You...”","Gao Ming was just about to lecture her when, from the corner of his eye, he spotted several cars approaching. He hurriedly pulled her forward to greet them.","“Oh, Zheng, you’re here! Was the traffic bad? Who’s getting married? You even had to trouble yourself by calling me...”","The woman’s obsequious attitude stirred a little curiosity in her. Exactly who had enough influence to make their secretary treat them like this?","Before she could investigate further, a thick red envelope was held out in front of her. It was substantial—and utterly mesmerizing.","Her eyes went wide. “Th-this...”","Gu Jingchen extended the envelope toward her. “Sorry to make you work overtime on your day off. Just a little wedding cheer. Please accept it.”","The woman’s eyes shone. She whipped around to look at Gao Ming. “Secretary, what do you think...?”","Gao Ming smiled and nodded. “Take it. It’s fine.”","For a minor matter like this, it couldn’t be considered a bribe.","The woman hesitated. “Secretary, I don’t dare.”","After thinking it over, she added, “You hold on to it for me.”","She wanted the money, but she wasn’t willing to take on the risk.","Gao Ming could only sigh helplessly. He accepted the red envelope, then handed it back to her. “Take it.”","The woman’s eyes darted toward the corner. “Secretary, go over there and give it to me.”","There were no surveillance cameras there. It would be safer.","Gao Ming was speechless. “The surveillance cameras at the back entrance aren’t on Saturdays!”","Big Sis nodded. “Mm-hmm. Go over there and give it to them, give it to them...”","It absolutely has to be foolproof!","[Girls, I’m feeling a bit better today, so here’s the update I owed you. Thank you for your concern, and thank you to Sister Yierlin for the Great God endorsement, to Sister “I’ll Definitely Get Rich” for the Xiu’er gift, and to Sister Lu Jie from Dimen Dao for the character summon. Thank you for all your gifts, everyone. I’m going back to write tomorrow’s chapter now!]"]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: How About Getting Married While We're at It","paragraphs":["The marriage registration process was incredibly fast. Before the clerk stamped the final seal, Gu Jingchen gave He Yunzhi one last chance to back out.","“Are you sure you want to marry me?” he asked.","He Yunzhi was an only child. Her father was the president of a university of technology and a deputy ministerial-level official.","In their marriage, he was unquestionably the one benefiting more.","With all the advantages she brought to the table, there was absolutely nothing for him to hesitate over.","He Yunzhi turned to him. “What about you? Are you sure?”","Sure you want to go crazy with me?","Gu Jingchen smiled. “I think I’m very sure.”","After all, she was quite beautiful.","He Yunzhi nodded and said to the clerk, “Go ahead and stamp it. We’ve made up our minds.”","The clerk wasted no time and stamped the documents at once, not giving them another chance to reconsider.","She had to make sure they understood that her red envelope hadn’t been accepted for nothing!","The bright-red marriage certificates were handed to them. He Yunzhi was so excited that she had no idea what to do next.","She had to... she had to...","Then she heard He Huanhuan beside her say, “You have to post this on WeChat Moments!”","Right!","She had to post it—on a post visible only to her parents, so they could see it right away!","Her eyes gleaming, she turned to Gu Jingchen. “Let’s take a picture together and post it.”","He Huanhuan eagerly raised her hand. “I’ll take it for you!”","He Yunzhi had originally intended to take a picture of the marriage certificates alone, but after hearing that, she suddenly changed her mind.","Following He Huanhuan’s instructions, she and Gu Jingchen stood in the designated photo area. Holding their marriage certificates, they faced the camera and wore what she thought was a defiant smile.","Completely unaware of the situation, He Huanhuan said, “Yes! Keep smiling like that! You look gorgeous!”","She pressed the shutter, capturing the brightest smile He Yunzhi had ever worn.","He Yunzhi practically snatched the phone away, quickly choosing the audience for the post and getting ready to publish it.","Caption: Sometimes, you just have to let yourself go.","One second before she tapped “Post,” Gu Jingchen suddenly said, “Why don’t you ask Huanhuan what kind of caption she would use?”","He Yunzhi abruptly looked up at him. Did he know what he was doing?","Gu Jingchen still wore that smiling expression. “When it comes to letting loose, isn’t someone who’s truly shameless better at it?”","Her heart gave a sudden tremor.","He really did know what he was doing.","He knew he wanted to let loose—and was he accepting that side of himself, too?","What Gu Jingchen wanted to say was that this tiny bit of recklessness was really nothing in his family.","After all, his family had a punk little sister who changed her explosively colorful hairstyle every other day, a would-be kept man whose sole ambition was to marry a rich woman, and someone who had taken his recklessness so far that he’d ended up behind a sewing machine in prison...","Compared with them, what did this little act of rebellion from He Yunzhi amount to?","But He Yunzhi didn’t know that. To her, everything she had done today had been outrageously bold.","That included this caption.","He Huanhuan glanced at it. “What is this supposed to be? Why did you post such a lame caption, Sister?”","“Lame? Then what kind of caption would count as letting loose?”","He Huanhuan spread her hands and began dictating. “We met! We fell in love! We made it legal!”","Meili immediately chimed in, “I’m into him because he’s young! I’m into him because he’s in great shape!”","He Huanhuan continued, “I’m obsessed! I love him to death! He’s the only one for me!”","Meili went all out. “We’ll be sleeping under the same blanket from now on. I’ll be able to turn around and kiss him whenever I want.”","“...”","He Yunzhi stared at them. “Isn’t that a little too shameless?”","The sisters clearly thought this was nothing. They hadn’t even put any real thought into it.","He Huanhuan asked, “Aren’t you trying to let loose? Why are you still afraid of going too far?”","He Yunzhi was speechless. There was such a huge gap between her and the two of them that she could barely keep up.","And yet, she couldn’t stop herself from feeling tempted. After pressing the delete key several times, she typed out a new line.","[We met, fell in love, and made it legal.]","She didn’t know why, but when she typed out essentially the same words, they instantly seemed much more restrained.","She steeled herself and tapped “Post,” then waited for the judgment to arrive.","She had already done something crazy. If she couldn’t face the consequences, then the rest of her life would remain under someone else’s control forever.","A video call came through almost immediately. She took a deep breath and answered.","Her father appeared on-screen, jumping with rage. “He Yunzhi! What the hell did you post on WeChat Moments? Stop playing with AI—it’s bad for your brain. Delete it!”","He Yunzhi held up her marriage certificate. “Dad, it’s not AI. I’m married.”","Her father froze. “What did you say? What have you done? Weren’t you going on a blind date today? You...”","He Yunzhi nodded and cut him off. “Yes. It went well, so we registered our marriage.”","The voice on the other end instantly rose several octaves. “What kind of nonsense are you talking about? Do you even know what you’re doing?”","He Yunzhi laughed recklessly. “Of course I do. Didn’t you two go crazy insisting that I get married? I did. So why are you upset?”","Before her father could explode again, He Huanhuan and Qi Meili leaned into the frame and greeted him.","“Hello, Uncle!”","Her father fell silent at once.","“This, this...”","His eyes hurt. His head hurt, too. It felt as though he’d just been assaulted.","Stammering, he asked, “This... they’re...?”","A mischievous glint flashed through He Yunzhi’s eyes. “My sister-in-law. She’s the Gu family’s heiress.”","Her father’s vision went black, and he nearly fainted.","What kind of family had Old Liang introduced to Yunzhi? How could they have raised such bizarre daughters?","Terrifying! Absolutely terrifying!","He didn’t even dare look at them for long. He hurriedly told He Yunzhi, “Come home! Right now!”","Then he hung up the video call in an instant, afraid that one more glance would make his heart seize.","He Huanhuan was puzzled. “Sister Yunzhi, your dad is so rude.”","She had greeted him, but he hadn’t even replied.","He Yunzhi couldn’t help laughing. “Yes, he’s always been rude. Ha-ha...”","He Huanhuan shook her head. “Don’t be sad, Sister. You don’t get to choose your parents. Just don’t pay them too much attention. We should focus on living our own lives.”","Yes. They only needed to live their own lives.","How had she failed to understand such a simple truth all these years?","He Yunzhi looked at He Huanhuan and nodded solemnly. “I know. I will.”","With that, she prepared to drive home. She had a grand gift to deliver to her parents.","As he watched her leave, He Huanhuan glanced at the Civil Affairs Bureau behind them and asked Han Mo, “Since we’re already here, should we get married while we’re at it?”","Han Mo gave her a helpless look. “You’re not old enough yet.”","He Huanhuan grinned mischievously. “My ID says I’m old enough~”","According to the age on her ID card, she had already turned twenty.","Han Mo helplessly pulled her toward the car. “Stop teasing me. I promised to wait two years for you, and I won’t go back on my word.”","He Huanhuan couldn’t help feeling a little happy, so she leaned closer and asked, “It’s only two years. Whether we wait with a marriage certificate or without one, we’re still waiting...”","Han Mo pushed open the car door at once. “Then let’s go get the certificate now.”","“Just drive!”"]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: Today Doesn't Count","paragraphs":["Inside Liang Zheng’s car, the atmosphere was inexplicably tense.","Meili glanced at him, then glanced at him again, but he merely drove with a stern expression, saying nothing.","Meili was puzzled. “Are you upset?”","Liang Zheng frowned at her. “Why would you use something as serious as feelings for a bet?”","Meili suddenly understood. “You want to kiss me?”","Liang Zheng pulled the car over and looked at her with utmost seriousness. “This isn’t about kissing. It’s about your attitude...”","Before he could finish, a flash of pink collided with him. Soft lips quickly pressed against his, then darted away.","His heart instantly softened. Suddenly, whatever attitude he was supposed to have no longer seemed important.","He cleared his throat. “Didn’t we agree that if you lost the bet, you wouldn’t kiss me for a month?”","Meili waved her hand dismissively. “Today doesn’t count.”","His dark brows lifted at once. “Really?”","Meili nodded unconcernedly. “Of course. We said the next month, didn’t we? Today isn’t part of it—mmph...”","After quite some time, Meili finally pushed him away. “We agreed on one kiss. Why are you acting like you’re addicted to it?”","His eyes were filled with undisguised amusement. “When did I agree to that? How come I don’t remember?”","He stared steadily at Meili. “Gu Jingchen got his marriage license.”","Meili rolled her eyes. “I was there, okay?”","She had been there for the whole thing, all right?","His gaze remained fixed on her. “Don’t you think they rushed into it a little?”","Meili shrugged indifferently. “Some people move quickly, and some take their time. Everyone has their own pace.”","“What about you? What’s your pace?”","Meili froze. Was he... asking for a relationship status?","The alarm bells in her head immediately began ringing. Her expression turned serious. “What exactly do you mean?”","Seeing her reaction, Liang Zheng smiled helplessly. “I just want to know your pace so I can keep up with you, isn’t that all?”","He reached out and took her hand, his expression utterly earnest. “I’m serious about you, so you have to give me a chance to get to know you, okay?”","She instinctively wanted to refuse, but his gaze was too intent, fixed tightly on her.","She couldn’t bring herself to say those words. “But how am I supposed to give you that chance? I don’t even know what I want...”","She didn’t even know what she wanted herself. How could she explain it to him and make him understand?","His grip tightened around her hand. Liang Zheng’s voice carried a faint, almost imperceptible coaxing quality. “You’ll figure it out. As long as we spend more time together, we’ll know, won’t we?”","Meili gazed at his handsome profile and nodded absently. “Yes...”","That handsome profile turned slightly toward her. “Then give me a little time alone with you. Is that okay?”","“Okay...”","“Then let’s not go back just yet. How about we get something to eat?”","“Okay...”","By the time He Huanhuan and the others realized Liang Zheng’s car hadn’t followed them, the two of them were already seated in a private dining room!","He Huanhuan listened to Qi Meili’s guilty voice over the phone and was utterly speechless. “He seduced you, and you didn’t even know to close your eyes? You idiot!”","Qi Meili insisted that she couldn’t close her eyes. If she did, he would surely take advantage of the opportunity to kiss her several more times.","Honestly, there was no point trying to explain anything to this kindergarten-level idiot.","He Huanhuan hung up angrily. “Fine, fine. You two eat. We’re heading back first!”","She glanced at the car ahead, then at Han Mo. “Do you think Sister Yunzhi is going to get yelled at when she gets home?”","She had a feeling that someone as highly educated as He Yunzhi must have a very strict family.","A sudden marriage would be considered completely outrageous in a family like that, wouldn’t it?","Han Mo nodded without hesitation. “She definitely will.”","He Huanhuan couldn’t help feeling eager. “Then do you think we should go save her?”","They could descend like divine heroes just as He Yunzhi was being besieged by her parents and rescue her.","How cool would that be!","Following her gaze toward the car ahead, Han Mo said, “That’s their family matter. We can’t interfere casually, can we?”","He Huanhuan couldn’t help worrying. “I feel like Sister Yunzhi has such weak combat skills. What if she can’t win an argument with her parents?”","He Yunzhi clearly looked like the obedient sort who had listened to her parents ever since she was young. Surely she wouldn’t be able to withstand their attacks.","Han Mo smiled and shook his head. “I think she can handle it.”","If she couldn’t, she would never have dared to get married on a whim.","Some people’s tempers didn’t reveal themselves on the surface. They accumulated their resentment quietly, little by little, until it reached the limit. Then they would erupt in one enormous, ruthless display that left everyone stunned.","That was the kind of person Han Mo believed He Yunzhi to be.","As it turned out, He Yunzhi really was that kind of person.","On the way home, she was in an exceptionally good mood—almost exhilarated.","The anticipation in her heart urged her to hurry home, to face everything as soon as possible.","She couldn’t wait to shatter that false sense of peace.","When she pushed open the door, her parents were sitting on the sofa exactly as she had expected, their expressions solemn as they waited for her to return.","They were waiting to pass judgment on her.","She smiled at them. “Why do you both look so serious? What happened?”","He Jingyao slapped his thigh hard. “Is what you posted on your social media real or fake?”","She slowly sat down on the smaller sofa. “Of course it’s real. Weren’t you always hoping I’d get married? Well, I got married today.”","She took out the marriage certificate, and He Jingyao quickly grabbed it and opened it.","The bright red seal from the civil affairs bureau flashed before his eyes. “No, no, this can’t be right. Today is Saturday. How could you get your marriage license?”","The civil affairs bureau wasn’t open on Saturdays!","He Yunzhi’s smile grew even wider. “Dad, are you joking? You’re the president of the Institute of Technology. How could you not know how easy this is? It only takes one phone call, doesn’t it?”","“Nonsense!”","He Jingyao was furious. “You’re abusing your authority! This is dereliction of duty!”","He Yunzhi nodded. “Then call the police and have us arrested.”","“You!”","He Jingyao’s face flushed red with anger. “Yunzhi, have you lost your mind? No matter how angry you were with your mother and me, you couldn’t do something like this!”","He Yunzhi smiled. “Really? You think I’ve lost my mind too? What about before? Every time you arranged a blind date, I told you I didn’t like those men. Why did you force me to keep seeing them? I told you they weren’t right for me. Why wouldn’t you listen?”","If she had felt strongly uncomfortable around someone the very first time they met, what was the point of continuing to see him?","If a man was so ugly she could barely look at him, would spending more time with him somehow make him less ugly?","If he was half a head shorter than her, would continuing to see him make him grow taller?","She had said no, no, and no. Why wouldn’t they listen to her and insist on forcing her to keep seeing those men?","They thought all those men, ugly enough to make her eyes hurt, were worth getting to know.","Well, Gu Jingchen was worth marrying.","At least he was handsome, tall, highly educated, and came from a wealthy family.","“What do you need so much money for?”","He Jingyao couldn’t understand. “Is the family short of money for you? Have we ever deprived you of anything? You’re our only daughter. We’ve raised you with all our hearts. When have we ever treated you unfairly?”","He Yunzhi didn’t answer. She simply raised her right hand.","A huge diamond ring gleamed conspicuously on her ring finger.","He Jingyao’s expression changed instantly. “Why did you buy such a huge diamond ring? It makes you look like a nouveau riche. Take it off. People will laugh at you!”","He Yunzhi held her hand firmly before her chest. “I’m not taking it off. I like it, and I’m going to wear it.”"]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: The Evil Granny","paragraphs":["He Jingyao shot to his feet, furious. “What will people think of our family if you go around like this? Anyone who didn’t know better would think I’d taken a bribe! Take it off!”","“And this marriage certificate!”","He flung the certificate at He Yunzhi’s feet. “A certificate obtained on a non-working day isn’t legal! I refuse to recognize it! Go cancel it immediately! If you wait too long, the only thing you’ll be able to get is a divorce certificate. Then you’ll be a divorcee—who would want you after that?”","A mocking smile tugged at the corners of He Yunzhi’s lips. A divorcee, unwanted. Once again, she had been reduced to an object.","A commodity to be appraised and sold, expected to maintain her value.","She had to be pure, have an impeccable past, be obedient, be sensible...","She bent down, picked up the marriage certificate, brushed it clean, and tucked it into her bag. “Whether you acknowledge it or not, I’m already married. I’ve already bought the wedding ring, and I’ve chosen this man. I’m not changing my mind.”","She rose and headed toward her room. “He’ll come to the house tomorrow to pick me up so we can move out together. I’m going to pack my things.”","“You dare!”","He Jingyao chased after her in a fury and grabbed her arm. “Have you lost your mind? You’ve only met him once! How much do you know about him? Do you even know what kind of person he is? Do you know what kind of family he comes from? You’re planning to spend the rest of your life with him?”","She stared steadily at He Jingyao. “Wasn’t it you who told me to meet him? Didn’t you know what his family was like? Who his parents were, and what kind of person he was? Shouldn’t you have investigated all that beforehand? You introduced him to me without knowing anything. So if something goes wrong, it’ll be your responsibility.”","Her gaze pierced He Jingyao’s heart like a knife.","“From now on, if my marriage brings me any unhappiness, it will all be your responsibility.”","Each word was heavy, pounding down on He Jingyao.","“Yunzhi, apologize to your father.”","Weng Meijuan rose from the sofa and looked at her with an intensely oppressive stare. “Apologize to your father. Apologize for being disobedient.”","“I’m sorry.”","He Yunzhi obediently apologized. For a brief second, the couple’s expressions softened—only for her to continue, “I’m sorry I waited so long to stop being obedient. That’s why it’s so hard for you to accept. I’ll be more careful from now on.”","Weng Meijuan’s face darkened to the extreme. “You really intend to marry that Gu... whoever he is?”","He Yunzhi smiled. “It’s not that I intend to. I already married him. Tomorrow, I’m moving in with him.”","“So you’re not going to listen to your mother anymore?”","“Mom, I have a husband now. I’m supposed to listen to my husband, right?”","He Yunzhi smiled at Weng Meijuan. “Wasn’t that what you taught me? That a woman should put her husband first in marriage and obey him? Now that I’m married, I have to listen to him. I can’t listen to you anymore, Mom.”","Weng Meijuan’s face turned livid. “Fine. Have him come here right now. I want to see what kind of man has bewitched my daughter into losing her mind.”","“You’ll see him tomorrow.”","But Weng Meijuan refused to let it go. “Call him over now. What? Does he know he’s done something absurd and doesn’t dare show his face?”","Looking at her parents’ accusatory expressions, He Yunzhi suddenly changed her mind.","She took out her phone and called Gu Jingchen. “My parents want to meet you. Come over to my house.”","After thinking for a moment, she added, “Bring Huanhuan too.”","Since they wanted to meet them, they might as well meet them properly.","Besides, she had supposedly lost her mind, hadn’t she?","Then she would let her outrageous sister-in-law give her old-fashioned parents a truly unforgettable shock.","Gu Jingchen and the others arrived incredibly quickly—so quickly that He Yunzhi wondered whether they had already been waiting downstairs.","Less than ten minutes after she hung up, the doorbell rang.","She went to open the door in surprise. Gu Jingchen stood outside holding two exquisitely decorated gift boxes. “We came on short notice, so I didn’t know what your parents liked. I picked up a couple of things at random. I hope they’re appropriate.”","He was certainly taking the initiative. They hadn’t even met him yet, and he was already calling them Mom and Dad.","He Yunzhi glanced down at the gift boxes. Their value was obvious at a glance.","She shook her head. “They’re perfectly appropriate.”","She stepped aside to let him in, and her parents’ expressions changed almost instantly.","“This is Little Gu?”","Gu Jingchen smiled and strode forward, setting down the gifts. “Mom, Dad, I’m sorry for coming on such short notice. I didn’t know what you liked, so I picked up a couple of things at random. I hope you won’t mind.”","A smile quickly spread across Weng Meijuan’s face. “Oh, you’re such a thoughtful boy. It’s the thought that counts.”","He Jingyao’s attitude softened as well. Smiling, he asked, “Was traffic bad? Come in, come in...”","...","He Yunzhi stood by the doorway, feeling that the whole situation was absurd.","Where had all the interrogation gone? Where were the harsh questions and attempts to make things difficult?","“Sister Yunzhi, why are you standing at the door? Come on in!”","He Huanhuan grabbed her hand and pulled her inside.","The moment they saw He Huanhuan, He Jingyao and Weng Meijuan’s eyes lit up. Their gazes shifted toward her and became impossible to pull away.","Weng Meijuan asked blankly, “And this is?”","Gu Jingchen smiled. “This is my younger sister, Huanhuan.”","Weng Meijuan vaguely remembered something about the Gu family. When Old Liang had introduced He Yunzhi to potential partners, he seemed to have mentioned it in passing.","She didn’t need to guess. This Huanhuan was probably the child who had been switched at birth.","She frowned. “Why is your hair dyed such a bright yellow?”","He Huanhuan grinned. “Auntie, so people can see me! Isn’t yellow an eye-catching color?”","Weng Meijuan’s frown deepened. “What does a young girl need to stand out so much for? Girls should be gentle and refined, not so attention-seeking...”","He Huanhuan looked puzzled. “Auntie, am I not gentle and refined?”","Did being eye-catching and being gentle conflict? Of course not!","She was simply gentle in a very eye-catching way.","Weng Meijuan said, “That still doesn’t mean you should dye your hair such an outrageous color. It makes you look like a bad girl.”","He Huanhuan smiled. “So girls with yellow hair aren’t good girls? What exactly makes someone a good girl? Does black hair automatically make you a good girl? If someone was born with yellow hair and dyed it black, would she still be a good girl?”","Weng Meijuan’s expression shifted. “You—you’re just being argumentative. Dyeing your hair is wrong in the first place...”","He Huanhuan continued smiling sweetly. “I really don’t understand. What about prematurely gray hair? Does that mean someone’s born bad? And if they dye it black, does that make them even worse?”","“You—you...”","Weng Meijuan was rendered speechless by the barrage of questions.","But He Huanhuan had no intention of letting her off. She pressed on, “Then what does it mean when an old lady dyes her hair? An evil old granny? Auntie, will you dye your hair when you’re old? Will you turn into an evil old granny?”","...","“Yunzhi!”","Weng Meijuan shouted at He Yunzhi in exasperation, pointedly ignoring Gu Jingchen.","He Yunzhi smiled unhurriedly. “Mom, does getting married on a whim make someone a bad girl?”","He Huanhuan shook her head. “No, that just makes her an impulsive girl. I’ll take you to dye your hair sometime, and you can be an impulsive bad girl for once.”","He Yunzhi nodded seriously. “All right.”","He Jingyao glared and shot to his feet. “You dare!”","How absurd!","How outrageous!","He had no idea that a rebellious girl like He Huanhuan was completely fearless when challenged. With a whoosh, she pulled eighteen tubes of brightly colored hair dye from her backpack.","“Let’s see whether I dare!”"]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: Impulsive Bad Girl","paragraphs":["She quickly asked He Yunzhi, \"Sister, what's your favorite color?\"","He Yunzhi was momentarily distracted and subconsciously replied, \"Purple, I guess?\"","He Huanhuan clapped her hands and said, \"Purple is great. Which old guy said that purple has a unique charm? It doesn't matter. Anyway, purple has charm!\"","Then, with lightning speed, she opened a tube of hair dye and quickly smeared it on the tips of He Yunzhi's hair.","She moved so fast that no one had time to react, and the tips of He Yunzhi's hair were all dyed a gentle shade of purple.","He Jingyao was furious. \"What are you doing? Yunzhi is an associate professor. She's supposed to teach at school! How can this be proper?\"","He Yunzhi glanced at the dyed tips of her hair on her shoulder, and her eyes softened instantly. \"It's fine. It looks nice. My students will like it.\"","She taught college students, not old scholars. Dyeing the tips of her hair was no big deal, right?","Gu Jingchen looked carefully at her hair and nodded in agreement. \"You can dye it a little higher. The color will be more harmonious.\"","\"Little Gu!\"","He Jingyao looked at Gu Jingchen with a displeased expression. \"Why are you joining in this nonsense?\"","His first impression of Gu Jingchen wasn't bad. Gu Jingchen had a handsome appearance, and his attitude when he greeted them at the door was very humble. He didn't seem like a dissolute person.","But how could he encourage Yunzhi to dye her hair? Wasn't that just nonsense!","Gu Jingchen smiled politely. \"Dad, it's just dyeing the tips of the hair. It's nothing. Nowadays, young people are very lively. Dyeing hair can help her get closer to her students. It's not a bad thing.\"","\"But it looks so ugly...\"","He was about to continue lecturing, but Gu Jingchen didn't give him the chance.","He handed his resume to He Jingyao and his wife. \"Mom and Dad, this is my personal resume. I'd like you to take a look.\"","He Jingyao glanced at the resume and was immediately shocked by his educational background. \"You graduated from Stanford?\"","Gu Jingchen nodded. \"Yes.\"","He Jingyao asked again, \"And you took over your family's company after graduation?\"","Gu Jingchen still nodded. \"Yes.\"","He Jingyao looked at him disapprovingly. \"You should focus on academia. Mundane things like managing a company should be left to others...\"","He Huanhuan couldn't help but interrupt and ask him, \"To whom?\"","He Jingyao frowned unhappily. \"Doesn't Jingchen have a younger brother?\"","He Huanhuan laughed. \"My second brother only knows how to spend money. Do you want our family to go bankrupt?\"","If they let Gu Jinghan manage the company, before she was even found, their whole family would be begging at her door.","One person would need a handful of rice. She'd have to give out five handfuls of rice to send them away.","Somewhere in the hotel, working hard, Gu Jinghan suddenly sneezed three times. \"Who's thinking about me so much?\"","After sneezing, he looked at the ledger again. \"Damn it! Was this the page I was looking at? It doesn't seem right.\"","The page he was looking at was the reimbursement form for the prepaid uniforms of the hotel submitted by the manager, Cheng Huaiyu.","The form clearly stated that each set of uniforms cost 580 yuan.","His brows furrowed involuntarily, and he immediately called Cheng Huaiyu. \"I've seen the hotel uniform reimbursement form.\"","Cheng Huaiyu's heart skipped a beat. \"What's wrong?\"","Did he notice that he was taking kickbacks?","Gu Jinghan was disgusted. \"Can you order some more high - class clothes? Is 580 yuan worth for a set of clothes? We're a high - class hotel. Can we wear clothes that cost less than a thousand yuan?\"","Cheng Huaiyu: ... It was he who wasn't greedy enough.","He immediately raised his hand and promised, \"Okay, boss. I'll order a batch of expensive ones right away!\"","\"Hurry up! I'm not short of money, you know?\"","\"Got it!\"","What He Huanhuan said was really not an exaggeration.","If the company was handed over to him, it would go bankrupt in a month or two.","He was too generous.","He Huanhuan's straightforward words left He Jingyao speechless.","Gu Jingchen was already 29 years old and had taken over the company for several years. It was impossible for him to continue his studies.","He could only sigh helplessly. \"What a pity. It's really a pity.\"","No one knew what he was pitying. He Huanhuan then turned to He Yunzhi and said, \"Sister, aren't you going to move? Let me help you pack your things.\"","He Yunzhi nodded. \"Okay.\"","She thought her parents would be angry, but unexpectedly, they didn't say a word to stop her.","The two of them looked at the resume in their hands and became more and more satisfied.","He was young, so he was in good health.","Good health was important for having children.","He Yunzhi was already 31 years old. If she didn't have a child soon, she would be an advanced - age mother.","Moving out was a good thing. It would be better for the young couple to live together to develop their relationship and have children.","He Yunzhi never expected that after just one glance, her parents would accept Gu Jingchen.","All those words about getting along and getting to know each other didn't count after they saw that excellent resume.","They also didn't condemn her for her impulsive elopement.","The outburst she had accumulated for a long time seemed like a joke.","She was a bit dazed as she took He Huanhuan back to the room, packed her things, and then went out with them.","Her parents even stood at the door to see her off, as if there had never been any arguments between them.","It was as if she and Gu Jingchen had been married for a long time, and today they were just visiting her parents' home.","Standing downstairs, she was a bit confused. \"How could this happen?\"","She thought there would be a big argument, that her parents would refuse to let her move out at all costs and scold her for being indecent, saying that she couldn't live with a man before the wedding...","She had imagined many scenarios, all kinds of quarrels and outbursts, but definitely not the current calmness.","She couldn't help asking again, \"How could this happen?\"","Gu Jingchen carried the luggage and led her to the car. \"Because I promised your parents that I would give you a perfect wedding.\"","\"So they just accepted it?\"","Gu Jingchen nodded. \"Yes.\"","Just like that, they accepted and handed their daughter over to him.","He lowered his head and looked at He Yunzhi. \"Yunzhi, I know what you want. But being unrestrained doesn't necessarily mean throwing a tantrum at home. Completely breaking free from your parents' control is also a form of being unrestrained.\"","\"You're completely free now, Yunzhi.\"","She didn't have to live with her parents anymore and didn't have to care about their thoughts.","She could really live unrestrainedly. He could handle her parents.","They were just old - fashioned people. Compared with the overbearing and selfish Old Mr. Gu, they were much easier to deal with.","He Yunzhi was a bit slow to react. \"But this wasn't what I originally thought. I thought I'd have a big fight with them, a fight that everyone would know about...\"","\"It's not necessary.\"","Gu Jingchen smiled at her. \"What you want is to live unrestrainedly, not to show off your unrestraint to others, right?\"","He Yunzhi nodded. \"Yes.\"","\"Then live a good life. Try to avoid those exhausting quarrels. If you can't avoid them, just leave them to me.\"","He still had a smiling face, and that smile carried endless strength, as if he could lift her up at any time. \"You've got to let me be of some use.\"","He Yunzhi nodded a bit nervously. \"Okay.\"","The car drove towards the city center. \"I've already prepared a house. Let's go and have a look together.\"","The sense of being married suddenly hit He Yunzhi, and she became even more nervous. \"Now?\"","Gu Jingchen looked at her, and the smile in his eyes was irresistible. \"Yunzhi, we're a married couple. A couple should live together. You know that, right?\"","A married couple needs to have a life together, and they also need to have an intimate marital life."]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: Gu Jingchen, Go to Sleep","paragraphs":["The car headed steadily toward the city center, toward their new home.","The new home Gu Jingchen had prepared for the two of them was a small, detached house in the heart of the city, tucked away from the bustle.","The landscaping throughout the complex was beautiful. As soon as the car drove in, the noise of the outside world was quickly shut out, leaving only a lush sea of greenery.","Their house stood deep inside the neighborhood, some distance from the road.","After parking, he opened her door with a faint smile playing at the corners of his lips. “Come on, let’s take a look at our new home.”","He had bought the house several years ago. Whenever work projects ran late, he would come here to rest instead of going home and disturbing his parents.","The house was only a little over eighty square meters on the first floor, which contained nothing but a spacious living room, a kitchen, and a bathroom.","His room—no, their room—was on the second floor.","Without giving He Yunzhi any chance to object, he naturally carried all her things upstairs and put them in the bedroom.","He Yunzhi did not have much. Her parents had always been strict with her, and most of her clothes were simple basics in black, white, and gray. They took up only a tiny portion of the wardrobe.","Gu Jingchen glanced at her clothes. “Let’s go shopping for some clothes tomorrow. Buy whatever you want to wear.”","Her heart skipped a beat, and she nodded seriously. “Okay.”","By the time they finished putting everything away, it was already getting late. Han Mo drove He Huanhuan away, leaving the two of them alone.","The entire house instantly felt empty, with only the two of them left inside. He Yunzhi felt a little uncomfortable.","She did not know what to say, but remaining silent seemed awkward too.","Noticing her unease, Gu Jingchen smiled and asked, “Would you like to take a walk?”","She immediately nodded. “Okay.”","As they reached the door, he naturally took her hand. She looked up in surprise, but Gu Jingchen did not look at her. He simply led her forward. “There’s a large patch of mock privet up ahead. It’s in full bloom right now. I’ll take you to smell it.”","The smile at the corners of his lips betrayed a hint of smugness, and she could not help smiling along with him. “Okay.”","The property management company had planted a huge patch of mock privet in the complex. The shrubs came up to their chests, and their small clusters of flowers were not particularly eye-catching, but their fragrance was extraordinarily rich.","Hand in hand, they strolled slowly around the flowering shrubs, breathing in the scent together and learning about the unassuming mock privet together...","By the time they completed their walk and returned home, the unfamiliar feeling had faded considerably.","She felt completely at peace, far more relaxed than she ever was at home.","At home, her bedroom door was never allowed to be locked, no matter the time of day.","Even though she was already thirty-one.","That oppressive tension had made it impossible for her to relax. After coming here, the pressure weighing on her heart had finally eased a little.","She let out a long sigh of relief inwardly.","This was nice.","Then she heard Gu Jingchen ask, “Should we establish three ground rules?”","She looked at him in surprise. “What?”","His gaze settled fully on her. “About our habits, about adjusting to each other’s personalities, and about...”","He paused abruptly. “About married life. If you have any thoughts, you can tell me. We can discuss them together.”","His gentle invitation made her blush instantly.","Could they really discuss that too?","How were they supposed to discuss it?","But they were legally married now. It did seem like this had become an important matter.","Although she had never been in a relationship, her age and education had given her plenty of theoretical knowledge.","She thought she should be able to handle it. She should, right?","Putting on an air of calm, she shook her head. “There’s no need to set rules deliberately. We’re married, not attending a class. Let’s just let things happen naturally.”","Her life had been constrained by rules and regulations for far too long—at school, and at her parents’ home too.","Now that she had come here, she did not want things to remain that way.","She wanted to be more casual, more natural, and also...","“Then shall I go shower first?”","When she heard those words beside her, her pupils trembled. “Huh?”","Now?","A mischievous glint flashed through Gu Jingchen’s eyes. “It’s been a long day. I’m going to take a shower on the third floor and relax. There’s a bathtub on the second floor. Would you like me to run a bath for you?”","Her face immediately flushed crimson, and she hurriedly shook her head. “No need! I can do it myself!”","Good heavens! She had misunderstood him!","What had she been thinking?","Even after she lowered herself into the bathtub, the heat in her cheeks still refused to fade.","She felt as though her mind was filled with thoughts she should not be having, yet perhaps they were not thoughts she should not be having after all.","She was already over thirty, old enough to legally possess and enjoy sex.","Besides, she and Gu Jingchen were now in a relationship that was legal, proper, and entirely acceptable.","She could not help thinking a little daringly: Even if they tried tonight, so what?","She had grown up under her parents’ control. She had been directed through high school, university, graduate school, and her doctorate, until she finally began working at a university.","For thirty years, she had lived according to her parents’ arrangements.","Her girlish worries had been about whether she would rank first in her exams and whether she would be scolded when she got home.","Puppy love, college romance, or even a late-in-life relationship—none of them had ever had anything to do with her.","And now, all at once, she realized that she could finally give it a try...","Her thoughts were still wandering when she faintly heard several soft footsteps coming slowly down from the third floor.","They were quiet, yet each one struck her heart like the beat of a war drum.","Suddenly, she became resolute.","Tonight, she was going to sleep with Gu Jingchen!","If she wanted to be reckless, then she had to be reckless.","People who had spent too long being obedient were still obedient even when they tried to be wild.","They had registered their marriage, and Gu Jingchen had met her parents and brought her out of her family home.","As long as they did not sleep in the middle of the street, how could that even count as being reckless?","But for He Yunzhi, making this decision of her own accord already qualified as the ultimate act of rebellion.","She quickly dried herself and opened the bathroom door, only to walk straight into a pair of eyes hazy with steam.","Those eyes looked at her with a smile. “Finished showering? There’s a television in the bedroom. Do you want to watch something?”","Her mind instantly stopped functioning.","“Should we sleep?”","“Hmm?”","For the first time, a trace of surprise appeared in those normally composed eyes, and she could not help feeling pleased.","So he could be surprised too.","That was right. He was clearly two years younger than her, yet why did he always act as though everything were under his control?","She was two years older than him. She should have been the one making all the decisions.","She held his gaze and continued, “Gu Jingchen, shall we sleep?”","Under her unwavering stare, his eyes trembled. It took several seconds for his expression to return to normal. Then he asked her in an unreadable voice, “Are you sure?”","She nodded smugly. “Of course.”","She was the one who had suggested it, so naturally she was sure. Not only was she sure, she intended to take charge and control the entire situation.","She...","She failed to notice the spark of fire that swiftly ignited in Gu Jingchen’s eyes, silently locking onto her.","His hand closed around her wrist in an instant. The bedroom door shut with a click, and a faint huskiness entered his voice.","“It’s dark now. It is indeed time to sleep.”","“...”"]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: Stranger Intimacy","paragraphs":["The room was so quiet it was almost frightening. He Yunzhi felt as though she could hear her own heartbeat pounding inside her chest.","Thump, thump, thump—like she had a fever.","But she had no mind to worry about her heartbeat. All her attention had been completely drawn to the man in front of her.","It was the first time she had ever examined a man from such a close distance—so close that she instinctively held her breath.","She remembered that when she had looked at him during the day, his features had seemed so gentle.","So why did he suddenly seem so much more imposing now?","Her gaze traveled down from his long eyelashes to his straight, handsome nose, then to his thin lips...","His lips quickly drew near and landed on her cheek. The soft sensation made her heart skip.","He asked in a low voice, “How does it feel?”","She hesitated for a moment. “Not bad.”","“Then shall we continue?”","Her face flushed a little deeper. “Mm...”","Her heartbeat seemed to follow his every movement, all the way down to her collarbone. Her body couldn’t help but draw back. “Here...”","“Is that not allowed?”","He looked up at her, his eyes filled with a gentleness that left no room for refusal. She instinctively shook her head. “No...”","His testing touches were filled with endless tenderness, making it impossible for her to refuse.","By the time they were completely joined, her eyes had begun to mist with tears—tears of discomfort and unfamiliarity.","“I’ve never... I haven’t done this before. I...”","She didn’t know what she was trying to say. Was she saying she had never been in a relationship, or asking whether he seemed so gentle because he had a lot of experience?","But he seemed to understand her anyway. Bending close to her ear, he murmured, “Me neither.”","She stared at him in disbelief. “Then why do you...”","He seemed so practiced at it.","The corners of Gu Jingchen’s lips immediately lifted. “Is that a compliment?”","He looked like a child who had just received praise, the happiness in his eyes obvious and unabashed. “I’ll make sure I perform well.”","She cried out at once, “That’s not what I meant!”","But it was already too late. His gentleness vanished. With overwhelming force, he led her running along the seaside, letting the waves sweep her along as they raced without restraint, giving themselves entirely to the moment.","By the time she was completely exhausted, he was still full of energy.","“Take a break, then continue?”","She collapsed weakly, like a fish washed ashore by the waves. “Isn’t that enough?”","But he merely whispered into her ear, “Tomorrow’s the weekend. We can sleep in...”","The next day, they really did sleep until noon. She didn’t even know when she had finally fallen asleep.","Yet her body felt refreshed and wasn’t particularly uncomfortable.","Had he helped clean her up?","She couldn’t help blushing at the thought. They had suddenly become so intimate—so intimate that she was at a complete loss.","She had assumed they would take things slowly: holding hands, then embracing, then exchanging feather-light kisses...","She hadn’t expected them to suddenly hit the fast-forward button and go straight into high gear.","She wanted to get out of bed, but the summer quilt clinging to her skin reminded her that she couldn’t simply rise like this.","“Awake?”","His lazy voice sounded from behind her, and her body instantly went rigid.","“Heh...”","The hand resting around her waist quickly noticed her stiffness, and he let out a soft laugh. “I’ll go out first?”","She nodded. “Mm...”","The glaring sunlight made the room far too bright—so bright that she couldn’t face the situation at all.","She curled up under the quilt, listening as the person beside her got out of bed and then went upstairs to the third floor.","She threw back the quilt and sprang up. After washing up, she got dressed and ran.","Yes, she had run away in a thoroughly spineless fashion.","By the time Gu Jingchen had finished washing up and came downstairs, the room was empty. She was long gone.","A broad smile crept into his eyes. Why was she acting like a little kid?","He picked up his phone and called He Huanhuan. “What are you planning to do today?”","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili were sitting in the living room, seriously browsing job apps.","“I don’t know. I was thinking of finding something to do.”","She felt that she had been far too idle lately. Every day consisted of nothing but eating, drinking, using the bathroom, and sleeping.","Was she turning into a little pig?","She used to have plenty of work she could take on!","“Give Wenzhi a call. She should be able to offer you some advice.”","He Huanhuan’s eyes lit up at once. “That’s right! Sister Yunzhi is a professor! She must be able to help us look for suitable jobs!”","After hanging up, she immediately called He Yunzhi.","At that moment, He Yunzhi was sitting in her car, unsure where to go.","She had almost no friends. In her daily life, the people she interacted with were either colleagues or the children of her parents’ friends.","She had made some new friends of her own initiative when she was in school.","But her parents had acted like detectives, frantically investigating the circumstances of those other families before ordering her to cut ties with her friends.","Her mother was a staunch believer in the idea that a mother should move three times for the sake of her child’s education, and as a result, she had kept an extremely tight rein on her daughter’s friendships.","Now, even when she wanted to find a friend to talk to, there was no one.","That was when He Huanhuan’s call came in. Once connected, the voice on the other end was bright and crisp.","“Sister Yunzhi, are you busy today?”","She shook her head. “No.”","He Huanhuan immediately invited her over. “Then come over to my place! Meili and I are looking for jobs, but we don’t know what kind of work would suit us. Can you help us take a look?”","“Okay.”","She thought she had finally found someone she could confide in.","She drove to the apartment complex where the two girls lived and hurried up to the fifth floor.","The moment she sat down, she asked them shyly, “I have a few questions. Can I ask you?”","The two girls nodded enthusiastically. “Of course! Go ahead, Sister!”","She looked at them with innocent eyes. “Jingchen and I slept together last night, but something feels a little strange... I feel as though we’re moving too quickly. But we’re married...”","She laid out her confusion very frankly, as naturally as if she were discussing an academic question with other teachers in the office.","He Huanhuan’s eyes widened. Then widened even more.","Wait—was this something she was supposed to hear?","Someone, please switch her back to the children’s channel!","Qi Meili, on the other hand, propped up her chin and listened with sparkling eyes. This was juicy! She wanted every detail.","Unable to contain her curiosity, she asked, “Big Brother was so gentle. Was he gentle in that way too?”","She asked the question bluntly, and He Yunzhi answered even more bluntly. “He was gentle at first, but later on, he became quite forceful.”","“My God! What a catch!”","Meili was practically grinning from ear to ear. “Then what’s there to be confused about? Sister, this is a top-tier specimen! You have to enjoy him properly—every day, every meal! He’s practically a tonic!”","He Yunzhi flushed with embarrassment. “But we’ve only just met, and we’ve only just gotten married...”","Meili slapped her thigh. “You’ve got a marriage certificate, so it’s legal! How else are you supposed to build feelings? You have to work them out this way! The more you work at it, the better it gets—the more fragrant and delicious!”","He Huanhuan looked utterly bewildered.","Children’s channel! Switch her back!","Yet she couldn’t help thinking that Meili had kissed Liang Zheng, while Sister Yunzhi had slept with Big Brother...","Technically, she and Han Mo had known each other the longest, but their progress was the slowest...","Why was that?","Oh. She had been stuck on the children’s channel this whole time...","Should she switch channels?","Did Han Mo want to switch channels?"]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: Meaningful Things","paragraphs":["The little embarrassment He Yunzhi had felt was shattered by Qi Meili with astonishing ease.","Meili practically wished she could crawl under the bed and live with the two of them. With a lascivious grin, she asked He Yunzhi, “Sis, just tell me—did you enjoy yourself?”","He Yunzhi nodded, her face flushed. “I did.”","Meili’s smile grew even brighter. “Then what are you hesitating for? Hit the highway at night and take the back roads by day. Run on both tracks at once!”","Keep things ordinary when they should be ordinary, and exciting when they should be exciting. That way, nothing gets in the way!","He Yunzhi’s face turned even redder. “Is that really okay?”","Wouldn’t it feel disjointed?","During the day, they still felt like somewhat unfamiliar people, yet the moment the lights went out, they became incredibly intimate...","Meili’s smile grew even more brazen. “Sis, don’t think about bed stuff when you’re out of bed, and only do bed stuff when you’re in bed. Easy.”","Her words were bold and outrageous, yet somehow He Yunzhi understood exactly what she meant.","Sex and everyday life were two different things. Physical intimacy and getting to know each other’s personalities were two different things as well. Each could progress at its own pace, and neither needed to be used as a reference for the other.","Once she understood that, He Yunzhi instantly relaxed. She finally had the energy to worry about the two of them as well.","She glanced at the phone on the table. “You two want to find jobs?”","The two nodded seriously. He Huanhuan propped her chin on her hand, looking troubled. “I feel like our life is a little too aimless. Every day is just eating, drinking, using the bathroom, and sleeping. We don’t do anything else.”","Just think—around this time last year, she had still been making money by attending strangers’ funerals and pretending to mourn.","Back then, she never would have imagined that a year later, having too much money would leave her feeling so aimless that she’d want to find something to do.","It sounded incredibly obnoxious, didn’t it?","But she really was bored. Lately, even playing on her phone had lost its appeal. She couldn’t bring herself to scroll through short videos, couldn’t finish watching Little Shuai and Little Mei’s movie recaps, and had even grown tired of looking at cats and dogs...","She wanted to cultivate a couple of hobbies to pass the time, but deep down, she was still a poor person at heart.","She couldn’t bring herself to spend money on expensive hobbies, and she had no appreciation for high-end sports.","The two of them searched online and found that the suggestions all boiled down to hiking, rock climbing, skydiving, or some other even more expensive sport.","But in their eyes, wasn’t hiking just swinging your legs while walking along the road? What was there to cultivate? Couldn’t you just swing your legs whenever you felt like it?","Rock climbing and skydiving, meanwhile, were too dangerous. They valued their lives.","What if something went wrong and they kicked the bucket? Dying would be a minor concern. What if they were sent back instead? That would be far worse than the sky falling and the earth splitting apart!","The two spent half the day researching at home before finally deciding to find some work.","It would be safe, and they could make a little money.","How practical was that?","After hearing them out, He Yunzhi shook her head. “Given your current circumstances, getting a job would be the most meaningless thing you could do.”","Neither of them had any educational qualifications. If they went out looking for work, the only jobs available to them would be the most basic ones—jobs that consumed their time and physical energy.","People without financial pressure had no need to take on that kind of work. It offered neither enjoyment nor personal growth. It would only waste their time.","She looked at the two of them. “You don’t need to earn money to cover your basic living expenses, so there’s no reason for you to sell your time and physical strength. That’s just consuming your life.”","Qi Meili nodded furiously. “Sis! You’re absolutely right!”","No wonder she’d wanted to die every day while working in a factory to pay Huanhuan’s hospital bills. So that was what it meant to drain away her life!","She’d always said that people shouldn’t work themselves to death. She just couldn’t understand what Liang Ye was thinking. Why did he insist on working that awful job?","At the neighborhood committee office, Liang Ye was brimming with enthusiasm.","“Ma’am, don’t cry. You’re crying so loudly I can’t hear what you’re saying... What happened to your husband? Did he cheat on you? Tell me how he did it...”","“Their families got into a fight? Why? The husband downstairs crawled into the stairwell and barked like a dog, scaring the people upstairs? Why was he barking like a dog? Oh, BDSM? You people really know how to have fun, huh?”","“...”","Liang Ye had to admit that his job at the neighborhood committee—mediating conflicts—was unbelievably interesting!","He Huanhuan rested her chin on her hand. “Then what should we do that would be interesting?”","But He Yunzhi corrected her. “Not interesting. Meaningful.”","She looked seriously at He Huanhuan. “Huanhuan, you have your family as a safety net. You need to make your life—and yourself—meaningful.”","Ever since He Huanhuan had decided to move out, Gu Jingchen had given her a bank card. Every month, he transferred money to her on schedule to ensure that her quality of life while living alone remained comfortable.","Since she had that financial support, she could devote herself to doing something more meaningful.","The two of them looked curious. “Like what?”","They had absolutely no idea what could count as meaningful.","He Yunzhi smiled. “For example, providing ordinary people with good jobs—or, more specifically, providing ordinary women with good jobs.”","Their eyes lit up. “We can do that too?”","Providing jobs for others—didn’t that mean becoming bosses?","Could they really become bosses?","He Yunzhi nodded with a smile. “Of course. As long as you have money and an idea, anyone can become a good boss.”","But starting a business wasn’t something you did by impulsively throwing money at an idea.","First, they had to figure out what they understood, what they were capable of doing, and what they actually wanted to do.","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili exchanged a look. Their lives before this had consisted of dyeing their hair, getting tattoos, waving their hands around to music, and eating spicy hot pot, beef noodles, and rice noodles across the bridge...","He Huanhuan had one additional skill: she knew how to mourn at funerals for money.","...","After summing everything up, the two of them felt too embarrassed to look at He Yunzhi. It seemed they had nothing respectable to offer...","But He Yunzhi listened with great interest. Their lives were completely different from hers.","In fact, it was a kind of life she had never encountered before.","Her eyes lingered on the colorful tattoo peeking out from beneath Qi Meili’s collar, and a hint of curiosity appeared in them. “Do you two really like tattoos?”","The two nodded, then shook their heads.","At first, they had gotten tattoos to look more intimidating and make sure other people wouldn’t bully them.","Later, it was to keep up with trends. Everyone in their circle had tattoos, and not having one meant falling behind.","Eventually, they simply got used to it. After getting enough tattoos, they became no different from eating and drinking.","If they saw a design they liked, they got it tattooed. If something interesting happened, they got that tattooed too...","Over time, they ended up covered in tattoos.","But if someone asked whether they truly loved tattoos, the answer was... not particularly.","After He Huanhuan came to this world, all the tattoos on her body had disappeared, and she had never gotten another one.","No one here would bully her. She no longer ran with the tough-girl crowd and had no need to chase a pointless trend.","For the two of them, tattoos couldn’t really be considered a hobby. They had served more of a practical purpose.","He Yunzhi nodded to show that she understood. “Then let’s think of something else. Do you have any other hobbies, or anything you know a lot about?”","The lives they had led before had been too simple—and too poor.","The only things they knew about were the everyday concerns of poor people: cheap clothes, cheap food, cheap apartments, and cheap cars.","At the mention of cheap cars, He Huanhuan tentatively raised her hand. “I like electric scooters. Does that count?”","He Yunzhi smiled and nodded. “Of course it counts.”","China’s electric-scooter market was enormous, worth several hundred billion yuan.","After all, whose household didn’t have an electric scooter?"]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: Would You Like to Change the Channel","paragraphs":["He Yunzhi quickly pulled up a market report on domestic electric scooters and showed it to the two women. “Look. According to the latest figures from last year, there are currently more than 350 million electric scooters in China, with annual sales exceeding 50 million units. This is a huge market.”","The two of them stared at the densely packed data on the phone, their eyes glazing over almost instantly. “Sister, how about you just give us a summary?”","They had been out of school for far too long. Whatever learning ability they once had, they had long since returned to their teachers.","He Yunzhi skimmed through the report and quickly summarized it for them. “Joining a branded dealership, combining online promotion with offline service—that’s an option worth considering.”","Their eyes lit up at once. “Really?”","Could they actually open an electric-scooter shop?","He Yunzhi nodded. “You can, but you can’t just jump into it recklessly.”","Opening a shop wasn’t something you decided on a whim. They had to take everything into consideration: calculating the initial investment, choosing a brand, selecting a location, analyzing foot traffic, and more. Only by planning everything properly could they at least ensure they wouldn’t lose money.","Far too many people started businesses without using their heads. They saw a franchise hotline online and called it without thinking. Whatever the person on the other end said, they responded with, “Yes, yes, yes,” and, “Mm-hmm, you’re absolutely right!”","They didn’t even have twenty or thirty thousand yuan in savings, yet they dreamed of becoming bosses from the comfort of home and making money while lying around.","They hadn’t even figured out that a steamed-bun shop had to sell steamed buns and a milk-tea shop had to sell milk tea before they started throwing money into the business.","Franchise fee? Pay it!","Mentor guidance fee? Small change!","Rent and renovation costs? Small change!","The shop hadn’t even opened, and they were already hiring several employees. How could a boss be expected to do the work personally? Would they still be a boss then?","They didn’t care about choosing the location, overseeing the renovation, or training employees. They didn’t care about anything.","Then, once the shop finally opened, there would be no business, no customers, and no money left to keep it running.","Within a couple of days, they would have to post a short video saying, “Then let’s say a proper goodbye~ The river of time flows into the sea~ We together...”","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili were both left completely bewildered.","He Huanhuan asked, baffled, “Were those people very rich?”","He Yunzhi shook her head. “Most of them didn’t have much money at all.”","“Then why would they do that?”","Wouldn’t it be better to save that money properly? Why waste it for no reason?","He Yunzhi sighed. “Because they want to change their economic status, but they don’t have enough understanding to do so. They want to get rich and change their circumstances, but they don’t know how. So they try to gamble with the little savings they have.”","To a certain extent, it was the mindset of a gambler.","He Huanhuan hurriedly shook her head. “We won’t do that!”","She couldn’t bear to waste money.","Even if the money came from Gu Jingchen and she didn’t have to work hard to earn it herself, she still couldn’t bear to waste it.","It was money, after all. Why waste it when it could be put to good use?","Still, after thinking about all the people He Yunzhi had described, she couldn’t help becoming more cautious.","Those people probably thought they wouldn’t waste their money either. No one started a business believing they were destined to fail.","It was only after everything had become irreversible that they suddenly realized every step they had taken was wrong.","After thinking for a moment, she asked He Yunzhi, “Sister, could you send me a copy of that report later?”","She wanted to study it carefully. She needed to understand the industry before deciding whether to open an electric-scooter shop.","Her serious attitude made He Yunzhi nod approvingly. “Sure. I’ll send you a few more documents later. Take a look at all of them.”","Foot-traffic analysis and planning, evaluating and selecting commercial locations...","Once she finished reading through all of that, she would have a much clearer idea of what to do.","The entire day passed with the two of them earnestly poring over those mind-numbing materials under He Yunzhi’s guidance.","They went through them bit by bit, asking He Yunzhi whenever they encountered something they didn’t understand. She would explain the obscure professional terminology in plain, everyday language.","It wasn’t until the sky outside had darkened that Meili clapped her hands and urged He Yunzhi to leave. “Sister, you and our brother are newlyweds. Hurry home—don’t make our brother spend the night alone!”","After spending the afternoon together, the three of them had grown much closer. He Yunzhi’s face flushed faintly, but she still stood up. “Then I’ll head back first. This week is my long week. Mark anything you don’t understand, and I’ll explain it to you again on Friday.”","Her teaching schedule alternated between long and short weeks. During a long week, she worked four days and had three days off; during a short week, she worked three days and had four days off.","Qi Meili nearly burst into tears when she heard that. They both worked alternating long and short weeks, so why had her factory’s “long week” meant working six days and taking only one day off, while the “short week” still meant working six days?","And if you asked what the difference was, the factory would tell you that during the short week, Saturday overtime came with extra pay...","Two extra yuan an hour...","After He Yunzhi left, the two of them leaned over the table and studied for another hour or so. They were still completely absorbed in their work when Han Mo called He Huanhuan.","Meili waved her off. “I’m not going. Just bring me back a packed meal after you eat.”","These days, she was living off Huanhuan. If the two of them started a business, Huanhuan would be the one putting up the money.","She had nothing to contribute except herself.","That was why she had to study even harder and understand everything thoroughly.","If they really opened a shop one day, she would also learn how to repair electric scooters. She didn’t want to be a hands-off boss. She wanted to be the kind of boss who could handle anything herself.","After being best friends for so many years, He Huanhuan naturally understood what she was thinking. She nodded seriously. “All right. You keep studying, then.”","Huanhuan was naturally happy that Meili was willing to learn. The more they knew, the more secure their business would be.","When she went downstairs, Han Mo’s car was already waiting there. She jogged over and climbed inside.","As usual, Han Mo asked, “What did you do today?”","Their daily lives were fairly repetitive: playing on their phones, going out for a stroll, visiting the park, feeding stray cats...","But today, He Huanhuan gave him a different answer. “We studied with Sister Yunzhi!”","Han Mo was surprised. “Studied?”","He Huanhuan nodded. “I want to find a job to pass the time, but Sister Yunzhi said that, given my current situation, I’d be better off starting a business and creating jobs for other people...”","She repeated everything He Yunzhi had told them. After listening, Han Mo nodded in agreement. “She’s right. There’s no need for you to go work for someone else. But if you want to start a business, have you decided what you want to do?”","He Huanhuan’s eyes shone. “Sell electric scooters!”","After spending the afternoon reading the materials, she had become even more determined. She wanted to open an electric-scooter shop.","She wanted to sell electric scooters and hire the “spiritual girls” who couldn’t find jobs as salespeople.","She had once been part of that scene herself, so she knew that many girls in that circle had a very hard time. Their fathers didn’t care about them, their mothers didn’t love them, and their families wouldn’t give them a single cent.","She also knew that many of the people in that circle weren’t bad. It wasn’t that they didn’t want to work. They had simply ended up as “spiritual girls” through a series of circumstances, and after dyeing their hair and getting tattoos, they could no longer find employment.","She wanted to give them jobs so they could support themselves and live stable, peaceful lives.","She earnestly explained her idea to Han Mo. After thinking it over, he said, “That won’t be easy. Have you considered how the image of the spiritual girls might affect the shop’s image?”","He Huanhuan nodded. “Of course I have. That’s why it’s only an idea for now. I’ll think it through carefully.”","She certainly didn’t want to end up making short videos and singing, “The river of time flows into the sea...”","Without realizing it, Han Mo began calculating how they might open a shop like that while balancing the store’s image with the spiritual girls’ employment.","Lost in thought, he suddenly heard He Huanhuan ask, “Han Mo, do you want to change the channel?”"]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: Take It Slow","paragraphs":["Han Mo froze for a moment, not quite understanding. “Switch what channel? Do you want to watch TV?”","He reached over and ruffled He Huanhuan’s bright-yellow hair. “Let’s watch after we eat. It’s getting late.”","“What are you talking about? We’re not even discussing the same thing!”","He Huanhuan slapped his hand away in annoyance, then voiced the little worry that had been bothering her. “...Han Mo, don’t you think the two of us are stuck on the children’s channel?”","Han Mo couldn’t help laughing. “What’s wrong with the children’s channel? You’re the youngest of the three, so of course you belong on the children’s channel.”","He Huanhuan pushed back her bangs. “But I’m an adult too! And we’ve known each other the longest. Isn’t it kind of ridiculous that I’ve been overtaken like this?”","Han Mo asked, “Overtaken how?”","“You know... like that!”","“What do you mean, ‘like that’?”","“...”","“Han Mo!”","“Haha...”","Han Mo finally lost control and burst out laughing.","That only made He Huanhuan angrier. “I’m being serious!”","What was so funny?","The car pulled over by the roadside. Han Mo looked at her with a smile. “I’m being serious too.”","Her bright-yellow bangs were a complete mess from all her fidgeting. Han Mo reached over and smoothed them back into place. “We’re not in a competition. Why are you so worried about falling behind?”","When it came to relationships, everyone had to move at their own pace. Each person had their own rhythm. Comparing yourself to others wouldn’t get you anywhere—it would only make you anxious.","He Huanhuan frowned. “Really?”","“Of course.”","He brushed a finger over the crease between her brows, as though wiping away her worries along with it. “Huanhuan, the two of us are different from them. Have you forgotten? We’ve been through being drifters together.”","Even without intimacy, their feelings wouldn’t change.","Back then, when Han Xuan had run him over, it was He Huanhuan who had pulled him out of the car. She had carried him away from the scene and hidden with him for two days in a dilapidated, abandoned house.","How could he possibly stop liking her just because they hadn’t been intimate?","“That’s not the point!”","He Huanhuan suddenly sat up straight and leaned close to his face. “I kind of want to kiss!”","She was curious!","Back when she was still hanging around the edgy crowd, everyone had been obsessed with dating and kissing. One day, they would get together with one person and kiss them. The next day, they would get together with someone else and kiss them again.","At the time, she had barely been able to survive, and she had thought they were all crazy for constantly kissing each other.","But now that her life had stabilized, she had unexpectedly become curious about what kissing actually felt like!","What was that saying again? Once your basic needs are met, you start thinking about sex.","It really wasn’t wrong. That was exactly what was happening to her now...","Her eyes locked firmly onto Han Mo’s... mouth, shining brightly. “How about I kiss you first?”","She was younger, and she would be the one making the first move. That made perfect sense, didn’t it?","Around Han Mo, she could always act however she pleased, without the slightest restraint.","The moment she finished speaking, she shot forward, planning to catch him off guard.","But a large hand instantly cupped her face, squishing her cheeks together and making her look even younger.","With a smile, Han Mo gently pushed her face away, making her cheeks puff out even more. “Do you really want to, or are you just saying that?”","He Huanhuan mumbled, “Of course I really want to!”","Han Mo pressed her. “Then why didn’t you want to before? Why do you suddenly want to today?”","“Um...”","He Huanhuan couldn’t answer. Of course it was because she had listened to that explicit conversation today, and her thoughts had gotten carried away with it!","But how could she say that?","Wouldn’t that mean exposing the private business of her older brother and Sister Yunzhi?","“You’re so annoying! Why are you making such a big deal out of a kiss?”","How had she never noticed what a nag he was before?","Fine! She wasn’t kissing him anymore!","She flailed, trying to free her face from his palm, when a shadow suddenly fell over her.","Then a light kiss landed on her forehead.","“More than half the year has already passed, Huanhuan,” Han Mo said softly. “Once this year is over, next year will pass quickly too. Time flies. Before you know it, you’ll be as grown-up and beautiful as Meili.”","When that happened, they could switch to another channel.","For now, the children’s channel was perfectly fine.","It was a light, gentle kiss—more like a blessing and a show of affection from a family member.","He Huanhuan’s heart suddenly jolted. Her eyes darted around awkwardly. “I—I know...”","Her parents had been completely absent from her upbringing.","Well, that wasn’t quite true. Her father was around—it would simply have been better if he hadn’t been.","Perhaps because she had been so deprived of fatherly love, she was completely unable to reject Han Mo’s tenderness.","She blinked and glanced at Han Mo, then quickly looked away. “Well... I’m not kissing you anymore. Let’s go eat...”","Han Mo watched as her face slowly turned red in his palm, the corners of his eyes curving with amusement. “You don’t even have half of Meili’s nerve, yet you want to imitate her?”","When Meili and Liang Zheng kissed, she might not have had any experience, but she had one advantage: her memory was terrible. She forgot about it as soon as it was over.","He Huanhuan, on the other hand, didn’t even know where to look.","“You’re so annoying! Let’s go eat!”","“Haha...”","Their attempt to switch channels had ended in complete failure, but for some reason, Huanhuan felt a little closer to the person beside her.","Over the next few days, the sisters did nothing else. They devoted themselves entirely to researching electric scooters at home.","They studied the industry, looked into how to open a shop, and considered how to strike the right balance.","In particular, once He Huanhuan told Meili that she wanted to provide jobs for young women from the same edgy subculture they had once belonged to, Meili’s enthusiasm for learning instantly reached its peak.","They had made it out of a difficult life, so they understood better than anyone how much pain lay beneath the laughter of those girls.","She absolutely had to help Huanhuan get the shop up and running—properly and completely.","She wanted girls who were struggling and helpless, just as they once had been, to live better lives than the ones they had known.","But the girls from that subculture did have a rather unconventional look, and they could easily scare away potential customers. There was no way around that.","They discussed the matter with He Yunzhi for several days, but still couldn’t find a suitable middle ground.","And so the issue remained deadlocked.","She hadn’t been born into wealth, with a golden spoon in her mouth. She couldn’t throw money away casually; it hurt her to waste it.","She had to prepare everything properly before opening the shop, before offering anyone jobs.","As He Yunzhi had said, at least during the initial projections, the losses couldn’t be too great.","If the preliminary estimates already predicted substantial losses, then there was no point in launching the project at all.","But although He Yunzhi had plenty of theoretical knowledge, she had very little experience with starting a business.","So when faced with this concrete difficulty, she couldn’t come up with the best solution right away either.","Until a week later, when she and Meili were at home, howling in frustration:","“Why does everyone in our circle love dyeing their hair and getting tattoos so much?!”","Although they were wailing, the black plastic bags over their heads were wrapped tightly in place.","They couldn’t think of a solution, and the frustration was driving them crazy!","So of course they had to dye their hair a new color to jolt their irritated minds!"]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: Open a Shop","paragraphs":["Two Black Plastic Bags stood in front of the mirror, deeply troubled. Their original goal had been to create jobs for edgy young women.","But if they forced those girls to stop dyeing their hair and cover up their tattoos, would they still be edgy girls?","Would that still be true to their original intention?","Besides, the two of them liked dyeing their hair too!","The Black Plastic Bags were removed, and He Huanhuan stared at the lavender purple and peacock blue reflected in the mirror. She let out a long sigh. “How can they not like hair this beautiful?”","Meili sighed along with her. “Who knows? It clearly looks great!”","Once their hair was dry, the misty lavender purple and intensely saturated peacock blue were beautiful and impossible to miss.","Beautiful. Absolutely beautiful.","But they were far from conventional. Ordinary people who had spent too long living within society’s invisible boundaries would naturally reject them on instinct.","If the two women were merely going out to turn heads, passersby would at most give them a few surprised glances.","But if they dressed like this to run an electric scooter shop, anyone who came looking to buy a vehicle would probably turn around and leave the moment they reached the door.","They were simply too trendy, too flashy, too unconventional for some people to handle.","After another sigh, Meili took a striking selfie of their hair and posted it to her social feed:","“Is it really that bad? Why doesn’t anyone like it?”","Liang Zheng’s message arrived almost immediately:","[Who doesn’t like it?]","They had only just dyed their hair, and someone already disliked it? Who was the first person she had shared it with?","Meili sighed and replied:","[Passersby, internet users, ordinary people, customers!]","The inexplicable reply made Liang Zheng’s brows draw together slightly. He immediately took a moment to call her.","“Are you having trouble?”","Meili shook her head. “It’s not really a problem. Huanhuan and I just want to open a shop, but...”","After listening to their concerns, Liang Zheng thought for a moment. “Perhaps you should consider emphasizing what makes you unique.”","Meili was surprised. “What do you mean?”","Liang Zheng spoke seriously from the other end of the call. “Since you can’t avoid it, try looking at it from another angle. There’s nothing inherently unpleasant about those distinctive traits of yours. What if you amplified them instead? What would that look like?”","Amplify what made them unique?","Amplify...","Meili’s eyes lit up at once. “I have to go! I’m hanging up! Bye!”","She quickly switched apps and searched online for some information. Then she excitedly turned to He Huanhuan.","“Huanhuan! We should open a shop that caters to young people!”","“Young people?”","Qi Meili nodded firmly. “That’s right! Young people!”","Times had changed too much. When the older generation bought electric scooters, they cared only about whether the vehicle worked and rode well.","Young people were different. They cared about appearance too.","They wanted their scooters to be attractive, cute, clean, and stylish.","If people cared about how their vehicles looked, then what about the shop itself?","He Huanhuan understood immediately. “Exactly! We can open an electric scooter dealership!”","They could decorate it to be bright, beautiful, and stylish, keeping it as clean and upscale as a car dealership.","They sold vehicles too. Their electric scooter shop would be every bit as impressive as a showroom for passenger cars!","The two women instantly felt enlightened. If they opened a beautifully designed, exquisitely decorated electric scooter dealership, then having salespeople with brightly colored hair standing inside would no longer seem strange.","Young people today were highly accepting of dyed hair and tattoos!","Haha!","Once they’d figured out the most troublesome issue, the two of them began looking into some of the bigger domestic electric scooter brands.","They barely needed to deliberate before settling on one with a youthful, vibrant brand image.","Everything after that was simple. If nothing else, the two of them certainly knew plenty of bosses and CEOs.","Her brother, Han Mo, Liang Zheng—any one of those guys only had to lift a finger, and they could slip in a favor, having their marketing departments put together detailed market research and location recommendations for the two women.","What was that saying again? Lean against a big tree and enjoy the shade!","And weren’t they enjoying it now?","Gu Jingchen had originally planned to reimburse all her franchise, renovation, and other expenses, but He Huanhuan frantically waved him off. “Oh, please! I want to open a shop, not rake in money. Why does every single one of you want to reimburse me?”","Her brother wanted to pay for it once, Han Mo wanted to pay for it again...","If a few more people reimbursed her, she wouldn’t even need to open the shop. She could just stand by the roadside handing money out to strangers!","When the grand opening finally arrived, their shop was packed with excitement. Several of Jiangcheng’s most eligible bachelor CEOs were working there for free as shop assistants.","All of them were tall and long-legged, dressed in high-end tailored suits as they helped push electric scooters around. It was a feast for the eyes.","Passersby couldn’t help asking, “Since when did Hao L start selling electric scooters?”","Black Swan electric scooters?","Still, the effect was undeniably excellent.","Following Han Mo’s suggestion, they set up two cameras and started a local livestream for the opening.","The bright, spotless two-story standalone building was filled with cream-colored electric scooters, neatly arranged exactly where they were meant to be.","Handsome male and beautiful female staff drifted in and out of the camera frame, and the livestream’s popularity instantly soared.","Electric scooters weren’t that expensive to begin with. Even the pricier ones only cost five or six thousand yuan—less than half a minute’s worth of tips in some livestreams.","The comments went wild:","[That handsome guy who just walked by! Call him back! I’ll send gifts!]","He Huanhuan immediately indulged the viewer. “Liang Zheng! Come here, quick!”","The moment he appeared on camera, his deep, striking features set off a flood of exclamation marks. He Huanhuan grinned. “No need to send gifts. If you want an electric scooter, you can place an order directly through the livestream and then come to the store to choose one~”","The comments grew even bolder:","[Do you get a handsome guy with every scooter purchase? I want the one who was pushing the scooter just now.]","She meant Han Mo. He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose.","[That one’s not available. I’ve already reserved him.]","Liang Zheng looked into the camera at that. “I’ve been reserved too.”","The commenters ignored him completely and continued spamming the chat:","[I’ll reserve you, then!]","[How much does it cost to reserve one???]","The beauty-loving young women in the livestream talked big behind their screens. Some who lived nearby even called cabs straight to the store.","But once they saw the men in person, every one of them blushed too hard to say a word.","Even when asking for a photo, they could only quietly ask He Huanhuan, “Could I take a picture with that gentle, handsome guy?”","He Huanhuan followed the direction she pointed in. It was Gu Jingchen.","Smiling, she nodded. “Sure, but he’s married~”","Handsome faces could be part of the sales pitch—but they couldn’t mislead people.","The young woman’s face reddened even more, her eyes shining brighter. “Just one photo from a distance will do.”","Yet her fingers were already tapping out comments in the livestream chat: [Girls! I checked it out in person! That gentle, handsome guy is married! God, he’s seriously something else!]","That was how young women were. When they saw someone good-looking, they liked him, admired him, and secretly cast him in little fantasies in their hearts.","But it was never harassment, crude objectification, or shameless flirting.","The grand-opening event could be considered a success. Once the livestream ended, the customers who had come to join the excitement finally began to drift away.","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili were so exhausted that they slumped over their electric scooters, unable to move. Livestreaming was exhausting. Running a shop was exhausting.","Liang Zheng stood beside Qi Meili, steadying the scooter beneath her. “Tired? Want to go soak in the hot springs?”","Meili lazily lifted her eyes to look at him. “I can’t take another step...”","Liang Zheng caught hold of her arm. “Then should I carry you there?”","Across the street, He Yunzhi’s mother quickly snapped a photo of the scene and sent it to Liang Zheng’s parents."]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: Tattoo","paragraphs":["Weng Meijuan had mixed feelings about her daughter’s whirlwind marriage. Setting aside her anger that He Yunzhi had registered the marriage without seeking her or her husband’s consent, Weng Meijuan was actually quite satisfied with Gu Jingchen as her son-in-law.","Gu Jingchen was impeccable in every respect. He had a gentle personality and treated her and He Jingyao with great respect.","His education, appearance, and conduct were all excellent. There was only one drawback: his family was a mess.","Other than Gu Jingchen, not a single member of the Gu family had anything to recommend them.","Weng Meijuan and He Jingyao were both graduates of prestigious schools. They had been graduate students at Capital University back in their day, so they placed enormous importance on education.","Yet apart from Gu Jingchen, not one person in the Gu family had applied themselves to their studies.","Gu Chengye had dropped out of high school, while Jiang Yulan had studied traditional opera since elementary school and had barely received any formal education.","Gu Jinghan and Gu Chacha weren’t interested in studying either. They had spent money to get into some private college in Jiangcheng and ended up with worthless bachelor’s degrees.","As for He Huanhuan, there was even less to say! She had dragged down the Gu family’s educational average to a whole new low—she had only graduated from middle school!","He Huanhuan insisted that in her original world, she had been admitted to high school!","She had dropped out of high school just like Old Mr. Gu, and that was fundamentally different from merely graduating from middle school!","Graduating from middle school meant failing to get into high school. She had gotten in but hadn’t gone.","There had been all sorts of reasons for that, including financial and family circumstances, but none of them had anything to do with her intelligence.","However, Jiangcheng was a model city for educational streaming. Every year, half of the students were filtered out during the high school entrance exams.","The original owner had been one of those students who didn’t make the cut.","Weng Meijuan worked in the education system. Using her position to do a little digging, she had learned the educational background of every member of the Gu family.","As a result, she despised the Gu family from the bottom of her heart. How ignorant, uncivilized, and backward could a family that didn’t value education be?","That was why she hoped Gu Jingchen would keep his distance from his family, and He Yunzhi should cut off contact with them altogether.","But after moving out, He Yunzhi stopped coming home. Even when Weng Meijuan went to find her at school, her attitude was cool and distant.","When Weng Meijuan told her not to associate with the other members of the Gu family, He Yunzhi had actually argued back, asking why she wanted her to do something so rude.","She had even asked whether that was the sort of upbringing one would expect from someone who worked in the education system.","Weng Meijuan had been rendered speechless.","There hadn’t been much to do at work that afternoon, so she had gone home early.","As soon as she arrived, a pop-up notification appeared on her phone, alerting her to a trending local event.","Weng Meijuan considered herself a cultured person and believed she needed to keep up with the times.","So after short-video apps became popular, she had downloaded one too. Whenever she had nothing better to do, she sent He Yunzhi videos filled with life advice and lessons on interpersonal conduct.","She usually ignored local trending notifications, but the words “brightly colored hair” in this one caught her eye.","She couldn’t help thinking of He Huanhuan’s yellow hair. She immediately tapped the link and was taken into a livestream.","In the livestream, He Huanhuan was sporting purple hair and smiling as she interacted with the comments.","“Have Liang Zheng make a heart with his collarbone? How are we supposed to do that?”","As she spoke, she tried making one herself in front of her collarbone. Weng Meijuan’s brows instantly drew together in disapproval.","What a disgrace! Absolutely indecent!","She raised her phone, intending to call Gu Jingchen and tell him to keep He Huanhuan in line.","But before she could exit the livestream, she saw Gu Jingchen appear in the camera’s frame.","Gu Jingchen smiled gently at the camera. “Our shop has just opened today. We hope everyone...”","Weng Meijuan’s vision went black, and she nearly fainted.","They had all gone to embarrass themselves at the opening of some little electric scooter shop?","She opened the livestreamer’s profile, found the shop’s address, and immediately got up to see what was going on.","By the time she arrived, it was already getting late. The shop’s opening event had ended successfully, and He Huanhuan and the others were preparing to close up for the night.","She stood by the side of the road and watched Gu Jingchen, Han Mo, and Liang Zheng dutifully wheel the electric scooters into the shop. Her brows were furrowed so deeply they could have pinched a He Huanhuan to death.","They were all outstanding young entrepreneurs in Jiangcheng. How could they be doing this sort of menial work by the side of the road?","What was worse, while Gu Jingchen and the others were working, He Huanhuan and another oddly dressed girl were sprawled across the electric scooters, taking a break!","The scooters were parked right by the roadside, and the two girls were lounging across them on the sidewalk. What kind of behavior was that?","Her face darkened instantly, and she raised her leg, ready to go over and reprimand He Huanhuan.","But after taking only two steps, she suddenly noticed that Liang Zheng had taken hold of the blue-haired girl’s hand!","Her eyes widened.","Liang Zheng and that blue-haired girl...?","She quickly ducked out of sight beside the road and took a picture of the scene, sending it to Liang Zheng’s mother.","[Sis Li, take a look. Is that your Liang Zheng? How did he get involved with some delinquent-looking girl?]","In truth, she knew the blue-haired girl was He Huanhuan’s friend.","But Weng Meijuan already disliked He Huanhuan. Naturally, she was even more disgusted by Meili, who was covered in tattoos.","In her eyes, Meili was no different from a social menace.","She crouched down and zoomed the camera in to three times magnification, carefully taking several pictures of the tattoos exposed on Meili’s body. She sent them all to Liang Zheng’s mother.","[Sis Li, look at all the tattoos on this girl! They’re terrifying! You need to keep a close eye on Liang Zheng. Don’t let some bad girl lead him astray!]","She didn’t stop to consider that, given Liang Zheng’s age, who exactly was more likely to lead whom astray?","But that was how prejudice worked. In her heart, Meili was a bad girl. Even if Liang Zheng were fifty or sixty years old, Weng Meijuan would still insist that Meili was the one who had corrupted him.","At the Liang residence, Li Changxin was practicing calligraphy in her study.","Her phone buzzed on the corner of the desk, but she paid it no attention.","Since retiring, her life had been extremely peaceful. Normally, no one contacted her.","And even when they did, it was rarely anything urgent.","She planned to finish writing one sheet before checking her phone, but it began chiming repeatedly, disrupting her concentration.","Who could be sending her so many messages at this hour?","She set down her brush and picked up her phone. Her eyes widened in shock.","What... what was this?","She enlarged the photos bit by bit. Despite the blurry image quality, the numerous tattoos covering Meili’s body were unmistakable.","As was her dazzling blue hair.","Li Changxin felt dizzy and hurriedly backed out of the photos.","She steadied herself against the desk and sat down, thinking calmly for a long while before deciding to call Liang Ye.","She remembered Liang Ye mentioning that the biological daughter the Gu family had found liked dyeing her hair.","Could that be the Gu family’s biological daughter?","After composing herself, she called Liang Ye. He answered with a cheerful laugh.","“Mom, how did you know I’d just gotten home? Did you secretly install surveillance cameras in my house?”","Li Changxin wasn’t in the mood to joke with him.","“Xiao Ye, tell me honestly. Is your brother dating the biological daughter the Gu family found?”","There was a three-second silence on the other end.","Then came an earth-shaking wail.","“My brother really likes Huanhuan? How could he do this? He’s so handsome! How am I supposed to compete with him?!”","To be fair, he did have a pretty accurate understanding of his own limitations.","Li Changxin ignored his lamentations and asked, “The girl’s name is Huanhuan? Are you close to her? What is she like? And why does she have so many tattoos?”","Liang Ye answered tearfully, “We’re really close. She’s a wonderful person and never wastes money. She has a tattoo... No, wait—what tattoo?”","How come he didn’t remember Huanhuan having a tattoo? The only person he knew with a tattoo was...","Qi Meili? And his brother?","His brother and Qi Meili???"]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: Would you like to cover up","paragraphs":["Liang Ye was having trouble processing what he had just learned. Qi Meili and his brother?","They were practically from two different worlds! How could they possibly be together?","He couldn’t help asking, “Mom, are you sure you didn’t get it wrong?”","His brother might be handsome, but he was incredibly boring. How could Meili possibly get together with him?","Besides, wasn’t his brother several years older than Meili? Wasn’t that just an old ox eating tender grass?","His phone vibrated. Li Changxin immediately forwarded the photo to him.","“Take a look. Is that your brother holding hands with that girl?”","The picture was crystal clear. Qi Meili was slumped on the back of an electric scooter while Liang Zheng held her hand, a smile on his face that he couldn’t hide.","Liang Ye stared at the picture in shock. “My brother looks so happy!”","There was no mistaking that smile. His brother was practically head over heels!","On the other end of the phone, Li Changxin couldn’t help sighing. “You said that girl’s name is Meili? What does she do? What does her family do? Do you know? Tell me everything.”","Liang Ye fell silent. Meili’s family was in very poor circumstances.","He didn’t know how to explain it to his mother. She would definitely never accept Meili.","“Xiao Ye, why aren’t you saying anything?”","Liang Ye stammered, “Well, I’m not really sure either. I only know that she used to be Huanhuan’s friend. Her family probably isn’t particularly wealthy—just an ordinary family, I guess... Haha...”","Li Changxin sighed again. “How did she end up with so many tattoos? Is she a bad girl?”","“No! Absolutely not!”","Liang Ye raised his voice in protest. “Mom, don’t say that about Meili. She’s a really good person.”","He’d asked Meili to help him download apps and bring in new users. Although she was always extremely annoyed by it, she downloaded every single one.","Some of those apps made the referral process incredibly troublesome. Meili would curse him out every time, but she always cooperated seriously and helped him complete the tasks.","She really was a good person.","Li Changxin glanced at the photo again. “Do they run an electric scooter shop? Xiao Ye, can you take me there to have a look?”","Whether this girl was truly good or not, she would have to see for herself.","Liang Ye hesitated. “Mom, that wouldn’t be right. We can’t go look at someone without their permission. It’s rude.”","But Li Changxin was determined. “I’m only going to take a look. If you don’t take me, I’ll have Auntie Weng take me.”","Liang Ye hurriedly agreed. “Don’t bother Auntie Weng. I’ll take you, I’ll take you...”","Liang Ye’s grandfather and He Yunzhi’s grandfather had been comrades-in-arms. When his grandparents were still alive, the two families visited each other often.","But He Yunzhi’s parents were far too meddlesome. Every time they came to his family’s home, they criticized this and complained about that.","After his grandparents passed away, the two families gradually stopped seeing each other so often.","That was probably for the best. After all, He Yunzhi’s parents had plenty to say about his family too.","For example, he had only attended an ordinary university. That alone had made He Yunzhi’s parents dissatisfied with his mother. They had lectured her countless times, asking why she hadn’t kept a closer eye on his studies.","A child’s academic performance had to be monitored strictly. As long as you pushed hard enough, there was no child you couldn’t force to succeed.","...","Even now, thinking about those words made him feel terrified.","He couldn’t imagine what kind of insane scene it would turn into if He Yunzhi’s mother took his mother there.","It was better for him to go. At least he could give Meili a heads-up and help her prepare herself.","Li Changxin glanced at the calendar and saw that it was Friday. “Let’s go tomorrow, then. You’re off tomorrow, aren’t you?”","Liang Ye refused guiltily. “The day after tomorrow. I have to work overtime tomorrow.”","Li Changxin knew how dedicated her son was to his job, so she didn’t suspect anything. She nodded and agreed. “All right. The day after tomorrow, then. I’ll have the driver pick you up.”","After hanging up, Liang Ye practically flew downstairs, hopped onto his electric scooter, and sped toward He Huanhuan’s residential compound.","By the time he arrived, He Huanhuan and Qi Meili had just gotten home as well.","They had been busy all day and were too exhausted to work on any projects. After having dinner with Liang Zheng and the others, they headed back.","Seeing Liang Ye, He Huanhuan was surprised. “Why did you come so late?”","Liang Ye knew they had opened a shop. Since the guys had to work on Fridays, there was no way they could take time off to attend the grand opening.","But he had already promised that he would go help He Huanhuan drum up excitement on Saturday.","Not that He Huanhuan needed him to do that. Whether it was livestreaming or offline promotion, her shop catered to a completely different crowd from Liang Ye.","So when she saw him now, He Huanhuan was puzzled. Hadn’t they agreed that he would go straight to the shop tomorrow to hang out with them? Why had he come to her home tonight?","She never imagined that Liang Ye would drop a bombshell after only a few words.","“Meili, are you dating my brother?”","Before Qi Meili could answer, he hurriedly continued, “Sister Yunzhi’s mother saw you holding hands with my brother! She secretly took a picture and sent it to my mom! My mom told me to bring her over to spy on you!”","The words hit Qi Meili like a barrage. She instantly crouched down defensively.","“Your mom is here? Where? Where is she?”","Liang Ye quickly explained, “Not right now. She told me to take her tomorrow. I lied and told her I had to work overtime tomorrow, so I pushed it back to the day after tomorrow.”","Meili stared at him speechlessly. “What difference does one day make?”","It wasn’t as if he had managed to get her out of it.","Liang Ye nodded earnestly. “Of course it makes a difference! We have one extra day to prepare!”","He cautiously glanced at Meili’s tattoos. “Well, um... do you think you could find a way to cover up your tattoos tomorrow?”","His gaze then shifted to her hair. “And your hair—could you dye it black again?”","“And your family background. I told my mom you came from an ordinary family. I didn’t mention that your parents divorced when you were very young... Shouldn’t we get our stories straight?”","He figured that even if his mother ultimately refused to approve of them, they should at least do their best to leave Meili with a good first impression.","But he never expected He Huanhuan and Qi Meili to glare at him in disdain.","Qi Meili angrily rolled up her sleeve, revealing a large tattoo covering her arm. “Do you think there’s something wrong with my tattoos? Is there something wrong with my hair?”","“And is there something wrong with my family?”","Liang Ye honestly nodded. “Well... it’s true that none of those things are exactly ideal...”","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes at him. “What’s wrong with our Meili? What’s wrong with dyeing her hair?”","Liang Ye stammered, unable to explain himself. “I’m just worried my mom will be frightened...”","If his mother was too shocked, wouldn’t it make things even harder for his brother and Meili?","He assumed that Meili was the one making greater sacrifices in this relationship.","It was only natural for him to think that way. The family business had long since been handed over to his brother, and among the second-generation heirs in Jiang City, his brother was at least in the top three when it came to wealth.","Not to mention that Liang Zheng was exceptionally handsome. A perfect man like him must have countless women hoping to date him.","Meanwhile, Meili had no education, no family background, no job, and no relatives...","It had never occurred to him that in this relationship, his brother was actually the one hoping to be truly taken into the other person’s heart.","Love had never been something that followed reason."]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: She Is Simply Herself","paragraphs":["Meili rubbed the tattoo on her arm. “This is what I look like. There’s nothing to hide.”","Even if she could cover it up for tomorrow’s meeting, could she really hide it for the rest of her life?","Besides, she and Liang Zheng weren’t even at that stage yet!","Why should she hide anything?","At worst, she just wouldn’t kiss him anymore!","A girl like her might look carefree, drifting through a field of flowers without a care in the world. But when it came to love, she was cautious and afraid to give her heart.","She was afraid of being hurt, and afraid that after gaining something, she might lose it.","When you had too little, you were especially afraid of losing what you did have. So afraid, in fact, that you could barely summon the courage to possess anything at all.","Her face showed no emotion—no anger, no anxiety. She merely glanced casually at Liang Ye. “This is what I look like. Bring your mother to see me if you want. She can look all she likes. I don’t charge admission.”","She was rarely this cold, and Liang Ye instantly found himself at a loss for words.","He looked at He Huanhuan as if pleading for help, hoping she could smooth things over for him.","But then he noticed that He Huanhuan was looking at him with a complicated expression too. She asked, “Liang Ye, are we friends?”","Without hesitation, Liang Ye nodded. “Of course we are!”","He Huanhuan said, “Friends aren’t allowed to look down on each other.”","“I wasn’t looking down on you! I—”","Liang Ye wanted to say that he hadn’t looked down on Meili. He just... he just didn’t want Meili and his brother to end up breaking up.","But suddenly, he couldn’t bring himself to say any of it. How was that not looking down on her?","He had placed Meili in the position of someone who needed to be judged and approved. That was why he had wanted her to make a good impression—to cover up her tattoos, dye her hair back to its original color...","He Huanhuan looked at him seriously. “Liang Ye, Meili and I have always been this way. If you want to be friends with people like us, then you have to accept us as we are. If you can’t, don’t come to the shop to hang out with us tomorrow.”","She and Meili were best friends. She already had friends; she didn’t need any who weren’t sincere.","With that, He Huanhuan pulled Qi Meili upstairs and left Liang Ye behind.","Despondent, Liang Ye climbed onto his electric scooter, unsure where to go.","He Huanhuan’s words echoed madly in his mind. He couldn’t help asking himself: Did he really accept them as they were?","Had he truly thought of them as friends?","He rode around like a lost soul until he reached the supermarket he often visited. That supermarket started discounting its products at eight every evening.","Heavy-hearted, he made his way to the discount section and picked up an eight-percent-off box of duck legs, along with a buy-one-get-one-free combo pack.","He was carrying the items to the checkout when a crisp female voice suddenly came from beside him. “Are you planning to eat all that tonight?”","Surprised, he turned and saw a young woman about his age pointing at the combo pack in his hands.","He shook his head. “Not tonight. I’ll eat it tomorrow.”","“Then don’t buy this combo,” the girl immediately told him. “The tofu will expire tomorrow. If you don’t eat it tonight, it’ll go sour by tomorrow. Come back tomorrow morning—the supermarket will separate the combo and discount the items again.”","She pointed at the roast duck in the pack. “The duck will be half price tomorrow morning. You should just buy the duck then.”","She sounded so certain that Liang Ye put the combo pack back. “Thanks.”","The girl waved dismissively with a smile. “See you tomorrow morning!”","She came every morning to check the discounts again. If Liang Ye came too, they would see each other.","Liang Ye didn’t even realize it, but he had just made a promise with a complete stranger.","He was a serious, earnest sort of person. Since she had told him they would meet tomorrow, he absolutely had to come to the supermarket. Otherwise, he would be breaking his word.","The next morning, he arrived right when the supermarket opened. Sure enough, he saw the girl waiting outside.","She was at the front of the line, and when she saw him, she smiled and waved.","As soon as the supermarket opened, the crowd surged inside like a flood. Before he could react, everyone had disappeared into the aisles.","By the time he reached the discount counter, all the discounted products had already been snatched up.","“You came so late. Of course you couldn’t get anything!” the girl’s bright voice rang out behind him again.","Then a half-price box of roast duck was held out in front of him.","He turned around in surprise. The girl’s eyes were full of laughter. “Luckily, I’m quick. I grabbed one for you!”","His heart began pounding wildly. He stood there dumbfounded, unable to say a word.","Seeing how foolish he looked, the girl’s smile deepened. She stuffed the roast duck into his hands and turned to leave. “Enjoy it! Bye!”","By the time Liang Ye came to his senses, she had already vanished.","He hurriedly began searching through the supermarket. Fortunately, luck was on his side, and he found her at the checkout counters.","He ran over and noticed that her cart was filled with discounted prepared foods—at least twenty or thirty boxes.","“Why did you buy so much? You won’t be able to finish all that, will you?”","When the girl saw him, she immediately smiled. “Oh, it’s you.”","She glanced at the prepared foods in her cart, her eyes filling with even more amusement. “I’m afraid it still won’t be enough.”","Liang Ye was puzzled. Did she have a huge family?","After paying, he followed her without thinking. He kept following until they left the supermarket.","He watched as she loaded everything onto her electric scooter, then prepared to ride away.","He wanted to follow her, but he also felt that doing so was inappropriate.","He stood there hesitantly, unsure what he should do.","Unexpectedly, after putting on her helmet, the girl turned to him and asked, “Why did you stop following me?”","His face instantly flushed red. “I—I’m not a pervert...”","“Haha...”","The girl burst out laughing. “Come on. I’m going to deliver these things. You can help me!”","Liang Ye’s eyes lit up at once. “Okay!”","He rode his electric scooter behind her into an urban village. The farther they went, the narrower and darker the streets became, and he couldn’t help feeling uneasy.","It was all his big brother’s fault!","If not for his brother and Meili’s relationship, he wouldn’t have been so careless as to follow a stranger here...","Oh no... He wasn’t going to get kidnapped, was he?","Just as his imagination was running wild, the electric scooter in front of him suddenly stopped. The girl took two boxes of discounted prepared food from a bag and pushed open a small door.","Liang Ye cautiously peeked inside. The room was tiny. There was a single bed, and on it sat an elderly man, hunched over with cloudy eyes.","The girl placed the food on a little stool beside the bed and called out loudly, “This expires tonight. You can’t eat it after it expires, so don’t save it for later, do you hear me? I’ll come by tonight. If you don’t eat it, I won’t bring you anything next time!”","The old man mumbled, “I know, I know...”","After speaking with him for a few moments, the girl got up and went to the next house. She continued until she had delivered all the food.","Liang Ye counted carefully. There were seventeen households in total, and the girl had brought food to seventeen elderly people.","He looked at her, unable to hide his admiration. “You’re a really good person.”","Then, somewhat dejectedly, he added, “If Meili were more like you, my mother would definitely approve of her.”","The girl asked curiously, “Who’s Meili?”","With all his pent-up frustration finally finding an outlet, he told her about his brother and Meili. “Meili is a really good person, truly. But she has a lot of tattoos, and her hair is dyed a really outrageous color. My mother would never accept her.”","He glanced at the plainly dressed girl. “If beauty looked like you, my mom would definitely accept you.”","He could tell that the girl didn’t come from a particularly well-off family.","She was wearing cheap canvas shoes, and her T-shirt hung loosely on her. Everything about her gave off an air of poverty.","But she was so kind and unpretentious.","Thanks to the way his grandparents had raised him, he instinctively believed that a girl like her was a good girl. If his older brother was in love with someone like this, his mother would be more inclined to accept her.","Unexpectedly, the girl burst out laughing. “You think I’m a good girl? But I have tattoos too, you know~”","She lifted the hem of her T-shirt, revealing a string of cat tattoos along her waist.","A teasing smile flickered in her eyes. “Am I a good girl now, or a bad girl?”"]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: This Is an Opportunity","paragraphs":["Liang Ye was a bit stunned. \"You... How come you also have a tattoo?\"","He never expected that a girl who looked so plain would actually have a string of tattoos on her body!","This was so strange.","The girl burst into laughter. \"Am I a bad girl now?\"","Liang Ye shook his head. \"You do good deeds. You're not a bad person.\"","The girl looked towards the urban village in the distance. \"I didn't do any good deeds. I lived here when I was a kid. All the grandparents here gave me food, so I'm just repaying them by bringing them food.\"","This didn't count as a good deed. It was just what she should do.","She looked at Liang Ye with a smile. \"Is your friend not a good person? You're not even closely related, but she was willing to help you when you asked her.\"","\"You're right. Meili is a very good person, but...\"","The girl waved her hand to interrupt him. \"But she has a lot of tattoos and dyed hair, right?\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"Yes...\"","The girl stroked her black hair. \"It's just about hair. What does it have to do with being good or bad?\"","She sized Liang Ye up. \"You're so old - fashioned. How boring. I'm leaving!\"","After saying that, she hopped on her electric bike and rode away without a single backward glance.","She rode so fast that Liang Ye didn't even have time to react, and she disappeared from sight.","He didn't even have time to ask for her WeChat!","Woo - woo - woo...","He felt as if a piece of his heart had suddenly gone missing. He had made her unhappy.","He didn't mean that. He didn't think that girls with dyed hair and tattoos were bad. He just...","Brother!","He had to go to his brother for comfort. It was all his brother's fault. Otherwise, he wouldn't have made that girl unhappy!","With tears in his eyes, he rode his electric bike to his brother's company. Liang Zheng had just finished a video conference. He was very surprised to see Liang Ye. \"What brings you to see me?\"","Liang Ye rarely came to the company because he couldn't stand his brother's office. It was so luxurious.","His brother's office was even bigger than Liang Ye's small apartment. It was such a waste! He felt heart - ache when he saw it.","But today, he didn't care about all that. When he saw his brother, tears streamed down his face. \"Brother, you've ruined me! It's all your and Meili's fault. If Mom didn't want to see Meili, I wouldn't have... She must think I'm a very bad person. Woo - woo - woo...\"","He cried so sadly and desperately, but his brother only had one thing on his mind. \"You said Mom wants to see Meili? When? How did Mom find out?\"","Liang Ye sobbed. \"Sister Yunzhi's mom took a picture of you two holding hands at the electric bike shop and sent it directly to Mom...\"","Liang Zheng's face darkened immediately. How could he have forgotten that He Yunzhi's mom was such a conservative person!","Liang Ye was still sniffling and crying. \"Brother, can you help me explain to her that I'm not old - fashioned...\"","His brother frowned impatiently. \"If you're not old - fashioned, then who is?\"","\"What?\"","The tears suddenly got stuck in his eyes. Liang Ye was completely stunned. \"Brother, why are you scolding me?\"","Liang Zheng frowned tightly. \"Why didn't you tell me first when Mom wanted to see her? Why did you put her in a difficult situation?\"","Liang Ye was a bit slow to react. \"I wanted to give Meili a heads - up...\"","Wasn't he thinking about Meili? Why was his brother unhappy?","Liang Zheng frowned even more. \"By going to her first, you're shifting the problem onto her to solve. Xiao Ye, you can't shift relationship problems onto girls. That's an irresponsible act.\"","Liang Ye was aggrieved. \"But...\"","Before he could explain, Liang Zheng asked him again. \"Xiao Ye, when you went to her, did you want her to change herself to please Mom and get Mom's approval?\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"Yes. I support you two.\"","He wanted to tell his brother that he definitely didn't oppose their relationship. He...","But then he heard his brother say, \"But this relationship is what I'm striving for. What you and Mom are doing will only make all my previous efforts go to waste.\"","\"Brother, what are you talking about?\"","Liang Ye's mind was in a mess. What was his brother talking about?","Was his brother pursuing Meili? Was that what he meant?","But how could that be? That was his brother! His brother was...","\"You're so old - fashioned. How boring...\"","The girl's words suddenly rushed into his mind. He was so old - fashioned and boring.","Yes, he was so old - fashioned.","Although he liked Meili as a friend, deep down, he thought Meili was far beneath his brother.","So he wanted Meili to change herself to please his mom and get his family's approval.","His eyes couldn't help but turn red again. \"Brother, I know why Huanhuan said that about me. I was wrong...\"","Liang Zheng walked up to him and ruffled his hair. \"It's good that you know. Go and apologize to them properly.\"","\"But what about Mom...\"","He didn't know how to tell his mom not to go and see Meili.","Liang Zheng gave a soft laugh. \"This isn't your relationship, so you don't need to worry about it. Leave it to me. I'll handle it.\"","After seeing Liang Ye out of the office, Liang Zheng sat still for a long time. He picked up his phone and put it down again, clicked into the chat box and exited it.","After a long time, he exited the chat box and turned off his phone.","He needed to take his relationship to the next level. This was a good opportunity, and he had to seize it.","Liang Ye had no idea what his brother was planning. With red eyes, he rode his bike to He Huanhuan's shop. As soon as he entered the shop, he started wailing. \"Huanhuan and Meili, I was wrong. I know where I went wrong. Can you stop being angry with me? I shouldn't have...\"","He closed his eyes and let out a long wail. Only after he finished did he open his eyes, waiting for forgiveness.","Instead of forgiveness, he was greeted by a camera pointed right at him.","Danmaku scrolled by one by one. \"What's this ordinary guy crying about? He's so whiny. I can't understand a single word.\"","\"I don't know. He suddenly rushed in and started crying. Is he a beggar?\"","\"Baby Huanhuan, give him a dollar. Don't mess with this kind of person. He might go crazy and be really scary!\"","\".......\"","Liang Ye felt like dying. How embarrassing!","He quickly squatted down and hid outside the camera's view. \"You're doing a live - stream. Why didn't you tell me?\"","He Huanhuan looked at the lively live - stream room and laughed so hard that her eyes were almost shut. \"Who knew you were so great and willing to sacrifice so much for the live - stream effect.\"","Meili was looking at the pre - sale links in the backstage. In just a few minutes, more than a dozen items had been sold. She said to him with a smile, \"You did a good job. Sister will generously forgive you.\"","She hadn't really blamed Liang Ye in the first place. They were all ordinary people. In the eyes of ordinary people, Liang Zheng was much more outstanding than her. It was quite normal for Liang Ye to hope that she would change.","Not to mention that Liang Zheng was his elder brother. The fact that he didn't jump up and oppose their relationship already showed that he had a friendly filter towards her.","Liang Ye squatted on the ground and smiled. \"Really? Are we still friends?\"","He didn't even notice that in his heart, he only regarded them as friends.","And those words about wanting to be with He Huanhuan had been completely forgotten."]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: Let's talk about it when it comes to marriage","paragraphs":["The next morning, the driver went to Liang Ye’s residential complex and picked him up.","In the car, Liang Ye glanced at Li Changxin and said cautiously, “Mom, try to be a little nicer when we get there...”","What if Meili got upset and ruined his brother’s chances of winning her back?","His brother was already a grown man. It wasn’t easy for him to find someone he liked.","Li Changxin had no idea that the brothers had talked things through the day before, much less that her own son had been the one pushing this relationship forward.","So she merely glared at Liang Ye. “I’m just going to take a look. How bad could my attitude possibly be?”","She had a gentle temperament and wasn’t the sort of person who picked fights with others.","Even if she didn’t like the girl after meeting her, at most she would go home and remind her son to think it through carefully.","Liang Ye fell silent. It was true that his mother had a good temper. But, Mom, Meili didn’t!","Meili had a terrible temper!","The car stopped a whole street away from the electric scooter shop. Li Changxin’s heart began pounding, and she hurriedly told the driver, “Stop here. This is fine, this is fine. I’ll get out and walk.”","Liang Ye looked out the window. “It’s still quite a walk.”","Li Changxin shot him a look. “Our car is too conspicuous. What’s wrong with getting out and walking a little with your mother?”","Before Liang Ye could answer, Li Changxin pushed open the door and slipped onto the roadside, hunched over like a cat, every inch of her exuding the air of a paparazzo.","But, Mom, their shop is at the next intersection. Wasn’t it a little early to start sneaking around?","He sighed helplessly and caught up with her. “Mom, could you stand up straight? You look like a thief.”","Li Changxin grabbed him and pulled him down too, turning them into two furtive little burglars. “Keep your head down. They already know you. And you’re not exactly handsome, so they’ll spot you at once.”","...","Liang Ye’s heart shattered. “Mom, didn’t you say I was very handsome?”","Li Changxin nodded perfunctorily. “Handsome, handsome. The more handsome you are, the more careful you have to be.”","...","After crouching and sneaking their way down the entire street, they finally saw the brightly lit electric scooter 4S shop at the corner.","Li Changxin hid behind a tree and cautiously peered toward the shop. Inside, there were lavender-purple, peacock-blue, pearl-pink...","Every girl in the shop had a head of wildly colorful hair. The sight made Li Changxin’s eyes ache and blur.","“Xiao Ye, help Mom figure out which one is blue.”","“Blue.”","Her presbyopic eyes frantically searched through the riot of colors. Blue, blue...","Where was the blue?","Oh. It was right in front of her.","Li Changxin stared in horror at the person standing before her: vivid blue hair, a vivid blue tattoo of a big fat cat on her arm—a very blue girl indeed.","Meili pulled her to her feet. “See, Auntie? I’m right here.”","Li Changxin stammered, unable to get the words out. “Well... I wasn’t here to look at you...”","Getting caught spying was incredibly embarrassing.","But Meili exposed her lie without hesitation. “Liang Ye already told me. Auntie, this is what I look like. I dye my hair, and I have tattoos. My family isn’t well-off either. My parents are divorced, and they’ve both remarried...”","She had nothing. But she didn’t think there was anything wrong with that, so there was no reason to hide it.","She had managed to raise herself into someone lively and cheerful. That was already pretty impressive, wasn’t it?","Li Changxin gave an awkward smile. “You’ve had a hard time, child...”","Meili nodded. “Mm. Auntie, are you done looking? I need to get back to work.”","Li Changxin hurriedly nodded. “Done, done... Go on, get back to work...”","Meili turned to leave, but someone suddenly seized her wrist, gripping it so tightly that she couldn’t break free.","She turned around in surprise—and saw Liang Zheng.","“You—you... why are you here?”","How had he ended up here?","Liang Zheng tightened his grip on her wrist, then stepped in front of her and looked sternly at Li Changxin. “Mom, you shouldn’t have come.”","For some reason, his arrival steadied Li Changxin’s nerves.","She straightened and looked at her son. “I just wanted to take a look. I didn’t mean to—”","Liang Zheng forcefully cut her off. “Why didn’t you ask me beforehand? Because you knew this was rude and intrusive.”","Li Changxin’s expression changed. “Zheng, I was worried about you...”","Liang Zheng lowered his eyes to Meili. “Mom, I’m not a child. At my age, I can make my own decisions about relationships.”","Meili could feel how resolute his gaze was as it rested on her. It was unmistakably firm.","A voice inside her told her: You’re done for. He’s chosen you without hesitation. You’re done for—you’re going to fall for him.","His grip around her wrist was tight, leaving her no room to pull away.","But she knew she didn’t want to.","In all her life, she had only been chosen so firmly twice.","The first time had been when He Huanhuan decided to be her friend. Back then, He Huanhuan had offended the school bullies and was cornered and harassed by them in the bathroom every day.","Meili had never been the type to meekly endure bullying, so she had taken the initiative to choose He Huanhuan.","She hadn’t even asked He Huanhuan’s permission. She had simply followed her with absolute determination. Wherever He Huanhuan went, Meili went too. Before He Huanhuan could even figure out what was happening, Meili had already dealt with the bullies for her.","The second time was now.","The man beside her spoke in a calm voice, as if he felt nothing in particular.","Yet his words made her heart race.","“I like her. I like her seriously—the kind of liking that means I want us to be together properly.”","Meili looked up at his stern, earnest face. For the first time, she wasn’t distracted by his handsome profile.","Did he really want to be with her properly?","Even if his family opposed them, would he still want to be with her?","As if she had heard Meili’s unspoken question, Li Changxin asked, “What if I don’t support you?”","Liang Zheng smiled faintly. “Mom, I’m not a child who relies on the family’s allowance to have fun. Your disapproval has no power to threaten me.”","Li Changxin grew angry. “But without the blessings of your elders, you won’t be happy.”","“Heh.”","Liang Zheng’s smile deepened. “Mom, do you really think that would stop me?”","Of course it wouldn’t. Li Changxin and her husband were not authoritarian parents. If Liang Zheng had decided to be with Qi Meili, then aside from swallowing their frustration and accepting it, what else could they do?","Well, they could pretend Meili didn’t exist.","But that sort of attack was easy to defend against. Liang Zheng could move out and live with Meili. If they didn’t interact, there would be no opportunity to hurt one another.","When elders disapproved of a relationship, everything depended on the couple themselves.","If he firmly chose you and stood by your side, he would never allow you to be treated unfairly.","Li Changxin was furious, but there was nothing she could do about him.","Her personality also made it impossible for her to jump up and berate Meili. So all she could do was glare angrily at Liang Zheng, then turn her even angrier glare on Liang Ye.","“Let’s go home!”","Liang Ye looked innocent. “Mom, why are you glaring at me?”","With nowhere else to vent her anger, Li Changxin gave it all to him for free. “You big mouth! You couldn’t even keep such a tiny matter to yourself! What can I possibly count on you for?”","Liang Ye cautiously asked, “Mom, have you accepted Meili now?”","Li Changxin climbed into the car with an irritated look. “What do I have to accept? Let the two of them date until they’re ready to get married first.”","Feelings are fickle—good today, bad tomorrow. Who knows whether they’ll stay together long enough to get married?"]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: At least it won't change for now","paragraphs":["This sudden predicament came abruptly and ended even more abruptly.","Before Li Changxin came, Meili had rehearsed several scenarios in her mind.","There was the intense version where she would storm into their store, causing chaos and looting, and then kick her flying with one powerful kick.","There was the verbal suppression version where she would scoff at Li Changxin, saying that a girl like her, a so - called \"cool girl,\" dared to have feelings for her son, and then mock that her son was the one chasing after her to kiss, which would make Li Changxin lose her temper.","There was also the idol - drama version where she would take out a check and let Meili fill it out at will. Then Meili would write 999999 on it, shocking everyone present.","She had thought of countless scenarios, but in each one, it was only herself dealing with these situations.","She would be invincible, bravely fighting back and knocking the person down with one punch.","However, her wrist was tightly held, and her whole body was enveloped by a warm and intense gaze.","She heard him whisper, \"Sorry.\"","\"Why are you apologizing?\"","His voice became even lower, \"Actually, I knew she was coming yesterday. She's my mom, and I could have called to stop her.\"","Meili's mind was a bit muddled. \"Then why didn't you call?\"","The hand that had been holding her wrist suddenly let go and then grasped her shoulder. His intense gaze met hers directly. \"Because I'm greedy. I hope we can get closer. I want to be with you, not just in a relationship where we only kiss.\"","She couldn't help but dodge his gaze. \"But you said we could take it slow...\"","\"I regret it.\"","His extremely handsome face moved closer to hers. \"I don't want to be a matchmaker, pairing you up with every good - looking person around you. I want an official status. Will you give it to me?\"","Their gazes intertwined fiercely, leaving her with nowhere to hide. \"I...\"","His big hand stroked her hair, and his breath surrounded her completely. \"I know what you're afraid of. What you want, I'll give it to you, definitely.\"","He had the ability to give her that sense of security.","The future was too uncertain, but at least for now, he truly liked her and was willing to give her everything he had.","Perhaps his eyes were too deep, and the words he said were extremely convincing.","She couldn't help but nod and reply, \"Okay, I'll trust you this time.\"","She felt a hint of coolness on her fingertips. Looking down, she saw a dark - blue diamond ring on her ring finger.","Liang Zheng smiled faintly. \"I originally prepared a pink one, but you changed your hair color these days. So I temporarily ordered a blue one. The color doesn't quite match your hair color. Don't dislike it.\"","Meili blinked. \"You ordered a pink one? What did it look like?\"","\"Want to see?\"","She nodded. \"Yes.\"","His big hand clenched in front of her eyes, and her heart tightened involuntarily.","Then he opened his palm, and it was empty. She wrinkled her nose and looked up at him. \"What are you doing?\"","Suddenly, a pink light flashed in front of her eyes. A large pink diamond ring strung on a thin, glittery chain was swaying in the air.","The rich pink color refracted countless gorgeous rays of light in the sun, indicating its high value.","Liang Zheng put the necklace around her neck. \"This one is very expensive. Wearing it means you're agreeing to be with me.\"","Meili instinctively took a step back, but it was too late. The cold touch hit her neck, and the necklace quickly hung around it.","She reached out to touch the pink diamond. \"How much does this cost?\"","Liang Zheng looked at the electric - bicycle shop across the street and smiled. \"It's enough to open seven or eight more shops like yours.\"","Meili's eyes widened instantly. Seven or eight shops?","This shop had cost He Huanhuan all her savings!","That was the money they had saved for buying a house. But unexpectedly, Gu Jingchen had paid for the house, so they took out the money to start this business.","Seven or eight shops like this? Didn't that mean it was worth more than ten million?","Liang Zheng looked at the girl in front of him with burning eyes. He deliberately told her the price of the diamond ring. He wanted her to know that money was a form of love.","He was willing to spend endless money on her, so he would also give her all his love.","However, instead of being touched as he had expected, the girl's face became paler and paler.","His confident heart couldn't help but feel anxious and insecure. \"Don't you like it?\"","\"Help me take it off... quickly...\"","Meili felt as if there were a thousand - jin weight on her neck, making her as stiff as cement. She couldn't even move, and it was difficult for her to breathe.","Oh no, what kind of normal person would wear a necklace worth more than ten million on the street!","But Liang Zheng obviously misunderstood her meaning. The certainty in his eyes was instantly shattered. \"Even if you don't like it, it's at least valuable. Keep it, okay?\"","\"Take it off first...\"","He didn't expect that Meili didn't even want to wear it for a moment.","His eyes fell on the pink diamond dejectedly. Was it not beautiful enough?","Or did she simply not like him?","He took off the necklace with a complex heart, and the pink diamond lay quietly in his palm. Maybe he was too impatient? Maybe...","The necklace was snatched away in an instant and tightly grasped in a small hand. Qi Meili glared at him angrily. \"Are you crazy! Why are you wearing such an expensive necklace around on the street! It's so dangerous!\"","If someone just casually took it off, she really wouldn't know what to do.","The light in his eyes suddenly shone brightly again. He reached out and held her hand. \"Then let's go inside the store and put it on, okay?\"","Meili glared at him again. \"Go to the second - floor lounge. It's too dangerous with people coming and going in the store!\"","He nodded smilingly. \"Okay.\"","But their clasped hands didn't separate again."]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: Finale (Goodbye, He Huanhuan)","paragraphs":["Meili and Liang Zheng were finally, completely together. A beauty addict and a certified beauty king were the ultimate match, and the two of them were so lovey-dovey that it was almost unbearable to watch.","With her heart completely opened, Meili would show off her enormous pink diamond to He Huanhuan whenever she got the chance. “Pretty, right? Want to borrow it for a couple of days?”","He Huanhuan couldn’t be bothered to indulge her. “No, thanks. Why would I wear the engagement ring that belongs to you two?”","Meili flashed her a sycophantic smile. “You can wear it. You can have anything of mine. Don’t you think Liang Zheng and I make a perfect couple?”","...","So that was what she wanted to hear!","He Huanhuan held the pink diamond ring up for a closer look. “If Old Man Gu ever saw this ring, he’d go crazy.”","If Gu Chengye found out that Liang Zheng had spent so much money on a diamond ring just to get Meili to agree to be with him, the old man would probably acknowledge Meili as his daughter overnight. Forget Gu Chacha and He Huanhuan—everyone else would have to move aside and let his beloved daughter Meili take center stage!","The thought made Meili laugh. “Then Gu Chacha would have one more assassination target to deal with. She’d be so busy!”","Mentioning Gu Chacha made them both sigh.","He Huanhuan asked Meili, “What do you think Gu Chacha is doing now?”","After Gu Chacha was sentenced, she completely disappeared from He Huanhuan’s life.","Jiang Yulan had tried to visit her in prison, but Gu Chacha refused to see her.","She refused to meet with anyone from the Gu family and completely cut ties with all of them.","Whether she was doing well or badly inside, whether she was suffering or adapting, had nothing to do with them anymore.","When her sentence was finally over, Gu Jingchen asked for He Huanhuan’s permission before driving to the prison to pick her up.","He hoped that five years in prison had made her understand her mistakes and that she could begin her life anew.","But he waited outside in the car for an entire day and never saw her.","After returning home, he asked around and learned that, because of her good behavior, Gu Chacha had been released more than six months earlier.","She hadn’t told anyone. She had left Jiangcheng quietly, leaving the country altogether.","For a long time afterward, they didn’t receive even the slightest news about her.","Then, several years later, Gu Jingchen went to the capital for an industry conference.","One of the executives traveling with him gave him a ticket to a performance by an overseas chamber ensemble. With nothing else to do that evening, he decided to go.","It was an ordinary performance—neither especially good nor especially bad, just somewhat dull.","Halfway through, he was about to get up and leave when the corner of his eye caught a familiar figure.","That figure quickly slipped out from backstage and hurried to the piano, replacing a pianist who looked unwell.","The performance continued soon afterward. Gu Jingchen silently sat back down and watched the slender figure at the piano, playing with complete concentration.","After the performance ended, he searched for the ensemble online. It was an Austrian group—not particularly famous in Austria, but frequently booked for performances.","He found the list of performers from that evening. Under the name of the pianist’s alternate was a name that looked vaguely familiar:","Alice Gu.","It was her.","After hesitating for a few seconds, he eventually stood up and went backstage. He spotted that familiar Eastern face easily among the crowd of white performers.","She was quietly removing her makeup, occasionally chatting and laughing with the people beside her.","Then she noticed Gu Jingchen behind her. Her expression froze for a second before quickly returning to normal.","Gu Jingchen called out, “Chacha?”","She didn’t even raise her eyes. “Sir, you’ve mistaken me for someone else.”","She wasn’t Gu Chacha. She was Alice Gu, a Chinese Austrian native.","Gu Jingchen wanted to ask how she had made it to Austria and how she had joined the ensemble, but asking those questions seemed pointless now.","He glanced at the person reflected in the mirror. Compared with the spoiled, willful girl she had once been, her eyes were much calmer.","Perhaps this was the best arrangement for everyone.","He shook his head and smiled. “Sorry. I must have mistaken you for someone else.”","Then he turned and left, disappearing completely from the mirror.","A colleague beside her looked curious. “Alice, friend?”","She shook her head. “Got the wrong person.”","That was right. He had mistaken her for someone else.","Two days later, a taxi quietly pulled to a stop across the street from the electric scooter shop.","Sitting in the back seat, Gu Chacha silently watched the brightly decorated storefront. He Huanhuan, now with light gray hair, was angrily lecturing a blonde-haired girl standing in front of her.","“Did you spend your wages on your boyfriend again?”","The girl shook her head firmly. “No way! Why would I spend money on a man?”","He Huanhuan’s expression darkened. “Then where did your money go?”","The girl looked guilty. “Well, I... Oh, come on, boss, stop asking!”","He Huanhuan glared at her. “You’re such a hopeless romantic! Don’t come crying to me later!”","The girl smiled ingratiatingly. “Um, boss, could you pay me last month’s commission early?”","Her boyfriend wanted to buy a new phone, and her commission was just enough to cover it.","He Huanhuan waved her off. “No! Commissions are paid every three months. No advances!”","“Come on, boss, please pay me! If I don’t buy him the phone, he’ll break up with me!”","“Then find yourself a handsome one afterward. Why are you wasting money on an ugly loser? Did you hit someone with your car and accidentally kill him?”","“...”","Gu Chacha quietly listened as He Huanhuan sternly reprimanded the girl until the girl finally responded in a pitiful voice, accepting the lecture.","A smile curved across Gu Chacha’s lips.","That family hadn’t been able to keep her, and it hadn’t been able to keep He Huanhuan either.","That was good. She had done what she wanted to do. And it seemed He Huanhuan had done the same.","She put on her sunglasses and said to the driver, “Sir, please take me to the airport.”","The taxi sped past the shop. Out of the corner of her eye, He Huanhuan caught a glimpse of the familiar-looking profile in the back seat. She frowned and thought about it for a moment, but couldn’t remember anything.","The two figures grew farther and farther apart beneath the speeding taxi, until they disappeared completely from each other’s worlds.","I’m sorry, He Huanhuan.","Goodbye, He Huanhuan.","[That’s the end! For now, this is where I’m going to stop the story. Since He Huanhuan is still too young, I don’t plan to have her and Han Mo become completely involved with each other. Sisters who mind that, please don’t come after me, hehe.","This is my first time writing a romance novel, so I don’t have much experience, and there are plenty of flaws. Recently, I’ve been studying hard to learn how good romance novels should be written. I hope to meet everyone again on the homepage very soon!","There will probably be another ten or twenty thousand words of bonus chapters, about Liang Ye, Meili’s married life, and He Huanhuan after she grows up, hehe~","But my author rank is too low! I might not be qualified to write bonus chapters!","I hope you’ll help me by giving the book a five-star review and sending a few free gifts. See you in the bonus chapters, and see you in my next book!]","The End."]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: Extra Chapter: Li Changxin's Dilemma","paragraphs":["Li Changxin was certain that Liang Zheng’s feelings for Qi Meili were nothing more than a passing whim.","The attraction that came from two different worlds colliding could only sustain a brief period of sweetness. It couldn’t last.","She couldn’t imagine what the two of them could possibly have in common. What could they even talk about?","Could Qi Meili understand stocks? Or could Liang Zheng appreciate those flashy tattoos?","But she waited and waited, year after year, until the two of them announced that they were getting married!","She objected. “You two aren’t from the same world. There’s no way this can last!”","Liang Zheng chuckled. “Mom, we’ve been together for three years, and our relationship is great.”","She broke down. “Three years is nothing! Can you stay together for thirty years?”","His smile grew even wider. “Then let’s find out together whether we can stay together for thirty years—or even longer.”","“You!”","Her objections had no effect whatsoever. All she could do was swallow her frustration and watch the two of them prepare for their wedding bit by bit.","When the wedding day finally arrived, she didn’t dare let her displeasure show. All the guests came from respectable families—what would it look like if she went around with a sour expression?","She smiled. She tried her best to smile. She wanted to cry.","Weng Meijuan even went out of her way to come up to her. “Sister Li, you’ve got some nerve. You can still smile at a time like this?”","...","Li Changxin ignored Weng Meijuan, but Weng Meijuan refused to let her off, hounding her relentlessly.","“At such a solemn occasion, she actually dyed her hair! What kind of behavior is that? If it were me, I certainly wouldn’t be able to smile!”","Today, Meili had chosen the most understated hair color she had ever worn: linen brown. It matched her wedding dress perfectly.","She had even suggested a long-sleeved wedding gown. In her own mind, she had already been very considerate.","But in Weng Meijuan’s eyes, even that little bit of consideration was practically the same as provocation.","Then Wenzhi walked through the door with highlighted ends in her hair, and Weng Meijuan’s vision went black. She nearly fainted.","“Wenzhi! Have you lost your mind? Don’t you know what kind of occasion this is? You’re making a fool of yourself!”","She abandoned Li Changxin and charged toward her daughter, which gave Li Changxin a huge sigh of relief.","Talking to that woman was exhausting.","To be honest, hardly any of the wedding guests believed that Liang Zheng and Meili were a good match. But who would be tactless enough to say so out loud?","It had nothing to do with them. They could just sit back and watch the spectacle.","Only Weng Meijuan had no filter—and an especially sharp, nagging tongue.","Meili had no family in this world, but that didn’t matter. Gu Chengye was more than happy to play the role of her temporary parent!","When it was time for the parents’ speeches, he delivered an impassioned address. He talked about how sensible the girl was, how difficult her journey had been, and how life was full of twists and turns beyond anyone’s control...","When he reached the emotional parts, he even wiped away a few tears. Anyone who didn’t know better might have thought he had truly witnessed Meili’s first twenty-some years of life.","Even Meili was left speechless. “When did I ever take beatings for other people and earn money?”","He Huanhuan, standing nearby, rolled her eyes. “That’s what I told him when I first got back. He assigned it to you!”","Whether Gu Chengye’s speech moved anyone else was impossible to say, but it left Li Changxin feeling thoroughly unsettled.","What kind of child had suffered so much in this day and age?","How had she even managed to grow up?","But sympathy was one thing. Li Changxin absolutely refused to accept her.","When the New Year came, it was customary to give the new bride a red envelope the first time she visited her husband’s family after the wedding.","Li Changxin spent the entire day muttering to herself that she had to give Qi Meili a proper warning with that first red envelope.","Jiye Liang was somewhat uneasy seeing how confident she was. “You’re already married into the family. Why make things difficult for her?”","If she really wanted to make things difficult, she shouldn’t have let them get married in the first place.","Now that they were married, they should simply get along.","Besides, the two of them didn’t even live at home after getting married. They only saw each other a few times a year. Why make things difficult for her for no reason?","But Li Changxin ignored him completely. “I’ve already made all the arrangements. Stay out of it!”","Although Jiye Liang didn’t agree with her, he didn’t say anything more while his wife remained so determined.","After all, deep down, he didn’t approve of Meili either.","On the morning of the first day of the Lunar New Year, Liang Zheng brought Meili to the Liang family home bright and early.","Li Changxin gave Meili a cold look. “You’re here?”","Meili nodded. “Yep.”","Li Changxin took a thick red envelope from her bag. “It’s customary to give the new bride a red envelope during her first visit to the family home after the wedding. This is for you. Take it.”","Meili obediently accepted the red envelope. They had a meal together, and then she and Liang Zheng left...","Jiye Liang waited for quite a while but never saw the troublemaking Li Changxin had promised. Unable to hold back, he asked, “Didn’t you say you were going to give her a warning? Where was it?”","Li Changxin let out a cold laugh. “I gave her one hundred thousand yuan!”","When giving the new bride a red envelope during her first New Year visit, people did it to bring good fortune.","Usually, they gave 99,999 yuan, symbolizing everlasting happiness and longevity.","But not her. She had given Meili 100,000!","At the mention of it, her voice was full of smug satisfaction. “I’m not blessing them! I gave her a nice, round one hundred thousand!”","Jiye Liang: ...","How, exactly, was that supposed to make things difficult for her?","Li Changxin shot him a warning look. “You’re giving her one hundred thousand too on the fifth day. No 99,999. Do you hear me?”","Jiye Liang was speechless. “I wasn’t planning to give her anything!”","The two of them had already given her one red envelope together. That was more than enough. Why should he give her another?","But Li Changxin refused to hear it. “You’re supposed to give one on the fifth day! That’s the day we welcome the God of Wealth. What kind of behavior is it if you don’t give her one?”","...","Jiye Liang wanted to ask how she could possibly call herself difficult when she was being this generous.","Even the God of Wealth himself wasn’t as easygoing as she was!"]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: Extra: Liang Ye's Love","paragraphs":["Liang Ye felt that something was wrong with him. He could no longer focus on work, and even the juiciest gossip failed to hold his attention.","Like the homeowner whose father-in-law used a bamboo pole to steal the neighbor’s underwear, only to get himself stuck hanging between the balconies and fracture a few ribs...","Or the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law who had been at odds for years, until the daughter-in-law lost her temper and poured pig-fattening medicine into the family’s water tank...","He wasn’t interested. Not interested at all.","He couldn’t stop thinking about that girl from the supermarket. After dwelling on her for several days, he finally couldn’t take it anymore.","He camped out at that supermarket for two whole days before finally spotting her coming to buy discounted vegetables.","He dashed over to her. “Hi! You’re here to buy discounted vegetables too?”","The girl glanced at him. “Do we know each other?”","Liang Ye’s heart shattered at those words. She didn’t remember him at all!","“I—I’m the roast duck...”","He brought up the crucial keyword, hoping it would jog her memory.","But the girl remained completely impassive. “What roast duck? Are you the roast duck chef at the supermarket?”","“No, no...”","Liang Ye felt so wronged that he could have cried. “I’m the one who wanted to buy that roast duck set last time, and you said it wasn’t worth it...”","The girl still showed no reaction. He looked so pitiful that he was practically on the verge of tears.","“I came to apologize. I shouldn’t have judged Meili like that. She’s a really, really good person. I shouldn’t have assumed she was a bad person just because she had tattoos and dyed hair...”","He poured out his apology in one breath. Once he was done, he turned around to leave.","He had originally wanted to ask for her WeChat, but since she didn’t even remember him, asking for it would be far too abrupt.","Forget it. He’d just go home. He’d never eat roast duck again. Sob, sob...","Unexpectedly, just as he turned around, he heard the girl laugh behind him.","“So, you know you were wrong?”","His eyes instantly lit up. “You remember me! You do remember me, right?”","The girl flashed him a brilliant smile. “Of course I remember you. You’re the idiot who doesn’t know how to buy discounted vegetables.”","Liang Ye nodded foolishly. “I’m not as good at it as you. Hehe...”","And just like that, he and the girl became friends. He chatted with her about supermarket discounts, Pinduoduo deals, and everything else under the sun.","The girl seemed to know everything. Vegetables should be bought online when they were in season, and directly from their source: garlic shoots from Henan, green beans from Shandong, mangoes from Sichuan...","No matter what it was, she could always get the best quality for the lowest price.","In the short half a month since meeting her, Liang Ye had been having the time of his life shopping!","Such a great deal! So satisfying!","He felt that he had fallen in love with her!","His admiration had blossomed into love. He was attracted to her strength!","He wanted to be with her—to buy cheap goods for the rest of his life!","After spending several days thinking long and hard at home, he finally made that momentous decision.","First, he called He Huanhuan.","“Huanhuan, I’m not going to pursue you anymore. I’ve found my soulmate. She’s so much better at saving money than you...”","He Huanhuan was stunned. “When did you ever pursue me?”","Wasn’t that harassment?","Purely verbal harassment!","Liang Ye ignored her. “Anyway, from now on, we’re friends. The purest kind of friends!”","He Huanhuan wanted to tell him that her purest friends were Meili first, her second brother second, and Han Mo—who wasn’t entirely pure—third.","The line of people ahead of Liang Ye would stretch all the way down the street.","But it didn’t matter. Second Young Master Liang’s greatest talent was his confidence.","After explaining things to He Huanhuan, he felt that he was finally, completely free.","So the very next day, he went to confess to the girl.","“Gu Xue, I like you. Let’s be together!”","Gu Xue kept her head down, inspecting the discounted vegetables. She didn’t even spare him a glance.","“No.”","Liang Ye was dumbfounded. “Why not? Don’t you like me?”","Gu Xue placed the vegetables she deemed suitable into her shopping cart one by one.","“I’m not in a position to date right now. Maybe when my financial situation improves.”","She couldn’t abandon the grandparents. She needed to earn money so they could enjoy a better old age.","But she wasn’t particularly capable. She could only work ordinary jobs, using her limited income to buy as many things as possible at the lowest prices.","She simply didn’t have the means to date—not even if she...","Even if she liked Liang Ye.","Yes, she did like Liang Ye.","He was the first man willing to patiently sit with her and study every possible discount.","She wasn’t especially beautiful, but she was fairly pretty. It wasn’t as though no men had ever shown interest in her.","But those men’s intentions were always obvious: they wanted to get married, and she seemed perfectly suited to be a wife.","In their eyes, she wasn’t a woman or a beloved partner. She was a product.","A cheap, practical product that could be taken home and put to use immediately.","She found it ridiculous. Because she was good at buying cheap things, those men assumed she would make an ideal wife and pursued her.","But the moment she introduced them to the grandparents, every one of them ran away faster than the last.","Only Liang Ye stayed.","Not only did he stay, he studied discounted vegetables with her and helped her deliver food to the grandparents. He was also very good at chatting with them.","Her life was difficult. All those hardships weighed heavily on her, leaving her unsure what to talk about with the grandparents.","But Liang Ye was different. His job at the neighborhood committee was easy, and although it didn’t pay much, he was spiritually well-off.","He could chat with the grandparents about anything and everything, making them laugh and keeping them entertained.","Liang Ye had said that he, too, had been raised by his grandparents. She figured that although his circumstances were somewhat better than hers, he must have his own difficulties as well.","She liked him, but she couldn’t be with him.","Her life was truly hard. She didn’t want to become a burden to him.","So it was better to forget it."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: Extra Chapter: The Lover Who Can't Be Driven Away","paragraphs":["Gu Xue had originally thought that after she turned him down, Liang Ye wouldn’t come looking for her again.","But when she arrived at the supermarket the next morning, she spotted that big, beaming smile from far away.","“Xiaoxue! Come here! I got the first spot in line!”","His smile was simple and pure, as if he had never confessed to her and she had never rejected him.","Somewhat awkwardly, she walked over. “Why did you come here today?”","She knew he lived alone. The evening discounts were already enough to get him by, so there was no need for him to get up early.","Yet he had still come. Why?","Wasn’t he angry?","Liang Ye naturally wasn’t angry. A little rejection like this was nothing to him.","Back when He Huanhuan wouldn’t even pay him any attention, he had still managed to keep himself entertained for several months.","Not to mention that Xiaoxue clearly had feelings for him. There was no way she could simply ignore him.","As long as she gave him the slightest bit of encouragement, Second Young Master Liang could stay happy for the rest of his life!","Grinning, he held his phone up in front of Gu Xue. “Look at this wheelchair. It’s electric. We can buy it for Second Grandma, and then she’ll be able to go outside.”","Gu Xue glanced at the screen. “It’s too expensive.”","“What? No way!”","Liang Ye tapped into his saved items and carefully compared the prices. “I searched all night. This is the cheapest one!”","Gu Xue tried her best not to look at him. “Reserve it, but don’t check out yet. The platform will recommend cheaper ones to you.”","Liang Ye’s eyes lit up once again. “Xiaoxue! You’re so good at shopping! You’re a genius!”","Gu Xue gave a bitter smile. What was so genius about her? She was simply too poor.","He didn’t know how difficult life was for poor people, which was why he thought she was a genius.","“Liang Ye, I don’t like you.”","She repeated those words once more. Liang Ye nodded vigorously. “I know. Didn’t you say that last night?”","His calmness left Gu Xue at a loss. “I said I don’t like you...”","Liang Ye smiled. “I know that now, so I’m going to pursue you! Until you fall in love with me, accept me, and agree to be with me!”","Gu Xue was a little dumbfounded. This wasn’t how things were supposed to go.","She was supposed to reject him, and Liang Ye was supposed to get angry and think, With conditions like yours, what makes you think you have the right to reject me?","You’re not even some stunning beauty with amazing qualifications!","If he had treated her that way, she would have known exactly how to respond.","She would have jumped up, slapped him, and told him to get lost.","She was much more familiar with that sort of process.","This situation, however, left her somewhat unaccustomed.","Unable to hold back, she asked, “But what if I never fall in love with you?”","Liang Ye grinned. “Then I’ll keep pursuing you!”","Pursuing someone was something he was very good at!","“But I have a lot of grandparents to take care of.”","Liang Ye nodded. “We’ll take care of them together! I like buying discounted groceries!”","“But my salary isn’t high, and I can’t save any money each month.”","Liang Ye beamed. “I own a house outright! After you marry me, you won’t have to rent anymore! That’ll save us money!”","“But...”","There were still countless buts in her heart, but Liang Ye wouldn’t let her continue.","“Everything you’ve mentioned is an objective condition, Xiaoxue. I’m asking about your heart. Do you like me?”","Gu Xue hesitated. “I—I do like you, but...”","“Then there are no buts! As long as you like me, there are no buts!”","Liang Ye was so excited that he practically vibrated with enthusiasm.","“Xiaoxue! We can take care of your grandparents together. You’re worried about housing, but I have a house, so we won’t have to pay rent in the future. I also have a salary, and we can keep buying discounted groceries. None of these are problems!”","Gu Xue nodded. “I know, but this isn’t fair to you. Without me, your life would be so much easier...”","“Heavens!”","Liang Ye grabbed her by the shoulders. “You have no idea how much better my life has become since I met you!”","Before, he wouldn’t even let himself buy whatever he felt like eating. Ever since he met Gu Xue and learned how to hunt for bargains across the internet, his life had practically taken off like a rocket!","It was wonderful!","People online often said that a stubborn, conflicted person needed a lover who refused to be driven away.","Gu Xue couldn’t exactly be called conflicted, but Liang Ye truly was impossible to get rid of.","He stubbornly stayed by her side, accompanying her and clinging to her until she had no room left to refuse him.","Eventually, she simply went with the flow, moved in with him, and began dating him."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: Extra: Meeting the Parents","paragraphs":["Gu Xue had been living with Liang Ye for over a year, yet she knew very little about his family.","She had never met Liang Ye’s older brother, much less his parents.","She had always felt that Liang Ye’s family didn’t seem to like him very much. They never came to visit him.","Liang Ye often spoke fondly of his late grandparents. She knew he had been raised by them.","He also talked about his brother a lot, saying that his brother was dating one of his friends—a girl who sold electric scooters.","He had also mentioned that his parents didn’t like his brother’s girlfriend...","So, in Gu Xue’s mind, Liang Ye was probably just a kid from an ordinary family.","His brother had a regular job and was more successful than Liang Ye, who worked at the neighborhood committee, so their parents favored the older brother and didn’t care much for Liang Ye.","She also knew that the brother’s girlfriend worked as a saleswoman at an electric scooter shop. Liang Ye’s parents disliked the girl, thinking her circumstances were too poor...","Gu Xue figured Liang Ye’s parents probably wouldn’t like her, either.","Her circumstances were just as bad. She had nothing, too.","Well, no—she had a whole lot of grandparents to look after.","That was why she only lived with Liang Ye and never brought up meeting his family or marrying him.","She didn’t want to be put through the wringer, and she didn’t want to get into ugly fights with his elders.","Until one day, Liang Ye suddenly said to her, “Xiaoxue, how about coming home with me to meet my parents?”","Gu Xue’s heart lurched. “What did you say?”","Had that day finally come?","Liang Ye, completely unaware of what was going through her mind, merely grinned and asked, “It’s my mom’s birthday today. Why don’t we go celebrate with her?”","Life with Gu Xue had been so blissful that he’d barely had time to pay attention to his family.","If it hadn’t been his mother’s birthday, he might not even have remembered to tell his parents that he had a girlfriend!","Heh heh heh...","He had decided that, on this auspicious occasion of his mother’s birthday, he would bring Gu Xue home to meet the family!","Gu Xue hesitated, but she didn’t know how to refuse.","After all, they had been living together for quite some time. Meeting each other’s parents was only natural.","But...","Forget it. She had to face it sooner or later.","She nodded. “All right.”","When the electric scooter pulled up to the Liang family estate, Gu Xue was dumbfounded. “W-Where is this?”","Liang Ye leaned close to her ear and whispered a complaint, “Over-the-top, right? My parents are so wasteful. Let’s not be like them, okay?”","Once they entered the estate, Gu Xue was even more stunned, to the point that she didn’t know what to say.","For the first time in her life, she learned that the gates of a rich person’s home could be so far from the actual house!","They had to ride the electric scooter for more than ten minutes!","Along the way, they passed countless housekeepers and servants. Whenever they saw Liang Ye, they warmly greeted him, “Welcome home, Second Young Master.”","Liang Ye nodded at them as naturally as could be. “Yep, I’m back to celebrate my mom’s birthday.”","“Auntie Li, don’t turn the water up so high when you’re watering the flowers. What a waste of water!”","“Uncle Zhao, you’re using setting two again! Setting one is enough for weeding. You’re wasting electricity!”","“...”","What a bizarre scene. Gu Xue suspected she’d gotten food poisoning from discounted mushrooms.","What? You say king oyster mushrooms can’t poison you?","Then what was all this supposed to be? If she hadn’t been poisoned, how could she possibly be here?","It wasn’t as if she were starring in some rich-girl Cinderella drama!","When the electric scooter stopped in front of the house, Liang Ye led her into the beautiful mansion, where she saw Li Changxin and Jiye Liang sitting on the sofa...","Only then did she finally come to her senses.","Good heavens! Liang Ye really was a rich second-generation heir!","A very, very rich one!","How could this be?","He looked so unassuming!","She had assumed Liang Ye’s parents would be extremely picky and give her a hard time, but they didn’t.","They merely glanced at her before smiling and beckoning her over. “You’re Xiaoxue, right? Come sit down. Xiao Ye really is something—if we hadn’t asked, he wouldn’t even have told us he was seeing someone...”","The warmth and kindness in their voices caught her completely off guard. Where was the difficult in-laws routine she’d been expecting?","Hadn’t people said his parents disliked poor people?","She remembered that Liang Ye’s parents had strongly disapproved of his older brother’s girlfriend. So why were they being so kind to her?","It wasn’t until she saw the beautiful woman who had entered with Liang Zheng that she finally understood what people meant by “tattoos and dyed hair.”","This wasn’t the tiny string of tattoos around her waist. These were large, eye-catching tattoos, accompanied by an entire head of strikingly dyed hair.","What an uninhibited girl. What a... unique girl.","She was sitting beside Liang Ye when the girl walked straight over to her and asked with a broad smile, “Are you Liang Ye’s girlfriend?”","She nodded. The girl immediately threw an arm around her. “You’re pretty good-looking! So why is your taste so unusual? You only like ugly guys?”","She: “...”","Liang Ye: “...”","The married couple, Li Changxin and her husband: “...”","Liang Zheng, however, laughed openly. His little brother really was rather ordinary-looking. Meili wasn’t wrong."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: Extra: The Stingy Shopaholic","paragraphs":["Ever since meeting Liang Ye’s parents, Gu Xue had been feeling a little light-headed with happiness.","His family was incredibly wealthy, while his parents and older brother were all so down-to-earth and approachable.","And because they knew Liang Ye was stingy, his older brother had secretly transferred a sum of money to her.","“Liang Ye is such a cheapskate. He hates spending money on girls, so keep this money and spend it yourself. Don’t tell him,” his older brother had said.","Gu Xue had never held so much money in her life.","She felt like she was about to float away. She wanted to buy things. She wanted to spend money.","But she was used to living frugally and couldn’t bring herself to spend big.","So she ended up heading in a rather peculiar direction. Pinduoduo had one defining feature: the more you bought, the more cheap products it recommended.","The more it recommended, the more you bought.","The more you bought, the more it recommended, and the more it recommended, the more you bought...","She could never finish collecting all her packages.","That evening, she once again dragged an entire cartload of deliveries home. Liang Ye looked both excited and tormented.","“Xiaoxue, what is all this this time?”","“Rice and storage containers.”","Gu Xue buried her head in the packages as she opened them. “Soft fragrant rice normally costs five yuan per half-kilo, but a few days ago the app gave me a huge coupon. Ten yuan for five kilos. What do you think? Should I buy it?”","Liang Ye nodded without hesitation. “Buy it!”","Then he frowned. “But there really isn’t any room left in the house...”","Ever since Gu Xue had started going crazy buying things on Pinduoduo, his tiny one-bedroom apartment had been stuffed full within days.","Now, whenever he came home, he had to ballet-dance his way inside.","On tiptoe~ lifting the hem of his trousers~","There really was no room left, no room at all!","But everything was so ridiculously cheap. Not buying it would practically be a crime!","Gu Xue opened all the packages. Each bag held five kilos, and she had bought thirty bags—the largest quantity required to get the lowest price.","She looked up at Liang Ye. “Why don’t we send some to your older brother and your parents? That way they won’t have to buy expensive rice themselves, and we’ll be helping them save money.”","Liang Ye’s eyes lit up instantly. “That’s right! We can help Mom, Dad, and my brother save money!”","And so, the two of them went completely wild with their Pinduoduo shopping.","Twenty pretty cups at the best bulk-discount price? Buy them!","Five pairs of export-quality shoes at the best bulk-discount price? Buy them!","Ten rolling stools at the best bulk-discount price? Buy them!","Once there was no room left in the apartment, they would haul out a huge woven sack, load it up, and deliver everything to Li Changxin’s house or to Liang Ye’s older brother.","Every delivery earned them another sum of money. Once they had money, they bought more things; after buying more things, they delivered them; after delivering them, they got more money; and with the money, they bought even more...","They bought so frequently, and in such enormous quantities, that Li Changxin developed a headache whenever she saw them.","“There really isn’t anything else we need at home. Stop sending us things...”","They delivered things so often, and in such bulk, that her house became a complete mess, looking more like a warehouse than a home.","She no longer even dared to go shopping, afraid there wouldn’t be enough room to put anything.","But the two of them simply refused to listen. Gu Xue looked solemn. “Mom, I still have a few Yukihira saucepans on the way. I’ll bring you two once they arrive.”","Liang Ye checked his orders. “I bought several large rugs. Mom, don’t buy any more rugs, okay? The ones you buy are all way too expensive! It’s a complete waste of money!”","...","Li Changxin suddenly felt that Qi Meili was wonderful. Absolutely wonderful!","At least Qi Meili didn’t buy things for her, pile things up in her house, or come over to bother her.","She just wanted to go out shopping and buy whatever caught her eye. How could such a simple, wholesome hobby be taken away from her?","Now, whenever she went out and saw a pretty cup or dish, Gu Xue and Liang Ye’s faces immediately appeared in her mind.","“Mom, that’s way overpriced. We can get it on Pinduoduo for ten yuan. You’re not allowed to buy it.”","“Mom, that shop of yours that sells leftover export orders? I can lock in the order three times on Pinduoduo and get it for ten percent of the price.”","“Mom, that brand’s factory has flawed items. We can buy the defective ones for only twenty yuan.”","“Mom...”","Good heavens!","Someone come and take these two away!"]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: Extra: Han Mo's Dream","paragraphs":["Han Mo had a dream. In the dream, he went to a county with a relatively poor economy.","In the dream, he was extremely lucid, so lucid that it didn't seem like a dream.","He was very certain that this county had never appeared in the first two decades of his life. He couldn't understand why he would dream about this county.","Until he saw a familiar face. The face was very young, with a head of light - blue hair, and the exposed arms were covered with large - area tattoos.","The most eye - catching were the two forearms. One had a blue Doraemon tattoo, and the other had a yellow SpongeBob tattoo.","It was exactly the same as the tattoos on Qi Meili's arms.","Instantly, the words He Huanhuan had said before popped into his mind: \"Buy one get one free. Then I have to choose the larger area ones!\"","He looked down at the young face, which was a bit younger than when he first knew her. She looked only fifteen or sixteen years old.","She was also more fierce than when he knew her. Her face clearly showed that she was not to be messed with.","He tentatively called out to her, \"He Huanhuan?\"","He Huanhuan was really annoyed. Qi Meili was so unreliable. They had agreed to meet at the cross - road of Beijing Road at ten o'clock this morning.","She had already waited for half an hour! And Qi Meili still hadn't come!","She would never believe her nonsense again!","She didn't have a mobile phone, so she couldn't even find someone to talk to!","She had noticed Han Mo on the roadside for a long time. In their small county, it was hard not to notice someone dressed so neatly in a suit.","What a poser!","Until the man in the suit turned around and called her, \"He Huanhuan?\"","Her eyebrows frowned instantly. \"What do you want?\"","All the young people in the so - called \"cool kids\" circle knew that she didn't like middle - aged men. So no one would usually introduce her to others for no reason. How did this guy know her?","Could it be...","Damn it! Could he be a debt collector?","Her eyes instantly widened. \"Your grandfather! I didn't spend a single cent of the money He Dayong borrowed! Stop coming to me for money! I have no money! But I have a life! If you have the guts, kill me!\"","As she spoke, her eyes darted around.","Han Mo thought she was going to run away. Unexpectedly, after looking around, she picked up a brick and pointed it at Han Mo. \"Get out of here, you poser! Otherwise, I'll smash your head open!\"","...","Han Mo remembered what Qi Meili had once said, that He Huanhuan was a bit of a big shot in their \"cool kids\" circle back then.","At that time, he didn't believe it. He thought that no matter what, He Huanhuan was so cute, and even if she was a \"cool girl\", she would be of the cute type.","Unexpectedly, she used to be so... well, \"cool\".","Especially with those tattoos all over her body, she was the epitome of \"cool\"!","He coughed twice. \"I'm not a debt collector.\"","He Huanhuan's eyes widened even more. \"Then what do you want? Speak up!\"","Han Mo was silent for a moment. \"Well... I'll transfer some money to you?\"","He remembered that He Huanhuan had said she used to be very short of money. Although this was just a dream, he still wanted to transfer some money to her so that she wouldn't have to worry about money.","Unexpectedly, He Huanhuan raised the brick even higher. \"I don't have a mobile phone! How can you transfer money? You poser!\"","...","\"Then I'll buy you a mobile phone?\"","He Huanhuan immediately threw the brick away. \"Handsome guy, you're so nice!\"","Five minutes later, the two of them arrived at the nearest mobile phone store. Han Mo pointed at the most expensive phone in the store. \"Let's get this one.\"","But He Huanhuan waved her hand. \"Just buy the cheapest one.\"","Han Mo shook his head. \"It's okay. I have money. The expensive one is better.\"","He Huanhuan gave him a disdainful look. \"My dad will steal the expensive ones! He won't steal the cheap ones!\"","...","In the end, they bought the cheapest mobile phone, which only cost three hundred yuan.","Han Mo took out his phone to pay. This dream was incredibly real. Even the details like the shop owner scanning the QR code to receive money were so vividly fabricated.","After paying, Han Mo subconsciously said, \"Do you want to add me on WeChat?\"","\"Add your dad! You old pervert!\"","Suddenly, the girl beside him threw out a curse, then turned around and ran away, disappearing quickly!","Han Mo was stunned. Did He Huanhuan think he was a pervert?","He looked at the shop owner in surprise. The shop owner shrugged. \"It's a deal. I don't refund money.\"","At the end of the street, He Huanhuan looked at the new mobile phone in her hand and burst out laughing. \"No wonder they all like to take advantage of middle - aged men! The money comes so fast!\"","That pervert, that poser, wanted to hit on her?","Today, she would let him know the truth from Zhang Wuji's mother: the prettier the woman, the better she is at lying!","Humph!"]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: Extra: Han Mo's Dream 02","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan took a detour and made her way to the intersection at Beijing Road. At last, she spotted the long-overdue Qi Meili, and immediately flew into a rage.","“You’ve got some nerve showing up! Why didn’t you just come tonight? You... Hey, what happened to your eye?”","When she got closer, she saw that Qi Meili’s eye was swollen black—a solid, inky bruise that clearly came from someone’s fist.","Her anger flared instantly. “Damn it! Who hit you? I’ll call someone to hack him to death!”","Qi Meili waved her off nonchalantly. “I already hit him back.”","Her father had been cheating, and she’d caught him in the act. She’d called her stepmother over to catch them red-handed, only for her stepmother to turn around and blame her, accusing her of ruining their marriage.","That had made her so furious that she’d beaten up both of them.","She rubbed her eye. “I didn’t mean to be late. You don’t have a phone, or I would’ve told you.”","“I have a phone now!”","He Huanhuan waved her new phone around proudly, showing off to Qi Meili. “Look! My new phone! Isn’t it awesome?”","Qi Meili was stunned. “Where’d you get the money to buy a new phone?”","She knew He Huanhuan’s situation better than anyone. Whenever He Huanhuan managed to get her hands on a little money, her father always found some way to squeeze it out of her. How could she possibly afford a phone?","He Huanhuan grinned. “I scammed it out of some old guy!”","She told Qi Meili how she’d tricked Han Mo into giving her the phone. “That poser clearly wanted to pick me up. Did he really think I’d let him? What a joke! I...”","As she spoke, Qi Meili’s expression suddenly changed.","Unable to help herself, He Huanhuan asked, “Why do you keep blinking? Does it hurt?”","Qi Meili looked past her with a pained expression. “When you say ‘poser,’ do you mean a guy in a black suit, kind of old but still pretty handsome?”","He Huanhuan nodded. “How’d you know?”","Qi Meili pointed behind her. “Because he’s standing right behind you!”","He Huanhuan instantly jumped. “Crap!”","She spun around. Han Mo stood beneath the streetlamp with his arms folded, smiling as he asked, “I only wanted to add you on WeChat. Why did you run?”","He Huanhuan glared at him. “You’re too old! I don’t play with old men!”","He Huanhuan was only fifteen at the time. To her, Han Mo, who was in his twenties, really did count as an old man.","Han Mo sighed and turned away. “Fine. I was going to treat you to a bowl of spicy hot pot...”","“Wait!”","“Hold on!”","Two ravenous voices sounded behind him almost simultaneously, and the smile in Han Mo’s eyes grew impossible to suppress.","He put on a stern face and turned back around. “What is it?”","He Huanhuan swallowed. “You’re really treating us to spicy hot pot?”","Meili glanced at his handsome face and swallowed too. “I want to sit next to you while we eat!”","Han Mo nearly laughed out loud. “I really am treating you, but you can’t sit next to me.”","Anyone who didn’t know the situation might mistake him for some kind of pervert.","They picked the nearest spicy hot pot shop. He Huanhuan and Qi Meili steeled themselves and selected fifty yuan’s worth of ingredients.","The two of them whispered to each other, “Take more. If we can’t finish it, we’ll pack it up and eat it at home tonight. Let’s enjoy ourselves for once!”","Once they had everything, He Huanhuan shoved the bowl into Han Mo’s hands. “Go pay.”","The shop required customers to pay before eating, which was the only reason she dared come here with him.","What if he turned out to be a bad guy who ran off without paying after they finished? Then she and Meili would be completely screwed!","After paying, their spicy hot pot arrived soon afterward.","The two girls were too busy eating to talk. They buried their heads and dug in.","Only after the hunger in their stomachs had completely disappeared did He Huanhuan finally have time to look up at Han Mo.","“Why do you keep staring at me?”","This guy was seriously weird. Why did he keep looking at her with that smile?","Did she have flowers growing on her face?","Han Mo shook his head with a smile. “Nothing. I just didn’t expect your tattoos to look like that.”","They were quite intimidating, but also rather cute.","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes at him. “Dumbass!”","He was being so sarcastic. What did her tattoos have to do with him? Were they bothering him?","He was asking to be insulted!","The moment she finished cursing him, Han Mo handed her his phone. “Scan this and add me as a friend. I’ll transfer you some money.”","He Huanhuan frowned. “Why are you trying to give me money again? What are you up to?”","These days, who just offered to transfer money to a stranger?","Her face scrunched up. “You’re not planning to harvest my kidneys, are you?”","Han Mo shook his head helplessly. “I just want to give you some spending money.”","“That doesn’t make sense!”","He Huanhuan firmly refused to take the money. “I don’t even know you. Why are you giving me money? What do you want?”","“Can’t you just think of it as the heavens dropping a pie on your head?”","He Huanhuan immediately covered her head. “In all my life, the heavens have only ever dropped rocks on my head. They’ve never dropped pies.”","...","Han Mo truly hadn’t expected that he wouldn’t even be able to spend his money.","He turned to Qi Meili. “How about I transfer some to you?”","He knew the two girls were close, and that Meili would spend money on He Huanhuan whenever she had any.","What he didn’t expect was for Qi Meili to wipe her mouth and give him a lecherous smile.","“I’ll take your money if you let me kiss you.”","...","Han Mo was speechless. “I’m giving you money, and I still have to let you kiss me?”","Qi Meili looked perfectly justified. “What? Am I not worthy of kissing you?”","Han Mo rubbed his temples. “I’m afraid the vinegar jar at your house will come and tear my company apart.”","Liang Zheng was absurdly jealous. He wished he could get rid of every good-looking man around Meili.","If he found out that Meili had kissed Han Mo in a dream, he might charge straight into the dream and rip Han Mo’s mouth apart.","Han Mo turned to He Huanhuan. “Aren’t you two short on money? Why are you refusing when I’m trying to transfer some to you?”","He Huanhuan leaned away from him. “Because you don’t look like a good person!”","What good person wore a black suit around a county town for no reason?","What a poser!","Han Mo asked, “Then what do I have to do to look like a good person?”","He Huanhuan thought about it, then stretched out her arm. There was still one bare patch on her wrist.","“Go get a tattoo with me. Then I’ll believe you’re a good person!”","...","In the end, he still followed the two girls to a tattoo parlor.","The moment the owner saw He Huanhuan and Qi Meili, he shouted, “You two! You still haven’t paid for your tattoos from last time!”","The two girls pointed at Han Mo in perfect unison. “He’ll pay!”","The owner stared at them in surprise. “You two have started scamming old men too?”","Han Mo helplessly pulled out his phone. “They’re not scamming anyone. We’re relatives, so don’t talk about them like that.”","After paying off the money the two girls owed, He Huanhuan pushed him in front of the owner. “He wants a tattoo. Hurry up and give him one.”","The owner stared at Han Mo in shock. His suit was perfectly tailored, and he clearly looked like a successful professional.","Did someone like that get tattoos too?","Han Mo thought to himself that this was only a dream anyway. Getting a tattoo wouldn’t hurt.","Still, he chose something quite conservative. He held out his wrist to the owner.","“Just two small characters will do.”","The owner asked casually, “What characters?”","Han Mo glanced at He Huanhuan.","“Just tattoo ‘Huanhuan.’”","He Huanhuan was stunned for quite a while before finally realizing what he meant.","“Why are you tattooing my name? Don’t you have a name of your own?”"]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: Extra: After the Dream Awakens ~ Jealousy ~","paragraphs":["Han Mo had been having a rather wonderful dream, and when he woke, the corners of his mouth were still turned up.","He opened his eyes and stared at the ceiling. He never would have guessed that the young He Huanhuan in his dream had been so reckless.","That was good. A fiercer personality meant she wouldn’t get bullied.","Remembering the vivid pain from the dream, he smiled and rubbed his right wrist.","A familiar twinge of pain suddenly crawled across his wrist, and the smile froze on his lips.","What was going on?","His gaze quickly dropped to his wrist. Two slightly blurred Huan characters were unmistakably visible on his skin!","That hadn’t been a dream!","It was...","He had really met He Huanhuan! The young He Huanhuan!","He practically sprinted to his car and drove to He Huanhuan’s apartment complex as fast as he could.","He Huanhuan had just woken up. With her head drooping, she leaned over the sink and brushed her teeth.","“Why haven’t scientists invented one-click toothbrushing yet? Why do we still have to brush our teeth ourselves when it’s such a trivial task? Why?”","Someone suddenly pounded hard on the door. She casually swallowed the toothpaste foam and went to open it with her mouth still covered in suds.","“Han Mo? Why are you here so early?”","Han Mo stared at her intensely. His eyes were full of excitement—and were they... red?","There were too many emotions for her to make sense of.","“What’s wrong with you?” she asked.","Han Mo fixed his gaze on her. “Huanhuan, I saw you!”","He Huanhuan licked the foam from the corner of her mouth. “Isn’t that obvious? I’m standing right in front of you!”","If he hadn’t seen her, wouldn’t that mean he was blind?","Han Mo shook his head excitedly. “Not the you from now! I saw the you from when you were little! You at fourteen or fifteen!”","He Huanhuan was speechless. “Are you still half-asleep? How could you possibly have seen me when I was fourteen or fifteen? I was living in my hometown county back then!”","She had transmigrated into a novel, okay?","Back then, the distance between her and Han Mo wasn’t just four or five years. There was an entire book between them!","“It was you!”","Han Mo firmly held out his hand. “Look. I got your name tattooed in my dream. You were the one who told me to do it. This is proof.”","On his wrist, the two faintly reddened Huan characters were clear as day.","He Huanhuan’s eyes widened. “You dog, Han Mo! You cheated on me after just one night apart?!”","...","Han Mo held his wrist right in front of her. “What characters are these?”","He Huanhuan: “Huanhuan.”","Han Mo: “And I cheated on you by tattooing that?”","He Huanhuan let out a cold laugh. “Who knows whose Huanhuan it is! There are plenty of Huanhuans in this world—He Huanhuan, Zhao Huanhuan, Li Huanhuan... Who knows which one you had tattooed?”","...","Han Mo helplessly recounted everything that had happened in the dream. “...It really was you. I took you and Meili out for malatang, and Meili even said... You said that anyone with a tattoo was a good person...”","He spoke with such conviction, but He Huanhuan didn’t believe a word of it. “You’re talking nonsense! That phone of mine was...”","She wanted to say that she had bought the phone herself, but suddenly she couldn’t remember when she had bought it in the first place.","And where had she gotten the money to buy it?","She racked her brain, but no matter how hard she tried, she couldn’t remember.","It was as if the phone had appeared out of thin air. One moment she hadn’t had one, and the next she did.","Could it really have been Han Mo?","She eyed Han Mo suspiciously, then glanced at the Huanhuan on his wrist.","“Meili! Do you remember this?”","She turned to ask Meili. Qi Meili shook her head without hesitation. “You’ve got to be kidding! How could I possibly have wanted to kiss Han Laodeng? I’m a very reserved person, okay?”","He Huanhuan’s eyes instantly widened. “See! Even Meili says it’s impossible! So which Huanhuan did you get tattooed for?!”","..."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: Extra: Endless Jealousy","paragraphs":["Qi Meili had been feeling strangely listless lately. In all her life, she had never felt this drained. Her arms and legs felt soft and weak, as if her entire body had turned to rubber.","She was a little frightened. “I don’t have some terminal illness, do I?”","The thought made her feel even weaker. “Huanhuan! I must have a terminal illness! Sob, sob, sob... I knew happiness was never meant for me!”","That was how it always happened on TV. Someone who had been unhappy since childhood would finally find happiness, only for something terrible to happen to them!","She had even married Liang Zheng. Of course she was going to die!","She didn’t want to die!","“Huanhuan! I don’t want to die! I still want to be your best friend forever! Waaah!”","Overcome with emotion, she burst into loud sobs, leaving He Huanhuan in a panic. Huanhuan hurriedly took her by the hand and comforted her. “Meili, don’t be scared. I’ll take you to the hospital. You’ll be fine. I’m sure you’ll be fine...”","If she was sick, they would treat her. They had money now, and Huanhuan would take her anywhere in the world for treatment if necessary.","After they arrived at the hospital and Meili underwent a battery of tests, she was completely stunned.","“I-I’m pregnant? How is that possible?”","He Huanhuan jumped up excitedly. “Holy crap! Qi Meili, you’ve created a human life! You’re amazing!”","Doctor: ...Why did that sound like anything but a compliment?","After reminding them of the precautions they needed to take, the doctor called for the next patient.","The two women supported each other as they walked into the lobby. Qi Meili rubbed her belly. “Holy crap! I’m about to give Earth a brand-new human being!”","He Huanhuan nodded furiously. “Meili! You’re the mother of Earth! You’re incredible!”","The two of them celebrated the good news while spouting complete nonsense, until a voice came from behind them.","“He Huanhuan?”","They turned around to see a somewhat familiar handsome face standing behind them in a white coat. He Huanhuan looked confused.","“Who are you?”","Meili was thrilled. “A handsome guy! What a handsome guy!”","Seeing that they hadn’t recognized him, Qi Yuan smiled. “My younger brother and I bought one of your travel packages a few years ago. Do you remember?”","The moment he mentioned it, the two women instantly remembered.","“It’s you! The Good Doctor!”","The handsome doctor who had taken them on a video tour of Sawa!","Qi Meili immediately sidled up to Qi Yuan. “Handsome doctor, long time no see! Are you married? Do you have a girlfriend? If not, I’d love to take you out to dinner sometime~”","She was pregnant!","And pregnant women needed to look at handsome men more often so they could give birth to a good-looking baby!","Qi Yuan chuckled. “It’s been several years, but your personality hasn’t changed at all.”","She still loved hitting on handsome men. He glanced at the two of them. “Why are you at the hospital? Are you feeling unwell? Do you need any help?”","Meili giggled. “We do, Doctor! I’m about to give birth to a new human for Earth, and I feel so tired. I need to look at a handsome man a few more times to soothe my exhaustion~~”","Qi Yuan was surprised. “You’re married?”","Behind him, Liang Zheng came out of the consultation room supporting Li Changxin, and happened to hear that exact question.","His expression darkened instantly. Li Changxin hadn’t seen Qi Meili and assumed he was worried about her. “It’s just my old problem. I’ll be fine after resting at home for a few days...”","Liang Zheng supported her as they headed in the opposite direction. “It’s good that it’s nothing serious. Getting it checked out puts our minds at ease...”","That night, the young couple lay in bed. Liang Zheng reached out to pull Meili into his arms, but Meili shoved him away.","“No!”","The doctor had said no sex during the first three months!","No matter how badly he wanted it, he had to hold back!","The scene from earlier that day flashed through Liang Zheng’s mind, so he asked, “I took Mom to the hospital today. Do you have a friend there? I think I saw you.”","Meili nodded. “Yes! He’s a handsome guy! Guess who he is? He’s the one who bought a travel package from Huanhuan and me back then...”","With a cheerful grin, she told him all about her connection with Qi Yuan and the story of how they had met. The more Liang Zheng listened, the worse his expression became.","No wonder he hadn’t been able to find them at the hotel in Sawa. So she had gone to wait for that doctor!","His heart was filled with all kinds of emotions, but he suppressed every one of them properly and didn’t let a single trace show.","Three days later, Qi Yuan was shocked to discover that he had somehow been added to the exchange list for Capital XX Hospital!","It was an extremely rare opportunity: he would be able to study at Capital XX Hospital for six months at the hospital’s expense. After he returned, it would also be much easier for him to earn a promotion in rank.","Opportunities like this depended heavily on connections. He had applied for three years without ever being selected.","He clearly remembered that he had been rejected again this year, so he had no idea why he had suddenly been chosen.","Still, it was a good thing. Without a second thought, he handed over all his work and set off for the capital with complete focus.","By the time Meili returned to the hospital for her prenatal checkup, he was already in the capital.","She had even wanted to get another look at him, but she ended up missing him completely. Can you believe it?","But her desire to see a handsome man was urgent. It wasn’t that she herself wanted to look—this was all for the baby in her belly!","So she set her sights on the idle Gu Jinghan and summoned him to the hospital with a single phone call.","Gu Jinghan hadn’t even gotten out of bed yet. When he received the call, he assumed something had happened to her and rushed to the hospital in such a panic that he didn’t even have time to put on a shirt.","When he saw her, her second brother was terrified. “Meili, what happened? Did Liang Zheng hit you? Your brother absolutely refuses to tolerate domestic violence...”","Meili beamed. “I’m pregnant! The baby wanted to see a handsome man, so hee hee hee...”","...","Gu Jinghan was speechless. “Why didn’t you just explain that over the phone?”","He had come all the way there without even putting on a shirt!","Meili looked at his firm, well-built body and smiled even more brightly. “You look better without one!”","If she weren’t already married, she would definitely have reached out and felt him up a couple of times.","After the examination, Gu Jinghan drove her home.","Halfway there, they happened to run into Liang Zheng on his way home. Gu Jinghan quickly drove ahead and called for him to stop.","The car window rolled down, revealing Gu Jinghan’s shirtless upper body and a thoroughly exhausted expression.","“Come get your wife already! She’s completely worn me out!”","Liang Zheng: ...","Let’s all die together!"]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: Extra: Didn't I Say That I Probably Forgot","paragraphs":["Liang Zheng had recently fallen into an appearance crisis. He had always believed that as long as he maintained his looks and figure, Meili would never cheat on him.","But he had overlooked one thing: age.","Gu Jinghan was indeed younger than him. And youth was a real asset.","That night, he lay in bed while Meili was engrossed in her phone, not even sparing him a glance.","Come to think of it, the two of them had gone almost a whole week without being intimate.","They had only just gotten married, and she was already tired of him.","In a low voice, he asked Meili, “What are you looking at?”","“Handsome men, of course!” Meili replied without even looking up. “Looking at handsome men is good for the eyes!”","Let the baby look at more handsome men. That way, the baby would grow up good-looking and have good taste, too!","It would be best to have a beautiful daughter, so she could admire handsome men together with her when she grew up!","Ah, how wonderful!","But all Liang Zheng heard was: Looking at handsome men is good for the eyes.","Did he no longer even serve the purpose of being easy on the eyes?","Well, that was how a face fanatic was. Once they got what they wanted, they stopped cherishing it.","So whom was she cherishing now?","Gu Jinghan?","That second-generation heir who was determined to latch onto a rich woman?","Hmm?","His thoughts instantly snapped back into place, and the corners of his lips curved into a smile.","Wasn’t Gu Jinghan determined to find himself a rich woman?","Then Liang Zheng would find him one—a rich woman who would keep him too busy to bother his Meili.","The next day, after finishing all his work, Liang Zheng sat in his office and began screening candidates with an exceptionally serious expression.","Every single unmarried female CEO on the domestic rankings was investigated. He had people dig up all the gossip surrounding them.","Their looks and personalities, their preferences in a partner, their attitudes toward romance...","Every detail was carefully sifted through, under Brother Liang’s personal supervision.","Until...","Liang Zheng looked at the woman’s profile in the email and smiled.","Song Tingyun, thirty-four, the Song family’s third child from Guangnan.","She had two older brothers. Last year, she had suddenly emerged to take the positions of chairwoman, general manager, and legal representative of Yuejia Group.","With a 31.5 percent stake, she had become Yuejia’s actual controller.","One of her brothers had moved to Canada last year, while the other had settled in Spain this year.","There was clearly quite a story behind it all.","Her capabilities were undeniable.","Most importantly, she had once dated a man overseas who came from a poor family, only for her family to forcibly break them up.","Liang Zheng looked at the photograph of the couple. The woman had a bold, strong appearance, with full features and clear, bright eyes.","She was tall and strikingly capable.","The man had upturned outer corners to his eyes and a faintly careless smile on his lips.","There was a relaxed, languid quality between his brows, along with a hint of innocent boyishness.","Liang Zheng pulled up a photo of Gu Jinghan and placed it beside the man in the photograph.","Their noses and mouths were three-tenths alike, their eyes and brows five-tenths alike. Add in that touch of innocent boyishness, and they instantly looked seventy to eighty percent similar.","Interesting.","He glanced at an event announcement on Yuejia’s official website, then took out his phone and called Gu Jinghan.","“Are you busy these next few days? If not, go to Guangnan for me. There’s something I need your help with...”","Three days later, at a closed-door real estate summit, Song Tingyun listened to the same tired platitudes and frowned impatiently.","Those old men, so old they were practically crumbling, were spouting clichés just as stale. It was unbearably boring.","Her gaze drifted lazily around the venue, trying to find something amusing enough to pass the time.","Then she saw a face—a young face that looked every bit as bored as she felt...","Her eyes stopped instantly. From that moment on, she could no longer look away.","Liang Zheng’s favor only required Gu Jinghan to help for a single day, but Gu Jinghan ended up staying in Guangnan for nearly half a month without returning.","By then, Meili was making unhappy little noises at home.","“Why isn’t Second Brother coming back? I don’t even have a handsome man to look at anymore!”","Liang Zheng smiled faintly. “He won’t be coming back anytime soon.”","Meili was puzzled. “How do you know?”","Liang Zheng sat down beside her. “Is he really that handsome? Isn’t looking at me enough?”","Meili pushed him away. “You’re too handsome! Looking at you makes me lose my head! I’m not even three months pregnant yet. It’s dangerous!”","Liang Zheng froze.","“What did you say? Pregnant? You’re pregnant?”","Meili blinked at him with her innocent, wide eyes.","“Didn’t I tell you? Maybe I forgot.”","..."]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: Extra: I'll Help You Fight Back","paragraphs":["Han Mo and He Huanhuan had made an agreement: everything would have to wait until she turned twenty.","As the final month arrived, he practically counted down the days.","He had gone over countless versions in his mind—how exactly he should confess to her.","Should he take her to a candlelit French restaurant? Or book out a spicy hotpot skewer shop, wave grandly, and tell her, “Take whatever you want. Eat as much as you like...”","That night, he lay in bed, staring at the calendar on his phone as he silently crossed off another day.","Three days left. In three days, He Huanhuan would turn twenty.","Then they could officially be together.","Their relationship was already steady, and in practice, being officially together would not change much.","But he still wanted to give her a proper moment. He wanted to confess to her sincerely, to tell her that he liked her—that his eyes and his heart held no one but her.","Closing his eyes, he thought: What kind of confession would He Huanhuan like?","Something romantic, or...","As he thought, his consciousness gradually grew hazy, his eyelids drifting shut.","When he opened his eyes again, he found himself standing on a muddy country road. A light rain drizzled from the sky, and from the far end of the road came faint, muffled sobs.","“Fuck their grandmas! They bullied me—I’ll kill them...”","The voice drew closer and closer. Then a small figure, blazing with fury, appeared before him. She looked barely ten years old, not even tall enough to reach his chest.","The little girl wore two messy braids and clutched a chipped kitchen knife in her hand.","Her face was streaked with scratches, red and raw—clearly the kind made by long fingernails.","The country road was narrow. When she charged up to him, she shouted furiously, “Move!”","A scorching rage surged in his eyes. He stepped directly into her path, staring fixedly at the scratches on her face.","“Who hit you?”","He Huanhuan looked up and glared at him. “Who are you? What business is it of yours?”","She held the kitchen knife across her body and faced Han Mo. “A good dog doesn’t block the road! Get out of my way!”","She was going to hack those idiots to death!","No one was allowed to bully her!","She, she, she... sob, sob, sob...","After she killed them, she would go to prison. When she got out, she would still be filial to Grandpa and Grandma...","She tried desperately to suppress the grievance and fear in her heart, but the tremor in her eyes betrayed her.","Han Mo reached out and gripped the battered kitchen knife, asking quietly, “You were bullied, weren’t you?”","That single question made her eyes turn red at once. Tears began streaming down her face. “Who are you? What does my business have to do with you?”","What was the point of asking all these questions? Even if he knew, he would not help her.","No one had ever helped her. She had long since accepted that reality.","But Han Mo tightened his grip on the knife. “Tell me. I’ll help you. I promise I’ll help you.”","Her tears came even harder. She clearly did not know this person, yet she could not stop herself from trusting him.","“It was those eighth-graders. They demanded protection money from me. I didn’t have any, so they beat me...”","The more she spoke, the more wronged she felt, until she could no longer get a full sentence out.","“I fought back, but there were so many of them... I couldn’t beat them...”","Remembering the helplessness of being pinned down and beaten moments ago, she could no longer hold it in. With a wail, she burst into loud, heartbroken sobs.","Han Mo’s heart clenched painfully at the sight of her crying. He knew He Huanhuan had suffered in the past, but he had never known she had suffered this much.","Hadn’t she found Qi Meili to protect her?","Where was Qi Meili?","Why wasn’t she here?","He bent down and gently wiped the tears from her face with his sleeve. “Don’t cry. I’ll take you back there and get even.”","Her tears stopped at once. He Huanhuan looked up at him with red-rimmed eyes. “Really?”","Han Mo nodded solemnly. “Really.”","“But...”","He Huanhuan hesitated. “A man who hits women isn’t a good man...”","If he helped her, wouldn’t that mean he was hitting women?","Wouldn’t that make him a bad person?","Her little mind couldn’t quite make sense of it.","Han Mo reached out and patted her head. “I’ll have someone else hit them.”","He took the kitchen knife from her and asked, “Where’s Qi Meili? Why didn’t you go to her?”","He Huanhuan looked utterly confused. “Who is Qi Meili?”","So she didn’t know Qi Meili yet. No wonder she had been bullied.","He took her hand. “Come on. I’ll take you to find someone to get even with them.”"]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: Extra: Just Follow Her","paragraphs":["He took He Huanhuan to the county town and wandered around the streets. As they wandered, the grievance in He Huanhuan's heart vanished, leaving only confusion. \"What are you doing?\" she asked.","Wasn't he going to find someone to help her get revenge?","Why were they just wandering around in front of the spicy hotpot restaurant?","She was so hungry from all this wandering that he didn't even take her in to have a bowl.","He looked decent, but why was he so stingy?","She couldn't help but suspect that this guy might be unreliable.","Could he... be a human trafficker?","At this thought, her pupils dilated in shock!","Damn it!","He must be!","She lowered her head and her eyes darted around.","Forget about revenge, she'd better focus on saving her own life first!","Her eyes fixed on Han Mo's thigh, and she madly calculated in her mind how high she should lift her leg to kick him hard and knock him out!","She tried to gather her strength. She tried and...","\"Here she comes,\" Han Mo said, reaching out and pushing her, instantly ruining her little plan. She looked at him blankly and asked, \"Who's coming?\"","A faint smile curled up on Han Mo's lips. \"Qi Meili,\" he replied.","She was her guardian angel.","In the distance, Qi Meili came strutting over, humming a song with her bright yellow hair standing out. \"Poor little cabbage in the field is yellow. With a step - mother, you get a step - father. Miser! Only gives me three yuan. Can't afford a bowl of spicy hotpot...\"","Her current look was extremely terrifying. Her golden hair was permed into a huge mess, her eyes were outlined with thick, all - around black eyeliner, and there were a dozen chains hanging around her neck. You could knock someone out with just one of them.","Han Mo pushed He Huanhuan towards her. \"Find her. She can help you get revenge,\" he said.","He Huanhuan was a bit scared. \"But she looks even less like a good person!\"","However, Han Mo didn't give her a chance to back out. He firmly led her to stand in front of Qi Meili.","Qi Meili glanced at He Huanhuan first, with disdain in her eyes. \"Kid, get out of the way if you don't want to get beaten up.\"","Then her gaze shifted upwards to Han Mo. \"Oh! A handsome old guy!\"","...","Qi Meili was only fourteen or fifteen at this time, so to her, Han Mo was indeed a middle - aged uncle.","Han Mo got straight to the point. \"Do you want to eat spicy hotpot?\"","Qi Meili nodded without hesitation. \"Yes! I haven't eaten all day. I'm starving!\"","Han Mo took off his watch and handed it to her. \"I'll treat you to spicy hotpot for a year if you help me with something.\"","Qi Meili looked at the watch. \"Is it 4:30 pm?\"","...","She didn't even recognize the Patek Philippe watch. She thought Han Mo was asking her to tell the time.","This time when he entered the dream, he didn't have his phone on him, only the watch he was wearing. It had come to this place with him.","Across the spicy hotpot restaurant was an old - fashioned shopping mall, and beside the mall was a small - fronted luxury goods and gold recycling store.","Han Mo pointed to the storefront and told Qi Meili, \"This watch is very valuable. If you sell it second - hand, it can at least pay for your spicy hotpot for a year. Do you want it?\"","Qi Meili frowned. \"What do you want to do?\"","She felt like he had something up his sleeve.","A year's worth of spicy hotpot was like a dream life!","Was he really just giving it to her?","Could he have done something wrong and wanted her to take the blame and go to jail?","Han Mo pushed He Huanhuan in front of her. \"She was bullied. You help her get her dignity back.\"","Qi Meili didn't believe it. \"Just this?\"","Han Mo nodded. \"Just this.\"","Qi Meili didn't really trust him, but her stomach was growling and her mouth was watering for spicy hotpot. So she followed him to the recycling store half - believingly.","The store owner was a greedy guy. Taking advantage of the fact that there were no competitors in this small place, he managed to price the watch, which was originally bought for over five hundred thousand yuan, down to fifteen thousand.","Han Mo was worried that the dream might end at any moment, so he didn't bother to bargain with the owner. He just asked him to pay in cash quickly.","After getting the money, he immediately took out a stack and gave it to Qi Meili. \"Here.\"","Qi Meili was shocked. \"Oh my god! It's really money!\"","Then he stuffed the rest of the money into He Huanhuan's hands. \"Hide it and spend it. Don't let your dad find out, or he'll steal it.\"","He Huanhuan looked at the money in her hand, a bit dazed. \"Why are you being so nice to me? We don't even know each other!\"","Han Mo wanted to reach out and touch her, but suddenly he felt his body lighten.","He quickly turned to Qi Meili and sternly told her, \"You took the money. You must help her get revenge. Do you hear me?\"","Qi Meili was counting the money one by one. One, two, three, four...","Damn it! She couldn't count them all!","She was rich!","Hahaha!","Beat someone up? Hahaha! It's a piece of cake!","She continued counting. One, two, three, four, five, six, seven...","Han Mo felt his body getting lighter. He quickly leaned over to He Huanhuan's ear and whispered, \"You should follow her from now on. She'll protect you.\"","He Huanhuan blinked, looking a bit scared. \"What if she doesn't want to?\"","\"Then just keep following her. After a while, she'll get used to it.\""]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: Extra: Together Forever","paragraphs":["At first light, Han Mo opened his eyes in bed. His hand instinctively reached for his wrist, only to find it empty—the watch was gone.","A smile tugged unconsciously at the corners of his lips. He thought, I really did help her back then, didn’t I?","The muddy country road from his dream came back to him, along with the old brick house at the end of it. In an instant, he remembered a house from long ago.","And he remembered what He Huanhuan had once said: “This house looks quite a bit like my old home...”","He thought he knew how to confess his feelings to her now.","Three days later.","Today was He Huanhuan’s twentieth birthday in the spiritual sense, and she had been looking forward to it all day.","She had never forgotten their promise: once she turned twenty, she and Han Mo could officially be together.","Now she was truly twenty—in every sense of the word.","It was a workday, and the shop was quiet. Resting her chin in her hand, she let her imagination run wild.","“Meili, what kind of surprise do you think Han Mo is going to give me?”","“Do you think he’ll land a helicopter right outside the shop and fly me off to one of those islands owned by foreigners...”","“Or maybe he’ll just transfer a few billion to me and say he’ll take care of me for the rest of my life?”","“And then there’s...”","Qi Meili couldn’t be bothered to answer. “Do you think a few billion can just be transferred at the drop of a hat? Watch fewer cheesy short dramas!”","He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose with a grin. “Then he can do what he did for you—give me two huge diamonds.”","Qi Meili nodded. “That, he could manage.”","Preferably in different colors, so the two of them could trade them back and forth. That would be much more practical!","But He Huanhuan waited and waited until the sky grew dark.","Forget a helicopter—even her BYD never showed up.","It wasn’t until they closed the shop and were getting ready to go home that the familiar beat-up car finally rolled to a stop by the roadside.","Han Mo looked slightly exhausted as he apologized to her. “Something came up at the company. I just finished dealing with it. Have you had dinner? If not, I’ll take you somewhere to eat.”","He Huanhuan was furious!","He had actually forgotten what day it was!","She glared at him, cheeks puffed out. “I’m not eating!”","Han Mo got out anyway and opened the passenger-side door. “But I haven’t eaten yet. Come have dinner with me, okay?”","“I’m not...”","She refused angrily, but Meili hurriedly poked her. “Go with him! Older men love pulling this kind of thing. He’s definitely got a surprise planned! I swear!”","Her husband, Liang Zheng, loved doing this sort of thing.","Whether it was a surprise or a present, he always insisted on putting it after a period of disappointment and anger, using the emotional whiplash to heighten the excitement.","People really did get like that with age.","He Huanhuan cast Meili a suspicious glance. “Really?”","If that was true, then she supposed she could temporarily put aside her anger...","Without another word, Meili pushed her toward the car. “Absolutely true! Go already!”","Once they were in the car, Han Mo still didn’t say anything. He simply asked his usual questions: what she had done that day, whether anything had happened at the shop, what she wanted to eat...","But her heart began to race despite herself.","This wasn’t the road into the city!","He really had prepared some kind of ridiculous surprise!","Hahahaha!","Her heart was practically soaring with excitement—until the car stopped somewhere completely unexpected.","She stood in front of a dark, dilapidated house, stunned.","“Isn’t this the place where we secretly lived after your car accident?”","Han Mo smiled and nodded. “It is. I bought it. From now on, it belongs to us.”","...","He Huanhuan was speechless. “What am I supposed to do with this thing?”","It was so old and run-down!","She turned to Han Mo and demanded, “How much did you pay for it?”","Smiling, Han Mo pushed open the door and led her into the pitch-black room. “The money doesn’t matter. What matters is that this place holds our memories. That’s precious, isn’t it?”","He Huanhuan wanted to say, Precious my ass!","Money was obviously more precious!","But when the moonlight filtered through the broken roof and spilled across the room before her, she couldn’t bring herself to say any of it.","“Ah...”","She let out a groan. “This is not the kind of proposal I wanted! It’s not romantic at all!”","Who wanted to be proposed to in a house this shabby?","It was seriously so shabby!","“This isn’t even as good as Meili’s! At least she got two huge diamonds!”","“There are.”","Beneath the scattered moonlight, a large diamond ring shimmering with dazzling colors appeared before her eyes.","Han Mo lowered his head to look at her, his eyes filled with tender affection.","“Do you remember when we first met? Your hair was dyed all sorts of colors. I spotted you at once...”","“Really?”","Han Mo nodded. “Really.”","How could he not have? She had been so eye-catching, so flamboyant.","He placed the ring in her hand.","“Huanhuan, I’m a very boring man, yet I fell in love with someone as bold and dazzling as you. Will you be with a boring man like me? Forever?”","He Huanhuan had imagined their confession countless times. She had pictured every possible scenario.","But never words this specific.","A solemn request to be together.","The answer was clearly on the tip of her tongue, yet she didn’t know how to say it.","Her eyes began to sting. Instinctively, she broke the solemn mood.","“Meili got two diamonds. Why do I only get one...”","She didn’t really want two diamonds. She simply felt a little unsettled, as if her heart hadn’t quite found its place.","“There are.”","Han Mo nodded seriously. Then, as if performing a magic trick, he pulled a dazzling diamond necklace from behind his back.","“Anything you want, you’ll have.”","“Then I want flowers!”","“There are.”","The pitch-black house suddenly lit up, revealing bundles and bundles of flowers piled across the bed behind them.","Huge bouquets, blooming in full splendor, covered the entire bed.","The very bed they had once shared.","She couldn’t help crying out in surprise. “Oh my God! Where did you get all these?”","Han Mo reached out and slipped an arm around her shoulders. “Do you like them?”","She nodded without hesitation. “I love them!”","“Then be with me?”","She blinked. “But there’s no...”","“There is.”","She puffed out her cheeks and glared at Han Mo. “I haven’t even said what it is yet! I was going to say—mmph...”","His smiling eyes suddenly came close, and his lips covered her deliberately teasing mouth, silencing every word she had been about to say.","“As long as it’s something you want, I’ll have it for you. We’ll be together forever, okay?”","“Mm... okay.”"]}]);
